r 1219(69): 43 shlokas Vadha means killing and the section is named after the killing of Karna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5753bdb48e84322020c4f42a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7033, 7035, 7036]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The gods brought everything that would bring him pleasure.
Suparna157 gave him a feathered peacock with colourful plumage.
The rakshasas gave him a boar and a buffalo.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/575ddbba8df5b38c4b59613c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[144]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O Sanjaya! I had no hope of victory when I heard that Yudhishthira had been defeated in the game of dice by Soubala39 and deprived of his kingdom, though his powerful brothers were still in attendance." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5762ae6f5e403319d714ef97> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 188 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9115]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All of them welcomed and paid their respects to the great-souled Krishna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5776ba8bb767024a4e2908ce> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8735]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I have heard about the rakshasas whom you killed in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/578ae265d6cffc946872c8f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9464]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Vishvavasu’s178 son Chitrasena became my friend and he taught me everything that the gandharvas knew." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/578eb20fc24fe90a34a6c6b2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7727]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Pursued by the terrible rakshasa with the upraised spear and in fear, he suddenly went to his father’s agnihotra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/57dcbff6bae20cf8b524035e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[481, 485]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Why are you not abandoning this withered tree?’ Having been thus asked, the parrot bowed its head down in obeisance and replied, ‘O king of the gods! Welcome.
’ The destroyer of Bala36 knew that the parrot was extremely devoted to dharma and that it was the performer of auspicious deeds.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/57ed684ec4527abb63a0bc3a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "17_Mahaprasthanika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[88]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Why has Krishna11 fallen down on the ground?” Yudhishthira replied, “O supreme among men! She had a great partiality for Dhananjaya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/580151f6cd28f489113ed94d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4770]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Having heard his words, the sages duly216 learnt the Vedas from him and began to practise dharma again." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5806e7aded2d1a94cfb10253> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8600]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The one with the white horses73 is the same to me as Ashvatthama." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5838d7619ea7aebce0a289ba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7693]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ 794(131) ‘K ti id “O h f i ! I thi ti i t ‘Kunti said, “O scorcher of enemies! In this connection, an ancient history is recounted, about a conversation between Vidula297 and her son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/584d9e944562daf16366eb3e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2759]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Triumph and enjoy the earth, or be slain and enjoy heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/586bc61beb879f162e82cedf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8265]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Bhima replied, “The paramatman without qualities683 pervades your body and can be known only through knowledge." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5879c86d12d1f9814615fdc6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12651]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He193 had the blazing Agni as his son, and three daughters who were good in their vows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/588779410a75137a00420dec> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8313]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He690 sent monkeys to search for Sita." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5888fdcbd0db75166511a846> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1610]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "After the two warriors had been shown homage, the queen herself placed her son on Damodara’s30 lap, with a pleasure that was more than usual." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/588bae337e8eb4e977f1c8e5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11082]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There are others who deviate from vows and rituals and are like rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/58999459c235a70194dc7e83> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[45, 48]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Then the immensely famous Hrishikesha6 Krishna went to see his sister and spoke to the soft-spoken and gentle Subhadra with tears in his voice.
Taking his leave from the beautiful one, Varshneya then went to see Krishna7 and Dhoumya.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/58c980fee276f2d5cfec6d8f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[199]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The six of them, with Yajnaseni38 at the forefront, circumambulated the fire and the brahmanas, rich in austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/58d3bc2f1af7844b6c59819c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4234]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king who is engaged in the yoga of samskara655 must know that the foremost components of royal dharma are improvement of the earth,656 not living by alms, protecting the subjects, compassion towards all beings and giving up one’s life in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/58db00e88b56096d5c3082f9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 22 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1278, 1283]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’”’ Chapter 1857(22) he brahmana said, ‘O beautiful one! In this connection, there is an ancient history about the ordinances for the seven officiating priests.
’ ‘“The brahmana replied, ‘Not knowing about the qualities is ignorance.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/58efa1f48543bd75ae46c669> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10131]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The rishis,13 those who are learned in the Vedas, the gandharvas14 and the apsaras15 always worship Rama on Mahendra, the foremost among mountains." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/58f7cd5d3a48b08243108d2f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21946]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Know that I was born in his lineage and my name is Sulabha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/58fd9a677071f4d4c92023ad> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7476]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You have killed the immensely powerful rakshasa who came here with the intention of killing us." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5936f596a0b3b284d66e7000> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25295]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! At the end of the destruction, it will again merge into Narayana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/59432702a6f5c370e51670ff> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10287, 10289]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """“O king! Let the warriors of Dasharha, Kukura and Andhaka26 always be intent on following your orders.
The army of the Madhus27 has infantry, horses, chariots and elephants.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/594360ddda5eeec81862990a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11029]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Nakula’s son used straight-tufted arrows to sever his168 armour from his body and it was wonderful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/59488c4ce18989bfe08012f5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3736]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because of Bhishma’s prowess, the Kurus, and the Andhakas and the Vrishnis, because of their policies, did not come under his85 sway." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5966a6588e5fc26c29c6c495> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7571]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Jataveda634 Agni knows the houses of the learned and does not consume them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/596b43db2c2a1a24094e9f52> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9083]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! On seeing that he117 was delighted with the Pandavas, the yakshas and gandharvas, stood around indifferently." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/596c7ce41c6f45ef3399e2e5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5059]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The one with dharma in his soul353 initiated himself into the horse sacrifice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/597dfbb6a422bd73567d5976> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[80]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 299(2) Vaishampayana said, ‘Those performers of unsullied deeds10 were ready to leave for the forest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/598374ef54ceef43b0490a43> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11326]" ;
        mbh:sourceText ") Jyoti;1263 (786) Suruchi;1264 (787) Huta-bhuj;1265 (." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/59a16661a8715344d386e3a1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[749]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Takshaka and Ashvasena25 were constant companions when they lived on the banks of the river Ikshumati in Kurukshetra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/59b5d4db5ad3ca6c356d8bb7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10147]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Then Krishna arose and embraced Madhava’s9 sister and lovingly said, “Let your husband not have a rival." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/59ca2299d6d4591680c910e2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7798]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Therefore, placing him402 at the front, let Bibhatsu strive his utmost to bring me down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/59e0e18747295653eca32ad7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14137]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Desire leads to anger, avarice and delusion in men and they perform deeds full of pride, insolence, ego and selfishness." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/59e7cc7d038c5c339162b8a1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3034]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Covered with arrows all over his limbs, he107 looked extremely radiant." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/59e90f627de9a4c4aaab3d7b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4795, 4797]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Gods, humans, ancestors, gandharvas, serpents and rakshasas survive on what is offered in sacrifices.
In this way, gods and ancestors survive on what is given to them.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5a01a41af6a190e73a58ab41> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6010]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Infantry was seen to kill each other." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5a0e4cb90432debabf8c0fd6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8765]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowing what must be done in the battle, the victorious Bibhatsu killed all the followers443 and himself rushed against Bhishma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5a107ac0aae8894e76cda956> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4805]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those two foremost rathas46 were successful in striking the target and covered Dhananjaya and Varshneya Vasudeva with showers of arrows from every direction." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5a282b28989e2ee82696792c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5742]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O king! In anger, the immensely strong Dhrishtaketu pierced Somadatta’s son287 in the chest with ninety arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5a3ee3125a39a8fd12ba6aa3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1436]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Therefore, thinking that one is powerful, one should never follow that which is not dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5a4f5be33802bcdee6351356> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6908]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His237 standard was golden and he brandished his giant bow, with a golden back." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5a4f6cfa14c8a44e36c1cfb2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7472]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He274 pierced Bhimasena with ten arrows, each of Madri’s sons with three, Virata and Drupada with six each and Shikhandi with one hundred." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5a56dd625c6d9ba22eb74d1f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3169]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "494 O descendant of the Bharata lineage! This is said to be the eternal dharma, spoken about in the four Vedas, followed by the four officiating priests495 and stated in samkhya yoga." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5a585c12ee763155a72deba3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2782]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Miserliness should be conquered with generosity." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5a6f4e6266de4295fbe8a6e9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2895]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He stood at the head of all the kings among men, like the king of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5a7730658e2dc1adc52d9c49> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[294, 297, 302]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The fortunate Shri and Nalakubara131 are always there.
O tiger among men! And also the three-eyed132 illustrious god, Pashupati Umapati,133 the wielder of the trident, the destroyer of Bhaganetra,134 with the unblemished goddess,135 and surrounded by hundreds and thousands of his followers136—dwarfs, horrible, hunchbacked, bloody-eyed, swift as thought, feeding on flesh, fat and marrow, fearful to see and hear, wielding many terrible weapons and like powerful wind storms.
”’ 236(11) ‘Narada said, “O king! In ancient times, in the era of the gods, the illustrious and indefatigable lord Aditya140 descended from heaven to see the world of men.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5a893387557db559f44e5732> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[498]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having encountered the trifle51 of Shalya, do not get submerged, with your followers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5aab22f1d7dda4f66f54faf5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24024, 24025]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ On being thus addressed, the great god spoke to those gods.
‘O gods! O fortunate ones! It is good that you have brought this to my notice.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5ab199a5619b6008d52d3813> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4702]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘ “Your son552 countered Bhimasena in the battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5ab98cebf195e9ad1fe0089a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[393]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "After the funerals of all the kings were performed with offerings of water, there follows the acknowledgement by Pritha108 of the secret story of how Karna was born from her." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5ac2c18e53cb9022a76e74fc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10337]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But in an instant, the immensely strong one125 picked up another bow and displaying the lightness of his hands, shrouded Phalguna with a storm of arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5aca40a9b9c72728149a16ee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3968]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Rama108 has told him that he is his equal." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5adc78e751ae9e3ab421236a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 29 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1634]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”104 On seeing this marvellous act, the thousand-eyed Purandara was surprised and concluded that the bird must be a great being." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5adc83162996ac40f3d1cfcd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13840]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At first, they were known as both gods and ancestors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5af5370c08d60479f91e09ed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[33, 44]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """We are greatly distressed at learning that you have been defeated by reprehensible enemies, in ways that are not in accordance with dharma.
Regular association with the righteous gives birth to dharma.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5af57305f146d859f85c9072> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8698]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Then Yudhishthira bore down heavily on him and oppressed by this weight, he4 could not travel very fast." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b0aadcec50b1a4aa1a078b1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8082]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Madhava412 was enraged in the battle and, as if he was smiling, pierced the rakshasa with nine arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b198b1998d6f436e526042a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6406, 6415]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """When they were defeated by the daityas, the gods purified themselves in this way.
A brahmana who is the performer of auspicious deeds and is learned in the Vedas and follows vows, must bathe and recite it111 in the presence of the sacred fire, amidst cattle and in an assembly of brahmanas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b3345f344cab46e0ced4e1c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[871]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Having uttered these words, the soft-spoken Krishna47 wept and covered her face in her hands, soft as the bud of a lotus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b33ec58394ac94455696cfc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5906]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "834 When a weak person is slain and cannot find a protector, the gods have arranged that a great and terrible punishment should descend." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b3e3886b528bb44951d064d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10026]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On hearing this, the lord Varshneya83 approved." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b405f3b2c86fbe7903e58a6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1402, 1403]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The king, foremost among those who uphold dharma, got down from his vehicle and entered the forest, with his brothers and companions, like the infinitely energetic Shakra162 in heaven.
When the one who was devoted to the truth descended, masses of charanas163 and siddhas and dwellers of the forest approached the lion who was an Indra among men and surrounded the intelligent one.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b415b08ad8221c14fe65274> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1486]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He thus obtained praise and reverence from the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b43890d534553f6af763171> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10660, 10662, 10664, 10666, 10668]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """There is no dharma superior to the truth.
Truth is the foundation of dharma.
The giving of gifts, sacrifices with dakshina, vows, agnihotra sacrifices, the Vedas and other manifestations of dharma result from the truth.
”’ Chapter 1485(157) ‘Yudhishthira said, “O bull among the Bharata lineage! O immensely wise one! Tell me accurately about the origin of anger, desire, sorrow, confusion, scepticism, lassitude, intoxication, avarice, jealousy, contempt, slander, intolerance and pity.
” ‘Bhishma replied, “Amongst beings, these thirteen are said to be extremely strong enemies.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b5b17855d46070afd8c38f7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4011]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods do not serve the needs of inferior people who are against sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b610740902e3b440c7bfb1e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7386]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kshatta975 is accomplished and wise and instructs us about these things all the time." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b63a89eb74933da2de32451> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3123]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His77 standard had been constructed by Vishvakarma on Indra’s78 instruction and it was extremely beautiful as it fluttered in the path of the sun." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b8729cde778df7e1ef5c451> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10768]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At the right time, it has been ordained by the self-creating one65 that he will be the cause of Bhishma’s death." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b87444779ff46094135eabe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7497]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He must be patient, tolerant, pure, swift, exhibiting manliness at the appropriate time, ready to serve, learned, ready to listen, accomplished in reasoning, intelligent, firm in his mind, ready to implement what is fair, self- controlled, always pleasant in speech, forgiving when there is a catastrophe, ceaseless in generosity, ready to act on his own, possessing excellent gates,983 pleasant to behold, ready to extend a hand to those who are distressed, always engaged in policy indicated by the learned, without ego, without opposite sentiments, without a tendency to act on everything, unwavering in pursuing a task that has been undertaken, a master who is loved by the servants, ready to bring people together, not rigid, always possessing a pleasant demeanour, generous, attentive towards the servants, without anger, extremely broad- minded, ready to use the rod of chastisement, not failing to use the rod of chastisement, a ruler who ensures acts of dharma, one who uses spies as his eyes, attentive towards enemies and always accomplished in dharma and artha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b8ee370437454c692af35f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4037]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With the welfare of the gods in mind, he thought for an instant." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5b9f8a00676077b8a0ae9c0e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[654]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods refuse to accept the offerings of one who gives away a frightened one who has sought succour." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5badd1636e898f22322ab191> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2903]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was like Manu70 himself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5bb303b32e8488d540293d19> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8306, 8307]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """For some reason, Sugriva was driven out by his brother687 and lived with me, for a long time, in Rishyamukha.
At that time, the immensely strong hero Dasharathi688 Rama, who was Vishnu in human form, roamed on this earth.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5bb6529627cf85cc45ef823c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2759]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Cruel in their intentions and prepared to give up their lives, all of them35 raised their standards and advanced against the Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5bb6a6e45a6e207e3f9aa5f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2242]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On witnessing Yajnasena’s133 blazing prosperity, Dhritarashtra’s daughters-in-law were not enthused." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5bc3115832e91e5c4ddbd51f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4637]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the god of all the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5bc6d6f33dd84d41f51877af> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 285 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17091]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When the wielder of the vajra begs for the earrings, you should not give them to him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5bccbed92493264e2c5ba562> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6927]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This maiden is like one born from the gods and a single son will be born to me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c1d63a123e270b6e31cc56c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1441]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They saw Krishna48 Droupadi, afflicted by great misery." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c275dd277bef8aeaf9a86fa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7051, 7054]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """“Pashupati’s40 festival will be held in the beautiful city of Varanavata.
” On Dhritarashtra’s bidding, these were the words they uttered.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c2adce287613a66f08c9a6e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15180]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Following Partha’s43 request, he placed him on the chariot and went to the centre of the hermitage, where Yudhishthira was seated." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c32390913ee20dae5d46a1d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[670, 672]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ Having said this, that supreme warrior among men looked at the rakshasa, his eyes wide with rage.
‘“When the one with the form of a cloud was slain, those sons of the Indra among men15 placed Krishna at the forefront.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c368797cb1982ae91c0965c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[753]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "130 His131 supreme armour was made out of iron and he was adorned with the best of gems." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c5b4bd6f45fcb70741f80f5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3233]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is a country named Aratta426 there, where dharma has been destroyed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c651c3c514c3bcd59532b92> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[163]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The two blazing planets, Brihaspati and Shani, are near Vishakha31 and have become stationary for a year." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c7425f81adc38302f322774> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11754]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“All of the Kapas are exactly like you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c755186f73c9784e78e7766> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17792]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Yudhishthira said, “The deer ran away with his29 kindling." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c88d5e938b8d3ea9f146587> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9651]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of men! Especially during shuklapaksha in the month of Koumudi,364 one must avoid all kinds of meat." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c8944f526fe68e0145127cc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2826]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! The kshatriyas82 saw that Saindhava took up the entire burden and roared and rushed to the spot where Yudhishthira’s army was." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c8e80aaa0db3dce65dcdd08> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2869]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that the Kshatriyas followed dharma, the one with thousand eyes and performer of a hundred sacrifices78 poured down sweet rain at the right time and the right place, so that subjects prospered." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5c96d35b0be30dfd8da6b7b6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9585]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowledge that cannot be defined is non-existent." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5ca571debda702e50224dc3c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5991, 5994]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """In the morning, the bodies of sages, emaciated from restrained diets, would be seen, lifeless on the ground.
Oppressed by the fear of the Kaleyas, the world lost all enterprise.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5cab58aa4a6fe6e2635dcbcc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8277]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ ‘“Goutama replied, ‘King Vaishravana’s266 dominion is Mandakini." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5cbc6bc97301309ced946d9b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[415]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is related the excellent story of Samvarta and Marutta, the discovery of the golden treasures,112 then the birth of Parikshit, who was burnt almost dead by the weapon and revived by Krishna again, the Pandava’s113 journey with the sacrificial horse that had been set loose, his combats with angry princes, Dhananjaya’s encounter with Chitrangada’s son,114 his great danger in the battle with Babhruvahana and the story of the mongoose in the great horse-sacrifice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5cbd7510cfa42784cf8f8a2f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1317]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Having been thus praised by the gods and all the sages, Suparna45 then decreased his energy and his splendour." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5cd0924a7beb98e79b8421b5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 316 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22737]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If a brahmana is not attached to an association with any of the qualities and if he always dwells alone, he will soon obtain supreme bliss." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5cd3d1c829489626c10c5a14> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15215]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“O illustrious one! I think that time, and destiny created by the gods, is inevitable for all beings and cannot be transgressed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5cecc8acdd71007c49cba97c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1677]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Horses with the complexion of atarusha60 flowers bore one hundred and forty thousand foremost rathas who followed Pandya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5d123148a245074d74c07d71> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[141, 142]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘“O Sanjaya! I had no hope of victory when I heard that, in the presence of all the kings, Krishna37 was taken, when the wonderful bow was drawn and pierced, the target fell to the ground.
‘“O Sanjaya! I had no hope of victory when I heard that Subhadra of the Madhu lineage was forcibly carried away by Arjuna and married in Dvaraka and when the two heroes38 of the Vrishni lineage set out for Indraprastha.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5d1438395baa042e835bedfb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20918]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "855 Budhyamana is spoken of as being both unmanifest and ignorant." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5d2767d9ca161dae9c6827cb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8057]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“It is known that except for the first eighty instants,35 when terrible dusk colours and night is about to descend, the rest36 is set aside for yakshas, gandharvas, rakshasas and others who can travel wherever at will." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5d42b545ab7ee7be1e867b7f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13158, 13159]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O immensely strong one! Be instated as the general of the gods.
O immensely strong one! Following your words, I will remain as Indra.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5d43ac31452230000eeaf90b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2267]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Sudhanva! I desire that you should give it41 back to Virochana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5d57dc8e85c3f6a0b1798b80> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6914]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” At this, the large number of gods approached the grandfather." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5d62302cebef0094d19d16be> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19428]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Devarshi Ushanas686 was always engaged in what was agreeable to the asuras and unpleasant for the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5d6e7246674f53da840af7da> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3526]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But he is seen by the gods and by the being who dwells in every heart." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5d7b764c1b3713d7c1b04535> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6963]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having returned the maiden to his disciple,224 Koushika225 left for the forest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5d848f45c4e47fc1877656e4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2410, 2413, 2414]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Your handsome grandson Lakshmana17 was at the forefront.
The king18 was surrounded by maharatha Karna, Duhshasana and Kripa.
With a white umbrella held aloft his head, he was like the king of the gods in his beauty.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5d8e586a64cd6977f1476b84> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7834]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Thereupon, the rakshasa became even more enraged." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5d998dc10f14513736199113> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13993]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing the four brave Pandavas advance into battle on their chariots and on seeing them as resplendent as the guardians of the worlds, the residents of Gandhamadana53 established themselves in battle formations." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5da768a275a0b6388cbadb21> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3796]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He142 thought, ‘For the welfare of the Pandavas, I will armour myself and kill Bhishma today." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5dce0e1b7573ffcd2a958eae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[838]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Uluka attacked like a bird76 and so did Shakuni Soubala." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5dd4cd92760bd4b78b8ab3d5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2101]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But this brave Shalya, the ornament of assemblies, is his298 equal." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5ddf165ce71829245d78fa2a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3729]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods made many attempts to dislodge him from his vows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5dedacfee076d86d6470bcbe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6768]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 124: 33 shlokas Chapter 125: 32 shlokas Chapter 126: 39 shlokas Chapter 127: 24 shlokas Chapter 128: 18 shlokas Chapter 129: 18 shlokas Chapter 130: 20 shlokas Chapter 131: 18 shlokas Chapter 132: 19 shlokas Chapter 133: 30 shlokas Chapter 134: 28 shlokas Chapter 135: 21 shlokas Chapter 136: 19 shlokas Chapter 137: 23 shlokas Chapter 138: 31 shlokas Jatu is lac and griha is house." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5dedfda02300452dfa152670> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3433]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "1269 Wood never satisfies a fire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5dfb17b1dfddbb4bd4ea12b9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 169 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9929]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 833(170): 22 shlokas Chapter 834(171): 9 shlokas Chapter 835(172): 23 shlokas Chapter 836(173): 18 shlokas Chapter 837(174): 26 shlokas Chapter 838(175): 30 shlokas Chapter 839(176): 42 shlokas Chapter 840(177): 24 shlokas Chapter 841(178): 38 shlokas Chapter 842(179): 31 shlokas Chapter 843(180): 39 shlokas Chapter 844(181): 36 shlokas Chapter 845(182): 16 shlokas Chapter 846(183): 27 shlokas Chapter 847(184): 18 shlokas Chapter 848(185): 23 shlokas Chapter 849(186): 36 shlokas Chapter 850(187): 40 shlokas Chapter 851(188): 18 shlokas Chapter 852(189): 18 shlokas Chapter 853(190): 23 shlokas Chapter 854(191): 20 shlokas Chapter 855(192): 30 shlokas Chapter 856(193): 66 shlokas Chapter 857(194): 22 shlokas Chapter 858(195): 20 shlokas Chapter 859(196): 19 shlokas Chapter 860(197): 21 shlokas Upakhyana is a short tale or episode and this section is so named because it has the short account of Amba, who was reborn as Shikhandi." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5dfc43a146cd80b38ca897cf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4835]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "5 With dakshina, a person may give away a cow with beautiful horns that are decorated with gold, along with a brass vessel to milk her, an expensive upper garment and sesamum seed to a brahmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5dfe264ea0b004fceb689460> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4908]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Svayambhu719 created the brahmana and the kshatriya from the same womb." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5e06caee2a409de68fc020e7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9284]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“As Indrani66 is to Harihaya,67 as Svaha68 is to Vibhavasu,69 as Rohini70 is to Soma,71 as Damayanti is to Nala, as Bhadra72 is to Vaishravana,73 as Arundhati is to Vashishtha and as Lakshmi is to Narayana, so may you be to your husbands." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5e1bd0c7a431bec6cced5157> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24707]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "These best of gods are engaged in great austerities and major vows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5e320dc5afe6a3faec305f4d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1646]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "How can you establish the entire universe in this evil-minded protector of herds, Bhoja’s37 servant? O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Or perhaps your devotion is not a natural one." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5e4c99ee5e3e44226bacb500> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7721]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! The kritya647 whom the great-souled one had created went to Yavakrita, and having deluded him, robbed him of his water-pot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5e5bb9f0d0c3112d97bfb33a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6395, 6398]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """There is a sacred object that the gods eat and it is supreme in the worlds.
Ghee is offered as oblation into the fire.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5e67cac5232f97af2afcc12a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 41 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1658]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Hearing these words of Bhishma, the kings became angry." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5e7ac4a1ac43f2c4dac02c3c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16695]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the gods! Listen again to my words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5e81d002b70b8d163f9c2029> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18326]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At this, the gods were satisfied." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5e97efcb26feae1edd422948> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4633]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is Shakra’s73 tirtha named Kumarika, frequented by the siddhas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5ea53a1ebfc9d4536a1918b4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7062]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Addressing Shantanu’s son, Bhishma, the immensely wise Vidura, Drona, the Bahlika Somadatta, the Kouravas, Kripa, the preceptor’s son42 and the illustrious Gandhari, Yudhisthira said, softly and meekly, “On Dhritarashtra’s command, we are going with our friends to the lovely and populated city of Varanavata." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5eb4ba00b070e55b503ab986> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10897]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Having been thus addressed by me, the handsome god of the gods, immensely radiant, supreme among eloquent ones, comforted me and spoke these words to me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5ed459a87ac998ee9b5cb683> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14326]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Know that sattva is the quality of the gods and that the other two98 represent the qualities of the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5ef60f87ba4fae61b1707879> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3172, 3173]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Let the Himalayas move from where they are established, let the sun be dimmed, let coolness be destroyed from the moon, if I deviate from this vow.
In the fourteenth year, if Duryodhana does not restore the kingdom to us with proper honour, all this will certainly happen.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5efad7c1b50b37579cb9f7cc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1, 2, 6]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """After Drona’s death, Karna is instated as the commander of the Kourava army.
Karna is the commander for two days, days sixteen and seventeen.
In the numbering of the chapters in Karna Parva, the first number is a consecutive one, starting with the beginning of the Mahabharata.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f00e6c837b61e9c75202d81> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14606]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’” ‘Sanjaya said, “O destroyer of enemies! O foremost among the Bharata lineage! Having addressed Arjuna in the battle, Parashara’s son135 went away to the spot he had arrived from." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f09ab3cb87950a5d245c80c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10071]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The aged one98 possessed all the qualities, like Yayati, the son of Nahusha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f0b06972b19bf42e77025d7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[119]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Are they27 acting in accordance with dharma, if they are not prepared to give up the kingdom? The Kounteyas have passed the prescribed period of concealment." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f3902d5fa7524cf94a12335> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10116]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lord of the Kurus107 possessed the gait of an elephant and a lion." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f393896791d59bb0dead048> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8913]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Kimpurushas, lovers with their beloveds, devoted to each other, can be seen on the peaks of this mountain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f5044567079dbc511ff00ec> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2472, 2474]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O lord! You are the one who is superior to the gods in all the qualities.
” It has been heard, that in this fashion, the gods bowed down their heads before the grandfather who is the lord of the three worlds and sought his favours, so that he might become the charioteer.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f52a71bacc5d83139306f8c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5024]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Sanjaya replied, “The valiant one15 was cheerful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f5b79c1f3de3a40ea36f8be> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6033]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is a famous class of extremely terrible Kaleyas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f87a5e0c26174533ca6d438> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[149, 150, 152, 154, 155]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Let messengers who travel swiftly go to Shalya,36 Dhrishtaketu,37 the lord Jayatsena38 and all the Kekayas.
Duryodhana is certain to send messengers to all of them also.
Therefore, let us make haste and let us request those Indras among men first.
‘“Send word to Shalya quickly and to the kings who are under his suzerainty, and to King Bhagadatta, who dwells by the eastern ocean.
And to Amitouja, Ugra, Hardikya, Ahuka, the extremely wise Malla and the lord Rochamana.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f88542238edf18f0b4724dc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4642]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the god of the gods and the god of all beings." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f8b2b77b346a01ac9223e57> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2397, 2399]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """” ‘ “‘The tigers among the gods then constructed the chariot.
Mandara327 was the axle and Mahanadi328 became the flank.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f8b9aa90fa31a73ddcc2698> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[172]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The terrible archer left for the battle and went to where the bull among the Bharata lineage16 was." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5f91e631a1c4bb420934cf5d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10628]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O one who is beloved of the sages! Wait for me on the boat." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5fb6de6380bf7e3d2e0667d2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5529]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Krishna! O Keshava! With his two arms, Arjuna rivals the thousand-armed Arjuna48 and always surpasses him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5fc9f749b51daa52a119aaaa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8337]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king76 then spoke to the rishi,77 ‘O Brahmana! O great sage! Give me Nandini in exchange for my kingdom or for 10,000 cows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5fcdd5e56dbc1558e70c0978> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8326]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This is the celestial path of the gods and humans cannot travel along it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5fd56c014e81fbc7adcf51ec> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5228]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On bathing at the lake of the gods there, pure and restrained in mind, one obtains a horse sacrifice and goes to supreme success." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5fea4ebbbbb0db17c31d14b2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24521]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king of the gods was cleansed of sin." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/5ffe9ced413235aa3352c20c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12656]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "49 Discerning Krishna’s intention and on seeing that he50 was stationed at the front, the destroyer of enemy cities, Bhimasena, approached and spoke these words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6007abbe822faed223a24857> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9913]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I will lead the rathas, together with your soldiers, against the soldiers of the sons of Pandu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/60094083ebd5672a565e4bec> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[459]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The men who are born there are those who have been dislodged from the world of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/600a0e9c9cc0316765507770> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14609]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I think that a person who follows dharma has had a successful birth if he has been able to please the illustrious one1 who has made his dharma manifest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6023bbc946c1349ba32ab077> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1131]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowing that daitya weapons had been released, he105 sliced them off by unleashing enormously powerful brahma arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/604395ad2b8dd1bd7cbb5b35> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9095]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Karna said, “O king! As long as Gangeya7 is alive, I will never fight." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6044e15a094be3a69cb9c81e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6039]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The cow should be of the Rohini type." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/60453f467299099300d39ee1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8250]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Sanjaya! That evil-minded son349 of mine repeatedly said in the assembly, ‘In the battle, Karna, Duhshasana and I will conquer the Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/604a438558830aa819d8f4d2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7998]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In time, this one with the beautiful waist will perform the objective of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/604c60401c847b3137ac8d46> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[379]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods protect me extremely well." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/604c96159d4bb8d11678d571> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3013]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When they advanced towards him in battle, Bhishma, Shantanu’s son, pierced Panchala66 with three and Satyaki with sharp arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/604d1c38805133e9d6d2e79d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1776]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having taken Pandavya’s6 leave, King Duryodhana set out for Gajasahrya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6063f08e9bbbf24a9c4244ef> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14255]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Know that your energy and anger have also been born from Rudra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6074c0bc8f99061538ea380c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6210]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "108 Look here and see if there is a groom who appeals to you because of his qualities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6076b054c741ffee39bd77ac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2068]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That abominable game of dice then began there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/607b4d522ece30eba4cb990d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5680]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘He256 heard from the Brahmanas that Subala’s daughter, the fortunate Gandhari, had obtained a boon by pleasing Hara, the god who robbed Bhaga of his eyes." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/60b2917886a7dfca3273a650> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24367, 24368]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The gods are satisfied through sacrifices.
The gods sustain the earth.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/60c3d06a5088588c916ee42d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11753]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He230 became a blue cloud in the sky, with Indra’s weapon231 in it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/60c75a0a7eadfc8c291153d1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[683]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! Like the currents of rivers make no impression on mountains, weapons hurled by the gods will cause him no pain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/60cc2fcaef9ac43aa34f0e7b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[737, 738]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O fortunate one! Follow me quickly and you will be able to see that supreme among gods.
’ As the goddess91 went on ahead, Indrani followed her.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/60d3a14d259dbe971cf43658> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5358]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Having thus reassured the king, the illustrious rishi Narada took his leave of the great-souled one324 and instantly disappeared." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/60d9794acc93cc8672b42069> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3699]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "463 Dharmaraja Yudhishthira saw that his464 strength was like that of Death and that he was slaying thousands of warriors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/60da3ce3e4b930baa827d6be> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3002]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Dhara was the son25 of Dhumra, and so was Dhruva, who had knowledge of the brahman." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/60e654bd204d2088382b8aa6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21005]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is sometimes born in the world of the gods, but is also born as inferior species." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/60ead596aaed39c965b99e4c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[866]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Having said this, the king gave orders that Sahadeva should be instated30 and readied himself to do battle with those whose deeds were terrible." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6109567079175e61091b4fc7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4643]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With straight-tufted arrows, Partha, tiger among men, destroyed the fourfold547 army of the sons of Dhritarashtra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/610fa4fd618372016b63b443> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[445]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The appendices are known as Hari Vamsha127 and Bhavishya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/611a7c01d190c258a73b412b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3070]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O unassailable one! I know from Narada, Devala, Krishna Dvaipayana and the grandfather of the Kurus208 that everything is based in you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/612906760bbc0ed82d51cdde> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10830]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If he211 gives up his life for the sake of a brahmana, he will be purified." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/616af1d6f7b08c749704bf65> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[194]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ The foremost among the Bhrigu lineage was incensed at this and he24 had fallen down on the ground, trembling, distressed and hands joined in salutation." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/616bb6eb921b89faceff4f3b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8343]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Worlds are ordained for such people." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/618dbeb740634987ff9f9d90> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8498]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I hurled the shami stick278 and performed tens of thousands of sacrifices for the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/61905edd4187f2d40f4910dc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 203 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9752]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All these rishis were paying homage to the grandfather." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6192f23ed9eb76b221e62151> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13483, 13484, 13485]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O son of a god! The gods will be under your suzerainty.
’ Having spoken these words to Mahasena, Shachi’s husband322 stopped.
He took the permission of the illustrious Tryambaka323 and left, together with the other gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/619b9c0b2f2c634a8e996287> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12903]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Hearing these words, the lord of the gods bowed in obeisance." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/61a0c7a47deace7c7528e56b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13371]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "315 Soma316 held a white umbrella over his head." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/61a3eb85649960463a7074cd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10218]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "28 The great archer Sutasoma, with energy equal to that of the sun and the moon, was born as a son from Bhimasena after he had performed one thousand soma29 sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/61b693ddbd5e0ae9168aaf1f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1250]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” The grandfather36 himself heard this extremely cruel curse uttered by Kadru, and driven by destiny, bearing in mind the welfare of all creatures, since the snakes had greatly multiplied, he37 and the other gods approved the curse." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/61c488ad52d3e4e8ac1b3427> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6552]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It was here that those gods, who had obtained the required boon, earlier drank soma at sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/61d9eb080a9ed6ad864471f0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10319]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His form was terrible, one that created terror among the enemies of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/61db94821cd93ec1d6429d95> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[474]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is a forest of bhadrasala87 there and a large tree named Kalamra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/61f2047e84fce87cd7e6f2c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2095]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Flower can be collected after flower, but the root must not be severed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/61f79da8d2a0541c02d271fa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12154]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! On seeing it, the rakshasa was frightened." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6201c1010c516698c7f5a799> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18304]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods were granting kingdoms and riches to those who performed good deeds and were taking them away in the case of bad deeds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/62141c3114a799f0c8931917> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9388]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Show your valour before Varshneya25 arrives with his Yadava army to restore the Pandavas to their kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6217bb74ca696bbfe633f089> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2662]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Just as the gods are propitiated, they must always be tended to." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6234878a831c4fb852678711> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5861]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He offered each deer in that great forest to all the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/62398574d12523f5178643a0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3263]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "7 If there is a desire to fight with Bhima and Arjuna, the sons of the Ashvins8 and Vasudeva, with Shini’s son9 who has raised his weapons, with Dhrishtadyumna and Shikhandi, with Yudhishthira, who is equal to Indra and can burn up earth and heaven with the ire of his thoughts—if Dhritarashtra’s son wishes to fight with these, then all the objectives of the Pandavas will be successful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/62451a13355935aed11ae7ee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13773]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Karna! What joy can be greater than the sight of Drupada’s daughter Droupadi, clad in red18 garments in the forest? If Dharmaraja, Bhimasena and Pandava19 see me united with this supreme prosperity, it is worth living." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6277ddb7bcafe03d20a8fe77> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10405]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O mighty-armed one! O supreme among men! Restrain them and the Kekayas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/627e6a896e096f8d6eca9843> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[252]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The Vedas should be supported with itihasa84 and the Puranas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/627ea33637e592b75f9373c9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17453]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the lord of the gods himself and it is you who should give me a boon, since you are the lord of all other beings and the creator of all beings." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6286c09ea4d21760d3937cac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16095]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Wisdom conveys one to what is most beneficial." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6288f01b7931eca7a5917490> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10182]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Thus honoured, the rakshasa honoured the brahmana back in return." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/62bbb2316e222faebb3507fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13254]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ At that, an extremely strong being, golden in complexion, sprung up from Skanda’s body to devour the offspring of humans." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/62df6566b4e9b1d04d4ace9d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5266, 5267]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Samkarshana751 always possesses strength and Gada752 is again delicate.
O Narada! Pradyumna753 surpasses me in beauty, but I have no aides.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/62fcc9c2bc1333682107e16a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15776]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "261 He262 is mysterious and has been spoken about in the words of the Vedas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/62ff9e9636095d938f82d1f6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[616]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ ‘“On hearing his words, which were full of dharma and artha, they abandoned the path of non-believers71 and resorted to the dharma of householders." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/631cc7d44f34f11de09cb6ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10217]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Autumn arrived, with masses of curlews and swans." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/632ff94d1a097a4d842786b5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22904]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Shuklapaksha and krishnapaksha incessantly progress." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/633741a8a5e8286051692a93> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13743]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You shine among them, like the one with the rays12 among the gods in heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63543dee999bf08acc89351d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7346]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O mighty-armed one! I will save you from the rakshasa who eats human flesh." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6358f64d1fa162d31e8d7b88> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8045, 8046, 8049, 8051]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Along with the offerings, flowers, curds and well-cooked food, auspicious, fragrant and agreeable to see, must be rendered to the gods.
Offerings made to yakshas and rakshasas must have blood and meat, mixed with liquor249 and decorated with parched rice.
Someone who eats only after honouring the gods with a first share becomes strong and noble.
One’s house is radiant because of the gods who are present in the house.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63598d5f4756c48da15177c8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[961]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then the sage engaged Pramadvara with Ruru, fixing the date for marriage as one when the nakshatra19 Bhagadaiva20 would be in the ascendant." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6377326637008602be31def9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2585]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Just as Matali controls the horses yoked to Hari’s351 chariot, Shalya will control the ones that are yoked to yours." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/637ffdd164e0527fd35182d5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10363]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I entered the city34 and told Satyavati everything." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63802becdf1a959794cd0f78> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1460]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It went to the tirtha72 named Alamba and saw many celestial trees there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/638b4ca35be4f5d07ad0d3f3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 24 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2374]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the gods! O wielder of the trident! Show your favours and kill the danavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/638c0b254713aa1c157c0277> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6327]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The wind always blows there and the gods shower down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/639b215869e4457e272ee1ef> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5014, 5015]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He obtained many rare boons, difficult even among the gods.
O descendant of the Bharata lineage! The destroyer of Tripura228 was satisfied and told him, “O Krishna! You will be more loved in the world.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63a2731210b093c61e94ccf1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5700]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Together with the brahmanas, those sons of Pandu then went to Prajapati’s377 altar, frequented by ascetics." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63ab53926e445dfdda51603c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1252]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was astride Surabhi’s descendant155 and was as peaceful as a fire without smoke." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63aceff2bfcb4f121ec74463> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9143]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Adorned with divine ornaments, he finds pleasure with the maidens of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63af68a96b79b702243fc2f6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16668]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That is spoken of as something that satisfies the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63bdf97b34025c469f5997e1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3775, 3779]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """There is an account of the four kinds of time for departure565 and a complete description of the three kinds of victory—victory for reasons of dharma, victory for reasons of artha and objectives, and victory that is asura in nature.
O Pandava! There are eight that are direct—chariots, elephants, horses, foot soldiers, compulsory service, boats, spies and guides for the road568 as the eighth.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63c49c1ece4d555f24e92e81> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4683, 4684]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ O king! It is said that thus did the sages speak.
O lord of the earth! In an attempt to prevent those self-controlled sages from becoming angry, the lord of yoga102 resorted to yoga and created one crore Rudras, one before every sage.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63cd2b7f5951661b28435feb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4987]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O king! On seeing that his brave and immensely strong sons had been killed in battle, Varshneya231 roared and attacked Bhurishrava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63deb1ad644de53b5a34e77d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4077]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The son born through a vaishya is a bandi or magadha1318 and earns a living through the use of words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63e2c71c6e770a6164595cef> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1537, 1538]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Vain about his valour, Purandara87 was amazed at this sight and contemptuously laughing at them swiftly passed over them, stepping over their heads.
At this they were angered and began a great act88 that would bring danger to Shakra.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/63e441a0535dedc530bc2ae8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[658]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In human form, with a complexion like that of pure gold, the rakshasa woman did not look like a rakshasa at all." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6400303bfbbc187b4dc51d20> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9501]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the gods were alerted by the roar." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/64038b1bace40630300b36a1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1148]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The other gods satisfied him with the sacrifice known as saptakapala144 and made them flow again." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6406ee477716d186851ec7ee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6886, 6887, 6888]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The Vaikhanasas were born, with the qualities of austerities and learning.
The handsome Ashvins were born from his140 ears.
Finally, the Prajapatis were born from his ears.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6417f3072004c720dbb1d0f5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4937]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Have you not seen the innumerable arrows shot by Kiriti? As he swiftly advances, they descend one krosha57 behind his chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/641e41fbc36861ac92bfabcb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1178]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then the warriors who were Shalva’s followers in battle shot hundreds and thousands of curved arrows115 at me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/642d1f01c6a0b8808aaab41b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16168]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The one who was victorious over his enemies wrathfully hurled the trunk of a shala tree at Indrajit." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/643923e9228c8f9c31b18f74> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2293]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having been pierced by that bull among the Bharatas, with an arrow that sliced through the armour on his body, the king139 fell down dead on the ground, like a tree140 dislodged from the peak of a mountain by the wind." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/643deeb7876bd16fd1da9173> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[424]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He went back to the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/64508b636143e9a718f33304> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1183]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "My heart trembles when I hear that the two Krishnas16 are united on the same chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/64517d319d9a70a5538e2e96> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9285]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "One who is full of adharma goes to hell." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/646de6e6753bb6b363fda323> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5547]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As before, the unblemished Satya244 summoned the rishi." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6471e2393822c9deb0a4d4d7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7528]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "626 We have heard that among the gods, there is a class of eight Vasus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/647665b1a7b1796dcc6ab58d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[228]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! These and many other ascetics who are rigid in their vows, riding chariots that are like the moon and themselves, as handsome as the moon Bhrigu and the seven great sages77 go there on Brahma’s instructions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/647c11f9c66c7cfa0db83fc1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9212]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘The immensely wise Kshatta3 had foreseen this and had spoken to the king, as soon as the wicked Suyodhana, the exterminator of his lineage, was born." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6483b479db7c003edc9a66d6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8047]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Your elder brother’s324 conduct is in accordance with dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/64a88720d4dc8566926d8a8f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 60 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4214]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 1038(61): 51 shlokas Chapter 1039(62): 23 shlokas Chapter 1040(63): 33 shlokas Chapter 1041(64): 60 shlokas Chapter 1042(65): 32 shlokas Chapter 1043(66): 43 shlokas Chapter 1044(67): 71 shlokas Chapter 1045(68): 66 shlokas Chapter 1046(69): 75 shlokas Chapter 1047(70): 51 shlokas Chapter 1048(71): 31 shlokas Chapter 1049(72): 35 shlokas Chapter 1050(73): 53 shlokas Chapter 1051(74): 58 shlokas Chapter 1052(75): 36 shlokas Chapter 1053(76): 42 shlokas Chapter 1054(77): 38 shlokas Chapter 1055(78): 46 shlokas Chapter 1056(79): 33 shlokas Chapter 1057(80): 38 shlokas Chapter 1058(81): 46 shlokas Chapter 1059(82): 39 shlokas Chapter 1060(83): 39 shlokas Chapter 1061(84): 30 shlokas Chapter 1062(85): 101 shlokas Chapter 1063(86): 50 shlokas Chapter 1064(87): 75 shlokas Chapter 1065(88): 59 shlokas Chapter 1066(89): 43 shlokas Chapter 1067(90): 50 shlokas Chapter 1068(91): 54 shlokas Chapter 1069(92): 44 shlokas Chapter 1070(93): 35 shlokas Chapter 1071(94): 18 shlokas Chapter 1072(95): 47 shlokas Chapter 1073(96): 45 shlokas Chapter 1074(97): 55 shlokas Chapter 1075(98): 58 shlokas Chapter 1076(99): 28 shlokas Chapter 1077(100): 39 shlokas Chapter 1078(101): 74 shlokas Chapter 1079(102): 105 shlokas Chapter 1080(103): 49 shlokas Chapter 1081(104): 33 shlokas Chapter 1082(105): 36 shlokas Chapter 1083(106): 54 shlokas Chapter 1084(107): 39 shlokas Chapter 1085(108): 41 shlokas Chapter 1086(109): 34 shlokas Chapter 1087(110): 39 shlokas Chapter 1088(111): 35 shlokas Chapter 1089(112): 45 shlokas Chapter 1090(113): 26 shlokas Chapter 1092(115): 24 shlokas Chapter 1093(116): 36 shlokas Chapter 1094(117): 62 shlokas Chapter 1095(118): 52 shlokas Chapter 1096(119): 28 shlokas Chapter 1097(120): 89 shlokas Chapter 1098(121): 49 shlokas The word vadha means death or killing and this section is named after the death or killing of Jayadratha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/64aa44cafaeaf543beb8843b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5808]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They were also pierced with arrows shot by Kripa, Shalya, Shala and the lord Chitrasena and their293 anger increased, like the gods when they confronted the assembled daityas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/64bbb658cd3f7f50afe994e9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1378]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rajarshi Pandava40 does not wish to win through the use of adharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/64d7af6dd6858557a53f7ec6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 79 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5148]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "What use is a bull that does not bear a load? What use is a cow that does not yield milk? What use is a barren wife? What use is a king who does not protect? What use is an elephant made of wood? What use is a deer made of leather? What use is a cart without a drive and a path? What use is a degraded field? A brahmana who does not study and a king who does not protect are always useless in this way, like a cloud that does not rain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/64eb7354db5d32efc4b86498> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13778]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The immensely fortunate Soma11 became a husband to all of them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/64ee9e15f9298e5d999d274b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7169]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Armour, ornaments, garments and weapons are strewn around." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/64f97fe1399d8945163ee2ed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3139]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The rear was protected by Virata, together with Kekaya, the king of Kashi and Shaibya83 and thirty thousand chariots." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6510bfe4778ffb81a416b538> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2632]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I obtained the Roudra weapon from Rudra, Varuna170 from Varuna, the Agneya weapon from Agni, Vayavya from Matarishvan171 and the vajra and other weapons from Shakra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/651c0c3a541d152159a2e1d8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 45 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1869, 1875, 1878]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O bull among the Bharata lineage! On seeing all this, I felt as if afflicted with fever.
O descendant of the Bharata lineage! I continuously heard the repeated blowing of conch shells.
O great king! Those kings brought all kinds of riches with them, when they came to the sacrifice of the intelligent son of Pandu.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/651c414e886f64c827e16c7f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17502]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 592(295): 17 shlokas Chapter 593(296): 43 shlokas Chapter 594(297): 74 shlokas Chapter 595(298): 28 shlokas Chapter 596(299): 29 shlokas Arani means wood used for kindling and this parva is named after that." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6544ea27189af883928cf890> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5847]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "295 Your son296 was unrivalled in his prowess and was like the king of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/655c012547540f04c906bb73> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2406]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The ten lords of the nagas, with Dhritarashtra331 as the foremost, constituted the shaft." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/655ddafa3ba0a27e7422bde0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3682]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He addressed his priests and advisers, “All of you have heard what the messenger of the gods has to say." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/656a7cd857835cd2c9538514> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 54 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3090]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If it is true that the gods themselves have decided that the king of Nishadha should be my husband, then let the gods direct me towards him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/657bb0258f8fbe8c8db843dd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5965]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the gods were happy and delighted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65851d7248d78fc615d0c2dd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[831]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He knows the divine tales about the gods and the demons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65866c8a54114e1a8ee39f17> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9098]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The destruction of the yakshas and the rakshasas had been determined by the gods earlier." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/658698716b781eb8b29fba59> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5678, 5679]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He saw that the supreme among rishis67 had arrived there before him.
Janardana embraced Krishna’s68 feet and the king’s.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65919a7b5d8c7b5a518a5ad2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[515]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Grant us leave." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/659d2a1aa65940c39497d178> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16393]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Monkeys and black-faced bears were his allies, creatures from a different species." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65a97fab0673505e852ff9b2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[381]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Nahusha44 said, ‘It is not desirable to possess nothing." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65b54dbbe0999eecd2e26702> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 34 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2432]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His energy was superior to that of Phalguna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65b695456f92d4216a676459> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1248]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Madravati’s95 brave sons will guard my chariot wheels." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65ba52985d16b519898b9aee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[956]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Vasudeva replied, “O best of the Bharata lineage! When he heard that the mighty-armed King Shroutashrava67 had been killed by me, Shalva marched on the city of Dvaravati." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65bed1d70df8b805aec901ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6328]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’” ‘Y ‘Bhishma continued, “The great-souled lord of the earth104 thought about the superiority that the supreme rishi had spoken about in his words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65d08d2ab6333097b401cac0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13530, 13561]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """No man has seen the other side of the Himalayas, or the dark side of the moon.
210 Darkness is seen when it approaches the moon and the sun.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65d82837094d55fcf02f5078> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5258]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing them resplendent in that great battle, with shining and golden armour, your immensely strong sons gave up the fight with Bhima." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65dcdb5890f7346bf8f1037b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8016]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Both were insulted when Krishna320 was brought to the assembly hall and Duhshasana addressed terrible and harsh words towards her, while all the brave Kurus looked on." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65de4f5e60a5af79c13efdda> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14808]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Whose wife are you? Whose daughter are you?”’ 547(250) Vaishampayana said, ‘Then princess Droupadi replied to the question that the foremost of the Shibis5 had asked." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65ef784b48079e6e14355664> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7061]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ ‘“The charioteer replied, ‘O Varshneya! O one who has truth as his valour! Know that I have no fear, even if the extremely enraged son of Jamadagni245 were to be stationed before us now." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/65f50bb3be11fccba2acf427> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[468]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He will devour the three worlds, with all the gods, the asuras and men." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/660a83a849d60f60cf9b5103> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 102 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6078]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Having said this, the one who was rigid in his vows, went to the ocean, the lord of the rivers, with the gods and the rishis who were successful in their austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/662a4fdac18d1fc34946bcb7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6262]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ’ ‘S Chapter 1210(60) anjaya said, “O king! The Kurus702 were driven away by Karna, whose chariot possessed white horses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/663facf9f1847fbd43045c15> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7917]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But surpassing all this noise, there were the roars emitted by Bhima." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/664dcd66da17e90c754a22f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 70 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4661]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“A kshatriya must always know and place dandaniti at the forefront, so that he can obtain what he desires and protect what he possesses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/664fb7402b3006e9bbdac28d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3028]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Tvashtri,32 in the form of a mare, became the wife of Savita33 and this fortunate one gave birth to the two Ashvins in the sky." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/665a92db73625db3206f1b0d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6338]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They went to the supreme destination, one that is extremely difficult for even the gods to obtain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/665eba150eca72908e46dbf1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5304, 5305]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """This sacrificial ground is worshipped even by the gods.
O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Even if a little bit is given there, it becomes great.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6679cb8289c9eacff221251d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7151]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Krishna! O mighty-armed one! Anga238 and Duryodhana are wicked and act against my instructions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66910832d8193031a0c7469e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4759]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "142 A man who bathes there and worships the gods and the ancestors, obtains the fruits of one thousand tawny cows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6698ab45c00d019e5d75cdfc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 27 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1461]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But right up to the boundaries of the ocean, the earth pays homage to one who is instructed by a disciplined brahmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66a5bfa448c14401dad0c12a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13732]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ Section 86 will conclude in Volume 9." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66ad92fc80e86a585421df16> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11170]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘“O great king! Panchala186 quickly pierced Drona in the chest with five arrows and roared like a lion." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66bbae754335766494569331> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[221]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Pandava! O descendant of the Bharata lineage! All the divine waters and herbs, Shraddha,73 Medha,74 Sarasvati,75 artha, dharma, kama, lightning, clouds bearing rain, the winds, thunder, the eastern direction, the twenty-seven fires that convey sacrificial offerings, Agni, Soma, Indragni, Mitra, Savita, Aryama, Bhaga, the Vishvadevas, the Sadhyas, Shukra, Manthi, the sacrifices, the dakshinas, the planets, all the stobhas76 and all the mantras uttered at sacrifices are seated there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66bcad4f9524d13f353f56a2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14160]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "77 Ego, attachment and consciousness are generated." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66c4ab9e766bf1e11a427a35> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8101]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! On seeing that the javelin had been destroyed, your son413 surrounded Madhava with a large number of chariots." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66c8e221454b7fee03560170> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[228]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "20 You went to Girivraja21 and vanquished the kings, with Nagnajit at the forefront, and the Ambashthas, the Videhas and the Gandharas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66cb06e14bda8a4fe4543c27> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[192]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O Sanjaya! I had no hope of victory when I heard that the son of Drona74 and others committed a horrible and infamous act by killing the Panchalas75 and the sons of Droupadi while they slept." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66cde3c4a2db286711b8b359> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2659]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If one fasts and bathes in Chitrakuta, Janasthana1214 and in the waters of the Mandakini, one obtains royal prosperity." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66ce8394558c06d8496ce1fc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5329]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘When Bhishma was preparing for the wedding, the eldest daughter of the king of Kashi, one who was devoted to the truth, came and told him, “I have earlier chosen the king of Soubha231 as my husband." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66cf524452e04137f0038beb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1345]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Pandya swiftly countered it with a vayavya weapon195 and roared like a gale." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66d2f8f42dfc5263c8fd5607> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4213]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those two were like Shakra156 and Vishnu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66f67ea121bf9220714b3756> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4554]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The immensely fortunate grandfather32 always dwells there, happily worshipped by the gods and the demons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66fb7fa2dd5091f0757dde17> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[938]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He raised him up, like Tarkshya84 agitating the water of the ocean and raising up a snake from it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/66fcfebcd78cbfd7c6f7c57e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4617]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The force of the Panchalas is like that of swans that leave Manasa544 for the Ganga." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6706756ef8b89680b579adab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8554]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Eunuch! Idiot! Glutton! You have no skill in weapons, but wish to fight with me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/67195b6a0269c7b8bd661092> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16457]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is recommended that offerings meant for the gods and the ancestors are for people like these." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6724671084577a30da89e178> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9626]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This was recounted by Bhargava108 to King Muchukunda." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6740f3f24b0bcf8248f1230a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5934, 5937, 5938]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He addressed the supreme gods and said, ‘O gods! I will act today for your welfare.
As they had been instructed, the gods collected the bones of the dead one.
Delighted at the prospect of victory, the gods went to Tvashtar400 and spoke to him.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/67485a60c3a038f1aa13feb6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2172]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "We will then have a game of dice among well-wishers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/674a2c1273061d4988962a06> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[502]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! There were those without flesh, with mouths like wolves79 and mouths like hawks." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/674ec1c6bf2ccae431390a51> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1423]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Semen results from desire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/675b8588dd7516f9a9f6e40f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8961]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“O fortunate one! First, take a portion and offer it to the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/675bc7da9db2dd7929587fbf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7068]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 132 Vaishampayana said, ‘O descendant of the Bharata lineage! When the king43 addressed Pandu’s great-souled sons, the evil-hearted Duryodhana was extremely happy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/676d68259bf3632845e1eea5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6878]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 418(121) ‘Lomasha said, “O king! When Nriga sacrified there with soma and gratified Purandara, it has been heard that he543 was extremely intoxicated." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/676f427c374a04ab66d3a718> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8821]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They are like the terrible vajra in their impact and Rama4 himself confronted them once in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/679b68cb0beaa80100b59682> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3381, 3383, 3385, 3387, 3388]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! However, Bhimasena sliced it into two with his huge sword.
In that encounter with Bhimasena, Kalinga became even angrier.
O king! But before they could reach him, the mighty-armed Pandava used his supreme sword to swiftly cut them down in the sky.
Bhanuman enveloped Bhima with a shower of arrows and roared powerfully, making the sound echo in the sky.
But Bhima was not prepared to tolerate that lion-like roar in that great battle.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/679cdfc0eee89b5a7be54ef3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5248]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Under Daruka’s34 whip, Vasudeva’s horses seemed to kiss the road and devour the sky." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/67a6b47f162b015398460887> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[861]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As they fell down, those men were angrily killed, like Pashupati111 amidst animals." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/67ca145144d01c2cfac9b8ca> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1815]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The charioteers shouted, “Yoke." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/67e053b6f2e78dd0d6d4a13b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4865, 4866]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """“O God! You should act so that he stops dancing.
” In a desire to ensure the welfare of the gods, the god188 went to the one who was dancing, having lost his senses in delight, and told him, “O maharshi! O one who is learned in dharma! Why are you dancing? O bull among the sages! Why are you so delighted today?” The sage replied, “O God! Can you not see vegetable juices flowing from my hand? On seeing this, I am greatly delighted and am dancing.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/67efc7026cfc31366a2ede98> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13196]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing this, the great-souled Vishvaksena100 and Dhananjaya honoured Varshneya101 and applauded him, since the undecaying one had repulsed the divine weapons of all the warriors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6807ea7352d674ae7e71d960> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9104, 9105]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """You have ignored me and the gods.
You have destroyed the yakshas and the rakshasas, with the strength of your own arms.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/681cbc6ef2453d923ba1fd72> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9080]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "12 The Pandava13 narrated it in detail, from the beginning." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6827d4e9da6d5530405dc1ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4541]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There was the sound of Devadatta27 and the roar of Gandiva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/682d39940c26d5984460e879> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10114, 10116]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """“Gudakesha1 has not brought dishonour to our lineage through his actions.
2 Partha3 knows that the Satvatas4 never lust after riches.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/684d1aeec30773031946d4c3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1002]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The son of the one who vanquished Paka2 conquered all the regions protected by the lord of wealth—Bhimasena the east, Sahadeva the south and Nakula, skilled in the use of all weapons, conquered the west." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/686528f0bdffd5b5473d32c4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[211]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They knew the use of celestial weapons and were equal to Shakra80 in energy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/687daca718afa073c5ca7ead> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3044]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Indra among kings! At this, the lord474 used his manliness to sever Arjuna’s arms and brought the weeping calf back to Jamadagni’s hermitage, back from where it was wandering around in the inner quarters." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6882934c884086e9f8786106> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2883]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A brahmana who performs ceremonies385 for shudras confronts destruction." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/688ae978b7060e519cb36e5b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4514]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘You have earned merit from the austerities you have performed on the slopes of the Himalayas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/688db359af9add3fef32da2c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4508, 4509]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Having obtained fruits, the sages returned from the mountain.
The illustrious one179 was pleased with Arundhati and spoke to her.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/689513185f63b36784dd10e0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2860]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Steadfastness constitutes the banks." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/68a31448630621d799b06639> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13448]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But even in this state, the illustrious one320 did not kill Mahisha in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/68adde05b0368ec25b3d5e49> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19513]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son! I do not see any destiny in this, nor any action on the part of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/68af9b7f25c60affa91c5e4c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2671]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, he does not censure dharma190 and follows it, as if he is foolish." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/68bdc92cdedd8442fb29bc5c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11164]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The one who had never been dispirited250 again questioned the son of the river251 about supreme dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/68c5e8b0bb363ff4e73c5dfe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23891]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The beautiful city of Pragjyotishapura1184 will be full of many kinds of riches." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/68e59bfaf18557985738878f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6417]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He despatched fifteen iron arrows in the form of half-moons towards Bhurishrava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/68fa62b52b1ff2d9b8fa71e3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "16_Mausala" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[263]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Chapter 1985(7) V aishampayana said, ‘The brave and great-souled Anakadundubhi34 was lying down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/68fdbe98b94f3b9a01a8973b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[340]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Sharadvata Goutama76 is immensely strong and can fight in many wonderful ways." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/691cfdf47995fc757fd320c1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10159]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage!18 The pure-souled Bhishma vanquished the lords of the earth and went to Gajasahrya19 with the maidens." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/692e4786efeadf1fccce4a08> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[843]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the equal of the gods in valour." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6934403f1d9e8f7b75ece452> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5678]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But the gods went to oceans, rivers and lakes." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69455e21a676daa5c050e54c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 101 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8043]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is through such offerings that brahmanas, other guests, yakshas, rakshasas, serpents, gods and ancestors are sustained." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69500f8a381963cb96210e04> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8979]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The great-souled one asked Dhrishtadyumna, “Where has Krishna gone? Who has taken her away? Is it a Shudra or one of low birth? Has a Vaishya who pays taxes placed his feet on my head? Has a garland been thrown away on a cremation ground? O son! Or is it a foremost man from our own varna, or is it one from a higher varna?50 Or has a lower being51 placed his foot on my head and defiled Krishna? I will be happy in my sacrifices if she has been united with Partha, that bull among men." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/695f5fefd56a6c3a91151eaf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[75]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Kuru lineage! There is a supreme club in lake Bindu, kept there by King Youvanashva19 after he slew his enemies in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6968cfcee000716ac1d679c2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13437]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! The army of the gods was struck by that falling mountain, which was terrible in form." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/697671dd7dccf595093b7e8e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6603]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O grandfather! I wish to kill that outcast among rakshasas myself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69779d33cda73bfbe63211cf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8981]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Agitating kinnaras, great serpents, hermits, gandharvas and rakshasas, the immensely strong one ascended the mountain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69796cb06318b5ba35c3f822> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5015]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Govinda! I have no interest in pardoning him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6980e79e2d31850210252b61> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2504]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O unblemished one! He347 is like Rudra in a battle and you are like Brahma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6998891f896046cb0c110b36> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4387]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He paid homage to the gods and the ancestors, conquered his rage and controlled his senses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69a3bc8f46309a5622280c01> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5447]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! There were many inhabitants of the city too, desiring to see Hrishikesha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69b1ac8fe0fae74d7479f9c8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6940]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When Pandava Bhimasena saw him, he deduced that he27 was a charioteer’s son and jeeringly said, “O son of a charioteer! You don’t have the right to be killed by Partha in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69bb3582a6a909fcc00c2d2c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7210, 7212]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The gods or the ancestors do not receive anything from it.
The gods and the ancestors receive nothing, like ghee that has been poured into a fire that has been pacified.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69c8260219668e5afc06ad14> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 25 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1455]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’”’ Chapter 1860(25) he brahmana said, ‘In this connection, there is an ancient history about the ordinances for chaturhotra,106 explaining why the rites are like that." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69df64b2fb3293527f99d533> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9378]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king of Panchala23 is virtuous and does not crave for riches." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69e824b0e50c95eada68e443> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9114]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 188 Vaishampayana said, ‘As soon as they saw him, all the Pandavas and the greatly illustrious son of Panchala18 stood up." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69ea85aa5cf2ad8f427146e0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5646]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Resort to the vows of the gods and you will obtain the fruits that have been recounted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69eda09a9287f6f0bbd9021e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3087]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If he wields the bow, the gods and the asuras are incapable of vanquishing him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/69ef8754c67b1abc2feb04d0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16708]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king will never deviate from his own dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6a0a23e8a0a4c3a4c674c5f5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11295]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kashyapa264 properly lit a blazing fire and cooked some extremely large fish, offering them to Goutama, the guest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6a2a9f0ff06488790c0a65b1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1324]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘I have made arrangements for the masses of samshaptakas to be engaged with Partha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6a3a78bb1210211ed58367a9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1565]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Gentleness can vanquish gentleness and gentleness can also vanquish harshness." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6a3c21827fe0cab222fc73ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1176]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "For the sake of the ambrosia, the asuras and the danavas17 grasped one end of the king of the snakes and the great gods grasped the tail." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6a5385372898d4b039d45ebd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3539]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is said that Narayana is Krishna and Phalguna54 is Nara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6a5fbf7dbcf543c0f9468fb6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5024]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I have lived with you so far to accomplish the wishes of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6a7c29c79729af16b293abf9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[482, 483]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O lord of the gods! I see him terribly exhausted and close to death.
O lord of the gods! I am overcome with compassion for him and my mind is agitated.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6a8961a09724f28fb3d33319> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1859]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king of Kamboja sends him black, dark and red skins of the kadali26 deer, expensive blankets, chariots, women and cattle and horses in hundreds and thousands." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6a907dea7dc637eca15c7393> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[515]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of men! Thus the maharathas79 looked after each other, living in disguise, but looking after Krishna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6aa92c5194d0223bcf3d73c0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[31]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They had oppressed Krishna5 at the time of gambling with the dice and had brought her to the assembly hall." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6aaabc7c29839e3adf95142a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23923]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! He knows that the supreme among gods1191 is superior to him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6ab0b8fb343647b08237f7fe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[350]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! Even the gods have faced unhappiness." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6ab4786f65e9abc2894bb001> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11104]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Linga will be in vain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6ac6b7c80c4d3c8244618701> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1715, 1717]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘Pandava45 then instructed his brothers to perform the funeral rites for the brave lord of the earth who had been Damaghosha’s son.
Then Partha,46 with all the other lords of the earth, instated his47 son in the kingdom of Chedi.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6ace1c2d663de9a3fdaa4265> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[484]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Oppressed by grief, he embraced Pandava15 reluctantly." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6ad0bc8f6f45d4102ee26335> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24063]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O gods! This is the certain fruit that you will obtain through my favours." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6ade56535bfef92aec6336ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[873]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king of the gods! O lord of the universe! You are worshipped by all beings." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6ae49237da9f0dfb1e45a70f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2594]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He49 was thus praised for his fighting and his fame by the ancestors, the gods, the charanas,50 the siddhas51 and the masses of yakshas and also by the large number of beings who were on earth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6af1edb6fe7c38d4eb8ea87b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6279]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Fool that I was, I did not know that by summoning two gods at one time, the fruits could also be doubled." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6afa75a56e747da2eba8945d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1698, 1703]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘“O king! But after that, your intelligence was confounded and you were vanquished in an unequal game of dice.
193 Even before the seed is released, the lord Ishana194 determines in advance happiness and unhappiness and pleasure and displeasure for all beings.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6afd2a0dc0ef112b8341a547> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7379]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Uddalaka got to know that he had been defeated by a suta591 and had drowned in the waters." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6b04a6704a31d96ae91b6da7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3057]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“When Duryodhana was born, the immensely intelligent Kshatta9 told us that it would be better to send this destroyer of the lineage to the other world." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6b1b7b034e446924a5c1e887> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2743]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ CHAPTER 1017(40) ‘Sanjaya said, “He72 repeatedly stretched the bow that he held in his hand and roared." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6b277a4914ee45c8ce1f70bf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4880]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They had skilled sons—Yudhishthira had Prativindhya, Vrikodara195 had Sutasoma, Arjuna had Shrutakirti, Nakula had Shatanika and Sahadeva had Shrutakarmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6b2d7c052ab8d75766aaa1c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2187]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Kounteya! A brahmachari who is asleep when the sun rises, one who goes to sleep before the sun sets, one with malformed nails, one with discoloured teeth, one whose younger brother gets married first, one who marries before his elder brother, one who maligns the brahman, one who is guilty of slander, one who is the husband of a didhishu, one whose first wife is a didhishu,271 one who has violated his vow of chastity, one who kills a brahmana, one who teaches the brahman to an undeserving person, one who does not teach the brahman to a deserving person, one who performs a sacrifice for ordinary people, one who sells the king,272 one who slays a shudra or a woman, one whose ancestors were contemptible, one who slays an animal without a good reason,273 one who sets fire to a forest, one who subsists through deceit, one who goes against his preceptor, one who abandons the sacred fire, one who sells the brahman274 and one who violates an agreement—all of these are sinners." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6b2e169bc43d6d3c5c6e9439> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3221]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When I am born in the wombs of yakshas and rakshasas, I then follow their kinds of conduct." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6b3708339d716e4d8a6caef2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4631]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the illustrious god who is the lord of all the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6b3b786d722e04fcac1352bc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4118]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Giving them oblations meant for the gods and the ancestors is tantamount to not giving these at all." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6b3c407ff92f72f452edeeb7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 153 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7876]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 153: 12 shlokas Chapter 154: 25 shlokas Chapter 155: 52 shlokas Chapter 156: 11 shlokas Chapter 157: 16 shlokas Chapter 158: 55 shlokas Chapter 159: 22 shlokas Chapter 160: 41 shlokas Chapter 161: 20 shlokas Chapter 162: 18 shlokas Chapter 163: 23 shlokas Chapter 164: 14 shlokas Chapter 165: 44 shlokas Chapter 166: 45 shlokas Chapter 167: 21 shlokas Chapter 168: 25 shlokas Chapter 169: 25 shlokas Chapter 170: 21 shlokas Chapter 171: 26 shlokas Chapter 172: 17 shlokas Chapter 173: 24 shlokas The parva is named after Chitraratha, a gandharva, whose stories figure in this section." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6b423e9be20d7c7cd67590c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1212]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Having been thus addressed, he95 replied in the proper way." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6b8b27891c3b00406dc9615a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3402]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Truthfulness, generosity, austerities, purity, peace, mental vigour and honour—all of these are in him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6bc37d4a5307c6e73fe0cd1e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15500, 15502]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The wind, the friend of the fire, began to blow in the abodes of the gods.
The thirty gods stationed themselves in that auspicious spot, desiring to worship her.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c0ab50770b85f253afeed76> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3976]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O scorcher of enemies! The band of samshaptaka kshatriyas110 have resolved, ‘Arjuna will kill us, or we will kill Dhananjaya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c0d79fa0b4ac6387c1c0d67> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1013]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Pragjyotisha was surrounded by kiratas, chinas9 and many other warriors who lived along the shores of the ocean." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c128c3923babc2cb0d4b593> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6686]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They sought refuge with the lord and god, the undecaying Brahma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c1b85bdfd02932bc509fc1d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8476]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’” ‘The gandharva said, “O descendant of the Bharata lineage! As he103 advanced towards them, the illustrious and energetic rishi Vashishtha stopped him with a roar." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c253dc5dd29950514b230e5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9019]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then the wise rakshasa grasped an extremely terrible javelin with a golden shaft and struck him with it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c3b5c49b5c407b1b4440974> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24016]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The entire universe was generated from the eight Prakritis." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c3edb625fb22ef81af93ef3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12586]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O king! He wrathfully spoke these words to Duryodhana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c41adca02673b34b400c5fe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23844]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "To accomplish the tasks of the gods, I will always manifest myself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c45557a9b9924ab8c04f1cd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6733]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The magnanimous one bathed there and offered oblations to the ancestors and the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c486cb5bb42f98fa72fff74> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5299]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! The gods and chakracharas worship him with sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c4dce6731eab1c18b71f30c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4462]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You should forget the king of the Kurus316 and the evil Jayadratha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c5842bb3d58f504614a44a9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10591]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "These virtuous and auspicious ones are Chakracharas404 and they roam around in Soma’s world." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c5f61ea254cc5afe972ceb9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[776]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They rushed to the end where Chaitya25 was, beloved by inhabitants of Magadha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c63f0f19f039714cf73b534> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10070]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Vasudeva said, “O bull among men! A svayamvara8 is the form of marriage for kshatriyas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c6d04ecaefc860275f27e8c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2595]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Karna, foremost among rathas, worshipped the chariot in accordance with the prescribed rites." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c73b191fe996c54a2efe202> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16134]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He enveloped the rakshasas with a large shower of arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c7a359180bc752a2859b7d1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6157]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "She is famous by the name of Jyotsnakali and she is second only to Shri91 in her beauty." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c7d7af9d3e6f0a923c6bf40> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2693]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The sage Krishna Dvaipayana arose regularly37 for three years and composed this wonderful history known as the Mahabharata." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6c8bbe91a3c3a1cfc5a04bfb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13970]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O sons!48 Ride them and fight the gandharvas in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6ca960dba152c7e13a5dc62d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6021]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ 398(101) ‘“The gods said, ‘All the four types of beings411 prosper because of these favours." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6cafc47af84c02435256c224> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6621, 6630]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """917 Dissension should first be used and silence918 and force thereafter.
O supreme among the gods! O lord of the immortals! There is no task that is as supremely difficult as ensuring prosperity for those who have varied means of subsistence.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6cb7ae130c200d3ac36cdfcb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7274]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those two supreme among men, Pandava and the slayer of Keshi814 were as resplendent as the fire and the sun in that field of battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6cc6291f516057b3679e3644> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10913]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the beings in the universe resulted from them—the gods, the large numbers of ancestors, the gandharvas, the apsaras, the many kinds of rakshasas, the birds, the animals, the fish, the apes, the giant serpents and many others that had different forms and strengths, travelling in the water or on the land." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6ccfa8a4abe31c08eeea6979> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[691]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Mama’ is death and ‘na mama’ is eternal." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6d1a4652722b623e60f82459> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5216]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "She is devoted in worship to gods and guests and servitude towards her elders." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6d27209969be636c62ea2f7f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[158]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Once you have determined the good, the indifferent and the bad, do you appoint them to the right posts? O lord of the earth! Do you appoint those who are avaricious, prone to thievery, quarrelsome and are under age? Do you oppress the kingdom with the strength of avaricious thieves, minors and women? Are the farmers content? Are the tanks in the kingdom large and full and placed at right distances, so that the harvest is not destroyed because of lack of rainfall? If food and seeds are scarce, do you grant farmers charitable loans at the rate of one pratika for one hundred?50 O son! Are the professions51 undertaken by those who are honest? O son! The happiness of the world depends on these professions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6d380e9afe736f6ab6f24c1c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10707]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They find delight with the nagas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6d5769db5d5b1cc217beddc9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14331]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The wielder of the vajra88 knows this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6d57f847d0d07392a9962916> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6168]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Seeing that Mahadeva was angry, Prajapati96 addressed him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6d6b5f060b75e830a22f79da> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9697]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is full of jewels everywhere and is incapable of being conquered even by the gods, the yakshas, the masses of gandharvas, the serpents, the asuras and the rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6d70b32510cc9b010a0719c3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[344]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O immensely radiant one! You have suffered hardships because of Jatasura61 and Kichaka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6d80b50efb8cd8d5f2e30952> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8319]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Worlds are ordained for such people." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6d841304691e2403604c7fce> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 12 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[606]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord! The universe, with all its asuras, gandharvas, kinnaras and giant serpents, is terrified at your wrath." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6d8cd141f3e668980781a73d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2971]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Varshneya! O one with Tarkshya459 on your standard! Sever my doubt." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6da16d402604ab39a4102239> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[755]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Beyond this is seen the world named Sama." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6dade1233b15de3702884b8d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3002]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "She should choose one of these gods for her husband." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6dc715a52461d7c850432799> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2839]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Among all those of Vasudeva’s lineage, Lakshmi380 is vested in Krishna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6dcca11b3d99e5fae2a9479d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 278 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19427]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O grandfather of the Kuru lineage! I wish to hear the truth about this from you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6ddd974cde5dd48a5fc08d37> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14574]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is freed from the many firm bonds, whether these arise from offspring or from the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6dde0b33a1f3afdac218152c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3115]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Today, the gods have come to us along their smooth celestial routes." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6ded137503d42ff200476127> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14095, 14115]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """67 Honey, oil, milk, butter, meat, salt, molasses, grain, fruits and roots are modifications of earth, mixed with water.
Desire, anger, distraction, avarice, confusion, fear, exhaustion, despondency, sorrow, excessive pride, insolence, lack of nobility —without any distress, the severity or lack of severity of these faults must be examined.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6df2fb88e8eaec23cb2658c1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2395]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘ “‘The gods said, “Let all forms be gathered from everywhere in the three worlds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6e05cb6b8767b149a045f4b7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11569]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "218 They became fire and the ocean219 and Garuda and Takshaka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6e244cea4f2322ee61ac5f22> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2042]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Vasava87 always showers down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6e2548c1075c08ca3c950392> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2426, 2427]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Savitri162 is the first among all kinds of knowledge and Prajapati among all gods.
Omkara163 is the first among all the Vedas and prana among all kinds of speech.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6e40e60019f9a1dfcd5b2abf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[399]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "From those energetic flames, hundreds and thousands of Hrishikeshas46 emerged, holding conch shells, chakras and clubs." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6e466cfdb50c953948734c0c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19011]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’” ‘Bhishma said, “Having been thus addressed by the grandfather, the illustrious lord who was the devourer of oblations662 accepted this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6e545d60a17b86fddc113a77> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1119]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘After that, the valorous Kounteya defeated the Suhmas and the eastern Suhmas in battle35 and marched on towards Magadha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6e5a38225ee502a4129a702c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5350]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of men! At that time, blue jays, shatapatras623 and curlews circumambulated the descendant of the Pandu lineage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6e6defaa5f65aa0164c40921> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10104]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Pierce." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6e6e6917b92c86959f214f57> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10107]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! On hearing the story of Amba, the daughter of the king of Kashi, her mother’s father10 trembled and arose." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6e74fd21665999623bc0e41e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7104]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They penetrated his armour and the supreme among rakshasas looked resplendent." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6eb60b1460ba17e72116b7c3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5276]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "302 On performing one’s ablutions there and worshipping the ancestors and the gods, one obtains a horse sacrifice and goes to the supreme objective." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6edd74b7b89b2316ea2542c3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13342]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Surrounded by the masses of pishachas and the masses of gods, he was radiant on that golden mountain, blazing with prosperity." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6eddd59eb0224e23c1af3dfb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1541]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In that encounter, he220 picked up another bow that was even more powerful and enveloped Nakula and all the directions with his arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6eef5fc84c611767c65865b0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[883]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That is the reason sages remain silent and perform diksha72 without speaking." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f014424376720f3da8346a2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11025]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But at that time,103 three-quarters of adharma will be established in the world." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f0b92c91378f29145150f26> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10252, 10253]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """In the prescribed fashion, Madhu’s slayer16 showed honours to Partha,17 Krishna18 and the priest.
‘When Yudhishthira was seated with them, he praised the king19 and spoke these words.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f0d25de446cf1aa2a46378c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2504]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But smilingly, he48 severed Soubala’s sword into two fragments in the encounter." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f1400bd30f4a797ff95a74e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8302]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I was born in Kesari’s field686 from Vayu, who gives life to the universe." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f2635a7d58ba69d51ecd712> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8303]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Worlds are ordained for such people." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f28dc2dfe2348e4a6e96483> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Which among these seems to you to be an attractive place to live in? O Indra among kings! Where will we dwell for a year?” Yudhishthira said, “O mighty-armed one! It will indeed be as the illustrious lord of all beings5 has said." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f3198c19adce11357e63d7b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9268]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Then the priest58 who knew the Vedas built and lit the sacrificial fire and poured offerings, with mantras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f330f7ff23f8759682dff70> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2316]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When the fourth moon arrived and the moon was full, the mighty-armed son266 of Pandu survived only on air." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f4e07a389931c3daad6484c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8952]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Prosper, the way a fire hidden in a cave gradually expands and spreads." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f6576f71050fb7b2470d43a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17015]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” O foremost among learned ones! What was that great fear concerning Karna? Why did the great-souled one2 not talk about it to anyone?’ Vaishampayana said, ‘O tiger among kings! Since you have asked, I will tell you about it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f6afc658a30354cfb93c097> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6357]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Using my intelligence, I have reflected on both—protecting myself in this battle and going towards Arjuna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f6ddaa4fc109bcbae6fb1ad> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8918]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“Adhokshaja17 was unsuccessful and has returned to the Parthas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f8bde63f3b6678b08e928fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7734]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“The one with the thousand eyes, the king of the gods, was delighted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6f8c77bbbfb4c2b8819d48ac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[433]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Karna was the equal of Rama89 and has been killed in this battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6fb6f831e6eae288b7f7258a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7793]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ 795(132) ‘“Vidula said, ‘If you wish to give up your manliness in your present state, you will soon follow the path travelled by the inferior." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/6fc2e8a6f6c53f8147c0467b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3873]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Together with Bhishma and Bhurishrava and an army, the lord of the Kouravas150 advanced against him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7007953aa8076b64a46aa2c2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9384]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "These lords of the earth have assembled because of the son of Dhritarashtra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7010949f879db0a50ad2cfbd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11305]" ;
        mbh:sourceText ") Viraha;1129 (671) Vishama;1130 (672) Shunya;1131 (673) Dhrita- sharira;1132 (674) Achala;1133 (675) Chala;1134 (676) Amani;1135 (677) Manada;1136 (678) Manya;1137 (679) Loka-svami;1138 (680) Triloka-dhrik;1139 (681) Sumedha;1140 (682) Medhaja;1141 (683) Dhanya;1142 (684) Satyamedha;1143 (685) Dhara-dhara;1144 (." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7010f2222be1a2f824137549> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3922]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "No one transgresses what has been established by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7016800fa096ffddfc586b50> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17566, 17567]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """An oblation obtained through good means is what satisfies the gods, such as bowing down, oblations, studying and herbs.
The worship of gods should be in accordance with what is laid down in the sacred texts.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7029a801870c39c7e59e4167> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23309]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When Ushanas1113 and Brihaspati are born in the future, they will also base their instructions on this sacred text." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/703c5cb31048646a20648bd3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12749]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rathas fought with horse riders, horse riders with elephant riders, infantry with elephants, horses clashed with horses and foot soldiers with foot soldiers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7043964cc6c775922e701f26> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6335]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Cows dwell in a region that is superior to that of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/704ea385c3c001a0ff1b8516> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5349]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Durmukha pierced Shrutakarma253 with seven swift arrows, sliced down his standard with one and pierced his charioteer with seven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7056b06f25f96b0b0dc2a671> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10756]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Drona’s son attacked the king of Panchala146 and Bharadvaja’s son attacked the Srinjayas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/706114632f248465912f200b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[106]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As Partha32 and the others entered, there was a shower of fragrant flowers and the sound of conch shells and kettledrums." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/706b8f3394d7c57f5e5d6e27> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 80 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4555]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O immensely fortunate one! It was in Pushkara that the gods, with the rishis at the forefront, attained salvation and great merits." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/708179aaa2c464e3811448f6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1468]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Though he had been pacified, prosperity110 did not desert the lord of Madra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7094b8b07117989152bfbf53> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2643]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Jishnu173 circled." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/70a6e9fcea1b763231c97a4a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2405]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I cannot see the directions and I am oppressed because of the curse159 of a Brahmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/70b40e92c34719ac9bcb13b2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4174]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Bhishma replied, “The son is said to be both shukraja1326 and kshetraja." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/70cf3243ab8e43e61e08807c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3023]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lord of Kosala103 pierced him in the chest with a barbed arrow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/70df17fde4c1d559abd739aa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2340]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Yudhishthira said, “I have as many143 chariots." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/70e2c79498d922b8e40489a7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2202]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Prana, apana, udana, samana and vyana are also like that." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/70f18e4fb586c8cb415bf8b7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3324]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘After this, the undecaying and powerful one51 went to Chamasodbheda." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/70feff5ca5ac94d69e814734> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15187]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In bewilderment, the king45 honoured all the sages who were there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7144c79583d98dafcd67ea50> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4710]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "120 On going to the supreme tirtha of nagas known as Sarpadevi,121 one obtains agnishtoma122 and attains the world of nagas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/714e218301c10ca6807dd3e4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 326 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23833]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O sage! Tasks undertaken for ancestors are held to be superior to tasks undertaken for gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/716001619918650894da7a3a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6828]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He thought of Haryashva Ikshvaku of Ayodhya, supreme among kings, immensely valorous and with the four constituent parts202 in his army." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7173c30fe336bcd05419f649> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12874]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! He65 was senseless with anger and shot eight arrows at Karna, striking his standard, his bow and his quiver." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7187b0bb192daba54502243b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4994]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "One obtains agnishtoma and goes to the world of the sages." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7192b4ea780f996f7bfadfbd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9962]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He142 said that renunciation and sannyasa is sacred and supreme dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/71bf3120fc8714a11ddb6cc3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11351]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! It was like the river Vaitarani201 that flows towards the capital of Yama’s kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/71c2816addb56b5ddc689c62> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11932]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“On seeing that this extremely terrible encounter was going on in the great battle, the best of men249 spoke these words to Dhananjaya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/71c7a048180e4a2d83463e23> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9320]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! From the time of birth in this world, a being has to enjoy the effects of his353 own earlier deeds and the fruits of the dharma he has resorted to." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/71de5422c817a815f20ac659> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3833]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The immensely asectic one then gave this text, known as Vaishalaksha582 to Indra, who was extremely devoted to Brahma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/71ef0b19b5ce9e6f10d55666> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2506]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They are like gods roaming around on earth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/71f4a9e90042beee8227d799> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10301]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘O descendant of the Bharata lineage! While Varshneya33 and Dharmaraja were conversing in this way, the great ascetic Markandeya, with dharma in his soul, was seen to arrive." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/71fcc72bf57cb2f1bebd241a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7851]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "312 Boast about your prosperity, as you used to do earlier." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/72015dc829d4a2145602f935> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22998]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having gone there, there is no decay, unlike the moon and the large number of gods, who tremble and fall ‘B down on the ground, ascending again when they have acquired merit." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7214a239d42aa2601df48769> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10212, 10213]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Bibhatsu24 saw in his son Maghavan25 himself.
‘The auspicious Panchali26 also obtained five sons through her five husbands.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/722134499868681fd5d6e4c4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1401]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There were one hundred lotuses and sougandhikas14 embossed on Suryadatta’s armour, plated with gold and as bright as the sun." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/722310dedc6a6ad14f5bd8e8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2517]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When discharged by me, Varuna’s noose315 cannot be resisted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7224750ee1716dd803c76080> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1063, 1064]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The women from Sindhu, Souvira, Gandhara, Kamboja and yavanas83 have surrounded the mighty-armed one and are trying to save him.
O Janardana! Jayadratha should have been killed by the Pandus when he seized Krishna84 and ran away, together with the Kekayas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/72386dba551c454038d1ab80> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24267]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is said that enlightened ones may serve Brahma, Shitikantha1218 or any of the other gods, but they obtain me, who is beyond them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/723dc7dfe2d33a1aced877ed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11635, 11636, 11637, 11638]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He and the other great asuras who were in the bowels of the earth were saved and were not burnt down.
The gods again got the worlds back, tranquil and without any dust.
The gods said, “Slay the asuras who are hidden inside the earth.
” O king! Addressed by the gods, he replied, “I am capable of using my austerities to burn down those who are inside the earth.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7240cab0cd53ec392b88dc55> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12120]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "55 Water was created from space." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/725f779e73f021c227358962> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[295]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Chapter 1995(5) anamejaya asked, ‘The great-souled Bhishma and Drona, King Dhritarashtra, Virata, Drupada, Shankha, Uttara, Dhrishtaketu, Jayatsena, King Satyajit, Duryodhana’s sons, Shakuni Soubala, Karna’s brave sons, King Jayadratha, Ghatotkacha and the others whom you have not mentioned, other kings who were blazing in their forms and whom you have named—how long did they dwell in heaven? Tell me about that." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/726df36592af8d1fc18f6b01> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9899, 9900]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Anjanaparva, Bhimasena’s grandson, brought down a shower of arrows and he74 looked like Mount Meru, with rain from a cloud pouring down on it.
Ashvatthama was like Rudra, Upendra75 and Indra in his valour and he was not frightened.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/726e279d70e5f44a1ad0ac1b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4975]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The valiant Bhima also picked up one7 that possessed the essence of stone and challenged the king, like a lion against another lion in the forest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7271e482f4c940b71e8e4932> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1891]" ;
        mbh:sourceText ") Urdhva-reta;725 (521) Jaleshaya;726 (522) Ugra;727 (523) Vamshakara;728 (524) Vamsha;729 (525) Vamsha-nada;730 (." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/72921d80934f90449e523560> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6162]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Having been thus addressed by her husband, she invoked Vayu299 for a son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/729a0d7637fc747ba07972d3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8411]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A strong person obtains Shri, an army and advisers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/72a77cf22d3e189d1e940f9c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9525]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Thereupon, on Dhritarashtra’s command, Vidura went to Yajnasena53 and the Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/72b5d2858e46d6c6e6993783> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2072]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Headless torsos could be seen, grasping the hair23 and raising sharp swords smeared with blood." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/72d41048b2fc4a5733a2543c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4523]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O god! O lord of the gods! If a person purifies himself181 and fasts here for three days, let him obtain the fruits that are obtained from fasting for twelve years." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/72d957d8b0388c42ec7a78f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3344]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Together with Ketuman, the angry Shrutayu113 arranged his troops in battle formation and advanced before Bhima and Chedi in that battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/72e6be480af205d393b19492> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11773]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It was as large as Indra’s weapon233 and he drew it back powerfully." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/72f0eee362ad1d907bdadff1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22139]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kin and well-wishers hurl a man into the fire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/72fa3058d257a8afe90dbca9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5534]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In this way, there were many other great sages who performed similar sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7312e743088175c466c155c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[58]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Where are all those maharathas, like tigers in their valour? Have those supreme men conquered other worlds? O gods! If all those maharathas have obtained this world, know that only in that case will I reside here, with those great-souled ones." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/732746a979bd6a1298877a6d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4928]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "202 Having performed ablutions there and engaged in the worship of the ancestors and the gods, one is cleansed of all sins and one’s soul becomes pure." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/733c46db5262b7a4000ab0f4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2689]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! The son of Vichitravirya’s son362 has always been kind towards me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/73436f6790eb54f8354e1384> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7914]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Taking him and his advisers prisoners, they showed them to Drona." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/73553e0a7ef62bf582a3ee93> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3091]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lords of the worlds and the great god91 should display their own forms, so that I may know King Punyashloka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/735b1961e8c8663df0455ff7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25407]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The intelligent one, the lord of the gods and supreme among intelligent ones, began to think." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7375b8a928ed8dbe63a954a0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8789]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The celestial routes were crowded with the heavenly chariots of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/73765c91a8f7ac9fc23e227b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11063]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They are successful and know about dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/737c8f416f3f13835bce483f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1080]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having pierced Yudhishthira with straight-tufted arrows, he94 brought Yugandhara down from the chariot with a broad- headed arrow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/73a157e497103062265b4f8f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3338]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Matysa Virata’s eldest son18 is terrible in form and is foremost among warriors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/73a7d8aded64845e9c206a18> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1033]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Alas! Shame! When Sushena’s mother78 has seen the mighty-armed Karna, with gold-decorated armour plates and who was never dispirited, she has fallen down, senseless." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/73b87ca86d62171ea322f630> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4302]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Speech fails him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/73f3a46cd42f51033583a426> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10020]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When Madhusudana79 heard that the invincible Bibhatsu80 had reached the region of Prabhasa after visiting all the tirthas, Madhava81 went to meet him, unknown to Kounteya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/74038ad9fcfcfbc5fffa5938> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4761]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "144 Having worshipped the gods and the ancestors and having fasted, one attains agnishtoma145 and goes to the world of Surya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/74083e0d1f9de8ca5c0cd3eb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6191]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Havya, kavya, offerings of water, rites of pacification, gifts of vehicles and garments, the nurturing of the aged and the young—all of these qualities are obtained through donations of cows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/742609199a2db8c739625bdc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3694]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“The mighty-armed son of the chastiser of Paka16 spoke to Krishna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/743237811ab16f82f15bb9cb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6974]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Drona’s horses are running away." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/743a01623dbad26e36d29412> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7312]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "139 Vaishampayana said, ‘Not very far from where they1 slept in the forest, a rakshasa named Hidimba lived on a shala2 tree." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/743fb53ac2d81e7bd2d6a461> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[195]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O brahmana! What are those sabhas made of? How long are they and how wide? Who waits upon the grandfather66 in his sabha? Who on Vasava, king of the gods, and who on Vaivasvata Yama? 67 Who wait on Varuna and Kubera in their sabhas? O devarshi! Tell us." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/744ee474cec219c40950b0a9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2132]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Triumph over enemies and enjoy the undisputed kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/746011da5162c2154e468461> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9646]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Therefore, the rites do not suffer if these are not offered to the ancestors and the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7469499b40d6afc1eda45c09> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2831]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "198 ‘When they had lost consciousness, Partha remembered Uttara’s199 words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7469630eb8fd3b636182c86c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8875]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Amazed at his deeds, the gods honoured him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/748bdeccfc9dbd342c4421c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12939]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ 511(214) ‘Markandeya said, “Shiva246 was the wife of Angiras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/74941db4e50ca63202dab068> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10492]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Among all the mortals on earth, they are regarded as gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7499139baaa5770ec6f4f403> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14338]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The traits of the dharma of renunciation102 are that this leads to the eternal brahman, who is not manifest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/749caeedae2a9073af63bc93> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5226]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Today, Radha615 will lose her son, or Kunti will lose me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/74add79525a9d12acfa0d2ae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16022, 16023]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """With Lakshmana leading the way, Vibhishana and the lord of the bears129 demolished the impregnable southern gate of the city.
He130 then invaded Lanka with a hundred thousand crore of monkeys.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/74c31398ef4152366e54eb99> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[113, 117, 118]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘After a few years, in an assembly of kings where the maiden Krishna33 was to choose her own bridegroom, Arjuna performed a difficult task and won her hand.
Thus, the king34 could now perform the rajasuya35 sacrifice.
Through the wise counsel of Krishna and the prowess of Bhima and Arjuna, Yudhishthira killed Jarasandha and the swollen-head king of Chedi36 and thus obtained the right to perform the rajasuya, rich in provisions and sacrificial offerings and full of merit.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/74c5df0c2c147d504094612a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7161]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The evil one is based here on Suyodhana’s63 orders." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/74db0e2a7bd06e68242ae73c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having been respectfully welcomed by those sages, he folded his palms before all those sages and asked them how their ascetic pursuits were progressing." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/74def3ceb378a758e78d648a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6292]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! There is no one in the three worlds who can withstand it, other than Nilakantha442 Maheshvara, foremost among the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/74df406ad14c9ccb1519a4b4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11677]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was surrounded by a large army of rakshasas, fierce in visage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/74e0e272d6c18165ff61d3ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[118]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Since that skilled one has been brought down in the battle, why should I have any fear about the battle? I will roam around on the field of battle and use my straight-tufted arrows to convey the bulls among the Kurus14 to Yama’s abode." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/74ea2ae8d9fe55e1ae2febfe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2425]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Dhritarashtra said, “The king53 shines like a thin and high flame." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/74fddb2491c544a7ce1383b3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15886]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I am a monkey and not a rakshasa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/750a0c11bd25cb810d08518a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16081, 16082]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The rakshasa struck the monkey with clubs and maces.
The monkey struck the rakshasa with trees, complete with trunks and branches.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/75241f6bda0304dc63ef1082> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[348]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Disregarding the cries of the lords of the earth, Yuyudhana44 brought him down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/753862b0949b287ee6da1599> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[932]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Where is he? Where is he? The lord of Soubha wished to fight me in battle and rushed around, from one place to another." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7544b38755200d11fdc3d4ba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1056]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He163 next released a multitude of arrows towards Ashvatthama, who was like a guest whohad arrived in a house." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7563bba8e3129b630192b7df> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11705]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The son of the suta possessed the valour of Indra and Upendra228 and was not frightened." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7569e1825053c45b6006dbd8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3752]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "We will certainly gratify the lord who is the god of the gods and his followers, in words, thoughts and deeds, seek their favours and bring the riches here." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/756a8535094229db05e49b4d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5774]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With Kunti and Madri, Pandu lived in the forest, like Purandara’s handsome elephant277 between two cow elephants." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/757121d0c81c4acec9c13005> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2101]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! It became divided into two, like the Ganga when it confronts a mountain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/757192ef3f574c0d41a671f7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[726]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king was delighted at what the king53 and Jishnu had done." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/757414d97fe1d5c85c178f18> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8449]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Panchala432 and the Somakas advanced against him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/757e646c2b1d93b7ff3fb13d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 213 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12836]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The danavas, terrible in form, were always able to vanquish the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/758125ac4bd8f05a53e20059> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14768]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was surrounded by great prosperity and was ascended on Airavata’s172 shoulder." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7583760eb3b9272aa2b598fc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 43 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2871]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The assembled devarshis, siddhas and charanas witnessed that terrible battle, equal to that between the gods and the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/75ba767c99eaf5edef52c768> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5974]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ The supreme among those who meditated, the ascetic Vamadeva, replied to him, as he841 was seated there, golden in complexion, like Yayati, the son of Nahusha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/75c06eeffb7ec63ec37222c0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1072]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having seen him lose his senses, his trained charioteer Daruki95 used his swift horses to take him away from the field of battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/75d4f9d65e22c9d5c30b5d5d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4879]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is through your grace that the gods are free from fear and can rejoice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7602e38b4858904af0b8dbce> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[743]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Kuru lineage! In all these dvipas, people and brahmanas observe brahmacharya22 and self-control and are truthful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/760d857412aaa58a009ce876> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3745]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Father killed the son and the son killed the father." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7612025d417724720f509b81> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10624]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the gods! They reside in vanaprastha and depend only on their own selves for maintenance." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7613fdc916dc3db51455fb65> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2141]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Even when he29 saw that an entire akshouhini was brought down by Bhimasena, either because of his delusion or because of his avarice, there still was no peace." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76164f4c48a7e7a6d2d34f43> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3545]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Surrounded by all these residences, the mountain looked like the world of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7625496f7158c7bacdce3310> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7682]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is said to be Brahma’s daughters —Lakshmi, Niti1033 and Sarasvati." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/762a9290041944032476be69> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1462]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Like an elephant without restraint172 in battle, a kshatriya’s strength declines, if it is not accompanied by brahmanas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76303714235f6021bc0de663> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[715]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But no man can go there without the sanction of the gods and the preceptors, without honouring virtuous well- wishers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7630bec1f5db22baa035ebce> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11851, 11856]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘“On getting to know that a brahmana had arrived, he153 suddenly arose and went to where the brahmana was standing alone.
I know everything about the devoted wife telling you to go to Mithila.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7635db64266acf25970bafb4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8858]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Thus addressed by Partha, he400 touched the ground with his head." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7640273ab41d969e8c8fe206> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22158]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Even if a person has been born in a hermitage and dies there, despite not having experienced desire and objects of pleasure, he obtains only a little bit of dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/764b50bb404517f113c9a7bc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10593, 10596]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """405 There are others who drink soma, like the gods.
They offer oblations into the fire and worship the ancestors and the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/764d7984a533b327207a85e4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24042]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O gods! Desiring to worship me, you have tormented yourselves through excellent austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76554a396488f8df2de6a229> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13451]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He roared, delighting the daityas and terrifying the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/765c94240be44bc7e86bc6c7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3749]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods approached the illustrious grandfather of the worlds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/765f7a1b533e87e6bae0f866> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2046, 2047]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O lord of the earth! Yajnaseni81 does not eat until she has seen to it that everyone has eaten and is full, even hunchbacks and dwarfs.
O descendant of the Bharata lineage! There are only two who have not paid tribute to Kunti’s son— the Panchalas because of the marriage alliance82 and the Andhakas and the Vrishnis because of friendship.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76777ff9296dc95508303150> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11760]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Shri1398 roams happily amidst them and they also sustain Shri." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/767fd9ed9a2b34a090c47981> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7176]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! Your brother-in-law250 picked up another bow and pierced Satyaki with eight arrows, following this up with another five." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/768bd554ac53817ebfe9af5f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4444]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Having got to know159 about the intentions of Sanjaya and his son, the immensely wise Krishna Dvaipayana arrived there and said, “O Sanjaya! Tell Dhritarashtra what he has asked." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/768c688d94ca36748043645c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3845]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Shrutayudha, Durdhara, Kratha, Vivitsu, Vikata, Soma, Nishangi, Kavachi, Pashi, Nanda, Upanandaka, Dushpradharsha, Subahu, Vatavega, Suvarchasa, Dhanurgraha, Durmada, Satva and Soma471 —these were valiant and extremely powerful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/768fded503d4a6c4ae2aaac2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "16_Mausala" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[230, 232]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! The gods, the best among sages and their eloquent followers worshipped the lord of everything.
Delighted, Puruhuta30 also honoured him.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7691e449932c2dec4ac7ff93> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1238, 1239]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The gods rejoiced a great deal and returned, keeping the ambrosia in safe custody.
For safe-keeping, the killer of Bala32 and the other gods handed over the vessel containing the ambrosia to Kiriti.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76a0a51de6fda1017a52567a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9179]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "17 The mighty-armed one obtained the great Indra’s bow, which was divine and indestructible, and equal to Gandiva and Sharnga18 in energy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76a1554d498dd426cc30a3da> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4461]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“The son of the chastiser of Paka23 was extremely delighted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76a34c18ae1c0573a3aa1746> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12816]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "While he roamed and travelled in many different countries, he228 created the many different sacrificial hearths that are mentioned in the Vedas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76a8d309886111faa875712d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25968]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! In ancient times, the king of the gods recounted this sacred account to an assembly of the praiseworthy Vasus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76c5cb5d6d3e84eeca323aa7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 16 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[645]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "She was no longer able to carry the child, whose body was as hard as a vajra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76c6f806aa16c320b5c292fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4802]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "560 Krishna told Arjuna, ‘The king561 has been severely wounded." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76ca723c8c64fa547a31f979> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6686]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He took Savyasachi348 with him and went to the nishada." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76d14f9afff8aa65b4ec5904> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16634]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods know such a person to be a brahmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76d84b4004642febc7c0a664> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7115, 7118]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The rakshasa was angry and in his rage, the immensely strong one killed the horses and the charioteers of the great-souled ones.
Those great archers were bereft of their chariots by the rakshasa and the traveller of the night swiftly rushed against them, wishing to kill them.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76e19f41e9c12326538f1b24> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5500]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Pandava! The sacred Sarasvati flows towards the ocean, with many pools354 and adorned with groves." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76e7842b883b32ec93c6a97f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2359, 2366]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Radiance is the sign of the gods.
Speech has the attributes of truth and is cleansed through vowels and consonants.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76e813327690803c7369b08e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11222]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Why are you acting in this stupid way? You were born in the lineage of a brahmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/76f4b7a33b1b8cc44822021a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11542]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They are haughty because of their strength and are given to incessant delight, as if they are like the large numbers of gods in heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/771faea7de0c131965d73234> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1254]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having seen that it was impenetrable, he was distressed and spoke to Arjuna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7728612f0e98b45dde90c5b2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[776]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme being! You are the refuge of all the rajarshis, the performers of pure deeds who withdraw from the field of battle32 and who have the knowledge of every dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7730b884abfc843547fe5ff5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[311]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He has taken away all my gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/773bfc0356f55542376a7fd1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[638]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! They36 were restless and moved around." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/773c3f280b1bf91ecd0f48e1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19911]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rites, beneficial ‘B sacrifices, officiating at sacrifices, donations and efforts to undertake auspicious deeds according to one’s capacity—these have been recommended for the sake of the departed ancestors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7740e5746a8179bd3746a25c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5599]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is no one greater than one whom the king of gods remembers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/774d08c385990b288bbfc2ee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9838, 9841]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Dharma and artha57 will be destroyed.
” As the miserable brahmana cried out to the Pandavas, Kunti’s son Dhananjaya58 heard his words.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/775850621700a6b671bffb89> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4722]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A terrible and extremely wonderful battle ensued, like that between the gods and the danavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7761697a17d694d4c96d916f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19597, 19598]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """715 Debts to one’s own self are repaid through words,716 eating leftovers and protecting one’s own self.
If one is interested in following dharma, right from the beginning, one should discharge debts to the various categories of servants.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77645e815a87b7791f429163> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16216, 16223]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """A learned person looks upon a learned brahmana, a cow, an elephant, a dog and an outcaste341 equally.
He leaves no trail, like a bird in the sky or an aquatic creature in the water, and the gods themselves are confused in trying to follow his tracks.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77664a3c8ceb8f22cfb43d7a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6482]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Regaining his consciousness, Kounteya321 tore apart all the bonds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77a61900c7179c678981a431> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1599]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! When they saw the commander224 advancing against the Panchalas on his chariot, a great uproar arose among the Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77ad7ac294903e57fe7e4de8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1426]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The unblemished Dasharathi166 lived in the forest on his father’s instructions, so as to maintain his own dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77b02ae961a54f6aef284857> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10631]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Suddenly, Svarbhanu54 swallowed up the blazing sun." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77c2599237e8808fef4e5ac5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4627]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Astride a supreme elephant, the Nishada545 is advancing against Pandava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77c619d3e2c596597971d34d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11642]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’137 492(195) ‘Markandeya said, “They138 had an immensely energetic and immensely radiant son by the name of Dhundhu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77d05ca22007089fe2a54ea9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4563, 4565]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """With his preceptor Kashyapa, supreme among sages, at the forefront, he performed a vajapeya187 and one hundred horse sacrifices there.
O Janamejaya! Rama189 gave riches to the brahmanas there.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77d3d8857d6249b338cf654e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11588]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Distressed, he spoke these words to Utathya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77ea44aaef963f3c32926c5f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10462]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O bull among the Bharata lineage! I shot a sharp arrow39 at him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77f143b0a16c3e92de1be5a6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2776]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "187 Duryodhana was extremely energetic and attacked Partha and the brave one188 attacked Duryodhana alone." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77f2b26ea4bff1e5f55bc036> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17705]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘The yaksha asked, “Who is a friend to one who is travelling? Who is a friend at home? Who is a friend to one who is sick? Who is a friend to one who is about to die?” ‘Yudhishthira replied, “A caravan is a friend to a traveller." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77f58770768a489d84123f04> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[158]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Chapter 1993(3) aishampayana said, ‘O Kouravya! Partha Yudhishthira Dharmaraja had remained there only for a short while." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/77fa2b2e19aee739352b59a9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3809]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "272 That spot of the god of the gods was beautiful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7821b505b1eff9492d4b739f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1839]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This203 represents meditation." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/782c2cbeffb767d2b945952b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9896]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that the chakra had been brought down, Ghatotkacha quickly enveloped Drona’s son with arrows, like Svarbhanu73 covering the sun." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7856f95c5b7bbbe058e430c0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6855]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There will be no sons of Dhritarashtra and the son of the suta535 will be dead." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/785af59923dc0928cce2f122> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2531, 2534]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """” The lord, the destroyer of enemies, was pleased and spoke about his qualities in many different ways, in the presence of the gods and the ancestors.
At this, all the gods united and made up their minds to kill them.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/785b6e52335b0eee01a25a3e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9897]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He will fight with valour, like Maghavan34 against the danavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/787636afeedff32e2ebac945> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11708]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O one who is great in vows! We do not desire to drink soma with the Ashvins." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/789027fdb90752ccbf0dab21> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[448, 451, 455]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘A twice-born who is learned in the Vedas, the angas129 and the Upanishads, but does not know this account, cannot be said to have any learning at all.
O Brahmanas! Just as the four kinds of beings131 are derived from the sky, all the Puranas132 draw upon this account.
The Bharata flowed from the lips of Dvaipayana133 and is immeasurable, sacred, purifying, salvation and the dispeller of sin.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/789f0aff3375c7f84d40d1c3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8497]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘The wealth of those who perform sacrifices, have good conduct and are noble should not be taken, as it belongs to the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/78a19735f4b65f15ac185c10> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2328]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ ‘“The woman replied, ‘O brahmana! I am constrained by the need for intercourse." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/78af101f5692a554404eb7ac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16401]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "How should one act, so as not to violate any rites that have been laid down?’” ‘Bhishma said, “Having been thus addressed, Gandhavati’s son368 spoke to his son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/78affea6146af9b5e4cdccd7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10231]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O fortunate one! If Jahnavi’s son21 does not act in accordance with my words, I will use the energy of my weapons to burn him down in battle, together with his advisers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/78baf7ce8a07f7895ff51f7b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8729]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having been killed by me in the battle, you will go to Yama’s residence, just as Ravana’s son385 was slain by Lakshmana, Rama’s younger brother." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/78bf9c5cb008499a336719c8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19535]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A king who is a coward, a brahmana who eats everything, a vaishya without exertion, an inferior varna708 who is lazy, a learned person who lacks good conduct, a noble person who is without a means of sustenance, a brahmana who has deviated from the truth, a wayward woman, a ‘free’ person who is still attached, a person who cooks only for himself, a foolish ‘“P person who is eloquent, a kingdom without a king and a king who has no affection for his subjects—all these are reasons for grief." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/78c301936477b00e5ae40045> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12004]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having obtained kingdoms, they wish to become gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/78ccb0ddb7fb2b5de16f879b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6316]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”877 I became the lord of the gods after killing in battle Vritra, Bala, Paka, Virochana, with his one hundred kinds of maya, Namuchi, who was difficult to counter, Shambara, who had many different kinds of maya, the daitya Viprachitti, all of Danu’s sons878 and Prahrada." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/78ccf06b6bfaf92731874806> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2031]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Karna was like Kartyavirya290 in his valour and the king’s mind turned towards him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/78df0756c1d01f291aea4905> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1802]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ CHAPTER 1002(25) ‘Dhritarashtra asked, “When they80 had returned and engaged in different divisions, how did the spirited ones on the side of the Parthas, and on mine, fight? How did Arjuna act towards the army of the samshaptakas? O Sanjaya! What did the samshaptakas do to Arjuna?” ‘Sanjaya replied, “When they had returned and engaged themselves in different divisions, your son himself attacked Bhima with an army of elephants." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79115d74b43658bd971a8d6e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11149]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Having thus spoken, the illustrious god, worshipped by the yakshas and the rakshasas, departed with all his followers, who could travel in an instant." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7914958f05da2dd798cf304e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[852]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "44 Having killed Hidimba, Bhima left with his brothers, placing Hidimba45 at the forefront." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/791d13ac6d742bcd707581de> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4877]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When the Panchalas and Somakas were being killed by Bhishma, the noble ones221 resolved to fight and attacked Bhishma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/792e328e16918c52357549f3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8392]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "For the sake of victory over Bhishma, the battle that commenced there among the Kouravas428 was terrible." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7943c312d7ef5739f2512fdf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9035]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He remained stationed in the path of the chariot419 and protected Saindhava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7944ae5f631cd4842e5f8ba6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4451]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods are devotedly faithful to you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7955c1e5de983bfc9d4a1bb8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[69, 70, 72]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Parjanya13 is supreme among those who shower down.
Dhritarashtra is supreme among nagas and Airavata14 among elephants.
O Vrikodara! Just as there is a foremost among each specific category, this young Gudakesha15 is foremost among all archers.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/795b328207609cbe6d1251dd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12721]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Duryodhana, Karna, Shakuni Soubala and the other foremost brothers53 protected Drona in the battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/798a82d69aa32befb133b627> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8994]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The clubs, maces, swords, spears, lances and battleaxes, taken up by the yakshas and rakshasas in their arms, began to blaze." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/798c77e18106395a45b25a63> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[660]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then there is Kesara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79a6c0045c8a5185d20ad68c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7550]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Having said this, rishi Dvaipayana took them to the house of a Brahmana and told the best36 of the Parthas, “Wait for me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79abff27d63f1ee7856966f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14945, 14947]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """” The brave ones then headed for the hermitage on excellent chariots, yoked to Saindhava19 steeds that had the speed of the wind or a storm.
On noticing it, the king20 spoke to Bhima and Dhananjaya.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79b74257038a1c59585f3b8a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7493, 7494]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O son! Because you are overcome by intolerance, do not destroy the Kurus.
The entire earth is touched by this, either on your side, or that of the Pandavas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79bafce2d3793b96a746e7fe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4458]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the gods! It is through your favours that the gods are always happy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79bc9344cfddab1fc023ee6a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[581]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "42 The one with dharma in his soul43 followed good conduct and gave away large quantities of donations." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79c1b361a3089a3f664bbf58> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2656, 2657]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Even if all the gods with Indra become your allies, these princes202 will not pardon you.
The great-souled son of Dharma203 always bases himself in dharma.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79c7c6fe91d179385f253f8a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[573]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When he advanced against Drona, which brave ones surrounded him? He47 crushed the large army of the Souvira kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79c870274a6186a3210505f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15568]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Fortunate are those who will see you consecrated with kusha grass, parched rice and shami91 wood, with a face like the moon amidst scattered clouds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79c93f1e3d9a8a7ee1a8c934> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2707]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Karna is contemptible43 and negligent." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79df40096cf06280e2af451e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2550]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On witnessing this superhuman feat, the gods applauded." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79eb49c6a4414455fc42c4d2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[554]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! O Janamejaya! Yajnaseni1 lived there in great unhappiness, serving Sudeshna, though she deserved to be served herself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79f7041b6403e78572e0c328> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 134 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11176]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If a woman does not desire any objects of pleasure, prosperity or happiness other than her husband, then she has a share in that dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79fb3d1e47fbb36ac0ab089d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9450]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Beings in the abodes of the gods are always satisfied and happy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/79fc1b4d8b5e943a5147c416> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5750, 5751]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The king of Nagapura270 accepted them all.
‘Then, to the delight of his own kingdom and city, Pandu returned to Gajasahrya271 with his vehicles.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7a006352438bd7e5b0bf9293> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10959]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O learned one! Whenever dharma goes into a decline and adharma96 raises its head, then I create myself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7a093cd504a3059d13b2455a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[489]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Using my energy, I will invisibly enter his supreme weapon, the vajra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7a13b0f7efac87d9e6f6eb8c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1136]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Which mortal man can stand before him? He is worthy of being honoured by all the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7a1c80175f5da5a705492864> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5324, 5326]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘Bhishma, supreme among those who wielded arms, thus won the maidens and left for Hastinapura, where the king of the Kouravas229 was.
The great-souled son of the one who goes into the ocean230 took care of the daughters of the king of Kashi like daughters-in-law, younger sisters or daughters and brought them to the land of Kuru.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7a24d48c0551cfca1db321eb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 78 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4433]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Kounteya! I will tell you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7a2652dd391c7302892f6445> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2799]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The grief of one whose property has been stolen, whose son has been killed, who has lost all in debt, who has been extorted by a king, or of a woman who has no husband, or of one distanced from his companions, or the misery of a co- wife, or of one deprived because of witnesses218—the lord of the thirty gods219 has declared these miseries to be equal." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7a3b7ce35454e11d9ee364f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4600, 4602, 4603, 4604]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The brave Anala58 is the mouth of the gods and has the wind for his chariot.
59 One then goes to the place where Sarasvati unites with the ocean.
O bull among the Bharata lineage! He obtains the fruits of one thousand cows60 and attains the world of heaven, blazing in resplendence like the fire.
One should stay there for three nights and offer oblations to the ancestors and the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7a4a7cbb7dab67bb8bf931b5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 213 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14635]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rigid in his vows, such a brahmana performs valiant and terrible austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7a606bb7170203d2d4e5acdc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11309, 11310, 11311, 11312]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """) Maha-karma;1176 (714) Krita-karma;1177 (.
) Kritagama;1178 (.
) Udbhava;1179 (715) Sundara;1180 (716) Sunda;1181 (717) Ratna-nabha;1182 (718) Sulochana;1183 (719) Arka;1184 (720) Vajasana;1185 (721) Shringi;1186 (722) Jayanta;1187 (723) Sarva-vijjayi;1188 (724) Suvarna-bindu;1189 (725) Akshobhya;1190 (726) Sarva- vagishvareshvara;1191 (727) Maha-hrada;1192 (728) Maha-garta;1193 (729) Maha-bhuta;1194 (730) Maha-nidhi;1195 (.
) Kumuda;1196 (731) Kundara;1197 (732) Kunda;1198 (733) Parjanya;1199 (.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7a6ba7e98af769cc4277987c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1449]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘One evening, when Kounteya Dharmaraja Yudhishthira was seated and surrounded by all the rishis, Dalbhya’s son Baka168 spoke to him, “O Partha! O supreme among the Kurus! Look! In Dvaitavana, the hour has come for brahmanas and ascetics to kindle their sacrificial fires." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7a92cddade0278b15c213457> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "17_Mahaprasthanika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[162]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If you abandon this dog, you will obtain the world of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7a9896c8ed8192137f5a8946> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2844]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Drupada76 had a daughter named Shikhandi, but later, she was transformed into a son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7aa2248aedb6b50bdbbd4f57> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9586]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "How was he killed in their midst? O Duryodhana! In particular, the lord of the earth37 sought assurance from you and me to save him from Arjuna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7aa6177f19fe88f51e016ed8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[224]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Indra of the gods spoke in this way to Yudhishthira, Indra among the Kouravas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7aa7eb9c6a375b9c9e92155d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4668]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Like amrita, it always revives the Indras among serpents when they die." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7aa873cafaa1246cf1e28cd2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8145]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Karna! You have been born in this fashion." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7aabc8014d9ac606d65f03a4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4304]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The drums of the gods sounded and a pure breeze began to blow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7aae29c8cc3c395f0dbbe3ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1826]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rathas clashed against rathas and horses against horse riders." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ab291e115eb630841489700> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 45 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2529]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A householder brahmana who does all this to the best of his capacity, is rigid in his vows and is controlled and pure, conquers heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ab70bb207887b69687f283b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 352 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25939, 25946, 25948, 25951, 25954]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’”’ Chapter 1680(352) he brahmana said, ‘O supreme among serpents! There is no doubt that this is extraordinary.
How can you then go? O brahmana! Tell me what is to be done and the reason why you have come here.
O brahmana! You should only go after you have honoured me and received my permission.
O brahmana rishi! This is not how you should depart.
In staying with me, what is there to think about?’ ‘“The brahmana said, ‘O immensely wise one! O serpent! It is exactly as you have understood it.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7abf86666b5db3b0d9e9e61a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2242]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Arjuna said, “O charioteer! Stop the horses at a place from where I can use arrows on that army, until I am able to see that wretch among the Kuru lineage131 in the midst of the soldiers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7acecad3e7156aea70eb6058> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[591]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The world of men is superior to the world of the gods, because the houses of men are full of many riches." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ada284f675bc346758b7461> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4252]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Dharma is evident in one’s tasks and without this, he662 is like a dog." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ae7ee115955d90ec18974db> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1077]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In this way, may your mind and intelligence always find pleasure in dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7af309c8ca4118b503d06d62> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8466]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Performing sacrifices, studying and accepting708 constitute the dharma of brahmanas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b0bd6cdcea466a91ee7bc17> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[556]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As soon as he saw her roaming around like a goddess, like a daughter of the gods, Kichaka2 desired her and was oppressed by the arrows of love." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b14ca9237442d19810af211> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5931]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! The gods bowed in obeisance at his feet and saluted him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b18e2e4303fa7c746d215bc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7759]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Happy are men to whom sons have not been born." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b1963e85b44e958e8899a90> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16140, 16141]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The forest-dwelling ones killed rakshasas by the hundreds and rakshasas killed the forest-dwelling ones.
136 But the number of rakshasas killed was more than that of monkeys.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b2367d3e9d069d739e025f6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6839]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” When the arena had become somewhat quiet, Bibhatsu14 began to exhibit the lightness in use of weapons he had learned from his preceptor." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b265e9f8fe0d10f9623d1d9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3161]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Among men, Pulastya’s sons72 were born as his brothers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b3b11e0e03c7d40b6ebc031> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[781]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I will capture the king, who is devoted to truth and dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b3b4617790f58e2edadceef> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13613]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowledge can be withdrawn into the supreme." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b509512d517a1d57ad39cae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11231]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is the god among all the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b5e08b060e922483c22a82b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11246]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That spot was like Nandana258 and was inhabited by yakshas and kinnaras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b649d5c28814a53c4d9a2cc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3947]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The child in the womb has been V destroyed by the brahmastra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b697a9bf5661d15d8f9862c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[342, 352]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """” Sudeshna57 replied, “O beautiful one! Those you speak of58 do not possess the beauty you have.
You are endowed with all the qualities, like a mare from Kashmira.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b747fe6060d1c5e2e172c49> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17962]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "We have heard that when Tvashtri544 came to visit Nahusha in earlier times, he saw that he545 was following the certain and ancient practice of the sacred texts and was about to kill a cow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7b963d77ebf1daa77bece24c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "16_Mausala" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[353]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He searched out the bodies of both Rama and Vasudeva46 and had them cremated by men who were accomplished in such tasks." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ba53ad9a685972edf2f0de8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11433]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Is there anyone who has a longer life than you?’ The owl replied, ‘There is a lake by the name of Indradyumna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7babfdcb715dd6009adefdd8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "16_Mausala" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[320]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This Vajra40 will be the king in Shakraprastha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7bad0a00a23fc13d178274f9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23971]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Therefore, all the gods abandon it and enjoy havya and kavya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7bae731db9694d1d9c197e2b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8744]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I am capable of handling this rakshasa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7bb70d4907575a5404dab3f3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8568]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Vrikodara! In a household, you can only urge cooks, servants, men and slaves to hasten in their tasks and are capable of reproaching them for the sake of food." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7bcdcef9e1621a5ea7c58492> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18794]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "634 White is supreme." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7bd64d6aa5f49a8e4e94c0e0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3036]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "472 O unblemished one! O great king! When his hermitage was burnt down, Apava473 angrily cursed Kartavirya Arjuna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7bd8fee97d9f7ce5d876098e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11011]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In that battle, there was an extremely fierce encounter between the man and the rakshasa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7bde11f0e6eeb5cc306bd8c4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6452, 6456]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O maharshi! What will this pointless conversation achieve?”’ 767(104) Janamejaya said, ‘He143 has been prone to evil from his birth, coveting the riches of others and confounded by avarice.
Why did his relatives and well-wishers not restrain him from this deviant path? Out of friendship and affection, why did the illustrious one144 and the grandfather not stop him?’ Vaishampayana said, ‘The illustrious one spoke appropriate words and so did Bhishma.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7bf4083580a6af497729e3a1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12263]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There was a terrible rakshasi9 named Jara and she possessed great valour." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7bf7b505503e21263ecb2e87> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15079, 15080]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Wishing to seize Souvira, in the vanguard, Partha28 slew five hundred maharathas, who hailed from the mountains.
In an instant, in that battle, the king29 himself killed one hundred brave and chief Souvira warriors who had attacked him.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7bfc9b53825f06a24cf5d1bb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 131 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10773, 10774, 10776, 10777, 10778]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Because of the undigested food from a shudra, one is dislodged from the status of a brahmana.
Such a brahmana becomes a shudra.
If a brahmana dies with undigested food in his stomach, whatever be the varna of the person from whom he received that food, he is reborn as that varna.
The status of a brahmana is extremely difficult to obtain and is sacred.
If one disrespects it and eats food that should not be eaten, one is dislodged from the status of a brahmana.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7c09c356c5a79a767989f3d1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5705]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The extremely sacred and supreme Brahmasara378 is there, frequented by rishis." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7c24f49e743659421ebd1cda> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9311, 9312]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """You will soon behold the lord of the gods.
’ Then, following his instructions, I ascended Mount Shaishira158 and practised austerities.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7c2dc3b0db6556cef520b972> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6360]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because of his fear, the slayer of Bala and Vritra451 showered down at the time of a drought." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7c3398847e3e52c37996390d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4047, 4048]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The Himalayas provided a celestial, golden and supreme seat, decorated with the best of jewels and divine gems.
All the auspicious objects were brought by the masses of gods, objects required for the consecration.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7c38b4e869c77ffa5c48b2e5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22512]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Vyasa saw that his son was approaching, like a fire scattering flames on every side." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7c4154aeb0dc9908ac3be5a6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9193, 9194]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """On seeing them, he was extremely saddened and said, ‘Shall I also become like them?’ Then, the god Girisha38 looked at the wielder of the vajra with eyes dilated with anger and said, ‘O Shatakratu!39 Enter this cavern, because in your folly, you have insulted me in front of my eyes.
’ Thus addressed by the lord, the king of the gods shuddered and shook, because of the curse.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7c69dfc8aa1f2aed7aceed94> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4556]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The learned ones say that he who bathes there and worships the gods and the ancestors, obtains ten times the merits of an ashvamedha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7c74df718b244922b763fcf7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12505, 12506]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O Yudhishthira! The sacred month of Magha6 has arrived.
One- fourth of shuklapaksha should still remain.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7c8502ead37001a86228c658> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[639]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Partha! Is it the case that your innate nature is afflicting you? You saw Krishna41 brought to the assembly hall in a single garment, when she was in season." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7c8b361b35848b50f7210d8b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10586]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A fish came up to him on the banks of the Virini63 and spoke to him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7c931a0760621d1aca8f8e27> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4950]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On going to that sacred tirtha and satisfying the ancestors and the gods, a man obtains the fruits of an agnishtoma sacrifice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ca88bcf1a46e30f413d9aa4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4061]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ’ ‘S Chapter 1188(38) anjaya said, “O venerable one! Kritavarma, Kripa, Drona’s son, the son of the suta, Uluka, Soubala and the king494 and his brothers saw that the army was afflicted because of the fear of Pandu’s son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7cacc8bbfd28faa5acb0754a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[303]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among those who uphold dharma! The earth, wind, space, water, light as the fifth, intelligence, the atman, the mind, time, the directions and the ten qualities15 are always a witness to good and bad deeds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7cb12a677f6ceb1a304d4f09> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9630]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As is prescribed, the wise Yudhishthira himself gave him offerings5 and once the devarshi was seated, reported the state of the kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ccce8148826fb4b9e9c655c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17185]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Indra among kings! Mrityu482 swiftly went to the spot known as Dhenuka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7cdd1910df59411fdc5b66bf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4285]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Even the gods will find it extremely difficult to accomplish these." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d0b2a07f19b3551d4c39742> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5583, 5585]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ This is what Vijaya367 told me.
You should protect him from rakshasas in difficult and uneven terrain.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d0bd85d6f445f4f12ef1ccc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14442]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kapila124 therefore presented himself there and Janaka became devoted to him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d2a54442bdff531b8440ec9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9468, 9471, 9472]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Without ignoring those, which I learnt properly, I specially devoted my attention to learning about weapons.
”’ 462(165) ‘Arjuna said, “When I was skilled in weapons and had obtained his confidence, Harivahana179 touched my head with his hands and spoke these words.
‘Today, the masses of gods are incapable of vanquishing you in battle, not to speak of humans of the world who have not perfected their souls.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d2ea09bd37b24d56c28c249> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9695, 9697]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """With arrows that were fierce at the tip, he brought down hundreds of other warriors, elephants, horses and chariots in that battle, like an angry Destroyer slaughtering beings.
O venerable one! As he was striking down enemies with this, the eldest of the Pandavas46 severed it into three fragments with two broad-headed arrows.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d33c22c464f945187f9b71f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7305, 7329]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """They surpassed Vaishravana382 in prosperity and Brihaspati in wisdom.
Armour and headdresses constituted the foam.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d40dadb9809e62fa71db6f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5245]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kin never tolerate the prospect of kin being maltreated by others." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d4f0b192548a683feb69404> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15491]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the gods! If you worship me from the forefront, so will the other gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d61f158e4935cc53cebf73a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5695]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The Kouravas repeatedly satisfied the gods, the ancestors and the brahmanas at Kanya tirtha, Ashva tirtha375 and Gava tirtha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d86562ed58623bb6ceafca6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10194]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "20 Dhananjaya gave birth to that atiratha21 from a Satvata lady, like fire is produced at a sacrifice from the womb of a shami22 tree." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d897d24735e2c665057cd29> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2968]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They entered the palace of the king of the gods and were received with homage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d89df65a0dc2a43186cbdcb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1995]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the eternal purusha, self-resplendent, the predecessor of the gods, without birth and omnipresent." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d91692639c2ee93b919324e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8068]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lord of the gods251 worshipped all the gods in the proper way." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d9a0a2a9646403df42f3688> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[960]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This daughter of Virata’s68 is the daughter-in-law of the wielder of Gandiva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d9a72337ea09c92fc7acb66> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10249]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The great-souled lord of beings was as radiant as the illustrious lord, when united with Guha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d9dcbe98ea2124a5d14785a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11927]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having struck the club down with a club, he248 advanced towards Bhima." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7d9faefcee507f880d82319a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6887]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! Like that, uncountable were the riches that Gaya gave away to the sadasyas545 at those seven sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7dc2ea827b25b2f99982c565> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6131]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I have used the eye of my mind to search in the two worlds of gods and men." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7dccace863c43cbe351dcb48> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7282, 7283]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """This is the lake named Kushavan, where there are one trillion584 beds of kusha grass.
Rukimini’s585 hermitage is here and she conquered her anger and found peace here.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7dd1291322b09d611192a00f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2699, 2702]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Even the king of the gods could not tolerate that.
When he fought for twenty-three nights with Bhargava Rama421 without being overpowered, my mind had gone out to him.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7dd35435e5046ba2d2591811> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9944]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On witnessing his terrible austerities and homage, the god Mahadeva Umapati74 Shankara was satisfied." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ddf46f03012d57fe379dd4f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5627]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O mighty-armed one! The tirthas are infested by rakshasas, who always bring impediments in the way of austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7de28c06eff5b205d8959954> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13183, 13185]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Having been thus instated by the masses of all the gods, in his ornaments, he looked happy and satisfied.
Pavaki275 was thus instated by the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ded0d8bba2fb1f0b4d903dd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19621]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is my view that under all circumstances, it is proper that they723 should always associate with virtuous people who know about dharma, not with those who are wicked." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7def0bd0bd0b2b29598d31da> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[446]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The ears83 are Nagadvipa and Kashyapadvipa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7df469edb00f693db2ba1246> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1563]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Disease, fire, water, weapons, hunger, predatory beasts, poison, rope and fall from height—these can be the reasons for a being’s death." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7dfd2701d8111ec40cd83e21> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9562]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The one who could not be killed by gods and men was killed in the encounter." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7dfee583d4ada3b0e9559c85> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1533, 1541]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He went to the spot where the gods had assembled.
The gods were distressed and confused.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7e022ad32cf2da100bafaf0d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11929]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Using his own sharp arrows, the rakshasa rendered all of them unsuccessful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7e274bb0132d67833dbf1fe0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1222]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Does King Dhritarashtra, together with his sons, make arrangements for the livelihood of the advisers? Are there ill-wishers, who dwell as well-wishers, and bring about dissension and ruin? O son! Do all the Kurus talk about the crimes committed by the Pandavas? When they see the masses of dasyus23 assemble, do they remember Partha,24 the foremost warrior? O son! Do they remember the straight- flying and whirring arrows released from the string of the bow? Do they remember the roar of Gandiva? I have not seen anyone on earth who is Arjuna’s equal or superior in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7e29b8b31d6eb0e6ae68464a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[158, 159]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! This brahmana is my priest.
He should be swiftly sent to Dhritarashtra.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7e6b0caec604b705883372de> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1066]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He struck Drona’s son with arrows that were like the vajra, the fire, or Vaivasvata’s167 staff." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7e8253acd2d9cd85c7099041> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6881]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Marichi was born from marichi139 and Kashyapa was born from Marichi." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7e8608c6a81525c4eaff5f75> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1435]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Through it, Isha106 was capable of destroying all beings on earth, the firmament and bodies of water." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7e89193c6162aaaac985bfa6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[135, 137]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! There were all the immensely powerful princes of the Vrishnis who had learnt the science of archery from Arjuna and were dressed in deer and antelope hides32 and other princes who had been similarly taught—Rukmini son,33 and Samba and Yuyudhana Satyaki.
Dhananjaya’s eternal friend Tumbaru was there, Chitrasena with his advisers and many other gandharvas and apsaras, skilled in singing and music, knowledgeable in the beating of tala35 and kinnaras, who were excellent pupils of laya.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7e8dcf9e47c1a8f6ecf7137b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10242]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the stores of austerities and are like the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ea71a7f562252229efb1209> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5255]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "295 Worshipping the ancestors and the gods, one will obtain the fruits of one thousand cows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7eb1bd16a7a5a09cabb076d5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5640]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The robbing of the kingdom, the defeat at the game of dice and the exile of my sons has not caused me as much of unhappiness, as that of the large and dark lady brought to the assembly hall in a single garment." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ec9de588e912ab741e34c28> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4917]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those two immensely strong sons of yours were like the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ecee256c7ba46343765a84a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1088]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son!147 Austerities, renunciation and ritual action—those intelligent ones who have determined the way to the supreme objective have said that each of these is superior to the preceding one." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ecf4fedc963195124e661c3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4284]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that the lances had been shattered, Bhagadatta’s son quickly shot a line of arrows303 at Pandava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ef5469b12406fbdaa6ae8ac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5667]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The Pandavas and Krishna66 offer you their respects." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7f2f59fcb733884240744f98> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[779]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They71 were overwhelmed and confused by the Pandavas and could not distinguish the directions and the sub-directions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7f379ee9b0a5799a62e31f17> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[233]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Vyasa replied, “The fire37 has a cheerful radiance and its flames rise up straight." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7f3fa27f9bb0171474c7987e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12030]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Intolerant, the handsome one quickly goaded her." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7f4304d40b5ea8a8fca046c3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3916]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This was the goddess Shri602 and she became the wife of the intelligent Dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7f5195c7379bf9cffbdc5f2e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2351]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "564 Desire, anger and avarice—these are the three types of doors to hell and destroyers of the atman." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7f57143f6c17dc53a9f6c95d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8154]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "These best of gods and men are your ancestors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7f6e2edcda2323790a8b43b5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14501]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lord100 entered his beautiful house, which was like Chaitraratha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7f76b0aa8e31a0e71b310ad3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4788]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Instructed by your son, there were fourteen thousand supreme horse-riders and they surrounded Soubala." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7fa43dab4e2213713fc8c6dc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 116 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7401]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He obtains a share in the fruits of dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7fb4a08171be5716f0a70fbd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6581]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! I344 and Devavrata shouted, ‘Fight." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7fb751d03f278b063dcfb050> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6515]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O bull among gods! Hear about the supreme greatness and power of cattle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7fb9abfe444a87fc4a590797> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3850, 3851]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! Through his mental powers, Mrityu588 had a daughter named Sunitha.
She was famous in the three worlds and gave birth to Vena.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7fdc92ce4348160b5139ba59> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6393, 6395]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The immensely fortunate one has been attacked by the evil-souled rakshasa.
’ On hearing the words of the grandfather, the maharathas used the utmost speed to quickly go to the spot where Kourava was—Drona, Somadatta, Bahlika, Jayadratha, Kripa, Bhurishrava, Shalya, Chitrasena, Vivimshati, Ashvatthama, Vikarna, the one from Avanti332 and Brihadbala.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7fe043d48065ca358789603e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1299]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘O descendant of the Bharata lineage! All of them were welcomed with honour—Dhritarashtra, Bhishma, the greatly intelligent Vidura, all the brothers with Duryodhana at the forefront, all the kings with the preceptor19 at the forefront, Subala the king of Gandhara, the immensely strong Shakuni, Achala, Vrishaka, the supreme warrior Karna, Rita, Shalya the king of the Madras, the maharatha Bahlika, Somadatta of the Kuru lineage, Bhuri, Bhurishrava, Shala, Ashvatthama, Kripa, Drona,20 Jayadratha the king of Sindhu, Yajnasena21 and his son, Shalva the lord of the earth, the greatly famous Bhagadatta, king of Pragjyotisha, all the mlecchas who lived along the shores of the ocean, the kings from the mountains, King Brihadbala, Vasudeva from Pundra, the king of Vanga, the king of Kalinga, Akarsha, Kuntala, the Vanavasya, the Andhrakas, the Dravidas, the Simhalas, the king of Kashmir, the immensely energetic Kuntibhoja, the immensely strong Suhma, all the other kings and warriors from Bahlika, Virata and his sons, the maharatha Machella, kings, the sons of kings, the lords of many countries, the immensely valorous Shishupala, invincible in battle, and his son, Rama,22 Aniruddha, Babhru, Sarana, Gada, Pradyumna, Samba, the valorous Charudeshna, Ulmuka, Nishatha, Pradyumna’s valorous son and all the other Vrishnis who were maharathas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/7ff8feeb4e9c8b0818f314a6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13487]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods returned." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/800d0bc2ae838976500a9c60> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3859]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That is how the cruel Nishadas were created590 and they dwelt in mountains and forests." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/80118f8746c15d6ff3da6134> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1202]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then arose the beautiful god Dhanvantari20 with a white pot in his hand, in which the ambrosia was." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8015ab46cafee86801b72b41> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3528]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The Dantolukhalinas were there too, as were the Ashmakuttas, Vaneyas72 and many other kinds of sages." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8024b42130465536d57d68ee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7155]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The encounter that ensued between him and those archers was tumultuous and led to the destruction of men, like the famous battle between the gods and the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/802f26d9eb40983273bb24b1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1555, 1557]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Through this, 144 cherish the gods and those gods will cherish you.
Because, cherished by the sacrifice, the gods will give you all desired objects.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/803e23956132267e6150959f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[926]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He had conquered the world of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/803ffb16f7bea91dcaf8b24b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6864]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, while Arjuna’s weapon was still travelling and roaring through the air, the brave one destroyed it with a great weapon that he had obtained from Atharvan Rama785 and which was capable of destroying enemies." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8049c8bcbf3e7cc29a804c24> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13064]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Together with the gods, the lord of the gods roared like a lion." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/804cc06288b52af0623e3318> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6158]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Addicted to fighting, they oppressed the thirty gods, the gandharvas, the rakshasas and all other beings." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/804d722560fff45a1ec0959a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8114]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They repeatedly made offerings to the gods and the ancestors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8052a3c3a535241cfad6e7f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2099]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Chapter 1700(19) udhishthira said, “O bull among the Bharata lineage! Why is it that at the time of accepting a woman’s hand in marriage, it is stated in the learned texts that one must follow dharma together? This sahadharma1155 has been spoken about by the great rishis earlier." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/805d47b0f6250d184dbe436c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10925]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "159 ‘“Bhima thought that your maharatha son160 had been killed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/80623b758e92cae23197e9fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2147]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "268 There were eighty-eight thousand of them and they were killed by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/806b81d87fca9c7d0bffc21e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 281 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19596]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is studying for maharshis, sacrifices and rites for gods, funeral sacrifices and donations for ancestors and honouring for men." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8072d98d6c81a0552319df6c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3670]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I can see that terrible club in my mind’s eye, made of steel77 and burnished with gold, like Brahma’s upraised staff." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/807bc9824eeb420e78813905> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4505]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In earlier times, Bhishma, supreme among those who uphold dharma, was observing a vow for his father16 on the banks of the Bhagirathi,17 like a hermit." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/807ce37d83d7512b44594d1a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14082]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He bears affection towards Dhananjaya and Vasava’s son74 bears affection towards him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/80873a3098509a8e6b5dd277> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6836]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The Krittikas131 saw it there and it was like the young sun in radiance." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/80a94dd18e6c0655a793519d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[519]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "To the south and to the north of Mount Shveta, is the varsha named Hairanyavat91 and the river Hairanvati." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/80d46f07579d09f8d14aaf2b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1341]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was like an angry Destroyer, or like the Destroyer of the Destroyer." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/80d772e15d9400f7c1d04539> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[252]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O immensely intelligent one! Listen to the one hundred and eight pure names38 that were recited by Dhoumya to Partha, best among great-souled ones—Surya, Aryama, Bhaga, Tvashta, Pusha, Arka, Savita, Ravi, Gabhastiman, Aja, Kala, Mrityu, Dhata, Prabhakara, Prithivi, Apa, Teja, Kha, Vayu, Parayana, Soma, Brihaspati, Shukra, Budha, Angaraka, Indra, Vivasvat, Diptamshu, Shuchi, Shouri, Shanaischara, Brahma, Vishnu, Rudra, Skanda, Vaishravana, Yama, Vaidyuta, Jathara, Aindhana, Tejaspati, Dharmadhvaja, Vedakarta, Vedanga, Vedavahana, Krita, Treta, Dvapara, Kali, Sarvamarashraya, Kala, Kashtha, Muhurta, Paksha, Masa, Ritu, Samvatsarakara, Ashvattha, Kalachakra, Vibhavasu, Purusha, Shashvata, Yogi, Vyaktavyakta, Sanatana, Lokadhyaksha, Prajadhyaksha, Vishvakarma, Tamonuda, Varuna, Sagara, Amshu, Jimuta, Jivana, Ariha, Bhutashraya, Bhutapati, Sarvabhutanishevita, Mani, Suvarna, Bhutadi, Kamada, Sarvatomukha, Jaya, Vishala, Varada, Shighraga, Pranadharana, Dhanvantari, Dhumaketu, Adideva, Aditya,39 Dvadashatma, Aravindaksha, Pita, Mata, Pitamaha, Svargadvara, Prajadvara, Mokshadvara, Trivishtapa, Dehakarta, Prashantatma, Vishvatma, Vishvatomukha, Characharatma, Sukshmatma, Maitra and Vapushanvita." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/80dffc4ded917796c90992a7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4756]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Having gone to Lokoddhara139 tirtha, famous in the three worlds, and bathing in that supreme of tirthas, one recovers140 many worlds for one’s own self." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/80e693229e16d9021f77eee7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1815]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If it203 is eaten up without a new crop, it dwindles like the Himalayas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/80f224efe97e408bc73f950c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3834, 3835, 3836, 3838, 3841]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The Brahmana rigidly stuck to his vows and when they were alone, Devayani also sang with him and sported with him.
Five hundred years passed in this fashion and Kacha stuck to his vows.
Then the danavas came to know that he was Kacha.
Without hesitation, out of hatred for Brihaspati and in a desire to protect the knowledge, they killed him.
O descendant of the Bharata lineage! When Devayani saw that the cows had returned home from the forest without Kacha, she immediately said, “O lord! The sun has set and the agnihotra fire141 has not yet been lit.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/80f553f24dfe134e32700ad9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16655]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods and accomplished people with good deeds walk along that path." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/80f750b73dc17631222937a3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2587]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The grandfather of the Pandavas was born on an island in the river Yamuna, in the womb of the virgin Kali1 and from Shakti’s son Parashara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8106c8c7440c745926d6f086> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5624]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He quickly pierced those brothers, who were like gods, with sharp and straight-tufted arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/810d93529eb89def3201221c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3114]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The asura who was his58 younger brother and was known as Suparna, became King Kalakriti on earth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/810db0ee68b6b80174dd957f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6701]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Therefore, knowing the fate of this world, be patient and listen to how the battle raged, like the terrible one between the gods and the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/810f640f0f370b444a4ab5c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4619]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Shambara5 has said that there is nothing worse for a man than a situation where he cannot see how food can be obtained, today or tomorrow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/810f83c9e8d54657acbec8a4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10393, 10395]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Desire results from greed.
Modesty is abandoned.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8117e5836e3a2dd9c5f68909> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6647]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Galava! The lord of riches183 was instated here on Kailasa as the lord of the rakshasas, the yakshas and the gandharvas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/812856de7759491b679ae29e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15411]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let Raghava69 go to the forest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/812d2f443f7bed55a3983702> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9086]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Drupada said, “Let the mighty-armed son16 of Kuru today accept my daughter’s hand in accordance with the prescribed rites." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8132178c99fac45a203b1901> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12600]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lord Damodara17 comforted her." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/813efffb1b1bacc006ae880f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kuntibhoja’s daughter1 also followed Gandhari." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8149cc474cef4da4bb7c5e57> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1880]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! The king of the gods, Yama, Varuna, or the lord of the guhyakas34 does not possess riches equal to Yudhishthira’s wealth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/814c7982da6227ecaf65c108> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25356]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In that way, the great waves of knowledge again merge into Narayana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/816c3548fa6995ea092e3332> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10268]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son!167 Birds, animals and elephants have always cheerfully resided under your delicate shade." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81739d4cc6203c990fb405ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5207]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Trust leads to catastrophe." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81946f9a681747990938b6c0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2203]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When the gods wish to vanquish a man, they distract his intelligence and they see right in what is wrong." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81ab25595de8acb0ec960f87> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14533]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is established in the ocean as the mouth of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81b123e30b582a10fd7e821d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2396]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! It has been said that three are equal in the field of battle—the Destroyer himself at the end of a yuga,14 Jamadagni’s valiant son15 and Bhimasena." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81b1b41140f9e55168e2b622> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4351]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Who other than the Kouravas will seek to fight with an army of soldiers protected by Krishna, Arjuna, Satyaki and Vrikodara? Their warrior is Gudakesha15 and their counsellor is Janardana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81c16be0a13194c44110f30f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2630]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "While Bharadvaja’s son looked on, the immensely illustrious one shot kshurapras, vatsadantas, vipathas, narachas, half-narachas, bhallas and anjalikas56 and covered that array of chariots." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81c3b3335a0f647c3736474c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8921]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That place is the sporting ground of the gods, beyond the access of humans." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81d53dc1c80b8cb054b3d7ba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6241]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "431 There he bowed at the feet of the great-souled Sagara and told him everything and he inhaled the fragrance of his432 head." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81d85c5c618646ee0f61c31c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9527, 9528]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He54 too received Vidura in the appropriate way and they courteously asked about each other’s welfare.
O descendant of the Bharata lineage! He55 saw there the Pandavas and Vasudeva.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81dbd33f4035f25370eb9d76> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1798]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods went away and so did the grandfather God." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81dce97af65a55779d6de1eb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8205]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord! In that other life, I was accomplished in jnana and vijnana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81dea431939ec9766fe01034> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "3 With the time for battle having arrived, Kouravya4 instructed that all of them should have signs and emblems, so that they might be recognized." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81df12d259f22ef3f9160ecc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1285]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The deeds performed by you in the battle are like those of the king of the gods, or those who live in heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81e5b355ca3f6d79cd2767af> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "17_Mahaprasthanika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[135]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the gods! Without my brothers, I do not desire to go to heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81f5980293a099a356a5ee57> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19918]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowledge represents the best path." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/81fb3288f9bfbb55ec8a842c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 252 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14884]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You will have to run away, when you see the wrathful Bhimasena." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8216b79963649ccd74d736a3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2674]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A person who possesses this kind of conduct is said to the best among sages." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/822c7dd6ab3e84ff13cceec5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[733]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "97 A kshatriya without the staff of punishment does not shine." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/823a5cbdc539dbe8b87f8784> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "16_Mausala" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[86]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "10 When Panchajanya11 was blown in the houses of the Vrishnis and the Andhakas, in every direction, instead of its sound, one could hear the terrible sounds of donkeys braying." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/824386067b00ac2487349748> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6722]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O gods! He will accomplish the desire that there is in your hearts." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8250312c84c2b71d15baf768> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12784, 12791]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Earth, air, space, water, and fire as the fifth—these are the great elements and the origins of creation and destruction of all beings.
Skin, touch, exertion and speech—these four have to do with the wind.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8269fd6f530d3cf059648a6a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[317]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They have not repaid their debts to the ancestors and the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/827abbb925b408eed36018d5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3396]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘He saw Madayanti237 and told her about his need." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/827fdd72324863c2af345aac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2379]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Therefore, the god of fire will burn you in Janamejaya’s sacrifice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/82801860fe7fd5c16229173a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4199]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But there is no doubt that I wish to see the illustrious one, the first among the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/828b3b358f24aa6eaccc937d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2063]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Among months, I am Margashirsha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8296ac51b368c25c6d9183a5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4870]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bhishma then affixed an extremely terrible and sharp arrow and brought down Varshneya’s219 charioteer from his chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/82b85871b06901ccf4dc014a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20046]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In such a case, if a person does not say anything, harsh or pleasant, in reply, if when struck, a person is patient and does not strike back, if when assailed, he does not desire anything wicked in retaliation, such a person is always desired by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/82bef31f40ded8f96f019e25> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1159]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "102 O Madhava! Brahmacharis with matted hair103 are hurling bows, javelins and the seats of chariots into the funeral pyre." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/82c0d88045f2acc60626361b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[588]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Gods and men who inhabit the earth follow these." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/82c8af52295b3aad7f9ea584> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4305, 4307]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘Delighted, Mahasena158 granted a boon to the gods.
” Having obtained this boon from that god, all the gods were delighted.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/82e0f431589ce00cec6868b9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3042]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When his horses were slain, Shankha alighted from his chariot and grasping a sword, ran towards Bibhatsu’s72 chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/82ec3c2bd44541406ae97fe8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1929, 1930]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """) Deva;1068 (850) Devasura-maheshvara;1069 (.
) Sarva-deva-maya;1070 (851) Achintya;1071 (852) Devatatma;1072 (853) Asambhava;1073 (854) Udbhida;1074 (855) Trivikrama;1075 (856) Vaidya;1076 (857) Viraja;1077 (858) Virajombara;1078 (859) Idya;1079 (860) Hasti;1080 (861)Sura-vyaghra;1081 (862)Deva-simha;1082 (863)Nararshabha;1083 (864) Vibudhagra-vara;1084 (865) Shreshtha;1085 (866) Sarvadevottomottama;1086 (867) Prayukta;1087 (.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/82efbffbeb68b6d72c0db382> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7958]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He has been created like another son of Jamadagni23 to destroy the Kshatriyas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/82f11572330472526562d415> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7078]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘This great archer who is Krishna’s son367 is like a second Phalguna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/83094150f33f2056dea8a82c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6580]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then, discarding the animal, he followed the path traversed by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/831e8f4c4334fda06a9c6bf0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1786]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Ambashtha pierced him with a stake that penetrated right up to the bones and he75 gave up his bow and arrows and fell down from his chariot onto the ground." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/83341d69130c61b71c420d0f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6237]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "429 He will satisfy Maheshvara430 and purify the sons of Sagara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/833e529c4819cf9e2473f811> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[830]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that his brave brother had been killed, the maharatha139 strung another bow and countered Shini’s descendant." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8347925a1fd27ec40c005417> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7519]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "618 There are six in Krittika." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/835dcf917e23d03d6e85788e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4460, 4462]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O one with an auspicious face! All the celestial states of the gods can be obtained through austerities.
Those men, who perform great austerities and cast aside their bodies on earth, obtain the status of gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8369c3be10a0e7a2229ff62b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8806]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "444 Grasp." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/83748c945050876371727ce6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9251]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Which chariot did he mount? Also tell me about the two Panchalas8 who protected the chariot wheels." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8376282ba9f22722e3335168> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14436, 14437]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """There was a brahmana lady by the name of Kapila121 and she was Asuri’s wife.
Panchashikha became his122 disciple and suckled milk at her breast.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8376e96c277b02ca512e245f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1664]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The preceptor184 and Kshatta Vidura also speak about peace." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8379bede4f9506ab9731b36d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8730]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”7 The rakshasa was driven by destiny." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8379d28ddd6f0bc3d2dca182> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[472]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "27 Then, with Samkarshana28 acting as my second, I killed Kamsa and Sunama, with Rama’s29 assistance." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8395448c739d9f7fb829cfa4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4610]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A man who bathes in Pindaraka64 obtains a lot of gold." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/83a0e17ba9c9d3fdc6cb96dc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6583]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A man who touches the water here, while reciting this verse, has the route of the gods as his path and sees it with his eyes." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/83ba87ec169128ab13c358f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8041]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Then the eloquent Ishana31 Shankara told her, “O fortunate one! You will have five husbands." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/83d21a701e8a523a54258dea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13782]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "15 Through his valour, the prosperity of the gods increased and the danavas were vanquished." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/83e5703a61d95f7ce6923638> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6699]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Your preceptor768 was Brahma’s equal and knew about great weapons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/83efa125ad3c60206873be29> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2450, 2451, 2453, 2454, 2458, 2462]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘ “‘He smiled and asked the masses of gods, “Who will be my charioteer?” The gods replied, “O lord of the gods! There is no doubt that whoever you employ, will be your charioteer.
” He told the gods again, “You decide who is superior to me.
” Having heard the words of the great-souled one, the gods went to the grandfather and having obtained his reassurance, spoke these words.
“O god! We have done everything that you asked us to, for destroying the enemies of the thirty gods.
Therefore, let the best of the gods be appointed as the charioteer.
The supreme of chariots has parts from all the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84029ff05f79b20914c9a227> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12713]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With these, he dispatched Drupada and Virata to Vaisvasvata’s52 eternal abode." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8414ef54b7fbc2978a653632> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1527]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Large numbers of arrows were swiftly released from Drona’s bow and they36 were like shattered boats tossed around on the giant waves of the ocean." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/841f1e001df1dbc27c85be36> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3171]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "497 You know all the itihasa498 and the Puranas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8429ae37c4654539dff60ace> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6905]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Yudhishthira asked, “How did the illustrious one paralyse the chastiser of Paka? For what reason was the great ascetic Bhargava angered? O brahmana! Why were the Nasatyas547 made to become drinkers of soma? O illustrious one! Tell me all this exactly as it happened." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8433fafa30083fbd0753f555> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6044]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "For the welfare of the worlds, this thorn of the worlds was removed as the lord of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8443e6fb1126d14cd4fea64e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[565]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” After consulting Sudeshna, Kichaka went to the daughter of the king3 and spoke to Krishna in a comforting voice, like a jackal confronting a queen of deer4 in the forest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8460839d2bb743341caf6cb4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19143]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of all the gods! Withdraw the destruction that you have wrought." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8461cd6685b646606b2133dc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9021]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With a complexion like that of the fire, he dwells in Prajapati’s abode for a padma number of years." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/846b7bf17ceeb2e113d15e68> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[224]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king of men! With hymns and rituals, they praise the valorous acts of the great- souled destroyer of Bala and Vritra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84a0503e0f61d49b24a470d6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7975]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In that encounter, when the horses were killed, Yudhamanyu quickly used a supreme arrow to sever his312 bow and arm-guard." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84c30bf4eab3999d1c881e8d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3564]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ However, Karna severed this and struck him449 with three arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84ce09d72dc8d02b92f7a056> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5935]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘He looked at Kunti and Madri and said, “Tell Kousalya, kshatta286 Vidura, the king and all his relatives, the lady Satyavati, Bhishma, the royal priests, great-souled soma-drinking and rigid-vowed Brahmanas and old citizens who live here under my protection that Pandu will leave for the forest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84d1c14220b120f7aa845e4d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[673]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The father was the equal of Prajapati57 and bestowed a name on him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84e7e2a56b1b3873f8e2030f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2126]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Though Partha is fierce, like the one with an upraised vajra in his hand,105 if all six chariots106 are united together, we will be able to repulse him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84e8a52fc63811862d3ce07d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1069]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Among the assembled sutas, an Upakichaka43 said, “Let us swiftly kill this unchaste one, because of whom Kichaka has been slain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84e9d5e9c2e77db812c39f7c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4125]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That large army was incapable of being assailed, even by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84e9f9b09e24f75457ebc88c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5597]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing Karna mangled by my arrows, the lord of men652 will remember the words that you had spoken about peace." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84f4549f9553cb36d2a3a606> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17406, 17407]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """I think that a son of the gods has come to us.
Since I have no offspring, I am certain that the gods have given me a son.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84f97ef68ec16a9c4d4d9455> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14843]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘He himself was the seventh9 and spoke these words to Krishna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84f9a254af21f26c4f9d1188> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17122]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O mighty-armed one! The spear of the king of the gods is such that, without killing hundreds and thousands of enemies, it does not return to the hand." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/84fdfd6a7e9b81c6876e6fba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2873]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But bound in the noose of dharma, out of respect for him225 and restrained by Arjuna, I am not doing anything dreadful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8506c9d21bc6e9ceb636cc32> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5225, 5226]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O descendant of the Kuru lineage! O King! On going to Matanga’s Kedara281 and bathing there, a man obtains the fruits of one thousand cows.
On going to Mount Shri282 and touching the water on the banks of the river, one obtains a horse sacrifice and goes to the world of heaven.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/851157538ae6cdf2f8b9409c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1172]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Svayambhuva Manu167 said that riches constituted the most important component of dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85210efbc90c3e83de5f2cd5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7425]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O noble lady! Know me to be the sister of the lord of the rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85229d14bdb3acf3745c859f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8004]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Wishing to kill Karna, he began to tire him out, thinking that this was a means for bringing the quarrel to an end." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85490d671ed0b06b8c9eb53a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3970]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Agni’s son122 began to grow there, pervading the worlds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/854b7cf2185b485009a13af4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10958, 10959]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """It was as if the Destroyer had arisen.
Brahma gave the blazing sword to Shitikantha233 Rudra, the one with the bull on his banner.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85573df67aaa65eef5c5f6b6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2523]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The maharatha is the conqueror of all the gods, the daityas and the snakes." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8562bafdf484e4bfb2092059> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7977, 7978]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """A pure man gives the gods these beautiful objects.
Whatever satisfies the gods is said to be beautiful.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/857989d03a4451f77ca87001> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3144]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Indrasena44 and the others arrived there, taking good care of the chariots, having remained away for one entire year." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8579d6fa617026e53aeb76c2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7193, 7195]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘“A person who performs a funeral ceremony and primarily feeds the offerings to his friends does not please the ancestors and the gods.
If a person performs a funeral ceremony only for the purpose of getting some people together, he does not walk along the path of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8596d42c1216959ec729779e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2673]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The learned man who recites Krishna’s33 Veda to those who are noble, generous, truthful and faithful, will attain great fortune." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85ab5a5ff4652a2f6e34fcde> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1206]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is worshipped by the gods and the gandharvas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85b18a86cafa8fac4e5f43ba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2984]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "464 O Kounteya! O descendant of the Kuru lineage! Bhargava465 was pleased at this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85bd3d9da4d8e42899a9920f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[564]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is my view that this chariot cannot be vanquished, even by the gods and the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85be4d39e704bb728d252e8e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4797]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As it willed, the maned animal333 began to wander along the shores of the ocean, in Vanga, Pundra and Kerala." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85ce18e961798951d4f88ed5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4594]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! Always devoted to yoga, the great ascetic192 attained success there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85ce7c56e7a6460f242803ce> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1758]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is said that Partha satisfied Mahadeva47 himself in a battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85d66fd4f064f30764bd9a52> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7715]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is no doubt that Savyasachi confronts a great hardship and the wielder of the chakra and the club288 is fighting with all the Kurus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85fa7cbdc9870c786dca889a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17805, 17806]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """It is known that the father is alone a collection of all the gods.
But because of her affection, the mother is a collection of all mortal beings and the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85fae21496a6fe39128bfadd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14463, 14464]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Lodestone and the sun- crystal130 drink up water.
131 When one is dead, why should there be a being that approaches the gods? There is certain proof that once one is dead, there is a cessation of action.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/85fee834d63765fcb71ae9bd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11023]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In treta, adharma took away one leg, but it was still established on three feet." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8627c602a6ce6b835ae5a47b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[941]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Though it was visible to gods and men, it was divine in origin." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/86505bb170d5678f14ce809a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5302]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Under Uttara Ashadha, if one gives jars filled with barley, ghee and large quantities of fermented liquor, one obtains all the objects that one desires." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8651e146636188661b03148e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6534]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A beautiful wood was created near the bank and named Rajashrama." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8658ce8b8707cc57cce82d83> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2195]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "448 Knowledge is superior to practice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/866883490c52d03265144625> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4303, 4304]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O Partha! If he performs rites669 and sacrifices for beings, ancestors and men, then he is established in the broad ashrama of vanaprastha.
If a king protects all beings and protects his own kingdom, he is effectively consecrated in many ways and established in the ashrama of vanaprastha.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/86723f51f9f711e231949e3d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2416]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son of Parikshit! O best of the Bharata lineage! Shakra160 performed one hundred sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/869b04a71ce9db093504ea7c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10889]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O god! The gods, the danavas, the rakshasas, the yakshas, the gandharvas and the nagas and all the mobile and immobile objects in the universe were inside your body." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/86ad6a89e69349ce4c0ab1ed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[29]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Maya! Build an assembly hall in which we will see the designs1 of the gods, asuras and humans." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/86ae1ff5ee1cd753c64f2901> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2370]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They were extremely resplendent and could be seen on the vimana of the king of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/86be0b10197dc701ff049e03> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[106]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! O great king! But some21 still hung down from their hands and were seen to be like stars in the firmament." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/86c41130b589b7c3fa0d547a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2777]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son of a suta! Led by Rama53 and Krishna, when the Vrishnis advance in battle, even the mountains will not be able to withstand the force." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/86cace29a40f81d35e65bca5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7828]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Ignoring the rakshasa, he turned his head away and continued to eat." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/86e239466762a999dac4e554> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "16_Mausala" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[105]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "While Daruka15 looked on, the four horses, supreme among horses and as swift as thought, dragged it away along the turbulent surface of the ocean." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/86f05e91b8b6bf47cf197d45> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16191]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Prana and apana have the wind as their refuge and the vacant spots in the bodies have space as their refuge." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/86f45db9284ede815ee75d23> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2316]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Armour and ornaments were shattered." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/86f5c1fb4512df6209cac8a9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7235]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Attack." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/870b69c448bafa6888e032ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1710]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Sanjaya! With the bow and hump64 of this kingdom destroyed, it has lost all enterprise." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/872599b02eae49416828e42e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12799]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Though the gods beseeched them, he paid no heed to their words and refused to bear the oblations." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8743bedc5f158afcd4553da6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6747]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The clash between those two great ones was like that between the lord of the gods and Virochana’s son777 in ancient times." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/874761320cbd2cc83ef37b57> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1376, 1377]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O bull among the Bharata lineage! You have always worshipped brahmanas like Dvaipayana152 and the immensely ascetic Narada.
He153 has control over himself and always roams at the gates of all the worlds, from the world of the gods to the world of Brahma and that of gandharvas and apsaras.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/87495d5bf971578fb1fb34aa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22301]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In a short while, he reached Videha, protected by the great-souled Dharmaraja1021 Janaka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8752a0418c226828cac0cb5d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3110, 3112]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The lord of the water99 promised to be present whenever Nishadha desired and also gave a fragrant garland.
Having granted these boons, the gods returned to the world of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/875c41fed990db4ecda9f1ec> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6837]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Umbrellas were scattered around, and whisks and fans." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/87610d1ae4f5c3c589c7ed46> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2988]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was like Manmatha83 personified in his richness of beauty." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/877b498e0b04e320c8af98ba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13072]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The mother of the Vedas166 honoured his japa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/87a2e75c1a30003ab624dfab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1909]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The foremost among scorcher of enemies263 was powerfully and severely struck and quickly affixed an arrow in Duryodhana’s direction." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/87c0d52bb550e590d6af29e5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[895]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘The duel started on the first day of the month of Kartika." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/87c4a9fec8e0965425e0d05f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[391]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Krishna neutralized the words and said that would not be, and Phalguna107 neutralized the weapon with one of his own." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/87d19bbcda08df1aa24c2748> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13537]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! The illustrious one, supreme among the gods, told him,6 “There will never be another man who will be as great a warrior as you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/87dcb883e0b24a92756173fd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8916]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because of his supreme dharma, he filled heaven and earth406 and ascended above." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/87dffd58f3d9486aaf74e7d7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[370]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The immensely radiant and great archer36 rushed towards the Pandava soldiers with great force, showering hundreds of sharp arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/87e3cd1d397b06fce5b04ad3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6706]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, Dhananjaya349 was the best in fighting with every weapon." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/87e8eb63cf9eef8c08d0e0f5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11133, 11135]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Discarding the gods, collections of bones106 will be worshipped.
In places meant for the gods, in sanctuaries and in the abodes of the serpents, the earth will not be marked by abodes of the gods, but by collections of bones.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/87efab461ede99474f03efa1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[532]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "While the Pandavas looked on, in the midst of that assembly hall, in the assembly of the Kurus, he102 had spoken to Panchali." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/87feb4844dfedeb20566c64b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1979]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The host of gods does not know of my origin." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8803267694dd5f4997b722b2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3871]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that Vasishtha had been brought by Sarasvati, he110 was overcome by rage and looked for a weapon so that he might be slain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8812cc688bd56e064b09790c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16980]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "453 The sages know that everything flows from the aggregate of the five elements." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8859dfafef808c4d61193d1f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9873]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Surrounded by these and many others who were skilled in recounting stories, Pandu’s son travelled like Vasava65 surrounded by the Maruts." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/88620c2217f8eaac1e6801ca> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11446]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Chapter 1495(167) ‘Bhishma said, “The rakshasa270 had a funeral pyre constructed for the king of the cranes." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/88620f41608d151920b6d795> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15836]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chitta272 devours Sankalpa and this is the supreme knowledge." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/888aade689166f8f5b14dd9e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14930]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the king of the gods and are proud of your strength." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8896561b212ff7e5318317d0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6304]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The battle fought by the Satvata archer325 was also terrible." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/889bf32a79703e57be9122e0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11768]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "She attended to gods, guests, servants, the father-in-law and the mother-in-law." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/889c10141c230aecb1dde894> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1411]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Remembering this, he set his heart on killing Shalya, just as Indra’s younger brother103 had asked him to." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/889f585efe8487c3e6ac4ffb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6162, 6163]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O gods! Their own great and terrible deeds will bring this on them.
’ O lord of men! Having been thus addressed, the gods and the worlds took the grandfather’s leave and returned to where they had come from.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/889f7923e092399fd6ecece6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9549, 9551]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Soumadatti10 is a great archer and is the leader of a mass of rathas.
O great king! It seems to me that the king of Sindhu11 is the equal of two rathas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/88a82bf9b0d9021fb9909fef> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6697, 6698, 6699]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ ‘“The gods said, ‘O illustrious one! Since you gave him a boon, that daitya is proud of his strength.
The gods are unable to slay him.
How can he be pacified? O grandfather! The boon he obtained from you was that he couldn’t be killed by gods, asuras and rakshasas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/88ae4ba5fe5febac791dcc97> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10304]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Indra, Yama, Vaishravana169 and Varuna, the lord of the waters, are not the wind’s equal, not to speak of a tree." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/88c866dca1fe099991bbb1c9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2928]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "236 Bhishma, Drona and the learned Goutama237 heard and said, “Peace! Peace!” On hearing those terrible omens, Gandhari and the learned Vidura became miserable and told the king." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/88d1ef66bd149a18c8d62c0f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[622]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kunti, Panchali, Ulupi and Satvati47 will never do anything that goes against these people." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8907134c0fc3e2372305e796> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2394]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When the descendant of the Kuru lineage145 saw that Goutama146 had been dislodged from his place, the destroyer of enemy warriors did not pierce him, with a desire to preserve his honour." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/89161a4988a234309bf2774f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9415]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the thirty gods! I seek you as my preceptor, so that I may learn about weapons from you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8919c84475d5a688f65f86dc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4373]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘You yourself, Somadatta’s son, maharatha Karna, Ashvatthama, Shalya, Vrishasena and Kripa will be stationed three govyutis17 behind me, with a hundred thousand horses, sixty thousand chariots, fourteen thousand elephants with rent temples and twenty-one thousand armoured infantry." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/891a02fd72f63e297a1a1af1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4536, 4537]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """“Excellent.
O mighty-armed one! O son! Excellent.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/892ed0ac49322c1ec3a47ece> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 196 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9475]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If my advice, leading to the supreme welfare I have described, is not followed, it is my opinion that the lineage of the Kurus will soon be destroyed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/892f7059f339993972074add> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6859]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! It was a terrible clash, like that between the gods and the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/893f5e45e93f2dd31d706883> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1043]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’131 Vaishampayana said, ‘Having heard about the death of his son and his kin, the king132 let out long and warm sighs and became immersed in deep thoughts." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8943d4821c49a69f41f558fc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2842]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "From the five Pandavas, five sons were born to Krishna,74 handsome and skilled in the usage of all weapons—Prativindhya from Yudhishthira, Sutasoma from Vrikodara, Shrutakirti from Arjuna, Shatanika from Nakula and the mighty Shrutasena75 from Sahadeva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/894506cdcbbb60bcca8e26bf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2917]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Kanka2 said, “It is through good fortune that the cattle have been recovered and the Kurus defeated." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8945f92a11be7a34c711aef8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 166 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13538]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O brahmana! However, you must never use this suddenly." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8960b2956bcca255f42d536c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1372]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Having been thus addressed, the immensely wise Yudhishthira, Kunti’s son, instructed Sudharma,7 Dhoumya,8 the suta Sanjaya, the immensely intelligent Vidura, Kouravya Yuyutsu and all the servants and charioteers, with Indrasena9 at their head." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/89688dc4c87e9872765878ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1280]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You have the lord of the universe and the lord of the thirty gods and because of this, you are assured of victory." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8970d442e6b4740b40bad94d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1763]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There, the descendant1 of the Kuru lineage saw many divine designs that he had never seen before in the city of Nagasahrya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/89784010d7d8bc60536b59a5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 221 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13477]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In battle, you have killed a hundred danavas who were the equals of Mahisha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8980feee208bdc67bc518c2a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13810]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Yajnasena’s daughter25 is also full of fire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8987ff1943432b509c64c57b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13687]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Their forms are the equal of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/898af7f2ce9c60e22a0d6f78> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4016]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There were the lords of creation, supreme among the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8993c17b7dba43980dc75e2f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22507]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There, he stood on a single foot for one thousand divine years, thereby tormenting the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8996e79fdab8b9505b32639b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[481]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "13 In that way, those destroyers of enemies14 also honoured their father, in accordance with dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8998e150717663589bf599a9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3046]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "41 Manu’s daughter Arushi became that wise one’s42 wife and Ourva,43 of great fame, was born from her, ripping open her thighs." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/89a5f4b1070e92ccb846a9dc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9214]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His voice choked with tears, Vrisha473 worshipped the feet of the immensely radiant one who had fallen down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/89b1efc23cf64002c5d8a322> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7199, 7200]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘“Then Somaka’s preceptor565 went to the supreme world and after some time had passed, Somaka also followed him there.
He saw him566 being cooked in a terrible hell and asked, ‘O brahmana! Why are you being cooked in this hell?’ Then the preceptor, who was being cooked in terrible fires, told him, ‘O king! I sacrificed for your sake and these are the fruits of that deed.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/89cd1937b03794538c656bfa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3260]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Even the gods praise his terrible deeds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/89ce8d9f98f48e943dfa7cd7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9176]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Agneya, Varuna, Soumya, Vayavya, Vaishnava, Aindra, Pashupata, Brahma, Parameshtha, Prajapatya, Dhatu, Tvashtu, Savitu470 and all the other divine weapons—among all the men on earth, Dhananjaya alone is the one who knows them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/89d0f9d9f0837002e4f7d6a3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11785]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "234 Fire was generated from his angry eyes." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/89d64b1e2093684f9fb90972> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6242]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I have served the gods through supreme sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/89ec1b59eca956f37c807d2b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21125]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O best among men! We have heard that the gods, the ancestors, all those who surround the world of the gods and mobile and immobile objects were their sons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8a01110463157bd5d8f67bec> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4662]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Dandaniti, when administered well, sets boundaries for people and is like a mother or a father, demarcating honour for the welfare of the world." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8a09cb403d9be951a69c4579> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7655]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” On hearing this, Vaishravana was surprised and delighted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8a0b8369f7974d81da473d52> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10513, 10515]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The dwellers of heaven were seated around Dharmaraja55 and he asked them, “Why have I not attained the worlds that should have been the fruit of my asceticism? What have I not done that this should be the fruit of my actions? O dwellers of heaven! I will do that which will get me the fruits of my asceticism and open that which is now closed.
” The gods replied, “O brahmana! Hear about the debts men are undoubtedly born with—to rituals, brahmacharya56 and offspring, and these are respectively discharged through sacrifices, austerities and progeny.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8a24234a5fb6c459a9f8fd1c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4278]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘O tiger among kings! The illustrious chastiser of Paka150 gave Guha151 a javelin, for the destruction of the enemies of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8a24fd715d49efce3543c1bb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2674]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was always like Brihaspati and Ushanas359 in policy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8a51c6f733d423c640ddb522> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[506]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Charudeshna and his brother,37 Chakradeva, Satyaki, I myself, Rohini’s son,38 Samba who matches Shouri39 in battle—these are the seven atirathas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8a61359837746ff6e7217dd3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1941, 1942, 1943]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """It was like the soldiers of the immortals or the asuras and made a sound like the salty ocean.
The son of the sun269 was like the lord of the gods in his valour.
As a warrior, he was equal to the best among the thirty gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8a94d8d2e949b895684dbdbf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4908]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among men! There is no other tirtha as sacred as Prithudaka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8aa9f25598fc9c9723d0b13c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6473]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Seated astride an elephant, the invincible ratha from the mountainous regions735 slew and brought down the lord of Kratha with arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8ab811511c467c546f56e47c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9302]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bhimasena had taken a pledge to kill your sons and at the time of the second gambling match, so had Partha18 about killing Karna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8ad5fd496599f3a10efb70fa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2806]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Thereupon, the ancient maharshi summoned Dharma60 and addressed him in these words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8ad626ffb408ac3530569906> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 164 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9613]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This brahmana always wishes for a long life." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8aeee7f2da4773fc6a30e438> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[537]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They have killed rakshasas, who can assume any form at will and are the enemies of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8afcedc5b3f6b19941276222> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6391]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "And five brave sons have been born to him, like the sons of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8b21429da6be02acaa2e199f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4994, 4995, 4997, 4998]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ ‘“The gods said, ‘O supreme among gods! The gods are afflicted by Vritra.
O chief among the gods! Be our refuge now.
’ ‘“Drona said, ‘He64 addressed Vishnu, who was stationed by his side and also the best of the gods, Shakra and the others.
He spoke these appropriate words to the best of the gods, who were distressed.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8b262719735fd14cf5968a9b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2391]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then the brave Arjuna released four swift arrows, golden at the tips and with straight shafts, from Gandiva and pierced his144 horses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8b4c77656b60cb3a75a9214a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9554]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Sanjaya! What did he33 say after that? Tell me all this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8b5cd35ef9cd750fd7784d2c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4244]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "These extremely valorous ones will confront each other, like Death and the Destroyer facing each other." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8b5ffd7d91e695b2d67fad8e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6358]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He covered Duryodhana with a great shower of arrows, like the slayer of Bala329 bringing down a shower of rain on a mountain during the monsoon." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8b688059b248c83960d9be59> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4826]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O bull among men! If one bestows one’s daughter according to the brahma form of marriage,3 one obtains female servants, male servants, ornaments, fields and houses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8b691d38fed6f816da4ae36a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6394, 6396]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """What is the reason for your going against that? I have chosen this great naga for my sustenance and have chosen the time.
O king of the gods! Now that this decision has been frustrated, I cannot cause violence to another, unlike you, sporting according to your wishes and your whims.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8b73f5733ac3e5b14ad0dd51> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7985, 7988, 7989, 7994, 7996, 7998, 8000, 8008]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """I will progressively tell you what is loved by rakshasas, gods, yakshas, ancestors and humans and what ensures benefit.
Flowers with an agreeable fragrance must be offered to the gods.
O lord! The gods always desire flowers that come from trees without thorns and those that are generally white in complexion.
Mild flowers from slopes of mountains should be offered to the gods.
They please gods with their fragrance, yakshas and rakshasas with their sight and serpents with their touch.
Gods are pleased instantly.
When the gods are pleased, they always honour those who revere them.
With the exception of sallaki,242 all extractions can be given to the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8b74f90c056d25260bf69388> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 55 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3747, 3748]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Many soldiers on the side of the sons of Pandu were seen to run away, with their armour discarded and with their hair dishevelled.
The soldiers of the sons of Pandu, and even the leaders among them, were seen to be as confounded as a herd of cattle.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8b78c943b2e1eba4dfb60218> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[560]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Sanjaya! How was it rendered unsuccessful? Tell me that." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8b85cc7c4afcd429698c08aa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9447]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "33 When those warriors receive the permission to return, let Duhshasana and Vikarna34 go to receive them with a magnificent army." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8bbd50f91e01568ded751ac1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2174, 2176]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """”’”’ Chapter 1876(41) ‘“‘B ‘“‘B rahma said, “Mahat originated first and then came Ahamkara.
It is said that Ahamkara is the reason behind the creation of beings.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8bc3019ba8a05aa5d57e5a29> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5611]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Out of love for Dharmaraja, the king who was Ambika’s son371 received them and gave them riches in the prescribed way." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8bc41ce193f9c9303b3a8327> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9331]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Like the Ganga, it is incapable of being crossed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8bdda6f9e0843c70d13d61b2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[643]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”49 Hearing Vidura’s words, Yudhishthira and Gudakesha Pandava50 were delighted and applauded them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8bf6a8ade01570c314e2b0de> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9062]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O destroyer of enemies! O you who are the equal of the gods! After hearing your reply, I will then make arrangements for the marriage according to what is proper." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c00d2e395508917c25de8de> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1691]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He went to Mount Gandhamadana and practised his austerities in Badari, Gokarna, Pushkararanya108 and the slopes of the Himalayas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c1750bf1a312f8d087e271c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15063]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Like a boat filled with gems on the edge of the ocean, riding on the back of a shark26 and destroyed, you will see the soldiers in your army destroyed and freed27 by the sons of Pandu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c20f87ba27575bf7547c969> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6529]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He taught him330 the four parts of Dhanur Veda331 and the usage of many different kinds of weapons, including all the secrets associated with them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c2d703ed1d795af58e8f074> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[809]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Arya23 always praised brave Sahadeva because of his honoured reputation, his conduct and his virtuous nature." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c35b68c129fab4a976b1ac5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14960]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the gods don’t know me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c3ad8f5a9748f0ccf4e8cf5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3156]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Shalya! Know that I will not be frightened, even if Vaivasvata413 with his staff, Varuna with his noose, the lord of riches414 with his club, Vasava with his vajra, or any other assassin advances against me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c3c72c6ad5714400d09fb44> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6214, 6215]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """They provide supreme oblations for the gods.
Svaha and vashatkara are always established in cows.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c4a244fa7c39f639777689b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2690]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Terrible rakshasas always live in the passes of mountains and in uneven regions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c4ae9a6b70763b275b69983> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24067]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In the sutras1202 of the Vedas, I will lay down that whatever share someone has given me at this great sacrifice will be proportionate to the share that he receives at those sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c679657e233aa42a212d7ac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[593]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You have spoken of me as the beloved of the king of the gods, deserving of happiness, and as one who will never be a widow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c6ac62716775292fa0001e1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3156]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Although Vidarbha’s daughter108 looked on, he decided that the time for setting a stake had come." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c8a5eed56c56cfd832011f7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4673]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I gave them also handsome horses with single hooves and the gods then obtained their rightful shares." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8c92095f621efe60ac25a3dc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15107]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With his arrows, the atiratha34 slew in battle Shibis, the foremost among Ikshvakus, Trigartas and Saindhavas, as soon as they came within range." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8cab561a6f1413db8751e675> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[667]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There are many sacred countries there, where Shankara11 is worshipped." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8cb6b9b51a6de638aa8c3cfd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1432]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This103 generates knowledge in brahmanas and confers them with intelligence." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8cbb4d67dd4c6d928c5cc9c7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9523]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Even the gods are confused in trying to follow his footsteps." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8cbe641a3cd85ef2b6658cc8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1455]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Since he does not know that Krishna is always everywhere, this Shishupala is only a child14 and utters these words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8cd2bbc7662fa9275c0ea32f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3539]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king of the gods can also transform himself into the form of the wind." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8ce37644fbe14e0e252e31b6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7528]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Father killed the son and the son killed the father." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8cec8165404db2bd58c82c12> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10261]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are full of jnana and vijnana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8cefb6cc9eb9cdd4783eb4fa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1668]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O charioteer! Advance slowly there and protect the rear." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8cf19dddd5e072e16e37577c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2733, 2734]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """His famous maharatha45 son Brihadratha was instated in the kingdom of Magadha.
Others46 were Pratyagraha and Kushamba, also known as Manivahana and Macchilla, and Yadu, powerful kings invincible in battle.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8cf32a5734094375714aea16> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2998]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘The grandfather23 had another son named Manu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8d0662a3bf1972a2f1848f45> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2387]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With all the valour in his arms, the courageous descendant of the Kuru lineage276 struck at his head with the sharp sword, one that even mountains could not resist." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8d20cdafcbe0c5cf7f2dd9fe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[243, 244, 245]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O rajarshi! These pure rajarshis, of great fame and renown, waited upon Vaivasvata Yama in his sabha.
There were Agastya, Matanga, Kala,92 Mrityu,93 performers of sacrifices, Siddhas, those whose bodies are based on yoga, those with fire in their mouths,94 the ancestors—those who live on froth, those who live on vapours, those who receive oblations, those who seat themselves on kusa grass and those others who have bodies.
95 Free from disease and in embodied form, the wheel of time, the illustrious conveyor of sacrificial offerings,96 men who performed evil deeds, those who died during the winter solstice, those of Yama’s officers appointed to reckon time, shimshapa97 and palasha98 trees, kasha,99 kusha100 and other trees and plants worshipped Dharmaraja.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8d30d798136409d60a27e463> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6931]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Suyodhana26 replied, “I wish for your eternal friendship." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8d3c1dee5cd410124c9cffba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[36, 37]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """2 When Ambika’s son3 went out on a pleasure trip, the V immensely energetic king of the Kurus, Yudhishthira, gave him every object of pleasure.
As in earlier times, cooks, chefs4 and confectioners served King Yudhishthira.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8d4873f479009c8cd176e951> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6944]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O brahmana! O son! In the form of varuni, the lord and god150 originally accepted Bhrigu and Kavi." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8d4e3e1e81fb77d07f29ce2a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11475]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O sage! You know about the celestial stories of men, serpents and rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8d578badf76f9e89db09deed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6711]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Virata, Drupada and Yajnasena’s son228 pierced him with five each." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8d5a6fc647620e4ab7920294> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8739]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘With great force, he dashed at the rakshasa, to engage him in a bout of wrestling." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8d7aaa051792b533bd5df758> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12886]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The illustrious one also saw that Varuna’s abode241 was red." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8d92e2a5097fbf9df8754d0c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13066]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On hearing this great sound, the splendid army of the gods lost its senses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8dab442042349ba704c4a905> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[974]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The Pandava45 and his brothers then went to the freed kings46 and in accordance with age, showed them homage and paid their respects." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8dad962294a082a19cfe1e43> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6258]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bestow children on her." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8db012eab7cfd3b5eb114861> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1148]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But because of his sacrifice, he surpassed the king of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8dc3341c47a2dea77f1c41b0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17451]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“O lord! O lord of the gods! I know who you are." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8dcd73b901cdbd5544cbcb0b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[700]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O valorous one! O great king! Such is the one whom the powerful Kukuras, Andhakas and Vrishnis64 ignored, because that was the right policy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8de2387c765b25cfa25e7f7e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 110 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9161, 9165, 9174]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! He conducts himself like the divine rishis and the rajarshis.
If a person eats only one meal a day, that too on every twenty-eighth day, if he does this for an entire year and if he conquers his soul and conquers his senses, he obtains the pervasive fruits that lead to a conduct like that of the divine rishis.
If a person eats only one meal a day, that too on every twenty-ninth day and if he devotes himself to a vow of truth for an entire year, he obtains divine and auspicious worlds where he is worshipped by divine rishis and rajarshis.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8dfb9a3ac7cd67cfa64ca5a8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2518]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that they were distressed, Madri’s powerful son49 restrained them with thousands of arrows in the battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e04f2cd6630dee9e90795ee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9144, 9145]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Sankarshana’s12 younger brother, the handsome and immensely intelligent Janardana, was made Arjuna’s guide and the controller of his horses.
‘On seeing that a great battle was imminent, the wielder of the plough13 entered King Pandava’s residence, in the company of Akrura and the others, Gada, Samba, Ulmuka and so on, with Rukmini’s son14 and Akrura’s son led by Charudeshna.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e0d1f93f2a19c583dd1aba1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25555]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Chapter 1667(339) rahma said, “O son! Hear about the eternal and undecaying Purusha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e1e150159295992b37f2549> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3224]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 709(46): 17 shlokas Chapter 710(47): 103 shlokas Chapter 711(48): 47 shlokas Chapter 712(49): 45 shlokas Chapter 713(50): 61 shlokas Chapter 714(51): 19 shlokas Chapter 715(52): 16 shlokas Chapter 716(53): 19 shlokas Chapter 717(54): 66 shlokas Chapter 718(55): 16 shlokas Chapter 719(56): 60 shlokas Chapter 720(57): 29 shlokas Chapter 721(58): 30 shlokas Chapter 722(59): 23 shlokas Chapter 723(60): 29 shlokas Chapter 724(61): 18 shlokas Chapter 725(62): 31 shlokas Chapter 726(63): 16 shlokas Chapter 727(64): 15 shlokas Chapter 728(65): 9 shlokas Chapter 729(66): 15 shlokas Chapter 730(67): 21 shlokas Chapter 731(68): 14 shlokas Chapter 732(69): 7 shlokas Yana means moving or journey as a verb and conveyance as a noun." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e1fae1fbd4163e63b296a97> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6384]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "These kings are being driven away, afflicted by their fear of Bhimasena." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e211caf25dc6d68f2bfcad3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[732]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The country near Krouncha is Kushala, while that near Vamana20 is Manonuga." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e3dfe0431edd41c03084ea2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12110]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The supreme among the gods sought Sharva’s1420 favours." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e4367a2949b99dea5ef6b60> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13847, 13848]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """I have thus recounted the four varnas among all the gods.
If a person gets up in the morning and recites the names of the gods, he is freed from all sins, ‘Y regardless of whether they have been committed by him or by others.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e4696d402ac2cd454d7cfeb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10269]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When Vasudeva and Dhananjaya were thus happily seated together, like the two Ashvins12 in heaven, a brahmana arrived." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e64e9290dc082aed5fcef3c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1506]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Slain, he fell down on the ground from his chariot, like a stellar body dropping down from the sky." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e65baf68e85c805d9f88ffd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2504]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You will kill in battle those parts of the gods, danavas and rakshasas that have been born on earth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e665270247a73efb39ee8f6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8010]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Aguru244 is the best among extractions and is desired by yakshas, rakshasas and serpents." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e66c4f62214408631c05701> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5930]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Kouravya! Establish76 your sons and I will establish the others." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8e82102008d19942c569e5a9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9007]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘There remained a mighty-armed and broad-chested rakshasa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8ea2b23fa1cb8b3ab78b420b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 289 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17233]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O brahmana! What purpose will boons serve me?” The brahmana said, “O fortunate one! O one with the sweet smiles! If you do not wish for a boon from me, accept this mantra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8eb849496a910592e0e52f97> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[100, 102]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘Noticing the vile stench, he spoke to the messenger of the gods.
What place of the gods is this? I wish to know that.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8ecbb232991094a6c50aaa68> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11199, 11201]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! In that supreme house, Goutama255 found pleasure with her.
He lived in Shabara’s256 prosperous house throughout the monsoon.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8eceede9ae85d76e1b91d292> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[283]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "J Behold Subhadra’s unvanquished son with the moon." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8edd468dc186435cb5107578> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4134]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! O Indra among kings! O descendant of the Bharata lineage! They were143 Shankukarna, Nikumbha, Padma, Kumuda, Ananta, Dvadashabhuja, Krishna, Upakrishna, Dronashrava, Kapskandha, Kanchanaksha, Jalamdhama, Akshasamtarjana, Kunadika, Tamobhrakrit, Ekaksha, Dvadashaksha, the lord Ekajata, Sahasrabahu, Vikata, Vyaghraksha, Kshitikampana, Punyanama, Sunama, Suvaktra, Priyadarshana, Parishruta, Kokanada, Priyamalyanulepana, Ajodira, Gajashira, Skandhaksha, Shatalochana, Jvalajihva, Karala, Sitakesha, Jati, Hari, Chaturdamshtra, Ashtajihva, Meghanada, Prithushrava, Vidyutaksha, Dhanurvaktra, Jathara, Marutashana, Udaraksha, Jhashaksha, Vajranama, Vasuprabha, Samudravega, Shailakampi, Putramesha, Pravaha, Nanda, Upanandaka, Dhumra, Shveta, Kalinga, Siddhartha, Varada, Priyaka, Nanda, the powerful Gonanda, Ananda, Pramoda, Svastika, Dhruvaka, Kshemavapa, Sujata, Siddha, Govraja, Kanakapida, the lord of great companions, Gayana, Hasana, Bana, the valiant Khadga, Vaitali, Atitali, Katika, Vatika, Hamsaja, Pankadigdhanga, Samudronmada, Ranotkata, Prahasa, Shvetashirsha, Nandaka, Kalakantha, Prabhasa, Kumbhabhandaka, Kalakaksha, Sita, Bhutalonmatha, Yajnavaha, Pravaha, Devayaji, Somapa, Sajala, Mahateja, Krathakratha, Tuhana, Tuhana,144 the valiant Chitradeva, Madhura, Suprasada, the immensely strong Kiriti, Vasana, Madhuvarna, Kalashodara, Ghamanta, Manmathakara, the valiant Suchivakrta, Shvetavaktra, Suvaktra, Charuvaktra, Pandura, Dandabahu, Subahu, Raja, Kokila, Achala, Kanakaksha, the lord Balanamayika, Samcharaka, Kokanada, Gridhravaktra, Jambuka, Lohashvavaktra, Jathara, Kumbhavaktra, Kundaka, Madgugriva, Krishnouja, Hamsavaktra, Chandrabha, Panikurma, Shambuka, Shakavaktra and Kundaka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8edd8d70d40509d183fefd70> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6296]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O king! On hearing these words, the great king Bhagiratha went to Mount Kailasa and satisfied Shankara443 through austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8ef836e2d4f70d32c0b93299> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[324]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kshatta19 and King Yudhishthira entered Dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8f230d07f3c6bb977810ba80> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2539]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "177 Pure and controlled, he will offer oblations into the fire twice a day." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8f235dd0b206cfb3e6b85330> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2522]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Even Death will not be able to escape, if you assault him with this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8f2aee14e604377b493f803b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6670, 6671]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O lord of the thirty gods! Know from these and the others that I have spoken about, to detect wicked men, since nature is always superior.
O supreme among the gods! I have described the knowledge of evil ones.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8f3e4b04074fb70620214427> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[726, 728]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Rathas were killed by rathas and mad elephants by other mad elephants.
Rathas were destroyed by supreme rathas, elephants by horse riders and foot soldiers.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8f4c979db2dd202c06560f51> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1826]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Shattered, it fell down, and Madhava13 was confused." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8f5b22e935b0d9d0cbce9910> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1980]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Through worshipping five, one obtains fame in this world—gods, ancestors, men, mendicants and guests." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8f6ca76ef21b0dc4f34c7ef3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[166]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Its wishes having been satisfied, it joined its hands in salutation and addressed Rama." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8f7d18f9508fdcbafff3fc43> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2174]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having again assumed his peaceful form, the great soul assured the scared Arjuna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8f83e5ddddde1f67a914f211> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10323]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bhutapati’s387 place had an extremely terrible appearance." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8f856540257d089bc0013941> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3545]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Duryodhana! O son!55 When you see Keshava with the conch shell, chakra and club in his hands, the terrible archer Arjuna grasping his weapons, and the two eternal and great- souled Krishnas56 stationed on a single chariot, you will then remember my words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8f932fac23f0a8a798d9cf2a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[320]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Shakuni entered dvapara17 and Dhrishtadyumna the fire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8fa6be2bbcc7e7df0d35b3cb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3754]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Nahusha protected the ancestors, gods, rishis, Brahmanas, gandharvas, uragas132 and rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8fbfdf980984e49e34ff4ba6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[901]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that the best of the Kuru lineage75 had withdrawn, they began to weep." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/8fe585f95bd06771dca6ece1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14202, 14203, 14204]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Because he was established in austerities and because his dharma did not decay, he88 could see the one with the universal form.
Having beheld the lord of the gods, he was delighted in his speech, his mind, his intelligence and his body.
Having beheld the origin of the universe, Narayana worshipped the one who wore a garland of berries89 and was the recipient of supreme radiance.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9001c7f8e87d32f0e05f912b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5304, 5305, 5306, 5307, 5308]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Under Shravana, by giving blankets and thick cloth, one roams around the worlds on white vehicles.
Under Dhanishtha, if a person is controlled and gives a vehicle yoked to bulls and garments with fine strands, immediately after death, he obtains a kingdom.
Under Shatabhisha, if one gives fragrances, aloe and sandalwood, after death, one obtains a world with apsaras and eternal fragrances.
Under Purva Bhadrapada, if a person gives rajamasha,39 he is happy after death and obtains all kinds of food and fruits.
Under Uttara, if a person gives goat meat, he pleases the ancestors and obtains the infinite after death.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/90296f0542979c49265484bc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18399]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, the deer again joined its hands in salutation and entreated Satya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/90402d0b19d8d9491bc424e3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10747]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lord of the gods happily granted this boon." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/905c1bd9a595064e5ced97c4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9896]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I certainly suffer because of my terrible fear of Vaivasvata." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/90630cbc8fb09c04e3e58130> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1760]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But Arjuna isn’t worth one kala48 of me or Duryodhana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/90829e9ec95e125b5dfcc431> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3399, 3400]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """If he is enraged, the great ascetic is capable of creating other gods.
”59 Hearing his words, all the gods were frightened.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/90af37c3b40eeec24762d77f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1596]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Vinata’s son tore them into pieces with his wings, talons and sharp beak, like the wrathful and enemy- destroying Pinaki99 at the end of a yuga." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/90bd77ea3a168fadb657c708> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2374]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowledge is the attribute of sannyasa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/90d8e87ca4697046d3e96b4f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2728]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the origin of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/90dc9ed0b180ba9d0e69637a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10057]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rukmini’s son3 and Samba, always invincible in battle, were intoxicated and wore divine garlands and garments, sporting themselves like the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/90e7ec5007d2811e819a41b4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3132]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "From that group62 came Samundrasena, renowned all over the earth, right up to the shores of the ocean, for his learning in dharma and artha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/90eaec63ee634f47ce9c3493> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10455]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Janardana let fly his chakra, radiant with its own energy, and small creatures, danavas and nishacharas49 were instantly cut down in hundreds and hurled into the fire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/90f05ca84d8c1bdadb2d5e34> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5828]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Svayambhu821 created dharma for the power of beings." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/90f16623bd5531bfad9497a3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8271]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Then the immensely radiant Vivasvat60 said to the best of sages, ‘O maharshi! You are welcome." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/910d2120a166770eeb14b7fd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3998]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Somadatta’s son161 hurled a gold-shafted and giant lance at him and it was like a serpent." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/91123edbd6f9cee0aaadbb7d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1785]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O best of the snakes! O immensely radiant lord! From there, I heard the sorrowful gods speak to the grandfather." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/911331d2cdb56182bba72cbf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7104]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Lamb is said to satisfy for three months and rabbit meat for four months." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/91162a410a78e781a09a25c8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2289]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O immensely wise one! The ancient battle between Arjuna, supreme among warriors and unvanquished in battle, and Bhava258 was unparalleled and extraordinary and made one’s hair stand up." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/912c77a021bd1c0ae155d9f9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6540, 6541, 6542]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """They were born from gods.
They were the equals of the gods.
They were like the gods in their beauty.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/91316175f40a6bb82ac62c9c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7367]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If a person eats what is left after gods, ancestors, servants and guests have eaten, he is said to be a person who only eats leftovers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9134e1cb818e7ea2b5e1d928> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6631]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O king! Having promised this, he485 told Varuna, ‘As a bride price, give me one thousand swift and white horses, each with one black ear." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/913bfd7370d1ff8ab7ee63f9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19441]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This was the foremost among the gods, who possessed many forms, terrible and amiable." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/915141408cc915ed4a52b9a3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6739, 6740]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """When he496 was worshipped by the supreme rishis, Pandu’s son derived supreme delight.
Accompanied by Krishna497 and with his younger brothers, he bathed his limbs in those tirthas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/915a204c8323221319043230> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6691]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In great wrath, he rushed towards Kartavirya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/915f8789a47782966f2086a2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[610, 612]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """” Thus addressed by the Ashvins, he14 regained his sight.
He15 was very pleased with him and told him he would obtain good fortune as the Ashvins had promised.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/918922bc3f9e203e666e0f6c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20577, 20600]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Prakriti is without attributes or taints, but she enters inside something813 that possesses attributes.
He is born as inferior species, as human, or in the world of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/919a240aa2cee8da72b197fa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9110]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "After consecrating Bhishma, the destroyer of enemy forces, as the general, he8 made the foremost of brahmanas recite and gave them a lot of cattle and gold." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/91acb2de3d870052c8e1f378> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13590]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowledge is above intelligence and the supreme215 is above knowledge." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/91d94fb6e0cbccd6520ee7c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1324, 1325]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘Seeing the state of her sons, Kadru began to praise Shakra46 in these words.
“O lord of the gods! I bow before you.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/91dfa3420f342fdd7c779809> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1187]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Her complexion is like that of Gouri87 personified." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9201f1e4f270c96f85a5b316> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4005]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Shakra’s bow112 sparkles in the sky in many hues and we do not know what it is." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9213ecf478af46b3d0457774> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14168, 14170]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O son!85 Because of those austerities, he became like Brahma.
He is supremely difficult to look at and is the lord of all the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/923ceadf99ddeb9cd3ff46c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[176]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Narada said, “A king who is always engaged in the protection of the four varnas63 passes his time happily here and attains Shakra’s world." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/924447c0cbcc81bfd7e96c7f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8997, 8998]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The immensely powerful one pierced the bodies of the rakshasas with his arrows and they roared, while roaming around in the sky and on the ground.
A great shower of blood rained down on the immensely strong one, flowing from the bodies of the rakshasas in every direction.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/925a6c0449a210989200c92c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13930]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among the gods! You should not be tormented." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/926d681ec8b16b1cdef222bd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[359]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The great sage Vyasa, of vast wisdom, composed this in 186 chapters94 and 6696 shlokas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9276267200ff3886f4add80e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[242]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O son! Pure rajarshis and unblemished brahmarshis78 happily attend upon Yama Vaivasvata there—Yayati, Nahusha, Puru, Mandhata, Somaka, Nriga, Trasadasyu, Turaya, Kritavirya, Shrutashrava, Aripranuda, Susimha, Kritavega, Kriti, Nimi, Pratardana, Shibi, Matysa, Prithavaksha, Brihadratha, Aida, Marutta, Kushika, Samkashya, Samkriti, Bhava, Chaturashva, Sadashvormi, the king Kartavirya, Bharata, Suratha, Sunitha, Nala from Nishadha,79 Divodasa, Sumana, Ambarisha, Bhagiratha, Vyashva, Sadashva, Vadhryashva, Panchahasta, Prithushrava, Rushadgu, Vrishasena, the immensely powerful Kshupa, Rushadashva, Vasumana, Purukutsa, Dhvaji, Rathi, Arshtishena, Dilipa, the great-souled Ushinara, Oushinara, Pundarika, Sharyati, Sharabha, Shuchi, Anga, Arishta, Vena, Duhshanta, Sanjaya, Jaya, Bhangasvari, Sunitha, Nishadha,80 Tvishiratha, Karandhama, Bahlika,81 Sudyumna, the powerful Madhu, Kapotaroma, Trinaka, Sahadeva, Arjuna, Dasharathi Rama,82 Lakshmana, Pratardana, Alarka, Kakshasena, Gaya, Gourashva, Jamadagni Rama,83 Nabhaga, Sagara, Bhuridyumna, Mahashva, Prithvashva, Janaka, the king Vainya, Varishena, Puraja, Janamejaya, Brahmadatta, Trigarta, King Uparichara, Indradyumna, Bhimajanu, Gaya, Prishtha, the unblemished Naya, Padma, Muchukunda, Bhuridyumna, Prasenajit, Arishtanemi, Pradyumna, Prithagashva, Ajaka, the one hundred kings from Matsya,84 the hundred Nipas,85 the hundred Hayas,86 the one hundred Dhritarashtras,87 the eighty Janamejayas,88 the one hundred Brahmadattas,89 the one hundred fighting Iris,90 the rajarshi Shantanu, your father Pandu, Ushadgava, Shataratha, Devaraja, Jayadratha, the rajarshi Vrishadarbhi, Dhaman and his ministers and, in addition, thousands of Shashabindus91 who departed after performing many great horse sacrifices, with copious donations." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/92878ef58aeb2808391236f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24895]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having performed rites in honour of the gods, he thereafter got ready to perform rites in honour of the ancestors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/92c66002d742abb1c12a131b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3557]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But he is not a sixteenth part59 of the great- souled Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/92ccf2a70ebeca59e07f015f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5394]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the warriors made out of flesh and blood, and even the gods, are incapable of defeating him in a battle, even if they were to unite." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/92d2c089e1f20b9f2bb9ed3b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15469]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With Kakutstha79 gone, Sita will be in my powers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/92f208bf555e295e595cb00d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5312]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With four arrows, he despatched his252 swift horses to Yama’s abode." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/93054c5ca3da021a7670d1b7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6125]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They were like supreme gods and asuras693 in ancient times." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9312f4174500733be8811e11> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 175 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12119]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "54 That lord and upholder of all beings created Akasha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/931745b9652e0b1b59793735> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5555]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Earlier, this was the path followed by the gods, when they killed the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/934eb5067af6161990f3f1cf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 167 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13660, 13663]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """My preceptor had always known that I, Vasava’s son, would have given up everything out of affection for him—sons, brothers, fathers, wives, and even life itself.
He was a brahmana.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9354f75e1738f332d4bc5bf9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2619]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” The suta was in his197 servitude, but was scared of the wrath of Drupada’s daughter." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9364c1815c86cf289a600fa3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3772]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With a white umbrella held aloft his head, Yudhishthira looked lustrous, like the king of the stars269 on the night of the full moon." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/936d36d4c8ce60a9f105f377> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25807]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The virtuous one approached him and the serpent asked, ‘O fortunate one! I hope you have been attentive in tending to the gods and the guests, as used to be the case when I was here." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9376707e66da201f374a4737> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16761]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Delusion, distraction, lassitude, sleep and lack of exertion—whenever these are indulged in, that is known to be the quality of tamas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/937a6f223cd78cd46a16b0fd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1811]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the gods! Please grant him a favour and pacify the fever in his mind." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/938616a1cec625b58e62e297> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[392]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The brave and powerful king of the gods began to think about this in silence." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/938b3d5d1279d74b02a5c83b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6111]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kalmashapada’s296 wife did this act so as to please her husband." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/939d09917d26a539281699ad> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1941, 1944]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """8 Conquer the five.
Poison kills one.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/93bb1cb786f3190ace30e694> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5609]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Resorting to his valour, the great-minded656 son of Dhritarashtra, evil-souled and evil in his intelligence, always disregarded us." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/93bcb4752437882d2c5fecca> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10977]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! It was like that between Jambha163 and Vasava in ancient times." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/93c914fb6a8bc934cd104507> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[806]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The seven rishis94 will bear me and all the brahmarshis." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/93d94815b4002e07c53b886e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6862]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He had a club in his hand and his 100 brothers circled him, with weapons raised, looking like Purandara15 of ancient times, surrounded by the gods at the time of doing battle and destroying the danavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/93ef3caa42b06416f60c8971> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3197]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I am the oblations that are offered to gods in sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/93f080797aa06b7365cfa144> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8149]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” The king said, “O brahmana! I have understood the purport of your words, about it being emaciated and also not emaciated1093 and also about the difficulty of obtaining." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/93f23173e0ec48287dfc9304> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2644]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Learn the music that is only known to the gods and is unknown in the world of men." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/93f5c96a1355ba83852a572f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2801]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! In that battle, the violent Shankha42 attacked Somadatta’s son43, who was also a violent warrior." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/93fbf3152023430939d8c79c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[775]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! It was like that between the gods and the asuras in earlier times." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/94020a26ece9edd34ce763ff> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9822]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If any one of them set eyes on Droupadi when she was lying with any one of the others, he would retire to the forest and live the life of a brahmachari53 for twelve years." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9402ca2ddc374475f550081f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6577]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Yama, Vaishravana752 and Varuna were also with Arjuna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/94097067f2a8b06ed5d1bd1d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[81]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Thus did he10 speak about Karna, supreme among warriors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9424feee7e39e026e2636cf7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3206]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The suta left the horses and the excellent chariot there and also the daughter Indrasena113 and the son Indrasena." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/943863cfcd484f07e83d9e46> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8048]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Others673 carried the Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9438a49bb609f4b2615cd600> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8884]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Through my preceptor’s grace, I have become skilled in the use of brahma and paurandara39 weapons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/943f27e3de2c269a10031c12> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7634]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "While the soldiers of the Pandus were routed, the one with the thousand rays394 began to set." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/944c62e6e5b6492122708c10> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[330]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All of them became gods and yakshas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9454ea15aaa10d8951bf5773> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7236]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He can topple the gods from heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9459e9548c5ebc3bca82bd7b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4498]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There, the gods and their lord forsake one whose merit has been diminished." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9478c4a138da3d4f5b48b07a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9707, 9710, 9711, 9712, 9713]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """18 Charanas19 sung their praises in auspicious songs that wished them victory.
They rose into the sky and went to the habitation of the gods.
Knowing that they were coming and aware of the boon that they had obtained from the illustrious one, the gods fled heaven20 and went to Brahma’s world.
With their terrible valour, they conquered Indra’s world and defeated masses of yakshas21 and rakshas22 and beings that frequent the sky.
The two great asuras then vanquished the nagas23 who dwell in the interior regions of the earth, all those who live in the oceans and all the mleccha24 races.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/94882b8a6d1345f4e19319c2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[62]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O gods! I am repeatedly tormented by this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/94b41a53c81e41817db97120> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3767]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "560 ‘“Preservation, increase and destruction were three categories that were the consequence of chastisement." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/94b657e20deca28a87cd5a6f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11819]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In kali yuga, he will be on earth in the form of adharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/94b6e4be628e0428d1bc7b37> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[485]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He can absolve you from all sins except those committed against Mahadeva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/94ba4b090bf41a1e11b6982c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12710]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "207 He created Shiva from his navel, Indra from his strength, Vayu and Agni from his breath of life, the two accents208 from his two arms, the universe and all the beings." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/94c80a884519ebc442eb8e1d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9668, 9669, 9672]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘“On seeing the terrible power of their austerities, the gods were frightened.
The gods created various obstacles to prevent them from attaining their vows.
Then the gods used the power of Maya14 on the two great- souls, wherein their sisters, mothers, wives and relatives, trembling and frightened, were oppressed by a rakshasa15 who chased them with a spear.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/94d84904520a24b99f1115e3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2760]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "For the sake of the meat of the deer, they wielded their bows and always made that race decay51—the king52 towards the east, Bhimasena towards the south, the twins towards the west and also towards the north." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/94f3c19ca7fb146ed7b354ed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2383]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Once they had obtained their objective and got the supreme amrita, the gods went to Prajapati155 with their brother156 leading the way." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9500257b12dc159665579902> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7342]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O extremely radiant king! Slain, they fell down on the ground from their chariots." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/95060a081da0d57764a84cae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[249]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "After touching the waters of the Ganga and the wind, the one with dharma in his soul resorted to yoga and pranayama, controlled his senses and lived on air, worshipping Divakara37 with offerings of flowers and fireless oblations." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9508b21f39eeef8497527bce> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3149]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having possessed Nala, he went to Pushkara105 and told him, ‘Come and play dice with Nala." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/950dfe019b9a76a47154b699> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6724]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "After some time, Drona again asked, “Can you see the tree? Can you see me? Can you see your brothers?” In reply to each question, Kounteya351 answered, one after the other: “I can see the large tree." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/95148f48e3beb451a0beaf7c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9082]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O king! At this time, on witnessing Karna’s valour, he422 drew his bow back up to his ears and dispatched Karna’s four horses to the land of the dead with four supreme arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9517a7575afedc381ebe00cc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1879]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Uttara said, “I have heard ten names of Partha56 earlier." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/952e1dc3c69463ccbd31622e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5100]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Aditya, Varuna, Vishnu, Brahma, Soma, Hutashana24 and the illustrious wielder of the trident25 find delight in a person who gives away land." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/954349c02e1818c152f7657e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "17_Mahaprasthanika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9, 13]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """J Chapter 1988(1) anamejaya asked, ‘On hearing about the duel with the clubs in the lineage of the Vrishnis and the Andhakas and on hearing that Krishna had ascended to heaven, what did the Pandavas do?’ Vaishampayana replied, ‘Hearing about the great carnage caused among the Vrishnis, King Kourava made up his mind to give up his life and spoke these words to Arjuna.
” Thus addressed, Kounteya1 only uttered the words, “Time! Time!” He agreed with the words his valiant elder brother had spoken.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9549209278a56480164a4a1e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9834]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The grandfather216 himself arrived, together with all the lokapalas, and the illustrious Mahadeva, with all his companions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/955b93cd6da4e265731aeca5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5157]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In battle, he is like the king of the gods himself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9574b8b5f58b203f9028871c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1334]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When Dasharha134 had left, Dhrishtadyumna, the son of Prishata,135 took Droupadi’s sons with him and left for his own city." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9581847da7c1af218e17caf3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1705]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son!62 On beholding my affection for my son, Kshatta63 had spoken to me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9590cf2d1083f05293488959> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5361]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! This is what Maya762 had said and that is the way it is." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/95a11bbaf33eeda94f870d0a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14461, 14462]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Because of that, the gods are afraid of him, even now.
In ancient times, the brave asuras had three cities in the sky.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/95a3101d518585c164263772> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2847]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that the sons and grandsons of the kings were silent, Dhritarashtra’s son223 smiled and spoke these words to the daughter of the king of Panchala, “O Yajnaseni! Let the question now be placed before the immensely powerful Bhima, Arjuna, Sahadeva and your husband Nakula." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/95a3d7b20bd80017ffbaf7fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23464]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They told him, ‘You have opted for the side of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/95f32e77d9cc13ecfdf39a17> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4607]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In this connection, Angiras’s son703 himself has sung two shlokas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/960b8701ffb27873f8634144> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14547]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” O king! The Pandavas, learned in dharma, swiftly left, together with the brahmanas who lived with them, and followed by Indrasena2 and the other servants." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/960c88982fea48c09ef9f55f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2346]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As they proceeded, they heard all the beings praise Phalguna’s5 qualities and Keshava’s6 affection towards the illustrious Arjuna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/96224c0234b64234cdd597eb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11178]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! On seeing that terrible arrow, the gods, the gandharvas and men spoke these words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9647252cdfdf6aa6f7ae6336> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3117]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Partha told Parshata, the commander of the army, ‘The vyuha75 known by the name of Krouncharuna is the destroyer of all enemies." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/964b7237af31f0b8a4edd9e1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[308]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among brahmanas! Why will they endeavour for my good? Krishna31 was in her season and was clad in a single garment." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/96598d6c5340ff673ef97ae9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2431]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When Susharma had been killed in the battle, he used sharp arrows to dispatch forty- three of his46 maharatha sons to Yama’s eternal abode." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/966390be78e3d05ed9f97279> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12280, 12292]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The gods, famous for their souls, have spoken about many kinds of taste.
Know them to be shadaja, rishabha, gandhara, madhyama, panchama, dhaivata and nishadaka.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/966a1f8af1b0e521acc0de0b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[893]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O sweet-smiling one! With the aid of Rama48 and Krishna, we are invincible in battle even with the slayer of Vritra,49 not to speak of Dhritarashtra’s sons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/966d9ea17617c16c7d2d4d04> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10266]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘While this was going on, the descendants of Kuru and Dasharha10 went to a beautiful region that was not far off." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9678d3c72b1548fc70c099ba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1864, 1867]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Vatadhana27 brahmanas, possessing the wealth of cattle, stood at the gate in groups of one hundred.
In Varuna’s brass pots, the ocean brought him ambrosia30 that was better than the one brought for Shakra by the wives of the immortals.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/96840a28bf7e8720221b8fee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10090, 10091]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘Those tigers among men, the Vrishni and Andhaka maharathas14 ascended their thrones, decorated with gold, covered with excellent cushions and adorned with gems and corals, with the radiance of blazing fires, like a hundred fires on their sacrificial altars.
When they were seated like an assembly of gods, the presiding officer and his companions told them about Jishnu’s15 conduct.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9684c23287c93ccd2c10de04> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6992]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because of this, Nahusha’s son230 obtained status in this world and the next." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/968b40f334e6788f2ea4452f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2771]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those two sons of the gods are maharathas and cannot be repulsed in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/96978d7f48bdfcef6177a920> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3901]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This night will give way to an excellent morning that will bring Vijaya’s41 victory." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/969e068ece9905e4389dd901> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[349]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king of Gandhara78 is united with his own army, which comes from Sindhu, Kamboja, Vanayu, Bahlika and other mountainous and unnamed regions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/96d30ddc8d2f89a07a58cf11> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[152]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O Sanjaya! I had no hope of victory when I heard that Dharma had appeared before Dharmaraja43 in the disguise of a yaksha and posed him questions that were correctly answered." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/96d7037c6e4117dc918ab647> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8672]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When the rakshasas and Bhimasena’s son1 had left, and they were without Bhimasena, who had gone to roam around as he willed, a rakshasa abducted Dharmaraja, the twins and Krishna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/96ed1d76f6d2a2f5fbde3b0d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8641]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "78 Let the king and Vidura speak." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/96f520d97762222c3946f3fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3707]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He then remembered the way he had protected Ruchi." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/96f94fcaf02539134f86a059> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2374, 2378]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The red and red-tinged umbrellas of the gods could be seen while they stood there, and their garments, garlands and fans.
These were decorated with many gems and were colourful and wonderful, brought by the supreme gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/96fce643091cc06523da23ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5902, 5903]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Placing Purandara397 at the forefront, they approached Brahma.
On seeing all of them, their hands joined in salutation, Parameshthi398 said, ‘O gods! I know the task that all of you wish to undertake.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97012985a943841b4f97d190> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5141]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“When Bhimasena had penetrated, Parshata Dhrishtadyumna swiftly abandoned Drona238 and went to where Soubala was." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97167656b4e52d89bdeed881> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8512]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You have already told us all the words spoken by the two foremost among the Kurus57 to the wicked one who is overcome by desire and avarice and thinks himself to be wise." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9725b132f3ada09eb8425ab9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1463]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Armour was the waves." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/975ae027d4a0c98030e0e383> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5062]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Living there for one month at the time of Mahalaya241 and eating once in three days, one is cleansed of all sins, the soul becomes pure, and one obtains a lot of gold." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9769a3c2204e2a3a990737c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5019]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of men! Rathavarta is towards the south230 of the goddess." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/977059b86dec390f5ba6f9c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1457]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Sanjaya! Pandava56 has already exhibited a kind of peacefulness that is extremely difficult to attain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9781a5d57a31ab909a158053> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1969]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Tandi recounted it to Shukra and Bhargava1130 recounted it to Goutama." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9783e753a86be077d20b2fdf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4061, 4063]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He will be devoted to the gods and grateful.
He will be self-controlled and not be distracted in offering oblations to the gods and the ancestors.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/978dbfe15bea4be4dd720aae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10420]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O extender of the Kuru lineage! If we were not present in this battle, the mighty- armed one130 is also capable of destroying the army of the Kouravas in an instant." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/979ad777c7adae9911fa69d4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2348]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They have golden harnesses and were happily given by Chitraratha144 to Gandivadhanva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97b942c90f9f05de9fed8d7b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7847]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Powerfully pushing the middle of his23 back down with one knee, the Pandava grabbed his neck with his right hand and his loincloth with the left, and then ripped the rakshasa into two with great force." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97bbaf53d52b30d73d93e1ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2637]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The valour of the Pandavas was vanquished and Dhritarashtra’s son200 grabbed it with force." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97bc8f0bbcd7e85147be0c62> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10072]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the equals of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97c3bd36a82b1490b4c4b45e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1432]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Struck and killed, they fell down in every direction." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97c7622d303416ca45601c78> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10096]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O unblemished one! While the one who had been born in a pot102 and your sons looked on, Yudhishthira angrily destroyed your soldiers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97d1ca363672a2f1b12e6246> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2522]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "CHAPTER 901(41) ‘Sanjaya said, “At that, on seeing Dhananjaya take up Gandiva and his arrows again, the maharathas1 let out a tremendous roar." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97e02b3ef8529efd4fa81055> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24950]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then he quickly went to his own hermitage, on the slopes of the Himalayas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97e7010def71e979993756ae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6966]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O king! On hearing Duryodhana’s many lamentations in the night, he358 regarded them as instructions unto himself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97eda0ea4f4ec9d82db4740c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 8 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[708]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If either is released against a brahmana who has conquered anger, both are extinguished." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97ee422b1a711f781e43be05> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "1 When King Dhritarashtra, with dharma in his soul, had performed the water-rites, the great-souled siddhas, supreme brahmarshis, Dvaipayana, Narada, the great rishi Devala, Devsthana and Kanva, with their supreme disciples, and many other brahmanas who were accomplished in wisdom and learned in the Vedas and all the snatakas2 in the householder stage, came to see the supreme among the Kuru lineage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/97ef7b81765031dd1cbd9199> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4853]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Bulls among the gods, supreme among the brahmanas, Nriga219 and the best among kings, lions among men, have performed extremely expensive sacrifices here." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/980740e882431dd1cf0e5776> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7178, 7179]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Wishing to rescue his son, the intolerant one arrived at the spot where he372 was fighting with Bhishma.
O king! In that battle, your father, Devavrata, attacked Partha in the encounter, like Svarbhanu373 against the sun.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/983298d51e3f7f89ef67d70f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1333]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! That is the reason that wise and extremely intelligent one is also known as Dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9859d53674c178fbe0278a2b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2851]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O man of good fortune! Why were these great warriors, the equals of the gods, born on earth? Tell me in detail." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/985ad31fe0f6a95a0bd51b1f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18071, 18093]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """566 The gods are themselves confused when they try to follow in their footsteps.
What will such a person obtain through austerities? What will be accomplished through sacrifices or his atman? If a person casts aside his upper garment, if he sleeps on the bare ground, using his arm as a pillow and if he is tranquil, the gods know such a person to be a brahmana.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9866b1b86d7f742358092cdb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9986]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ CHAPTER 835(172) ‘Bhishma said, “O lord of men! I then informed Kali6 Satyavati, the advisers, the brahmanas and the priests and allowed the eldest maiden, Amba, to leave." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/986edc2e4113be4517064e95> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[981]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, in advance, the great gods have devised an antidote." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9877a8e6665a792ac3b92a2c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10437, 10439, 10440]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ ‘The two Achyutas47 saw the angry Shakra and the assemblage of the other gods.
When they saw the gods advancing from every direction, they angrily repulsed them with arrows that were like the vajra.
Repeatedly, the resolutions of the gods were shattered.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/987ceeb8fa6ef0ad12434377> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1330]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 1327(26): 44 shlokas Shraddha is a funeral ceremony for dead relatives and this parva is named after that." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/98836c5d2e896221940fc07d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16306]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The firmament was then crowded with all the gods and gandharvas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/98899a581b121e61cc1df252> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4562, 4563, 4564, 4565, 4566, 4567, 4568, 4569]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """That man obtains Brahma’s eternal world, without decay.
Whatever sins a woman or a man has committed since birth are all instantly destroyed from bathing in Pushkara.
O king! Just as Madhusudana34 is the origin of all the gods, Pushkara is known as the origin of all the tirthas.
He who lives constantly and purely in Pushkara for twelve years obtains all the sacrifices35 and attains Brahma’s world.
He who performs agnihotra36 for one hundred years and he who lives in Pushkara on the night of the full moon in Kartika are like equals.
It is difficult to go to Pushkara.
It is difficult to perform austerities in Pushkara.
It is difficult to donate in Pushkara.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/989b417b828f8ae6fb60642f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8888]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! While all the brave ones among the Kurus looked on, he453 used sharp arrows to sever it into three and made the three parts fall down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/989f7e31d4c99c803274d5c4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5370]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“After this, listen to what I have to say about the gods desiring to perform a sacrifice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/98a087b24888126ad5497e23> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13070]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They burnt the army of the gods and made them writhe on the ground." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/98a7c13cbd806231f1ef8f83> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8535]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Drona advanced against the son of Panchala435 in the great battle and used straight-tufted arrows in the great clash." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/98affe0ea56ba8277a2b1306> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2321]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "We bow down before the one who is the god of all the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/98c022decd3be1f96d45bd49> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13392]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "To bewilder all the gods, the firmament, with all its nakshatras, blazed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/98c5f2e21871455bf264bc58> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10528]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Pierce." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/98dfa1a2060956ebb3238fa7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 17 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[892]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Varshneya! Listen to my words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/98e8235ead78eb5892e1e20b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 108 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8245]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is advancing amidst the soldiers, like a second Phalguna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9900be135423402cfb394120> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10009]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When I was swiftly falling from the vimana on which Shakra is seated, I asked the illustrious supreme sage42 to free me from the curse." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/99127525d504b862052bee82> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[760]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rule the kingdom of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9913a96f85012dce97f60d07> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1787]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When I witness Pandava’s hardships, I think that earlier karma114 determines the destiny of beings." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/991f14ee0139ee387dd5c6cf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[647]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! That fight with the trees between the chief of the rakshasas and the supreme among men lasted but an instant." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/992414de18fb05d87d3afad2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7379]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But I have witnessed the power this rakshasa has unleashed on men." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/99344b9ee55210853983b764> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1001]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“On seeing King Shalva’s strength, all the young descendants80 of the Vrishni lineage emerged, to do battle with him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9938d004ac7cce987c04a857> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17020, 17031]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Jealousy makes up the leaves.
464 Distraction is severed through renunciation and by resorting to supreme tranquility.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/993ccccb09129eaafe886358> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5166]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When he reached his city, which was like Purandara’s216 city, the descendant of the Puru lineage was happy and thought that all his desires had been fulfilled." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9942b0da1a450dc212af9e80> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10604]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Dakshina must be given at the five sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/995c408ffa159b599ac4fadb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4693]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! You have no interest in being a king on earth or being a king of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9962a37e96bc821aabf2642d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7875]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O bull among the Bharata lineage! Those on your side could not find a protector." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/99687345e8438f9379aba805> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12540]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "May you become a Vasu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/997d016386406a6aebf6df6f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[154]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O Sanjaya! I had no hope of victory when I heard that the king of Matsya44 had with great honour bestowed his daughter Uttara on Arjuna and he had accepted her for his son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9991d27b12ca84e20dd3dda2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13145]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kill the enemies of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/99bb4e99c980359910b5b06c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[418]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Just as Uchchaihshrava85 is supreme among horses, Vaishravana86 is supreme among yakshas87 and the great Indra is supreme among gods, Karna was supreme among those who could strike." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/99d0b5d38d3b3117767037f9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6369, 6370]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Then that great-souled king was given another son named Bhima by Matarishva316 and he is immensely powerful, best among those who are strong.
Puruhuta317 gave Kunti this son.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/99d479d17ac24f8ba6f026fd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21095]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of men! Ego876 is created from Mahat." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/99e57e9ee1d8b64dd0116de1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[980]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Semen is created from blood and enters a woman’s womb." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9a126752df60fbd921017009> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9803]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I did not faithfully offer food at sacrifices meant for the gods and the ancestors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9a27484779c8da70d841b794> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13887]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Hearing this, the supreme ones among the gods were delighted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9a29b54af475d19947f16eb4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8805]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The mighty-armed one394 struck and brought Satyaki down on the ground." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9a34cc234203005c790a4f9f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[371, 372]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The sage, the son of Parashara99 and master of great knowledge, composed this in 170 chapters100 and 8909 shlokas.
‘Thereafter follows the most wonderful Karna Parva, where the appointment of the wise king of Madra101 as charioteer is described.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9a3a33041e587ecba6b5abd3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4948]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The brave lord5 advanced in the direction of Samantapanchaka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9a4c75c9e80cca06d43cd7ca> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4498]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O bulls among gods! I had a conversation with that cheerful one." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9a5769d8ef59d6ae371f8fe5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2854]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In ancient times, after destroying the Kshatriyas on earth twenty-one times, Jamadagni’s son77 went to Mahendra, supreme among mountains, and began to practise austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9a6d78f85b4cb5283d2fa95d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[554]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He himself instructed the gods that an assembly hall, with the best of rooms, should be constructed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9a8a39a1534c60f9b317ff09> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12425]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Desire, anger, fear, avarice, sorrow, anxiety, hunger and exhaustion influence everyone." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9aac27e99838e1b0b4c89a66> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1341]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 321(24) Vaishampayana said, ‘When the lord of the Dasharhas137 had left, Yudhishthira, Bhimasena, Arjuna, the twins, Krishna138 and the priest139 ascended chariots that were extremely expensive and yoked to supreme horses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ab0934ab38459e8b4f0a1b6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9210, 9211, 9213]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He ordained that the woman, the most beautiful in the worlds, who was none other than Shri44 herself, would be their wife in the world of men.
Thereafter, accompanied by them,45 he46 went to the god Narayana, who is beyond measure.
‘“Hari48 plucked two hairs from his body.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9afd97b7f33e2699609d182a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7039, 7040]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O son! Why should we not deserve death35 from the descendants of the Kuru lineage, those great-souled ones and even inhabitants of the entire world?” ‘Duryodhana said, “Bhishma will always be neutral.
Drona’s son36 is on my side.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9b0a10f5c253985a57e6df48> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[824, 825, 826]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O Krishna! It was he37 who caused virulent serpents to bite him38 all over his body when he slept, but that destroyer of enemies did not die.
On waking up, Kounteya killed all the serpents and he killed his39 favourite charioteer with the back of his hand.
Once again, when they were asleep and unconscious with the arya lady40 in Varanavata, he41 tried to burn them.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9b0a11698b60de6fde58f6f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12082]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Maharathas were struck by the rocks and fell down, shrieking loudly." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9b16160fe60a85e72113caa7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2455, 2457]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The king entered the palace, which was like the residence of the king of the gods.
‘Entering inside, he approached the prosperous gods324 and worshipped all of them with jewels and fragrant garlands.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9b29dddf07118efe7134eba0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7903]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods are always satisfied with sacrifices and humans with hospitality." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9b2be7f29cf176e1c910e2df> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4726]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘At this time, there was a conflict between the gods and the danavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9b3dff07db3eed6263757303> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9310]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Full of shame, Duhshasana softly spoke to him, “O king! If Dhananjaya3 had not been disguised as a Brahmana, he would never have succeeded in obtaining Droupadi." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9b4ff9a822ee5cc04f63063e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2415]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O illustrious one! It was in a desire to see you that I came to this great mountain, beloved by you, lord of the gods, and the supreme abode of the ascetics." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9b7b3c742c7fa9b3592f1a31> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5078]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O bull among the Bharata lineage! At the right time, sacrificial stakes were erected—six were made of bilva, six were made of khadira355 and six were made out of sarvavarnina." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9b824c81267c82e5a2b4a1c7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9342]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "14 Or let them15 incite Krishna16 against them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9b8611028865ddc0be989f4b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11591]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! A duel commenced between the man and the rakshasa in that battle and it was terrible in form." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9b881bc9af99bc78ece340b3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3286, 3289, 3291]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! The sacred river Malini, which gladdens the heart, flowed by and created beautiful and large pools89 of water.
‘The king, whose chariot no one could obstruct, entered that enchanting hermitage, which was like the world of the gods and beautiful everywhere.
Chakravaka90 birds swarmed along its banks.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9b9e7dbc7855c9396983d64c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2398]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On hearing that their husbands and sons have been killed in the battle by the Pandavas, all the women of Nagapura42 will weep today." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9bb706d1f9dd6800bf769318> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5004, 5005]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """On performing ablutions there, engaged in the worship of the ancestors and the gods, there is no doubt that after discarding one’s body, one attains the status of a Ganapati.
‘“‘O Indra among kings! One should then go the place of the goddess that is difficult of access.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9bd3029c0f332d2c241870f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12754]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "She gave birth to a daughter, the two Agnishomas and five other fires." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9bdc23e3bc1a82a1c8a4f128> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9487]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O king! At that, I spoke these words to the king of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9be1f9d34d1953a9099288b4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1225, 1229]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """90 Taste is born from that.
Doubt is born from that.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9be37a7fe2de748168f67f25> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6645]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The goddess182 performed austerities here to obtain Maheshvara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9c15b43abe17f6bfc5fb8a87> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5424]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Kouravya! This is the great-souled Bhargava’s340 Mahendra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9c22e939bb0f3e0722f709fc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18288]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He lives near the gods and has not been worshipped by men earlier." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9c2da3d96f6b92e17781027f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2368]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among snakes! Astika will send the sacrifice153 that is being performed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9c435fcc0693224e22eb2720> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 63 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5279]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Under Rohini, to free oneself from debts, one must give brahmanas the meat of deer, food, ghee, milk and other objects of food and drink." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9c646d5922de404c4a3a66a8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2980]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! On seeing him engaged in those terrible austerities, the thousand-eyed Purandara knew that he was capable of giving birth to a son who would be his463 equal." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9c6c12dfe73707ebf104cbb1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10576]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ 482(185) Vaishampayana said, ‘Then the Pandava60 again spoke to Markandeya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9c6c473d2281531103d04700> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25964]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! He1397 performed the sacraments for him to be initiated into the way of dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9c7e93738eee126ad11166b5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14470]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Having been thus addressed and with the welfare of the gods in mind, he remained immobile for a thousand years." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9c81b50c10c80009dacd07cf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6489, 6490]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """But they also knew about Dhananjaya’s valour and thought that he738 was like an oblation that had been poured into the fire.
Kiriti, the slayer of enemy heroes, saw that the best of men739 was without his horses, which had been slain.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9c96c951035bf89dd7dffaa0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7810, 7811, 7813]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """After Vyavasaya, Tejas1059 remains awake, for the cause of protection.
The medicinal plants and herbs come after Tejas and the mountains after the plants and herbs.
After that, the goddess Nirriti1060 remains awake and after Nirriti, it is the stellar bodies.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ca6ac1e02a57692dca7db97> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14313]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods who are stationed in heaven bow down before him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9cb08cc482e7e62f4572182e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3030]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Sahadeva and the king5 have made their intentions clear through their gestures." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ccd949477bbf3710f5afcda> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3160]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then the suta110 came and told Damayanti, ‘All the citizens are waiting at the gate with a specific purpose." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9cd6e23852d7d60ab773acb7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9087]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The handsome lord of riches was seated on his supreme Pushpaka,119 constructed by Vishvakarma120 and coloured along the sides." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ce0da93f234a06ac65770bb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1978]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Listen to them—the resolution of the gods, the intellect of the wise, the humility of the learned and the destruction of those who perform evil deeds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ce4a5c35a87835dda7eed09> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 201 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12222]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O brahmana! This entire universe, everything in this universe and everything that cannot be vanquished and the great elements have the brahman in the soul." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ce669b822689d0d5cf62854> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5364]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O brahmana! I know those two brave Krishnas,326 the slayers of enemies, just as the powerful Vyasa knows Pundarikaksha327 Vasudeva and Dhananjaya of the three yugas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9cf7e7b04f3db8239d729bb8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[233]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On hearing about the agreement made between the son of Angiras16 and the king of the gods, King Marutta was enraged." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9cff2363f9b2c5236bd9995b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6896]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The rajarshi pleasured with her like Ravi210 with Prabhavati, Vahni211 with Svaha, Vasava with Shachi, Chandra with Rohini, Yama with Dhumorna, Varuna with Gouri, Dhaneshvara212 with Riddhi, Narayana with Lakshmi, the ocean with Jahnavi,213 Rudra with Rudrani, the grandfather214 with the altar, Vasishtha’s son with Adrishyanti, Vasishtha with Akshamala, Chyavana with Sukanya, Pulastya with Sandhya, Agastya with Vaidharbhi, Satyavan with Savitri, Bhrigu with Puloma, Kashyapa with Aditi, Richika’s son215 with Renuka, Koushika with Haimavati, Brihaspati with Tara, Shukra with Shataparva, Bhumipati with Bhumi, Pururava with Urvashi, Richika with Satyavati and Manu with Sarasvati." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d04611efe3733f21fc7189e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4616]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If I do175 what others refuse to accept, how can that bring my welfare?” When King Yayati spoke these words, Vasumana, supreme among kings, addressed him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d05f744c703966c186bc1aa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4192]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Yudhishthira asked, “How are the sacraments1330 of such a person performed? Who undertakes them? What kind of girl should he be married to? O grandfather! Tell me this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d1b48b12dcae6fbd0efd98f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17499]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Having defeated Saindhava40 and got Krishna back and having heard the ancient and detailed accounts about gods and rishis from Markandeya, they left Kamyaka hermitage with the brahmanas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d21ca869af4b6e5a1cb09d6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10049]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Indra among kings! Drona’s son slew Balanika, Jayanika, Jaya and Shrutaharya95 and sent them to Yama’s abode." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d481e7e9b612d50cee0ede9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2379]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O bull among the Bharata lineage! He obtained weapons from Rama314 and Shakra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d4b2cc514daa7b8abf3ab5f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10880]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "To ensure the welfare of your sons, he countered the rakshasa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d4e9849ef513090330f9456> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6665]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O large-eyed one! The gods are bowing down before you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d4f9edd6126baaa81593e89> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2534, 2537]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O conqueror of enemies! You must now accomplish a great task for the sake of the gods.
My chariot will descend to earth for you, driven by Matali.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d51e6be4dd0e4a402a744ca> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6915]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Since she knew the truth, Kuntibhoja’s daughter21 fainted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d5465b67f7ad6ea3f3c7317> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[245]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O tiger among men! Before this, the one who had defeated his enemies had ruled over Anga." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d5719fa6aecede585b6804b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13635]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Affectionate towards his son, he was unwilling to fight and was full of sorrow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d5a365eab81ea6d5524ac6a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2189]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Are the sons118 obedient to their elders? Are the commoners obedient to his rule?” ‘Vidura replied, “The great-souled king is well with his sons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d617d0ea701766f4fb0b623> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2363]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The vimana143 of the king of the gods had one hundred thousand golden pillars." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d76f8d0d7eda6f6a4c3c31a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[438]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the kings and all the hierarchies of kshatriyas on this earth claim descent from Aila9 and Ikshvaku." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d7ea6b57bb6c86e0a05a499> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5051]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Indra among kings! Let arrangements be made for the sacrifice, so that there are no blemishes." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9d951269c105d253c1040112> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2894]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He wields a trident and is the lord of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ddcb73997378507328d4ff7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12898]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There were also many apsaras, yakshas and rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9de01320f5f15e1ea12817e7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22728]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son!1059 Discard all possessions and conquer your senses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9de961ae5e376ba0e9b9d64a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3051]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Then Drona, Somadatta, the maharatha Bahlika, Vidura, Drona’s son,6 the valorous son of the vaishya,7 Bhurishrava, Shantanu’s son8 and maharatha Vikarna collectively said, “Don’t have the gamble." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9df6898f85530fe8ff5b7d53> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5083]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Worshipping the ancestors and the gods there, one obtains a horse sacrifice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9dfd576e815dd77c596cea26> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[72]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "17 Vrishaparva18 is always faithful to his promises and I have kept it in his sabha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9dfd9a6ff4968106524e3033> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5202]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rathas fought against rathas, horse-riders against horse-riders, elephants against supreme elephants and infantry against infantry." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9e097544b0aaf487e2449fcb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7149]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Attack." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9e17809958970f9cad599e4a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9693]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He45 pierced Bhimasena with ten arrows, each of Madri’s sons with three arrows, Virata and Drupada with six each, Shikhandi with one hundred, Dhrishtadyumna with seventy, Dharma’s son with seven and the Kekayas and the Chedis with many sharp arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9e2c00aad1a776631678b340> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "16_Mausala" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[200]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He saw him immersed in yoga and a giant serpent was emerging from his mouth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9e3db080372dd0474bfdf5c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12693]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In ancient times, in this world, Prajapati109 and the gods, along with masses of rishis, performed sacrifices and austerities, thus attaining Brahma’s world." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9e3e765e398bb2551484143d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 247 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14757]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 545(248): 17 shlokas Chapter 546(249): 13 shlokas Chapter 547(250): 9 shlokas Chapter 548(251): 21 shlokas Chapter 549(252): 27 shlokas Chapter 550(253): 26 shlokas Chapter 551(254): 21 shlokas Chapter 552(255): 59 shlokas Chapter 553(256): 30 shlokas Chapter 554(257): 10 shlokas Chapter 555(258): 16 shlokas Chapter 556(259): 40 shlokas Chapter 557(260): 15 shlokas Chapter 558(261): 55 shlokas Chapter 559(262): 41 shlokas Chapter 560(263): 43 shlokas Chapter 561(264): 73 shlokas Chapter 562(265): 30 shlokas Chapter 563(266): 68 shlokas Chapter 564(267): 54 shlokas Chapter 565(268): 40 shlokas Chapter 566(269): 14 shlokas Chapter 567(270): 29 shlokas Chapter 568(271): 27 shlokas Chapter 569(272): 26 shlokas Chapter 570(273): 33 shlokas Chapter 571(274): 31 shlokas Chapter 572(275): 69 shlokas Chapter 573(276): 13 shlokas Chapter 574(277): 41 shlokas Chapter 575(278): 32 shlokas Chapter 576(279): 23 shlokas Chapter 577(280): 33 shlokas Chapter 578(281): 108 shlokas Chapter 579(282): 44 shlokas Chapter 580(283): 16 shlokas Harana means abduction and this parva is about Droupadi’s abduction by Jayadratha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9e442ba91e72f96175da0663> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17112, 17113]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O god! You know about the great strength of weapons I have obtained from Jamadagni’s son11 and from the great-souled Drona.
O foremost among the gods! Grant me permission to observe my vow.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9e583363106cdf74291789f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4752]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "We have heard that Ashvavana, Abhishyanta, Chitraratha, Muni and the famous Janamejaya185 were his five sons, through the intelligent Vahini." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9e59dbd4e0aac5e3e9e806c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9618]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘The vyuha constructed by the preceptor is extremely impenetrable, even to the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9e7cc0ed349ea722878ba550> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3180]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A part of Shri74 herself was born on earth out of love." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9e944e3901aeb4eccced9413> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7014]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Karna! When you, Suyodhana, Duhshasana and Shakuni Soubala brought Droupadi to the assembly hall in a single garment, did dharma not show itself to you? When, in the assembly hall, Yudhishthira, who was not skilled at dice, was defeated by Shakuni, who was skilled at dice, where did dharma go then? O Karna! During her season, Krishna798 was under Duhshasana’s subjugation in the assembly hall and you laughed at her." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9e9a567cba539e13036113bc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3796]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "We have heard that three forces have come together on a single chariot now, the two Krishnas92 and the stringed Gandiva bow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ebae818cc8f2e34438f9f84> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8744]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The space between the base and the tip of the thumb is said to be brahma tirtha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ec273698fada263c591e3b5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4366]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The wives of the gods showered down excellent flowers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ec976c94c144438ac737ebd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5669]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Satyavati, the great-souled Krishna254 and I have ensured that the likes of you are established, so that the threads of our lineage continue." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ec9e160ed249232f1bf0a54> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1055]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘O queen! Grant me leave." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ecd7a779d8c4e3d24acf4ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1038]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On arriving in Divahprastha, Senabindu’s great capital, the lord17 set up a base there, with his fourfold army." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ee8df4b26466775176fd032> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7805]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In battle, he is the equal of the best, the wielder of the vajra21 himself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ef5de75034b6c91da3128eb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4018]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the rakshasas were rebuffed and forced to leave that house." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9f0948a8b3732fc94433087a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11262]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O maternal uncle! Slay the Kounteyas, like Pavaka’s son198 against the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9f187057bb8394f957fb2cd6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13299]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "None of them saw that he had left, in the company of the bulls among the rishis." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9f1a19c84abc616f28feea3b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1189]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Material objects used in rites86 are seen to be destroyed by rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9f688f077860df8ce92ed62e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9641]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The shafted arrows from Gandiva, empowered with mantras, sliced off their heads, wherever they were." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9f6d3431d15115413d5f9675> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11520]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Agni1386 is golden in complexion, without any smoke and the flames rise upwards together." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9f741a2ef72f5227fe9ad562> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12399, 12401]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’” ‘Markandeya said, “At these words, he178 entered and saw an extremely beautiful house.
It was like a house of the gods and was worshipped by the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9f7831e37580c2a46cc46244> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[982]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Varshneya124 used to take pride in you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9f7d1bb6cff36f34c99c2434> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5855]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Evil- souled ones who possess other wickedness cannot go there either." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9f909dcf82c5e1b748657408> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1481]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With the king of Matsya having lost his chariot, he21 captured him alive." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9fbc4606c75de9e22fc1aa19> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10893]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O unblemished one! O destroyer of enemies! For what purpose is everything in the universe inside your body? For how long will you be established here? O lord of the gods! I wish to hear this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9fe27b57ac4c99a7b779de4d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6460]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rare is a well-wisher who offers beneficial advice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9febcd4a9e43d513d0ddc25c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[68]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You did not follow the beneficial advice of Vidura, Drona, Gangeya14 and Keshava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9ffa240a40c43f19fd725b95> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 273 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19039]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Accept one-fourth of the disquiet that has come about because of killing a brahmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/9fff201d84e5cb87c91d5504> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2340]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are Ishana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a045daca293f9d3e559d70b0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2239]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘ “When the rathas were routed, three thousand giant elephants surrounded and attacked the five Pandava rathas34 from all directions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a066f7838f8790dce4fdf52c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2036]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His mothers254 also rushed to the spot where King Srinjaya was." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a081e6ee724f10c4c088319c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 124 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9477]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those great archers were stationed there, surrounded by the Panchalas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a09ed63d50f68db5c057bed7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7386]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You bring disrepute to all the chief rakshasas, your ancestors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a0aa4114f229896a85564db0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[561]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! All the other gods are also delighted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a0c6bd677a6da189ca9495bb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 186 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10894]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is a brahmana’s desire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a0ee012a9d8c53a9c55a203a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 5 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[166]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "60 O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Corrupted by bribes, do your advisers see falsely when disputes arise between the poor and the rich? Do you abhor the fourteen royal vices— atheism, falsehood, anger, negligence, procrastination, avoidance of the wise, laziness, restlessness of mind, consultation with only one person, consultation with those who are ignorant of artha, failure to act on something that has been decided, divulgement of counsel, abandonment of beneficial plans and addiction to material objects? Is your study of the Vedas successful? Are your riches successful? Is your marriage successful? Is your learning successful?” ‘Yudhishthira asked, “How does the study of the Vedas become successful? How do riches become successful? How does marriage become successful? How does learning become successful?” ‘Narada replied, “The Vedas become successful in agnihotra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a10fe253c948a77d6a14fa9b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4399]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "675 Dispel the pride of our enemies." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a1302b2b19b1ce549f260b78> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23918]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This great Upanishad1190 is in conformity with the four Vedas and sankhya and yoga, and is referred to by this name in the pancharatra rituals." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a134b7fac19f19c828fb18db> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[630, 631]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He was like the lord of the gods88 himself.
”’ Chapter 1291(8) ‘Dhritarashtra asked, “When Drona’s maharatha son headed towards the camp, were Kripa and Bhoja frightened? Did they retreat? Were they restrained by the inferior guards and did they run away? Did those maharathas think that they89 were irresistible and refrain? Or did they crush the camp and kill the Somakas and the Pandavas? Did they follow Duryodhana’s supreme footsteps in the encounter? Were they slain by the Panchalas and did they lie down on the ground? What tasks did those two accomplish? O Sanjaya! Tell me that.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a138c2b730fdf0ebe5ea4edf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9423]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! O extender of the Kuru lineage! Go to my abode and learn all the weapons there—those of Vayu, Agni, Varuna, the masses of Maruts, of the Sadhyas, the grandfather,176 the gandharvas, the serpents and the rakshasas, those of Vishnu, the nairritas177 and my own." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a151b1914ee836ab32cfd0a6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2041]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowing that this was the desire in my heart, the supreme among gods spoke to me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a154ab0840660209b365ff16> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4051]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! At this, the angry Bhimasena, Parshata Dhrishtadyumna, Droupadi’s sons, Abhimanyu and the Pandavas who were Madri’s sons167 discharged many different kinds of weapons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a1877ad04437abf160324c50> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1980, 1982]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O great king! As tribute, the shudra kings who lived in Bharukaccha55 brought one hundred thousand slave girls from the Karpasika region.
They also brought ranku56 hides, fit for the best of brahmanas, and horses from the Gandhara region.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a188ecbc9b59ed63eb74dc7b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14443, 14445]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Bhava destroyed the sacrifice111 in his wrath and later granted them freedom from fear.
At that time, the prosperous gods could find no peace.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a18aa1cce933d41aba7639f8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3796]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Many years ago, a great fight occurred between the gods and the demons over who would rule over the three worlds, with all their movable and immovable riches." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a1abba712b1d220c41d2aac2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[473]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was followed by the brave and great-souled Dasharha,9 Yuyudhana10 and Yuyutsu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a1b6488c2044703645770f76> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18357]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Gods are frightened of men because they always act contrary to the words of the gods, in every way." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a1c0c5b7d34df07c4700e53a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[891]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There were gigantic rakshasas terrible in form, the performers of cruel deeds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a1dc3246ddb23a3722a9d038> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22259]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! Thinking about dharma, he1016 chose Brihaspati, learned about the Vedas, the Vedangas and their commentaries, as his preceptor." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a1ed8f8ab911175428abd050> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14618, 14620]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """For the next fortnight, he lived like a pigeon, collecting one drona of vrihi.
He sustained his body on the food left after gods and guests had eaten.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a2050b3f237ddb8a96785bd7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4158, 4159]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O descendant of the Bharata lineage! With his507 charioteer brought down in the encounter, his horses were seen to run around here and there.
With Yudhishthira at the forefront, they508 powerfully attacked Drona’s son, supreme among the wielders of weapons, and showered down sharp arrows.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a20acd7b79edb4eb1efe557e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1509, 1515]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Union ends in dissolution.
Ill-wishers do not ensure sorrow.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a21a138dffa9c639af16acab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3240]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Indra among men! The lord of the stars40 was afflicted by tuberculosis and was freed of his curse there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a24bc1014bd9c6fce2d5f728> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2728]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O lord of men! Thus did the great-souled and great Maghavan43 Indra bless the great king Vasu, out of his love for him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a2599b5e6a6258e03f19e74b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[313]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When he went there, as was prescribed, the sons of Pandu offered him water to wash the feet,57 the gift for a guest58 and a cow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a25d4cbd2af5169230e971aa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[646]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among the gods! Depart." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a27867a6d2b6278af1b457f8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11017]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” At these words, the supreme among sages began to speak again." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a2791ccf48285fa5f9cbfae0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12790, 12791, 12792]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """At agnishtoma sacrifices, the Niyata is the best rite for sustenance.
223 ‘“On seeing Niyata arrive, he224 was frightened and hid in the ocean.
The gods sought him along every road and every direction, but could not find him.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a27bf5f967d7fc805a4f9e54> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5531]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Even if I am slain, who can be more fortunate than I am? There are human objects of pleasure that gods deserve." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a29126c130482468d856a629> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3268]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bees84 swarmed over the creepers and there was a supreme beauty there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a2a9df9988c207e50b0075d0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4547]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ ‘“There is in the world of men a tirtha of the god of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a2c59ec6f1c94a9686041577> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1735]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! The powerful Dhrishtadyumna quickly conducted Virata, the maharatha Dhananjaya the great-souled Yajnasena,51 the immensely strong Bhimasena, Bhishma and Dhritarashtra, the great warrior Sahadeva the brave, Drona and his son, Nakula Subala and his son and the sons of Droupadi and Subhadra52 the kings of the mountains." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a2e943076b927675da900d83> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5641]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! The son of the naga king’s daughter triumphed in this way." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a2f4826d722143ec11b3e226> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5479]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 751(88) Vaishampayana said, ‘After meeting Vidura, Janardana Govinda, the destroyer of enemies, went to meet his father’s sister46 in the afternoon." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a2fe13b7e3d1f7ac25428124> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2959, 2960]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """It looked like a drinking ground that had been used by Death and had just been abandoned.
Large numbers of demons wandered around and large numbers of rakshasas frequented it.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3046f218610d069e980b407> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8101]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I was earlier called Chitraratha40 and have now become Dagdharatha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a30ba394d6314dcf798bc79f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11731]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, the rakshasa again assumed a form that was as small as a finger." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a31866be365eb5f5b35cd2c9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 112 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8386]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On receiving the sign from Vrikodara, he was filled with great delight." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a338f92fdd5042eb92a65523> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4746]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king who was Jarasandha’s grandson331 saw that it had arrived in his territory." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a348ba9e0e767e4ec24b85f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3863]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Gandiva is supreme among bows, Keshava among all beings, Sudarshana97 among all chakras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a34e2455e69e1cebd7b29ebf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Chapter 1220(1): 52 shlokas Chapter 1221(2): 65 shlokas Chapter 1222(3): 50 shlokas Chapter 1223(4): 50 shlokas Chapter 1224(5): 27 shlokas Chapter 1225(6): 41 shlokas Chapter 1126(7): 44 shlokas Chapter 1227(8): 46 shlokas Chapter 1228(9): 65 shlokas Chapter 1229(10): 56 shlokas Chapter 1230(11): 63 shlokas Chapter 1231(12): 45 shlokas Chapter 1232(13): 45 shlokas Chapter 1233(14): 41 shlokas Chapter 1234(15): 67 shlokas Chapter 1235(16): 87 shlokas Vadha means killing and the section is named after the killing of Shalya.
Shalya is appointed the supreme commander of the Kourava army.
Nakula kills Karna’s sons.
Duryodhana kills Chekitana, the prince of Chedi.
Ashvatthama kills Suratha of Panchala.
Yudhishthira kills Shalya and Shalya’s younger brother.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a34f5f82758cf483470d0462> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6582]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Brahma, with the brahmarshis and the Prajapatis755 and Bhava,756 on his celestial chariot, also arrived at the spot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3552f97425d08bb7bf9170c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[891]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Kashyapa asked, ‘How does the body go away and how does one get another again? How is one freed from the hardships of this cycle of life? Having freed oneself from the body, how is one united with the atman? Having been freed from this body, how does one obtain another end? How does a man enjoy the fruits of the good and bad deeds done by him? If one is freed from the body, what kind of acts can be undertaken?’ ‘“The brahmana60 said, ‘Thus asked, the siddha replied to the questions, one after another." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3684998c64e95dc65084f27> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4108]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Nala’s horses182 heard the roar of the chariot and hearing this, rejoiced, just as they had in Nala’s company earlier." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a36c9391b8a7837e1ad16588> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[369]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The brave Shrutayu and Shrutayudha81 and the valiant Chitrangada and Chitravarma, foremost among men, are stationed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a371a20373701d1812923ab4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3489]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Iron emerged from stone." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3791ec41300dfb2f9a5e258> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14698, 14703]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """These worlds are supreme and are worshipped even by the gods.
These eternal gods of the gods do not crave for happiness.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3894c3353b1dc27b09288c1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13025]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Japakas are praised." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a392c59f6d5b5d7fddc70592> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9173]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Prajapati Manu said that a king possesses seven attributes—father, mother, preceptor, protector, Agni, Vaishravana60 and Yama." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a39fe7360c67925f3a7710ee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4894]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "222 He was skilled in dancing and singing and was worshipped by the gods and the brahmanas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3a93787602a17d905293964> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10243]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In a battle, they can kill even the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3afa0bc1b094e2a46bf6812> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1682]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The famous Babhru’s40 wife-to-be was travelling to the Souvira region to be married." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3c1dad892c76f1f419bff36> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2614]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In a desire for the kingdom, hear about the exile11 as a result of the game of dice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3c8249828e3cc15de4e628c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[263]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is beautiful and white, ruled by Varuna, with many rooms and seats." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3daefc119fc8bbcdd694804> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17058]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If the slayer of Bala and Vritra7 comes to me and begs for the earrings to ensure the welfare of the sons of Pandu, it will extend my fame in the world and increase his ill fame." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3e9d1beb3b8f2c69a904356> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23298, 23299]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Right at the beginning, the sacred text was ornamented with the syllable ‘Om’.
The rishis first recited it at the spot where the compassionate one1111 was.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3fa96ef0f140efa2eb67d03> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[415]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Know me to be the king of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a3fb32abf6a2ba6e51a36936> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6461]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On learning this, Dhritarashtra’s powerful son320 revealed the evil side of his nature." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a407832d322421eb7508d56d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1368]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” King Duryodhana swiftly accepted Vaikartana12 Karna’s words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a42ea90af4db582bb90da568> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "16_Mausala" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[146]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Seeing that Shini’s descendant was being struck, Rukmini’s son25 became angry." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a48a93faf8d0ba6288e28d7e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3538]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At that great sacrifice, performed in accordance with the indicated rites, the gods were also agitated." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a4ade94c4ac4349562a79ffa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14222, 14238]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Vapour rises from bodies of water and becomes separate raindrops.
O one who is worshipped by the gods! I desire to think about you.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a4bdc4671bbd24bcd230b29c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18904]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the soldiers of the gods and the asuras clashed against each other." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a4d46160eeb986db953d643b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5710]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "380 The great Akshayavata is there and the Pandavas performed chaturmasya381 and the great sacrifice of the rishis there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a4ed6dcfdddc3b2caba27509> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1147]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "100 Kripi101 is full of misery and the sorrow has made her lose her senses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a526ae719ab409fd6e75af2a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13303]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is extremely unfortunate that the dharma of brahmanas177 has presented itself before me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a52a1daf75cc24cbb989f7bf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7231]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! This is the path followed by Richika’s immensely energetic son571 when he traversed the earth, immersed in yoga, on the banks of the stream Roupya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a536724246946b5642210dbd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[403, 404]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Shachi’s consort68 saw a woodcutter who had arrived there, engaged in his work.
On seeing him, the chastiser of Paka69 quickly said, ‘Listen to my words.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a5374e340bc44842e2f3004c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9399]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If these are impossible, one can take from an eminent person, even if he follows dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a54a420cf6981b5be2e720ad> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3448]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Kourava! The three vargas522 are dependent on rajadharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a5516936296640b3f287ac74> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[567, 568]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Together with his brothers, Partha111 arranged the soldiers on their side into a vyuha.
112 O bull among the Bharata lineage! On discerning that he was stationed in that fashion and on seeing that his own forces were running away, your son113 used his manliness to restrain them.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a5553988a45cd83a020a553d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4242]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The Pandava is Kartavirya’s135 equal in the valour of his arms." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a55a507deda692f252f3dc32> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15317]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The wise one made him the general of the armies of both the yakshas and the rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a590000399a917ae8cc6ea55> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 52 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2248]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Women sung to them and the descendants of the Kurus went to sleep." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a5a399a3109f850cfa96817b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5722]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The amazed Shakra265 gave him a shakti266 and said, “Whoever you wish to kill among the gods, the asuras, humans, gandharvas, uragas and rakshasas with this weapon, will certainly be killed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a5aebe170b3086ed8f8267a7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7096]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Taking leave of all the mothers47 and circling them with respect, they said farewell to the citizens and set out for Varanavata." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a5b4f0b62221d6d0596b0a81> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9216, 9217]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """One of them49 became Baladeva and the second one that was black became Keshava.
Those ones who were like Shakra and were earlier confined in the mountain cavern are none other than the valorous Pandavas, while the Pandava Savyasachi50 is a part of Shakra.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a5c027079bb3494b1a644224> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1327]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kshatta29 Vidura, knowledgeable in every aspect of dharma, was in charge of the treasury." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a5c20c8dc00bae9abb494482> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1619]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ At these words, she told Krishna, the son32 of the Yadu lineage, ‘O immensely strong one! Please pardon Shishupala’s transgressions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a5e14a2a78cfbc3e4060dc61> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9021, 9023]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """” After the priest had spoken these words and was quiet, the king57 looked at the humble messenger and instructed Bhima, who was next to him, “King Drupada’s priest is worthy of respect and let him be given more than normal homage.
” O ruler of men! Bhima did as he had been instructed and he58 accepted the offerings and happily seated himself.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a5e853070c6df14d0c631910> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7547]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I support the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a6057249f4440ff914d2496a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9300]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, if the being is full of dharma, it obtains happiness in this world349 or in the next." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a6331d1d09bafe5d73120385> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5268]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Durjaya and Vikarna pierced Krishna’s son250 with five iron arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a6420eb5cc2b865cd1815d27> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4932, 4933, 4934, 4935]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """There Yogeshvara Sthanu Vrishadhvaja205 is always present himself.
One who goes there and worships the lord of the gods becomes successful.
Varuna’s tirtha Oujasa206 is resplendent in its own energy.
There Brahma, the gods and the rishis, rich in austerities, instated Guha207 as the general of the army of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a66ce65e2808bb3e77ca75a1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[430]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When the heads had been cut off, Maghavan71 was freed from his fever and happily went to heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a673d543a42b1f473ae0f77d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1976]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kamboja gave riches in the form of skins of eda,49 fine cat skins lined with gold, the best skins from deer, three hundred horses with parrot- like noses that were grey and of mixed colours and three hundred she- camels fattened with palm,50 pulses51 and nuts." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a67556aea4a9eb3830f192d5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2958]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In the midst of the Kurus, he said unhappily, “Devala240 has said that there are three stars241 for a man—offspring, deeds and learning, since these are the source of creation." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a68f0c4720db7e29b16c0d5e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7742, 7743, 7746]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He is now lying dead, killed by a powerful rakshasa.
He was pursued by the rakshasa with an upraised spear.
651 He was then swiftly killed by the rakshasa with the upraised spear.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a6bb323407e1e132194ec222> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2932]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Daksha’s daughters4 were Aditi, Diti, Danu, Kala, Anayu, Simhika, Muni, Krodha, Prava, Arishta, Vinata, Kapila and Kadru." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a6bd3c67d66cb59fc5b347ac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3977]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "She will choose a second husband at the time of sunrise, because it is not known whether the valiant Nala is dead or alive." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a6c3a0c029e07ab65fd4f391> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17125]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "14 Vrisha15 then recounted to him everything in detail, all that he had witnessed and the conversation that had taken place between them in the night." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a6d818bee00b0b8cd9814a0e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[456, 459]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """I will not offend the sight of those who have resorted to vanaprastha52 and dwell there with their families.
53 I will satisfy the ancestors and the gods with wild fruits, water and eloquent words.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a70233de43f63581113a2f77> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[904]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having multiplied myself through my powers of yoga, I am present in many forms, in agnihotras,7sattras8 and other sacrifices and rituals." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a70f4aa32f58e1d6c7913ca7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7898]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Drona heard that Rama11 wanted to give away all his riches." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a722bd6b7d9bff6b4fe4f85f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6974]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Seeing him32 humiliated and robbed of his riches and under his complete control, Drona remembered his earlier enmity with Drupada and said, “I have laid waste your kingdom and your capital." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a72476caf88c49d2975d66d5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7793, 7794]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He was given the supreme lordship over all subjects and made the upholder of all kinds of dharma.
When the sacrifice started, according to the proper rites, Mahadeva1056 honoured Vishnu and gave the rod, the protector of dharma, to him.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a7344b80afcf20fa2616aaf7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2209]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "460 Briefly, hear from me what is that kshetra, its nature and its transformation, and cause and effect within it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a741c34a5da219ad36514984> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13948]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kunti’s son was dexterous, swift and valiant and in a short instant, enveloped him51 with a net of arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a749b5e21da3f2721393c5cb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[210]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! There were many others who resided in the southern directions, preceptors from among the mlecchas26 and kings from the east and the north." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a75da7fbe899ae5fa2d376dd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2744]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“The daughter of the river was named Girika and the king49 made her his wife." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a789ef5fbc995d4bd062e097> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10109]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When there is a difference of opinion on this, Svayambhuva Manu53 has categorically stated, ‘The observance of rituals determines varna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a78cc14304075057d7e75c94> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6842]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That is the reason gold is the best ornament for the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a78e53290d46404611632019> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6541]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is in the east that Daksha’s women154 gave birth to subjects." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a7927e332606b327cf0e1666> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7026]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The thirty-three gods, the lords of the directions, Rudra, Dhatri, Vishnu, Yajna,155 Pushan, Aryama, Bhaga, Amsha, Mitra, the Sadhyas, the Vasus, Vasava, the Ashvins, the water, the wind, the sky, the moon, the nakshatra, the planets, the sun and all the separate objects that are offered to the gods156 went there to see Kumara, Agni’s son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a79487e9944cf9f047648272> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3353]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Purandara98 therefore told Menaka, “O, Menaka! You are the best of the celestial apsaras in your qualities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a79accf0d4e4fd64f12fccd7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10971]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "235 He grasped the sword, which was like the Destroyer, the sun, or the fire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a7ad70f523bb18f9e16046ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2400]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The tiger among men had been requested by Vishtarashrava316 himself, Dvaipayana, Devasthana317 and Jishnu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a7bbc5cf5bb5673d8200b40a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5839, 5840]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """823 Because of this, Shri824 was enraged with him and no longer dwelt with him, going instead to the chastiser of Paka.
825 O lord! He826 was tormented when he saw Shri with Purandara, but this was the consequence of his resentment and insolence.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a7c498d427fe221f50902e00> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7814]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They are certainly capable of dislodging the king of the gods from his seat." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a7ced1164250d9bb5ce992a7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16564]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Through her restrained words and worship of the gods, she satisfied her father-in-law." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a7ddb8ea49578a9f562844e1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18600]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This612 is difficult to be given up by those who are evil in their intelligence." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a7efd79c4bd3557c88277630> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6575]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But what can I do so that the powerful and blazing Shri does not abandon me?’ The radiant one907 was accomplished about dharma, artha and kama and knew about the precepts of rajadharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a7f544da9d9178b4e1b434be> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9186]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When the game of dice was over, he36 spoke to the weeping goddess, ‘Bring him here." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a7fb409b9326e9f4894098c2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 46 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2541]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "178 A brahmana must wear linen or cotton clothes, or deerskin, or garments that are dyed reddish brown." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a803447093f7f551f03d1867> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1171]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If we return from the battle without killing Dhananjaya, or if we retreat because we are afflicted by his weapons, those7 will be ours." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8035b1086662ae0d203ef3c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1214, 1215]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """25 ‘Then the great lord Hari26 abandoned his unparalleled feminine form and made them tremble by hurling many weapons at them.
On the shores of the salty ocean thus began the greatest of terrible battles between the gods and the demons.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8082a7059aafdf786bda464> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 131 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9928]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I am a son of the Pandavas and they never retreat from a battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a80867bd3a2e6d3d4955034a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8038]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I will ‘Y tell you about the qualities and fruits associated with rendering offerings to gods, yakshas, serpents, men, ghosts and rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a809319d394c8ba96d1200a6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7370]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They eat and find pleasure with the gods, the guests, the ancestors and their sons and grandsons there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a817fc060663a31258cb0651> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10031, 10032]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Having given them permission to leave in accordance with the proper form, the immensely radiant Pandava went to sleep on a well-made and divine bed.
O descendant of the Bharata lineage! He told Satvata84 about the tirthas, mountains, rivers and forests he had seen.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a81f09b45bf6973bec39d2c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14884]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I see you in your resplendence, stationed as the king of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a83422cdbefa3c99f3769189> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3758]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They instructed the soldiers that they should set out under a good nakshatra and on Dhruva’s day." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a83bf2cb4c27674da1e4b891> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3962]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Having been thus addressed, Maghavan148 agreed and set out with the assemblage of thirty gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a86130d39df1c70cfe25eff3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9296, 9297]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """” ‘After the Pandavas had taken a wife, Hari75 sent them many golden ornaments, adorned with pearls and lapis lazuli.
Madhava76 also sent them expensive garments from many regions, blankets, deer skins, jewels that were beautiful and soft, and expensive beds, seats, vehicles and vessels, adorned with diamonds and lapis lazuli.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a86d23f35dd6cd07d26b4b38> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11834]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was surrounded by thousands of rakshasas with distorted forms." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a87c7caa299c06d2e143285a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[168]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Among the Kurus and the Srinjayas, who are the ones who remain alive and who are dead?” ‘Sanjaya replied, “O king! Shantanu’s son28 was brought down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a87fd6a23fbe76a76f0739d9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5494]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! At this, Arjuna was enraged and unleashed the aindra267 weapon." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a880ce14f7e00da7a225e6c1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3464]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having seen everything with his divine sight, the illustrious one was pleased and said, “O fortunate one! What you have done secretly today, this act of union with a man without my sanction, is not against dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8852e671635c098c3fd53f0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4645]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was like Death and the Destroyer." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a885394998a79fcc031789b5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3809]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Or she is like the night of the full moon when the moon has been swallowed up by Rahu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8b6ad11394cbc48b5c588d8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5901]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Despite that, I have become evil-hearted and my lowly mind is spent on the evil chase of deer, deserted by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8b6dde774e3ce6a3ecb906b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24451]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When he had merged into the paramatman, Dhatri1239 collected his bones and constructed the vajra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8c56e8d9fb401142a591424> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2083]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rathas fell down from their chariots and elephant riders from their elephants." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8d036611f11a781d147a6d2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11152]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The extremely beautiful one among the gods430 then began to speak everything about the dharma of women." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8d5eb6d0c353d6db6e9446c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13913]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the large number of gods went to the grandfather and asked, ‘O lord! O god! Who is roaring like this? We cannot understand this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8d604a0e2ea1ed42d510fc0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[707]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is incapable of being defeated in battle by all the gods and the demons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8d74d687a4e50fe24b78944> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10151]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Having heard that Arjuna, the best of the Pandavas, had reached Indraprastha, supreme among cities, the pure-souled Pundarikaksha10 Madhava went there with Rama11 and all the other warriors and maharathas from among the Vrishnis and the Andhakas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8eb971c567d16a13ead7028> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14823]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king7 has gone east, Bhimasena south, Jaya8 west and the twins to the north." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8ee3cdc7577c155d4512a49> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[310]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "71 In Sambhava Parva is described the birth of various kings, Brahmanas and the sage Dvaipayana, the partial incarnations of the gods are recounted, the births of the daityas, danavas72 and powerful yakshas, and of nagas,73 snakes, gandharvas and birds and all the other diverse living creatures; the births of the great Vasus from the Bhagirathi and in the house of Shantanu and their subsequent ascent to heaven and the birth of Bhishma from their energy is described, his renunciation of the kingdom, his adoption of brahmacharya, his adherence to the vow, his protection of Chitrangada and after Chitrangada’s death, his protection of his younger brother,74 and his subsequent placing of Vichitravirya on the throne." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8fdb1e3abf7ae8edeec4d59> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10431, 10432]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """On seeing that the king of the gods was about to hurl the great lightning, the gods grasped all their respective weapons—King Yama his kaladanda,36 the god of wealth his shibika,37 Varuna his pasha,38 Shiva his vichakra,39 the two Ashvins luminiscent oshadhi,40 Dhata his dhanu,41 Jaya his musala,42 the immensely strong Tvashta a mountain, Amsha his shakti43 and the god of death44 his parashva.
45 Aryaman grasped a fearful parigha46 and walked around.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a8fedc6a56071678b4692827> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14760]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Shachi’s lord!169 He may be170 among camels, cows, asses or horses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a906cee175e35378cea95350> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[377]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Tumburu, Narada, Vishvavasu, Haha and Huhu63 went there and satisfied the foremost among immortals with different kinds of hymns." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a90a9a5347b346eb7f66b0e8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9560, 9563]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Those who steal100 from the sacred texts are against dharma.
All of them are the worst among men and are against dharma.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a90d6b93468e6e8ba1136822> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[97, 99]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """To become sacred, the asuras and the gods performed rites.
It is through sacrifices that the great-souled gods became even more powerful.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a92310a8a16e73173bc235bc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7641]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Vasudeva said, “Many kinds of acceptable and beneficial words were spoken by me and the rishis, but he289 did not accept them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a92df9e61b8db8a38b9e7e65> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[494]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O one who is like the gods! Tell me what you wish for." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a93123a3411364c0685609c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5950, 5951]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Clad in golden armour and armed with maces, the Kaleyas402 rushed at the thirty gods, like mountains on fire.
Unable to withstand the force of this onslaught, the thirty gods broke their ranks and fled in fear.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a947f3906741cb4524bc79be> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[561]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” On hearing this, he6 began to worship the Ashvins with verses from the Rig Veda." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a9528e6ed1e3c871119543c1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5636]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "59 It was an insult to them that Krishna60 was brought to the assembly hall and Duhshasana and Karna addressed her in harsh words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a95992e03402d87b8e2f9d70> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9270]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As was appropriate, they asked him about the welfare of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a962723119d72f2fd40c0a36> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1975]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A person who know the exact truth about the attributes and the qualities and everything about the gods, is cleansed of all sin and is freed from his bonds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a96faff94d26d64f4d8ed0c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9394]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that the son of the wind10 was distressed and extremely enraged, Dasharha smiled and replied to the son of the gambler." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a987aa5c0b8e578a76ca295d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13984, 13990]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ Having thus addressed him, Krishna brought him58 down from his chariot, though he sighed like a serpent and his eyes were red with rage.
O descendant of the Bharata lineage! When its59 fierce energy was dispelled, the intelligent Bhima looked resplendent, like the sun that arises at the end of the night.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a9915fcecfeaa3b3a68504fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12370]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Without any pride, one should worship the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a9c53193ce8873e9dc39cdab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1628]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Chapter 1973(42) uta11 said, “On hearing of the reappearance and departure of his forefathers, the learned King Janamejaya was delighted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a9d5506ac3b32d1088d6fdf4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1056]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having left all that, and all the earlier difficulties, behind, the bulls among the Kurus132 only wish for conciliation with the Kurus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a9d5b0f5547557c09729e5ef> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9991, 9993]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The lord consumed those rakshasas, with their horses, charioteers and chariots, with his arrows.
He severely consumed one akshouhini of nairritas88 with his arrows, like the god Maheshvara burning down the city of Tripura in the sky.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a9d9bd14fe25f981a90518f7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[426]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Apparently obedient to the king71 and maintaining a middle position,72 we will protect ourselves and wait to see many weaknesses emerge in the Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/a9dafedceaae5ac85dd2316d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11143]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rathas attacked even more powerfully, astride their chariots." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aa1c97f6ed614987aa6cffcf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8478, 8479]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """For twelve years, the king had been swallowed through the energy of Vashishtha’s son, like the sun is swallowed by the one who swallows104 at the time of an eclipse.
Thus freed from the rakshasa, the king reddened the great forest with his energy, like the sun illuminates the evening105 clouds.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aa367865014570b46d9d8b0a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5517]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ When Dharmaraja52 spoke these words, the brahmana replied to Dharmaraja." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aa3fabe9d3e11328f637cb38> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8065]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Stationing himself in front of Bhishma, he411 grasped another bow and shot twenty-five arrows at Arjuna’s chest and arms." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aa5d556c8bf536a7b784c2ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13207]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They swiftly went to the lord who was the general of the gods and said, ‘O son! Without any reason and driven by anger, our divine husbands have abandoned us." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aa923f43fa79d4752d09dd2c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3112, 3115]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """121 In the battle, the atiratha122 looked as beautiful as Janardana.
The lords of the earth looked at his body, though even the gods found it difficult to glance at it.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aaa9926aa06c80bc8dd5c884> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1019]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among gods! Truthfully, there is greater pleasure in being a woman." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aab6e886c2f484940230220a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24356]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the one who is engaged in the welfare of gods, men and the universe." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aac63bb4becfad97f9a69d6a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5634]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Meanwhile, urged by the dharma of time, I obtained the world of the ancestors62 and was brought before Dharmaraja." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aad21a9f3018dff13a43b2ac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7903]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Severely struck, Karna wavered a little." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aae2d6f66b7137097a7cecaf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[80]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "These will ensure welfare for Ajatashatru15 and also ensure welfare for King Duryodhana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aaf9e6adee026b667101b795> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[986]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king50 was then famous for the protection of his kingdom and in accordance with dharma, did whatever was consistent with dharma, kama and artha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aafe2ef5a01141cb01d4f0e4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 102 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7527]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There was lamentation in the army of the sons of Pandu and they lost their senses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ab16ffb081fa5556433cd7d5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6975]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "We have heard that this is like making gifts of all the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ab1ee89ed9ba856cc312f78f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10456]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "For the gods who reside in the household, one must always offer flowers and sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ab3575b4227c2ace0bd0fe48> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8442, 8444]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O best among the Kuru lineage! This path will lead you to Sougandhika forest703 and the grove of the lord of riches,704 guarded by yakshas and rakshasas.
A man must specially honour the gods there.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ab4d15e6b74febd60499e7df> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 57 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4847, 4850, 4851]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """If a person touches a tree full of flowers or a tree full of fruits and gives it to a brahmana, he obtains an excellent house that is full of many jewels and beautiful women.
If a man gives garlands, incense, fragrances, unguents, objects required for a bath and wreaths to a brahmana, he is without disease and obtains a place in the worlds meant for kings.
O king! A man who gives a house full of seeds and beautiful beds to a brahmana, obtains an excellent and auspicious house that is full of many jewels.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ab5a117f8082b283237b3302> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[43]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Krishna said, “It is known to all of you how Yudhishthira was defeated by Soubala4 in a deceitful game of dice and lost his kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ab5ad427ec9727f3f2d0a7f9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14962]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Why are you abandoning him now? Is it because of his acts or because of mine?’ ‘“Shri replied, ‘Dhata and Vidhata191 cannot control me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ab5b895e045da4a010ddf3ee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9506]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O ruler of the people! The Dasharhas48 are powerful and numerous." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ab7a489f0241de80f2e68538> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17978]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It has been the eternal view that all the four modes represent paths followed by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ab7bd4a5b09a2282a46d8a89> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9111]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is on a supreme seat and is served by the daughters of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ab8ba0a263c1cc9280ebdaf6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1103]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because of his respect for me, Hridika’s son100 desisted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ab93293ffb6fef1fbd2de096> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5414]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Koushika Vishvamitra335 performed a sacrifice there with Shakra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/abba7a4824830046a2bfa97b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4893]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On the command of Vasudeva, supreme among men, Pritha198 accepted him in her arms." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/abd11c0f0df779454cb39431> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2463]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Tryambaka297 touched the immensely energetic Phalguna and everything that was impure in his body, was immediately destroyed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/abee17b1680696875a86e3ce> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5669]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Insolence gave birth to vanity and vanity gave birth to anger." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/abf2ced2e109168dc8f4ce00> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15090]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "While they showered arrows on him like monsoon clouds, Madri’s son slew them with one large arrow32 each." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/abfa6686cfb2d920c66a922c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6007]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They worshipped the unvanquished Vaikuntha405 Narayana and sought refuge with him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac033ba9afb8af437960967a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """After Drona’s death, Karna is made the overall commander.
Bhima kills Kshemadhurti (the king of Kuluta), Satyaki kills Vinda and Anuvinda from Kekaya, Droupadi’s sons kill Chitrasena and Chitra from Abhisara, Arjuna kills Dandadhara and Danda from Magadha, Ashvatthama kills Pandya, and Arjuna kills large numbers of the enemy (primarily the samshaptakas1 ).
On the seventeenth day, on Karna’s request, Duryodhana asks Shalya to be Karna’s charioteer.
Bhima kills Karna’s son, Satyasena and some of Duryodhana’s brothers, Kripa kills Suketu from Panchala, and Arjuna, Bhima and Karna kill many of the enemy.
Uttamouja kills Sushena, Karna’s son.
Karna kills many warriors on the Pandava side and, in an inconsistent statement, Satyaki kills Sushena, Karna’s son.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac1842958d1ecb5f189d8495> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1914]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "90 O venerable one! On seeing that Bhagadatta was shattering the army and on also being challenged, he91 was caught in two minds and thought, ‘What is the best course of action for me? Should I return here, or should I go to Yudhishthira?’ O extender of the Kuru lineage! Thus did Arjuna reflect in his mind and decided that he should kill the samshaptakas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac1bb8bf7a1be2bf28900008> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13111]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Tell Drona that Sharadvati’s86 son has been killed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac1e17eb93215b154abc3c2b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[315]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The warrior killed many enemies in the battle and was then slain by Drona." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac1e7f2f6e55fbbd3e2f6cd1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4600]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O best of the Bharatas! The army of the Bharatas541 presents a miserable sight." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac2792cc5378fb066086355b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5507]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘The fires that Sahadeva lit along the Yamuna were one crore356 and the gifts were hundreds of thousands." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac279f67af5e5393c5ef691b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3210, 3211]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O bull among the Bharata lineage! Kiriti’s99 soul is beyond measure.
In return, he struck Bhishma with twenty-five arrows, Kripa with nine, Drona, tiger among men, with sixty arrows, Vikarna with three, Artayani100 with three and the king101 with five arrows.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac2d4aa6bf6c4fc78e4a2d13> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4588]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Bhagavan1 replied, “O mighty-armed one! I am present." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac341edaca48ee8326a0ab9b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6694]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Arjuna’s heirs490 became very angry at Rama." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac5b12d6902001d518c23d18> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3764]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Varshneya and Jivala166 will always follow your instructions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac6ae797d3b78c8d96608963> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3206, 3207]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Shantanu’s son, Bhishma, was protected by warriors who were led by Saindhava97 and those from the east, Souvira and Kekaya and encountered him with force.
Who other than the grandfather of the Kurus and the two rathas Drona and Vaikartana98 are capable of withstanding the wielder of the Gandiva in battle? ‘“O great king! Bhishma, the grandfather of the Kouravas, pierced Arjuna with seventy-seven iron arrows.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac88650f73b0fbed82eb5d34> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15069]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Attack." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ac961d72047f8b3f0f67c71f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3275]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He awoke when one yama was left of the night." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/acb029eefb40ee6b2e7300ff> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9080]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If a person only eats ghee on every thirteenth day and if he continuously does this for a year, he obtains the fruits of a sacrifice performed by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/acb4c419242f51fb378e0c90> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[703]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among the masses of gods! You decide on a way for him to be freed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/acd3c33ca0048391b00e5f62> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22214, 22215]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He always talked about the conduct of the gods.
O son! Because, Krishna’s1010 matted hair blazed through those austerities, even today, it is seen to possess the complexion of the fire.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/acde39ac9c006afb04040d22> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7000]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Partha! Abandon the thought797 that only befits a coward." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ace267a5307b50c584cf9685> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8944]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He touched with his hands the feet of King Ajamidha46 Yudhishthira and said, “I am Krishna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ace2c7898fcfebeb7b47338d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10799]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O venerable one! Having been thus pierced in the battle by Dharma’s son, Madhava151 trembled with rage and afflicted him with seven arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ace4707904fb70cbec91a0e7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2177]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Desire and anger are like two large fish that are caught in a small net and lead to the destruction of wisdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad047f1e3a9201d68fa4894a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9826]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ CHAPTER 1108(131) ‘Sanjaya said, “After his son65 was killed by Satyaki, though he had decided to fast to death, Somadatta became extremely angry and spoke these words to Satyaki." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad0b8c8a1af38c0aa485c4f5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10908]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The god of gods replied, ‘You will have a female child, who will be male." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad16dc9c45a56172b483fb8d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17292, 17293]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """That is the reason the Creator ordained the practice of moneylending.
One must remain established in the pledges that have been made to the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad26731a7b1e489f49634294> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1317]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“Everything that the aged one9 has said about the Pandavas is full of dharma and artha, is appropriate, and has been argued with reason." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad37aa3fdeeee7e71072ceed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6609]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, Satyaki had gone on ahead and he220 attacked Bhima." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad459dfcb0bbf74e99d33f70> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3153]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There are those who are householders, devoted to worshipping gods and guests and following the conduct of pigeons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad5416402f0bad66d8069f89> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6923]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having countered Kritavarma, who was like the thousand-armed one239 and like an ocean that cannot be agitated, Satyaki left." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad5e0810d436cfa5f3915952> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4185]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! In that encounter, as if he was smiling, the king179 sliced off Bhima’s radiant bow from his hand with three sharp arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad6d8ed9016e534fedf3cff2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[565]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let us appoint him king of the gods and the lord of the thirty gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad84b95bfcc24c54360cd89f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3152, 3153]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ On beholding Krishna and Pandava31 and Kouravya Duryodhana, stationed with the club in his hand, Rama said, ‘Since I departed, forty-two days have elapsed.
I left at the time of Pushya and have returned at the time of Shravana.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad86131bcbebf113117773f6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[657]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Soma is futile unless it is rendered as an offering." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad8633e90db99c05bd5c828a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5291, 5292, 5297]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Under Svati, if one gives riches, one obtains the auspicious worlds that one desires and also obtains great fame.
Under Vishakha, if one gives a bull, a milk-yielding cow, a basket, a wagonload of paddy and garments, then one pleases the ancestors and the gods.
Under Anuradha, if a man fasts and gives embroidered cloth and garments, then he obtains greatness in heaven for one hundred yugas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad8c6c45cdadf3336d32d6ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6489, 6491, 6493]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He told the immensely radiant Vishvamitra in gentle words, ‘What dakshina150 will I give you for having performed the task of my preceptor? Man’s rites only succeed when dakshina has been given.
Dakshina is the fruit of a sacrifice, obtained in heaven, and is therefore said to constitute peace.
What will I give my preceptor?’ The illustrious Vishvamitra knew that he had already been honoured by his service and repeatedly asked him151 to go away.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad8fdcb36c386bd71b765853> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1132]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Having thus conquered many countries and extracting riches from them, Pavana’s powerful son41 then reached the Louhitya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ad9c37cc70ed50b78852612b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15284]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Riches, objects of pleasure, status and prosperity are all temporary and uncertain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/adac80fb338e9b28163327e3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 24 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1202]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Kouravya! Hearing this pleasant news about the destruction of our enemy, you should be content and can decide on what should be done next." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/add04c8b3f5aa7549e416ebb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12866]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the gods! I desire that an invincible one like you should be my husband." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ade12c45bfe064b5427f42f8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4160]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Chapter 1392(64) ‘Bhishma said, “O Pandava! The dharma of the four ashramas, the dharma of tribes642 and that of the rulers of the worlds are based on the dharma of kshatriyas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ade21c2b77cc7a03febeb9ae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5052, 5053]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O you who are as valorous as Vasava208 himself! A slender-waisted wife of one of the vasus saw the supreme cow, which belonged to the sage Vashishtha and was capable of fulfilling every desire, roaming in the forest.
She was amazed at its conduct, power and riches and showed it to Dyou,209 who had eyes like those of a bull.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae0cc9ad1e966b7c078e2f6b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13214]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The terrible battle that raged was like that between the gods and the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae19d2f04e44edd19222e799> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2605]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The pure one352 joined his hands in salutation and spoke to Dasharha Pundarikaksha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae1c55a940fd09ae96c966d5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[172]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Do you listen to words of dharma and artha from the aged, who always know what brings artha? Are honey and ghee given to brahmanas to increase crops, cattle, flowers, fruit, dharma and artha? Do you always give all the artisans materials, implements and wages for a period up to four months? O great king! Do you examine the work and praise the creator? Do you honour good ones among good people? O bull among the Bharatas! O lord! Do you follow all the sutras, especially those about elephants, horses and chariots? O bull among the Bharatas! Are sutras on the science of arms, instruments and architecture of cities regularly studied in your house? O unblemished one! Are you familiar with all the weapons, brahma danda62 and all poisons that destroy enemies? Do you protect your kingdom against fear from fire, snakes, predators, disease and rakshasas? Knowing the ways of dharma, do you nurture like a father the blind, the dumb, the crippled, the deformed, the orphaned and mendicant ascetics?”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Having heard these words from the best of the brahmanas, the great-souled bull among the Kurus happily bowed down and worshipped his feet." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae2811266328be75c83482f5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13360]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Heaven appeared there in personified form and spoke these words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae2c864d50ad945aa08cd773> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3303]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Through their austerities, knowledge and humility, they can be successful in obtaining everything that exists in the world of men and gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae2ff815523a97137af2bdb4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[709, 710]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O gods! You must be patient and endure him for some time.
’ Having heard the pure and true words of Vishnu, which were like amrita, all the masses of gods, the preceptors86 and the gods went to the region where Shakra had hidden himself, anxious with fear.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae3bb26186cb71b967ebe07e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3450]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! The Kalinga surrounded Bhimasena with lances, clubs, swords, spikes, scimitars121 and battleaxes." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae3bc754dc4275fc70d12a24> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[593]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“On approaching near, the lotus-eyed Krishna4 was terrified and closed her eyes in fear at the sight of something never seen before." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae3ec762bfd7bc59920b2521> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1293]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those bulls among men could have slain even the gods with the force of their weapons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae5c18fbb3c2e3b466a9f187> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11259]" ;
        mbh:sourceText ") Prana;733 (." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae6e2b476dd50964fc0d882f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8318]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He regained his wife, who had been lost like the knowledge of the Vedas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae9abeef4c60e7160b78d9ee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13850]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son! These, Kanva, the son of rishi Medhatithi, Barhishada and the saptarshis24 who created the three worlds are in the east." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae9adeff7fd044601676fb59> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6166]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” An extraordinary event occurred as soon as Vrikodara300 was born." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ae9e7ed0c476b2d247dec193> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5458]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When I was taking him across the river, the best of sages felt desire for me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aed354f39daf8bb2134b7ff0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 89 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6509]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The great army of the sons of Dhritarashtra were generally made to retreat." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aedab9881771b20a2ec4e200> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5514]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods do not shower rain in a country that is without a king." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aef49651cb85c2ac9e7cf54c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3876]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O fortunate one! Your waters will change to blood, acceptable only to the foremost among rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aef5c95cc718cf719018eb8d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18584]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Though Mithila610 is blazing, nothing that belongs to me is burning." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aefb8616570e969c281b1733> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 118 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9794]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I was not a brahmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/aefdb4dee0239f373e800f77> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3422]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But I think the gods have ordained this for me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af0205b3f0304de775c98474> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1560]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Marichi’s illustrious son91 again told her, “Take good care when you bear these auspicious seeds in your womb." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af0778dea56e914be3cbe697> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[531]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let all the gods accept their respective shares and receive the soma that has been extracted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af0a3232df33370b95bce48b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[273]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then Richika4 and his other ancestors appeared before this bull among Brahmanas and said, “Calm down, refrain, be pacified." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af0c00b1f93a020aba1c3bc0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6251]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ The rakshasa, terrible in form, agreed to these words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af122a89a87b7d5b61c86ded> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11583]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The mighty-armed rakshasa approached and smiling, flung the head, with a distorted face and dreadful hair, onto the chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af1b3f4dbe6a60b9965b2b89> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9789]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods, the danavas, the rakshasas, the yakshas, the asuras and the gandharvas, together with masses of birds and serpents, will not be able to withstand you in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af1f8ff56bf07e362dc9b891> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[50]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You should now perform many kinds of sacrifices, with large quantities of dakshina, satisfying the gods with soma and the ancestors with svadha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af2e73a46bf5e87523f928f9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1779]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that Vishvaksena255 had been pierced, the immensely strong Partha Dhananjaya struck Satyasena with sharp arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af2ef91c34af56e68da91ebf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8073]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It was covered with blue grass and frequented by the gods and the gandharvas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af31e5cf7bddd6c0aea2c32f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12431]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Janardana! When we are alive, and so are you, how could Hidimba’s son have encountered his death in the clash with the son of a suta? O Krishna! While all of us looked on, and so did Savyasachi, he22 blunted us and killed Bhimasena’s son, the immensely strong rakshasa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af3505bdae16a1a90cc63cd9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24410]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because of this, the gods are prospering and we are suffering." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af453e86760f31e3248fc3a9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5340]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’” ‘Narada said, “Having spoken these words and taking his317 leave, the illustrious rishi Pulastya, pleased and in a delighted frame of mind, immediately disappeared." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af55c242c5e0b7d6ca0f9ff9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8190]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Puru’s descendant worshipped Anshuman53 when he arose, with devotion, obedience, selflessness and purity." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af6b32708d4dae7534eafe8a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3124]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "33 He is just like a child of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af6e103dd61ce92736a7eb75> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20676]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That is the reason all those qualities are seen to originate with Prakriti." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af869623ae1da7701a857efe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3688]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The daughter of the Vrishni lineage262 summoned Virata’s daughter and told her, ‘O Virata’s daughter! O illustrious one! One should not lament." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/af92aa59bb6951b4c1a01264> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2532]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Maghavan159 himself applauded Pandava’s swiftness with weapons and so did the gandharvas and apsaras who had assembled there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/afb8564badfd834f316881f7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7274]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Arjuna is greater than what Jamadagni’s son257 has said." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/afc15d6e445907852cac010f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5631]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It was as if in all the parts of the country, Krita Yuga249 had arrived." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/afc1ed5425a6bf0ac2d9e9eb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3686]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O invincible one! Casting aside her sorrow V and with the permission of the king,260 Bhima and the twins, who are like Yama, the one who knows about dharma261 then began to think about his funeral rites and gave away large quantities of gifts." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/afd04e1032ca6656ea31c971> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[790]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You should not be the equal of the asuras or the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b0142b087a27e826b195f0ba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1103]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Swiftly release Sairandhri." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b01dac9de0e7ff10eea25c9f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[934]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Accept the gods’ share, and your own, when they are offered into your mouth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b01e1fd51b05d6028826f07b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4438]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When Brihadashva had left, he198 heard from wise ones, brahmanas and ascetics that Savyasachi Partha was engaged in terrible austerities, surviving only on air." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b02183d317d5cf37ce8f7030> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4655]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Look, our path to the world of the gods has become visible." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b029af83ceb1a042d60f7d46> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2535]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Overcome by anger, he confronted Partha in that battle and showered him with arrows, like Parjanya160 showering rain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b03508183d9208079ad64da9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7718]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A rakshasa with terrible eyes, fearful in form, arose." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b039f22ed71eb7405b78f733> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4683]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This was after the great Tarakamaya battle208 had been fought." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b044a7437f7e01ea5264d0d0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2823]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Goutama’s semen fell on a clump of reeds and from that were born twins, Kripa66 of immense strength and Ashvatthama’s mother." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b0498d83fb4768da82b8283b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1579]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Darkening the worlds with a great storm of dust created by his wings, the giant bird overwhelmed the gods, and overcome with that dust, the gods were deluded." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b058b82188fd87a5dd5c1ebc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9918]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This is on the assumption that you are repenting your wicked deed and are looking towards dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b0652089e33c8f3c9dbb8229> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25639]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "After some time, when he was seated, Shachi’s lord1371 asked him, ‘O brahmana rishi! O unblemished one! Have you seen anything wonderful? O brahmana rishi! You wander amidst the mobile and immobile objects of the three worlds, always curious." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b06b2fa38cf1dd40077dfb09> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10134]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kunti’s son lived there for a year and the lord spent the last part of his period5 in Pushkara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b072df3e6bc85b2a4de495b0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5802]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was like the Destroyer at the time of the destruction of a yuga." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b07e16ab4b1a000404500541> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3702]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That powerful king was known as Chakravarti126 and Sarvabhouma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b095431b39f324184619a140> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 59 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3754]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O original lord! With the brahman having been destroyed, dharma has also been destroyed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b0ca420de0a9edd062bedbcd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8856]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If I have severed your arm then, that is not against dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b0d681bf5c2294a0e40f4064> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[539]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Following the ordinances laid down in the sacred texts, he cheerfully worshipped the king of the gods with the best of honours." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b0d6901af5d80b88f8d302ad> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3945, 3946]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Cheerfully, the lord of the thirty gods returned to heaven.
O descendant of the Bharata lineage! O supreme among kings! Namuchi’s head was submerged in those waters and he118 obtained many eternal worlds that grant every object of desire.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b0db6bd3999f822c705d413c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2503]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O venerable one! It was as if five-headed serpents had been slain by Garuda." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b0e44a5885bf04607c22f6e9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1280]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kounteya32 blazed in anger and he rushed towards the enemy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b10815ce87103855649acab0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[946]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king who was the descendant of the Kourava lineage78 was initiated there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b10acaf2f89d5cf71d39e0cb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9415]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“He joined his hands in salutation, showed a great deal of honour and told Koushika, ‘O, brahmana! What do you wish to do here in the night?’ Vishvamitra assured Matanga86 and replied, ‘I am hungry and have almost lost my life." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b10e1822e421b3efe94bc00e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7291, 7292]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The ancestors and the gods are not pleased at such oblations.
Some people should be barred from places where oblations are being offered—chandalas, shvapakas, those attired in yellowish-red garments, those with leprosy, those who are outcasts, those who have killed a brahmana, a brahmana born from an inferior lineage197 and those who are the relatives of those who are outcasts.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b11b2b426aa00c48b28121a0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2937]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods themselves were tormented by the force of these austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b12a11794436a7cb2108eba1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4672]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The one whose soul was immeasurable34 invoked the brahmastra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b153f9cafdb18055554c83f9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1913]" ;
        mbh:sourceText ") Mahat;956 (." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b15a7da23dc05a1568ce71bf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[450]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is the one who punished the two yavana14 kings Mura and Naraka and now, with unlimited powers like Varuna, is the king of the west." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b15da02b78a8acfc88b0ba4f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 14 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1324]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘The two rishis said, “The maharathas who have fallen down earlier were knowledgeable about many weapons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b16512c8e7f53406bcaea6ae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14388]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Gandhari’s son! O lord of the earth! In your sight and in the presence of your army, the suta’s son94 was frightened of the gandharvas and fled from the field of battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b168a125a4b1261e4c75a09b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13044]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then the strongest of the strong saw his father Agni approach and together with the group of mothers, he257 received his worship." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b170ff7a9c263323b73401be> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[715]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That great encounter was like that between the armies of gods and asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b17498610892da6b652f2c0d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17381, 17382]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O son! Fortunate are the ones who will see you crawling around on the ground, uttering inarticulate words and covered in dust.
O son! Fortunate are those who will see you become a youth, like a lion with a mane, in the forests of the Himalayas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b1a6e44bcc5f66bbfadeefed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6548, 6549]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """In an encounter, both of them were the equals of Kartavirya743 and Dasharatha’s son.
Both of them possessed valour that was like Vishnu’s bravery and both were Bhava’s744 equal in a fight.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b1aefcf62de1c4af5944e36b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11089]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those who deviate from their vows and ordinances are said to become Brahma- rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b1b06d0e1141bbe08b501d93> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16503]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This is the ashrama of vanaprastha, followed by those who are not distressed from observing vows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b1c90c6e004ce8683af6b4cc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6853]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son! The gods performed a great sacrifice of varuni." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b1ce00e562208ef996e9131d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9158]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If a person eats only one meal a day, that too on every twenty-seventh day and if he offers oblations into the fire for an entire year, he obtains great fruits and is worshipped in the world of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b1cf4673f277ee34f82c32c8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[914]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Kouravya! It was my absence from Anarta58 that led to all your misfortunes from gambling." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b1d0cad93c8607f0e4caaaa2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20829, 20835, 20838]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Both840 have been said to be destructible and perishable.
Mahat and the other qualities are respectively generated.
The qualities merge into its quality and the single one that remains is Prakriti.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b1de0f314f6ed6892faed682> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13207, 13208, 13214]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Vows and good conduct are truth.
Om is truth.
Heaven is established in truth.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b1e647858edc544e973a5a65> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8443]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let Karna and Arjuna be like Rama53 and Janardana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b1efa8f1f0d80ddd67b7f050> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2845]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Arjuna’s Gandiva, Krishna’s chakra and Tarkshya and the ape on the standards382 only generate fear among cowards." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b1f656113ab2e9e9f072b2d1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7994]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Kounteya669 looked at her." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b21e13f778aa31d792744edb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2408, 2410]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """332 Fortitude, understanding, permanence and humility were the staffs.
The guardians of the world, the lords of the gods, the water, the dead and wealth,333 were made the horses.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b247167f7c86cb78c9789636> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11742]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Since both the worlds had been taken away from them, the gods were distressed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b24df5d3dee5a0ca7dd42c9e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12907, 12908]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Having performed the sacrifice in accordance with the prescribed rites, the great-souled ones243 offered oblations to all the gods into the well-kindled fire.
The Adbhuta fire, the bearer of oblations, was summoned from the sun’s circle.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b2505916884807a9923c5a45> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2215]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Therefore, Soubhadra’s142 powerful son came to be known as Parikshit." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b26620ca607ab23e53841a24> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5378, 5380]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """I can also renounce the kingdom of the gods, or anything that is greater than both of these.
The earth can give up its fragrances, the water can give up its juices, light can give up its diverse forms, wind can give up its sense of touch, the sun can give up its radiance, the smoke-crested flame can give up its heat, the sky can give up its sounds, the moon can give up its cool rays, the slayer of Vritra233 can give up his valour, the god of dharma can give up dharma, but I can never give up the truth.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b26d21abf599751e9daec828> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2075, 2076]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """140 Those great-souled ones behave like the gods in heaven.
They are said to move upwards and like the gods, can create.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b2763daa6a35bb2751871d70> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[381, 383]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """This wonderful parva with diverse meanings is known by those good at numbers as one with fifty-nine chapters102 and 3220 shlokas, composed by the great sage who wished to spread the fame of the Kuru lineage.
Once the sons of Pritha103 had withdrawn, the warriors Kritavarma, Kripa and the son of Drona104 came to the field of battle in the evening and saw the intolerant King Duryodhana lying on the ground, his thighs broken and his body covered with blood.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b27920724152481db3e4904e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3304]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A rakshasa named Kalmashapada433 was about to be submerged in a pond and said, “Begging is filth for a kshatriya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b28712749f2057a6052eab86> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9366]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Sharadvata8 is a giant fish." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b299c9303de7c81841a24286> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15013]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They are named Nanda and Upananda." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b29f233cb506a3541a278bf1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23213]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They always knew the truth about what had been laid down for the gods and the ancestors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b2a1252fd1729022eb187e2a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7716]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Jamadagni said, ‘Let the person who has stolen the lotuses study in a prohibited way, let his friends eat at his funeral ceremonies230 and let shudras eat at his funeral ceremonies." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b2b3f5324ab6367b2a3cdd28> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4533]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "173 He is self-resplendent and because he controls174 the gods, he is known as Damodara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b2c5e8c7490b9fb60e1b340f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8762]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The kings Brihanta, Manimana and the valiant Dandadhara, Sahadeva, Jayatsena, Meghasandhi of Magadha, Virata and his two sons Sankha and Uttara, Vardhakshemi, Susharma, King Senabindu, Abhibhu with his sons Sudamna and Suvarchasa, Sumitra, Sukumara, Vrika, Satyadhriti, Suryadhvaja, Rochamana, Nila, Chitrayudha, Amshumana, Chekitana, the immensely powerful Shrenimana, Chandrasena, the powerful son of Samudrasena, Jalasamdha, the father and son Vidanda and Danda, Poundraka, Vasudeva, the valorous Bhagadatta, Kalinga, Tamralipta, the king of Pattana, the maharatha Shalya, king of Madra with his sons, the brave Rukmagandha and Rukmaratha, the Kourava Somadatta and his three maharatha sons Bhuri, Bhurishrava and Shala, Sudakshina, Kamboja, the Kourava Dridhadhanva, Brihadbala, Sushena, Ushinara’s son Shibi, Samkarshana, Vasudeva, Rukmini’s brave son Samba, Charudeshna, Sarana, Gada, Akrura, Satyaki, the immensely powerful Uddhava, Hridika’s son Kritavarma, Prithu, Viprithu, Viduratha, Kanka, Samika, Saramejaya, the brave Vatapati, Jhilli, Pindaraka, the brave Ushinara, all famous as descended from the Vrishni lineage; Bhagiratha, Brihatkshetra, Jayadratha, the king of Sindhu, Brihadratha, Bahlika, the maharatha Shrutayu, Uluka, King Kaitava, Chitrangada, Subhangada, the patient king of Vatsa, the king of Kosala." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b2d1277e12a362c419c81ffe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2538]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 650(54) Vaishampayana said, ‘He161 arrived with great speed, showering a great net of arrows, like clouds charged with rain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b2e9a2bcc006667bd2c34d67> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6170]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "315 Protected by his mother, he grew up in the world of the nagas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3238615c900980c9c4e3b46> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9981]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O maternal uncle! Kill the Kounteyas, like the son of the fire86 against the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3252667f7900ea8efbc029d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[916, 918]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """114 In their presence, even the lord of the Maruts115 would have been unable to kill them.
Having caused that extremely great carnage of men among the Pandavas, those maharathas116 met each other and exclaimed, ‘This was fortunate.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b32746ec7f3dba125ece173b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3046, 3047]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """A mortal one who causes displeasure to the gods wishes for death.
O beautiful and unblemished one! Therefore, save me by choosing from the supreme among the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3534af3438e2eab19708752> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6720, 6721, 6722]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He satisfied the king of the gods and gave the earth to the officiating priests.
O lord of the earth! He constructed a golden altar that was ten vyamas491 long and nine in height and gave it to the great-souled Kashyapa.
O king! With Kashyapa’s permission, the brahmanas divided it into many pieces and they492 thus came to be known as Khandavayanas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b35da44eb1b2d538c7423567> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[63]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "After making an agreement15 with the Pandavas and persuading them and their followers to turn back, Madhusudana Krishna then left for his own city, in glory like Purandara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b35da68f9a50d9eabd3fbe6b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[332, 333, 334]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Having obtained divine weapons for his elder brother, Savyasachi85 battled the Nivatakavachas of Hiranyapura.
Partha86 then returned to his brothers in Gandhamadana.
In the cattle expedition, Kiriti87 fought a battle with the gandharvas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b363d47961cfa69b015329ee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1998, 1999]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He will be like the king of the gods in his radiance.
But protect him from the king of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3654a271d90a255297e3302> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23265]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was famous as Akhandala’s1104 friend and was devoted to Hari Narayana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3688bc392e25fa58ffa5a9f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3036]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "38 O king! These are the classes of the gods, recited in sequence." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b375f7f60526cf2a3aaf9fc4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16003]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You alone are guilty of forcibly abducting Sita." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b39d781f61ecb23204c6e02d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7838]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Tread carefully." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3b5bd1f010e97bcdbf14e11> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 157 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10692]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Envy flows from desire and rivalry." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3d1b0557b32c9d4aabad21f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13979, 13980]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """To pacify the narayana weapon, Nara and Narayana56 forcefully dragged Bhima away, together with all his weapons.
While he was being dragged away, maharatha Kounteya57 continued to roar loudly and this fanned the extremely invincible and fierce weapon of Drona’s son.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3d314ec14dc209e49a29e46> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7726]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "We have heard that whatever is seen in the judicial process is dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3e5a0609b701eb8edb53633> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14419, 14427]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He is the one who bears oblations to the gods with his hands.
I bow down before the supreme among the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3f24115f368c11e3dbf15bc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[612]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Today, after a long time, the gods have granted me the wish that I have had." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3f4a3152e0975585a44742d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[800]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Surely the arya21 does not know the difficulties Dhananjaya has to confront, or those that Ajatashatru22 is immersed in, having become addicted to evil gambling." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3f6fda1f1242aee6ad969f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[115]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having thought for some time, in a voice that was distracted and choking with tears, he19 said, ‘King Duryodhana was immensely strong and the only brave one." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3f888bd53a07e064d5d774b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6523]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the gods! Milk, curd and ghee are pure." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b3ff3644fa89d8923df9e0a5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10802]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The stealing of gold, the theft of a brahmana’s property, living a life of pleasure, the drinking of liquor205 and sexual intercourse with women one should not have intercourse with are sins." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b4047f99de667c8d3e93d99a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9844]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The Pandava59 was unable to enter the room." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b40b85626ca87af83fdb25cc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5614]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Borne on the best of white horses, they urged them in the battle, looking for the wicked one." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b40dd569c062da81e67216e7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9974]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Therefore, when he376 is satisfied, the ancestors and the gods are also satisfied." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b41db5207986b5fec2130457> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2831, 2832, 2833]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Through the curse of the gods, the son of the king of Gandhara69 became the enemy of virtue and a destroyer of beings.
The other70 became Duryodhana’s mother.
Both71 were skilled in material pursuits.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b42c038eb47641dcdd52dbbb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5693]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! O king! Filled with joy, they attacked your soldiers, like the immortal Indra and Upendra284 attacking the army of the daityas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b44124cc7b32d3980a6bbaef> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4502]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Tell me what merits are obtained by someone who circles the earth14 and visits all the tirthas? O brahmana! Please tell me this in detail." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b4444fac9c488294636e1972> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[168]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O Sanjaya! I had no hope of victory when I heard that Shukra52 and Surya53 united to bring victory to the sons of Kunti and fierce beasts of prey were always around us." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b44a1856bf03bbf4414833f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[220]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having heard that Madhava48 had left, he himself set out for the city of Dvaraka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b45baea6460d7075a0ac646b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11218]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! Karna’s armoured son191 quickly pierced Satyaki from every direction with sharp arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b46cb87a65d4ede0894b5422> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13904]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The directions, and all the gods, with Shakra28 at the forefront, were frightened." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b46eb6f4d2923107670a9956> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1434]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "167 Therefore, thinking that one is powerful, one should never follow that which is not dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b48841d99afbc63158b177c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2378, 2382]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Those who hate the gods are capable.
” ‘ “‘The gods said, “We think that their energy and strength is double that of ours.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b48899114772ccaa2ddd1e9f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8116, 8118, 8121, 8122]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """When offerings are rendered to gods who reside in the house, they are pleased.
However, through such an act, the gods are pleased a hundred times more.
After bowing down, learned people perform many acts of ablutions and these please the gods.
When they are worshipped in accordance with the rites, the gods accept the offerings and are delighted.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b48c351d91130bd492eea558> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1550]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Show mercy to the king of the gods who is a supplicant before you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b49772a15ecf0b31554672d0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4472]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Equip it with weapons, flags, spears, spikes and staffs." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b49fffe16e542ed46fa0509e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2939]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "While he was thus engaged in austerities, Harivahana1236 appeared before him and asked, ‘O Matanga! Why are you tormenting yourself? Why have you given up the pleasures that men like? I wish to grant you a boon." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b4ab43ca184626d5072b8ab1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 127 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10321]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing him, all the rishis bowed down their heads." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b4aefd0d7426ac6f05fa2e70> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4081, 4083]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """In the battle between the gods and the asuras, he140 angrily killed fourteen million terrible daityas with his bare hands alone.
141 They destroyed and defeated the enemies of the gods and possessed all kinds of earthy forms.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b4afaafe0fdd0a4a64a2a8ca> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4423, 4426]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Where is the cause for sorrow? It is said that this account brings about the destruction of Kali.
Those who recount Nala’s great tale and those who listen to it often, are never confronted by calamity.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b4c2ca970317ab835439b8a7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6345]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Through his strength of mind, he controls them in battles between the gods and the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b4d16e5f8c043c627ec33c01> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9291]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "While avoiding adharma, one should try to obtain these three." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b4d22b8dfc000b8f144f1afa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2747]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Thinking that the command of his ancestors should be followed, he went out to hunt, thinking of Girika, who was exceedingly beautiful and like Shri50 herself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b4db27772bdc607e015aaf5c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4649]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods have been created from your words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b4e6d4257f3a2e427c32add5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[638, 639]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Like Maghavan10 hurling his thunder, he brought it down, like Yama’s staff, on his11 head.
But in that battle, the rakshasa could be seen, completely unmoved.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b4f1be4473a2314837f106d4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1698]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O father! The entire earth is on my side and not on that of the Parthas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b4fb78683a6192786c33d57d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5481]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” O descendant of the Kuru lineage! When Bhishma approved, Kali242 thought of the sage Krishna Dvaipayana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b505000a86b2a72dcb0a10f5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4437]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O one who is equal to the king of the gods! Righteous ones always provide standing to those who have been deprived of their happiness." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b50c779ae364c08ca3e8e204> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4159]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The bull among the Pandavas78 arose from his seat and affectionately embraced Arjuna with his arms, inhaling the fragrance of his head." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b512376ba8644c1770f0d1a5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 48 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4075]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "These sons are born from brahmana mothers and are the worst of their lineages." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b53fb2b4ef5e10579e209a40> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12734]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "212 When Tapas213 witnessed the great fruits from austerities, an extremely wise son named Purandara was born to him, with a desire to pass on these fruits." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b5406235a0661d7052a6b3eb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7379]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that Duhshasana was afflicted by hundreds of arrows, the king267 urged the Trigartas to advance towards Yuyudhana’s chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b55645586ac45f8f9137b3b8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7785, 7786, 7787]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """1048 Death became the lord of living beings and the fire of energy.
The lord announced that Ishana1049 would be the protector of the Rudras.
Vasishtha became the lord of brahmanas, the fire1050 of the Vasus, the sun of energy,1051 the moon of nakshatras and Amshuman1052 of herbs.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b5596da56ea18e0f2d632c83> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5292]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Pardon what I have spoken because of my fear about dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b55b29ae3a43909ac09c9db1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14357, 14358]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Various rakshasas possessed the intelligence of the brave samshaptakas.
They were overtaken by rajas and tamas90 and wished to kill Phalguna.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b561f6534a2094dad7f84392> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[387]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That is the reason, with the gods, you attack and kill the asuras and their relatives." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b57564d1ad2ebfb832324a35> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17133]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ ‘“Narada said, ‘The god who was restrained in speech477 heard Sthanu’s words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b58722383ebb8157daa232f4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6079]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Men, nagas, gandharvas, yakshas and kimpurushas417 followed the great-souled one, in a desire to witness the extraordinary feat." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b5926f9d341a23e1a8900a78> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 187 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10862, 10866]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O descendant of the Bharata lineage! She became a river in Vatsabhumi, known as Amba.
O king! Through her austerities, half of the maiden became a river in Vatsa.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b5983f573dbec48099960c02> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10930]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Indra among kings! Shikhandi81 became supremely skilled in painting and the arts." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b5a3acb526ba0fb724eba8de> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[765]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I am bereft of my senses when you fight with tigers, buffaloes and lions in the inner quarters and Kaikeyi19 watches you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b5bb94e9ddd8817336100087> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3761]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Having been thus addressed by all the gods, the illustrious Svayambhu558 replied, ‘O bulls among the gods! I will think about your welfare." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b5c325b4d054cc13eaa95f37> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1588, 1608]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ 265(40) ‘Bhishma said, “This one27 was born in the royal lineage of Chedi with three eyes and four arms.
Then the Yadavas Samkarshana28 and Janardana went to the capital of the Chedi kingdom to see the Yadavi who was their father’s sister.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b5eefb79895f5ede6ae51c7e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 29 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2968, 2969, 2970, 2971, 2973, 2974]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """1240 One is whirled around in the state of being a friend of a brahmana for a long period of time.
After two thousand births in this way, one obtains the status of a brahmana who earns a living by selling weapons.
One is whirled around in the status of a brahmana who earns a living by selling weapons for a long period of time.
After three thousand births in this way, one obtains the status of an ordinary brahmana.
After four thousand births in this way, one is born as a learned brahmana.
One is whirled around in the state of a learned brahmana for a long period of time.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b5effc0e02ae7b34bba136b9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1227]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I desire to have a boon, or a curse, from none other than Maheshvara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b5f6c103193af66805265882> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2529]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In the presence of the gods, he spoke about his349 many qualities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b5fa95ba3346af3214e78d9d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10255]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O best among the Bharata lineage! This is a conversation between a shalmali tree165 and the wind." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b5fb882b0ab0101c76fccb71> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12469]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having spent fifty nights in that supreme and beautiful city, the bull among men remembered that this was the period the foremost among Kouravas1 had indicated." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b60b909edfc27ada935accb4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24922]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lord of the gods faced the eastern direction and himself declared these special rules." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b62390eb4c006ef2cc587521> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1, 2, 6]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """After Karna’s death, Shalya is instated as the commander of the Kourava army.
Shalya is the commander for a single day, day eighteen.
In the numbering of the chapters in this parva, the first number is a consecutive one, starting with the beginning of the Mahabharata.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b643ca95d2235a4552dccf73> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5653]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In earlier times, you rendered your help in slaying the enemies of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b667bea345e3478726e15169> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5495]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! There is the grandfather’s351 holy lake, by the name of Pushkara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b67cd271eeaa6fe2b9e21a4f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[587]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It was like that between the gods and the asuras and increased one’s fear." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b686e979b870ababa7064d3b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10928]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I alone knew, through a spy, through Narada’s words, through the words of the god80 and through Amba’s austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b68733f006ff9ec4374da7f6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5354]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I will give him one thousand deerskins that have been brought from the country of China42 and whatever else deserves to be given to Keshava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b696487fe9baad888a61a223> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[225]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having created beings, Prajapati26 ordained tasks for them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b6c32a0369ced494b14e0996> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3907]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But all that seemed to be dispelled by the storm of arrows that Karna and Madhava476 shot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b6c48e01aaed1161b53f3002> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19129, 19139]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The infinitely energetic lord of the gods was overcome by rage and a terrible drop of sweat manifested itself on his forehead and fell down on the ground.
All the gods were terrified and fled in the ten directions.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b6e3318492828124a20b6639> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6311]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He struck Karna with sharp and iron arrows and pierced his eldest son711 with eight arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b6f8e6da509d89b95bbb87fd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2582]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 54: 24 shlokas Chapter 55: 43 shlokas Chapter 56: 33 shlokas Chapter 57: 106 shlokas Chapter 58: 51 shlokas Ansha means partial or secondary incarnation, while avatarana means descent." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b70261f28988803fbbf638e1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12096]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods and the asuras were incapacitated and miserable." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b70bff8d565f42ddd4bccd62> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15928]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He must bow down before the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b70ec32ac32439102a36b6fc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23834]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I alone am the original father of the gods and the ancestors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b732ab65a6b24a1bdd0d06d1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6658]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Drona taught the Pandava how to fight in narrow confines345 with clubs, swords, spears, javelins and lances." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b734743bf5b48a48e264a816> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1647, 1648]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """When good deeds are performed for a sacrifice, the gods are favourably inclined towards you.
When gods are honoured through animals, they become lords of the passage.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b741649ed84202cf99304e1e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2032]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The Simhalas offered the best jewels found in the ocean, lapis lazuli, pearls and conch shells and hundreds of covers for housing elephants." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b745fc88e1d451ab745961e1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2913]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Hari84 replied that thus it would be." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b74a962d9004e7891e34021e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1336]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Vajigriva180 now finds delight in the world of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b75f0a584c12a75b1ec4dc6b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7136]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” On the eighth day of the month of Phalguna, when Rohini57 was in the ascendant, they left for Varanavata and saw the city and its people." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b76e6e94c821193f96eb1d2e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3835]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Krishna and the lord26 took the permission of the kings and the relatives and retired to their inner quarters." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b77a8797316e4189349d4246> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23458]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods are of the view that animals should be offered." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b7a037d285bcb2aa4f4006c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20558]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I will enjoy the fruits of good and bad deeds in the world and then go to the world of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b7a89bed5945d902d255e6a5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1693]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowledge is attained by the faithful, the unwavering and those who control their senses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b7e0c3c4ea433c0ad08e7eed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5260]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Restrained and controlled in diet, one treads the path of the gods, and a man thus obtains the merits of a divine sacrifice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b7e12e3ca19421c98d69f0a7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3823]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Pandu’s son96 is handsome and intelligent." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b7e4bb6940b0725a0623fbed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[550]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, the rishi who was Satyavati’s son27 got to know in advance about her wicked intentions towards the Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b7f2ba21dda059dae6a8a600> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4688]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O tiger among men! A pure man who bathes in Rudrakoti obtains the fruits of a horse sacrifice and rescues his lineage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b8158e9f50f386fdef354ea0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3993]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing them, Sharva52 smiled and said, ‘O foremost among men! Welcome! Arise! Be free of exhaustion." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b82a73ac54b0a637b0060d81> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2243]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "308 It has been heard by us that the daityas were then defeated by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b841b4b6a632793418a90d56> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11210]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ CHAPTER 858(195) Vaishampayana said, ‘O best of the Bharata lineage! Having heard this, Kounteya112 summoned his brothers in private and spoke these words to them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b857ef89e5bde53dba1babe6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8168]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Having been thus addressed there by your son, your son336 agreed and attacking Bhimasena, covered him with arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b8623c0c21e4474a38ef6d5f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5469]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O immensely intelligent one! They were uttered on the occasion of a sacrifice of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b86c4cb16ae077ed856793da> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2662]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He looked like Mount Udaya,413 with the sun blazing its crown." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b86cae84a1b438cb3208f404> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6095]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Therefore, discard your vanity and go to Dhananjaya82 before a weapon has been affixed to Gandiva, the best of bows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b87eba75aee26a34f1df50c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6864]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ He208 applauded Galava and accepted the maiden." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b8aed228df03128280e38bb5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7250]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Having said this, surrounded by his relatives, Ambika’s son75 tendered offerings of water to Pandu’s sons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b8b3f379c04d44d77fe24e5c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[456, 457]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O great king! There is also the powerful Bhishmaka Chaturyu21 of Bhoja, a friend of Indra’s and a slayer of enemies.
Through his learning and strength, he has conquered Pandya22 and Krathakaishika.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b8bab76bd435ba1e28613373> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10934, 10942]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O lord! Through what deeds does a man obtain a long life? O lord of the gods! Through what great austerities does one obtain a long life? On earth, because of what deeds does a man obtain a short life? O god! O unblemished one! You should tell me about these perverse deeds.
Some are extremely wise and have insight about jnana and vijnana.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b8c975592d9f60063ff56ca4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5009]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They were seen to be as beautiful as a collection of gods in the firmament." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b8ce2e9a319a6b9f2615d3b5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8246, 8247]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """22 O mighty-armed one! When this atiratra23 sacrifice is observed, the immensely strong Ghatotkacha will be the shamitar.
O Krishna! Because he was born from a fire, the powerful Dhrishtadyumna will be the dakshina at the sacrifice when oblations24 are offered.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b8d90249e689d0d78b01dd91> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4087]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In anger, Indrasena’s mother180 had cursed me earlier, when you had abandoned her and I have been sorely oppressed since then." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9029e593e31284f74ea825a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5877]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He may worship gods and be free of egoism." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9191e765e981f17309700f3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9425]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Hunger destroys dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9262de371ffd76f38e82a2d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6651]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Madhava! The tears on Krishna’s765 face will be comforted today." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9274056f3dcf5258b2827b3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1294]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 256(31) Vaishampayana said, ‘The victorious Nakula went to Hastinapura and the Pandava18 invited Bhishma and Dhritarashtra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b94b24a57b8fe8caa9aff48f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 168 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8477]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He sprinkled water sanctified with mantras over him and freed the good king from the terrible rakshasa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9642e81a63e4f2dccf1c973> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19042]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the lord of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b973ffc2811ad485a7fb5ce6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3110]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chandra, the best of Diti’s sons and as handsome as the lord of the stars57 in the world, became rajarshi Rishika on earth, supreme among kings." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b97c9c2bd3c218a96ff2a63d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11115]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“After some time had passed, Naravahana Kubera100 was touring through the worlds and arrived in Sthuna’s residence." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b980259d0f319909ce80baea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8287]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that Vishoka426 had been wounded, the powerful Bhimsena struck the king of Madra in the arms and the chest with three arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b99bdf8e76c0da93b3199cb0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2793]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Having seen that the elephant had been killed with an arrow and that all the warriors had run away, the foremost among Kurus191 retreated on his chariot from the field of battle and went to a spot where Partha was not present." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9a5f5e78836ae01ee5d3643> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "16_Mausala" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Pandava heard that only Vasudeva and Rama2 had escaped." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9adc9b77f75bc6d0ae0d2c4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22246]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The drums of the gods were sounded with a loud roar." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9c47e55c220d3c7a04dda6a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[54, 55]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """They uttered their blessings and he set out, ascending his swift and golden chariot that had Tarkshya9 on its banner.
Carrying his club, chakra, Sharnga10 and other weapons the lotus-eyed one left at an auspicious and excellent muhurta,11 tithi12 and nakshatra, pulled by his horses Sainya and Sugriva.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9c7985565c24e979e30092d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17276]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Else, I will leave in anger and will curse that brahmana22 and your father." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9cc075635fef55fe1363b67> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[530]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bhima then challenged the wrestler, who was like Vritra83 himself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9de0d4b6f3a83aabeb3014e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12602]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "103 The gods must be pleased and the ancestors must be satisfied." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9decdf4d40b7b03db008001> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6460, 6472]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He was radiant, like a son of the gods.
467 Ornaments with a similar sound were also tied to his wrists.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9eaa6d811a831446f2a77a4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23311]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among brahmanas! King Vasu1114 will obtain the sacred text prepared by you from Brihaspati." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9f7640cd15f6ab724754b3f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9143]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Indra among men! O mighty-armed one! The gandharvas, the yakshas, the rakshasas, the inhabitants of Alaka127 and all the denizens of the mountain will protect you, and the supreme among brahmanas, on my orders." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/b9fbcfd5f2c76f38cd95a923> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9236]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ The god of gods, extremely pleased with her, again uttered these holy words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ba0a2c27eba1df3681581b3c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15241]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Tvashtra48 himself created her, so that she might be Rama’s beloved queen." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ba26c47c970c25729826652a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15135]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Happiness does not come to a man because of serving the mother and the father, worshipping the gods, or because of following other good qualities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ba34a9f0b8888837c72dc999> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11757]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! He destroyed the weapon that had been used by Ghatotkacha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ba3e67010c583454bd1ff379> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 120 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6821]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "How can it be said that he and his brothers must live in the forest? It is appropriate that the army of Dasharha should march out today, with many kinds of weapons and coloured armour." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ba470bba56068da72dd277f5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10182]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This large river17 entered into the ocean of the Pandus and filled it up to the brim, to the great despondency of their enemies." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ba4fa2423157ca6721f953cf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3247]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Supreme among those who wield spears, he killed many in that way." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ba53dbc964babdb1cefc28c8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5370]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bhishma and Drona are atirathas329 and Kripa and Drona’s son330 are invincible." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ba570ec4117918090312111b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8611]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ 172 ‘The gandharva said, “Having been thus addressed by the great-souled Vashishtha, the Brahmana rishi118 controlled his anger, which would have destroyed all the worlds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ba78c5e8583223253c95c280> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 43 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4035]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "What could be given to him? All the riches had already been given away to the gods, the gandharvas, the rakshasas, the bhutas, the yakshas, the birds, the serpents and great-souled ones without any bodies." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ba79bf1150880370f7d9d711> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11118, 11120]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O lord of the gods! These rivers, with the waters of all the tirthas, have approached near you, so that you can touch their waters.
425 Purusha is said to be someone who possesses the powers, but has no sense of ego.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ba7ac541fc3bfea7c7c46bf3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14332]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is Shankara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ba821dd9b21f9492dc0c5adb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 104 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5723, 5724]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """” Earlier, he was known by the name of Vasushena.
But after this deed, he became known by the name of Vaikartana Karna.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/baa938b085fd7f9ab08e658f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6077]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Having heard the words of the thirty gods, the sage said, ‘For the sake of the great happiness of the worlds, I will do what you desire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/baad3227ef9c9c3870cef038> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11657]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They attacked the tens of thousands of gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bac121f9358af7478fd47bbf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1300]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In ancient times, Mahadeva was gratified and gave Rama159 a battleaxe that was sharp at the edges." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bac886e6a555f6f385e62140> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7265]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Loud sounds of lamentation were heard among beings in heaven, in the sky and on the ground." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bacb720c594dfc8a6e3212e9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6672, 6674]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Though she was a woman, she used harsh words and spoke to the gods.
Therefore, all of you gods will no longer have offspring.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bad4b5455d77b13adfe58992> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9380]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His son24 also has all the good qualities and is attached to the Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bad5b7ef9f4262d9f9167fb8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3911]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With his preceptor’s permission, he then prepared to return to the land of the thirty gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/baeaf70ae5926b1fa8c23173> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6982]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The valiant one241 saw that the vyuha had been shattered by the Pandus and the Panchalas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bb050f4a0da5523db3154095> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4883]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At this time, it was the twelfth lunar day in shuklapaksha of Magha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bb0af14deba2ab7aa9cdf13c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12708]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Slain, they fell down on the ground." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bb0d3b9a372ffe24dd2ad3a1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16204]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowledge is generated through energy, never through the qualities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bb108cfcf1cf99d7022704e1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21339]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If it902 emerges through the feet, the person is said to go to Vishnu’s region." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bb321b611ce31564499588bf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1987]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, let it not cause injury to the gods or destruction to men." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bb44d9d49fbdeddc5effcc18> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2668, 2669]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Insolent because of their strength, they are now talking about killing the gods.
Having been granted the boon, they do not show regard for the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bb45e8a5b813d6f2153efd01> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14237]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Why should one lament about that? O Indra among kings! Listen to my words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bb5122668901fd626007b7c4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1506, 1507]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O unblemished one! This was certainly destiny, to accomplish the tasks of the gods.
All of them were born on earth as incarnations, as parts of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bb56e40361a4e5ecea7c3098> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[102, 103]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """In this way, the man22 may be able to persuade Dhritarashtra’s son and bring him around to what is in our interest.
”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘While the foremost among the Madhus23 was thus speaking, the foremost among the Shinis24 suddenly stood up.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bb5b5ab60e0174656b45883a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10948]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O virtuous one! Desire, anger, happiness, fear and delusion—know them to be different forms of me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bb993339612f5782556541b5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8401]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "After the curse on the great king, the rishi93 recognized that the rishi94 was none other than Vashishtha’s son, as powerful as Vashishtha himself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bbaa02485a7a79224b5d8c1a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4226]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Desiring to catch fish, those kaivartas1331 arrived at the banks of the Ganga and the Yamuna and covered a part of the water with nets that were joined together." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bbb6bfa47804bf4646f3b004> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2701]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Believing that he was trying to become the king of the gods through the practice of austerities, he tried to wean the king away from his austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bbc854cb457f4300213d49fa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11526]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing this, your son212 spoke these words to Duhshasana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bbe01a33388c8d1164ef8afe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21613]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As she roamed around the entire earth, she heard from various tridandis940 about the lord of Mithila, who was pursuing emancipation." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bbef31815fb7d6fa7bdd6f3e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2544]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ While Krishna was speaking, a great sound of lamentation arose in the army of Dhritarashtra’s son, but the other one7 remained silent." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bbef44be78617a2d8e4c4a4c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11563]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’” ‘Bhishma continued, “The king was silent and Pavana1390 spoke again." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bbfa8890194a7368dd9dbd1c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4008]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Kuru lineage! While he was advancing towards Arjuna, Panchala struck Sharadvat162 in the shoulder with three arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc0314ca1b900daa31ea82e7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1893]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "248 Once they came down from the world of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc0da1a82e865fd9996136de> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[950]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Brahmana! O sage! At this time, Menaka16 conceived a child through the king of the gandharvas, named Vishvavasu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc0e32bcc2cb63b3be2e0d60> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2793]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Some time earlier, while searching for the king, Pandu’s son3 had arrived there and had asked them about your son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc1f85e603582c3d0ee46ce8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10728]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He obtains the world of heaven and finds delight with the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc21f6b3a118675f473f0482> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4469, 4484, 4489, 4491]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Hence, the lord of the gods asked her to boil those berries.
The best of the gods spoke these words to the maiden, who was extremely firm in her vows.
O one with the beautiful brows! It will clean all sins and be known by the name of Badarapachana.
O immensely fortunate one! O beautiful one! In ancient times, in this supreme tirtha, the saptarshis had left Arundhati177 and gone to the Himalayas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc2aa22a068db8f657b6c876> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[747]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that Nakula was without a chariot, Droupadi’s immensely strong son, Sutasoma, wished to save his father70 in the battle and attacked." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc396dafbee3eb39ae40ce86> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[710, 711, 712]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! In that encounter, the tiger among men struck Prativindhya97 in the abdomen and killed him.
Slain, he fell down on the ground.
The powerful Sutasoma98 struck Drona’s son with a javelin and again attacked Drona’s son with a sword.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc3caefa955829951fef4967> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1081]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This is the celestial Akshara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc56eb719cbff09a9c613796> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11646]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He asked, ‘I should be incapable of being killed by gods, danavas, yakshas, serpents, gandharvas and rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc5f2298f902af60de43b559> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11184]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In a great battle, this ocean of soldiers cannot be ruffled even by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc5fbbeda5820d0704134b6c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1955]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Garhasthya is the second and vanaprastha comes after that." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc60b2a9fe89feab0a187d6b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17517]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods dwell in the five senses of all beings—Aditya, Chandrama, Vayu, Brahma, Prana, Kratu499 and Yama." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc6680da476e394f4e5162d1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[443]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is certain that my heart has the essence of the vajra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc826fd8601a1633a803bff2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5644]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Though she had protectors, Krishna62 found no one to protect her then." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc8e8131397517a872ed62ff> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11230, 11232]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Worship the ancestors and the gods.
Discard vanity and always be humble.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bc992fe3c099999b8539944f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23178, 23181]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """However, those two1092 wished to enhance dharma and were engaged in austerities there.
What daily rites should they engage in? They are illustrious gods and the ancestors of all creatures.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bcb67087b9bea9c98c048ff5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2547, 2562, 2564]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He must purify himself and always offer water to the gods.
He must always control his speech and eat after the gods and the guests have eaten.
He must eat limited quantities and seek refuge with the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bcb78e52f7cb5cce42ed5520> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5777]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘The river’s son278 heard that King Devaka had a daughter born from a Shudra woman279 and that she was young and beautiful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bcd35dbd95bdb514145b3646> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1613]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Our beloved preceptor77 follows brahmacharya and the Vedas and never deviates from the right course of action." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bcf77e3122b065669a9e9fdd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9554]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If that is what the brave Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, Bhimasena and Arjuna, the twins,1 who are bulls among men, and Rama2 and Krishna, learned in the precepts of the law, desire, then the Pandavas should go there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bcf7ef3a128e05d6422f6688> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9628]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘When those great-souled ones were thus seated together, devarshi3 Narada,4 who was travelling as he willed, happened to come there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bcf80c748b589eaa8e49446f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13083]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The thirty gods were delighted and played on their musical instruments." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bd0dc3c0e306cd943515421f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7542]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘The lord33 also comforted Kunti." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bd18e9be4fde4062d4527499> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[212]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods, the gandharvas and the divine apsaras, attired in sparkling garments, will serve you now and ensure your comfort in heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bd293a8191c62dbc5048b7f3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10970]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But the king88 again ascertained the truth of the matter, that the daughter of Panchala was actually a maiden, and swiftly marched out." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bd29c7ee780d8813f6526cd8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3561]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Krishna250 said, “The great-souled kshatriyas performed extremely wonderful deeds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bd3031a2aeb1044c46e5cf67> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5356, 5358]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The immensely strong Sutasoma saw that he254 was without a chariot.
O king! The brave Shrutakirti255 then attacked your son Jayatsena in that battle, wishing to kill the illustrious one.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bd482fd55fdca2567d24c9a3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1758]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! When Krishna, supreme among the Satvatas, had left for Dvaravati, only Duryodhana and Soubala57 Shakuni, bulls among men, remained in that celestial sabha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bd55cb68ac9176e4c04fe43e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2800]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son of Dhritarashtra! Remember how Indras among men193 are supposed to act." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bd59ba142dbae49e10669942> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8092]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It was frequented by those who worshipped the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bd64ec141a5c13ec070e3515> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3193]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I am the eternal god of the gods and there is nothing superior to me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bd99f1e3dd4eb68e4483f1fa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5955]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Pandu then again said, “Go to Nagapura289 and say that Pandu has left for the forest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bdaaa899bfde27d706d8ab00> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4832]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "176 O extender of the Kuru lineage! If one goes to the well named Kimdatta and offers a measure177 of sesamum seeds there, one attains the supreme objective and is freed from all one’s debts." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bdb04f8260aba3e9f010dd53> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23226]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ Chapter 1650(322) hishma said, “Having been thus addressed by Narayana, the supreme being and best among men, for the welfare of the worlds, the best among men1098 spoke these words to Narayana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bdb35d9f7520aec10f7bf769> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1035]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Having established the kingdom, he set out with Kuluta16 and swiftly threw Senabindu out of his kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bdb559c87a51f949b3481fc6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6919]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lord148 determined that for purposes of deciding a son, Angiras should be Agni’s." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bdc62a59c09366608927e32a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1004]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Janaka gave up riches, offspring, friends, the many jewels and the path of fire131 and became one who shaved off his head." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bdcd6074de5c26b9cdde4bdf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[748]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You lived in the abode of Vairaja28 with Brahma himself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bdcfecd2d22c5ea218134881> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1523]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With Bhishma at the forefront, the Kurus ignored it when she was seized by that lecher67 and was forced to weep." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bdf17fbde438231a33cd5bdc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8824]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O best of the Bharata lineage! When that javelin, hurled angrily by Bhishma’s powerful arms, was severed with five arrows by the enraged Kiriti, it was shattered and fell down on the ground, like lightning446 dislodged from a mass of clouds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bdffd8cb5b17cfb7bc5db400> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[379]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! Kavya Ushanas64 also goes to the summit, with the daityas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be10aa533443fdf497e860cb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5926, 5931]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """But the sun ascended the Asta mountain301 and could no longer be seen.
Rakshasas, pishachas and others who fed on flesh were seen in every direction, in hundreds and thousands.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be1323224f22f32462f04b5d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2185]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The palace was like Kubera’s abode and the one with dharma in his heart117 went to Dharmaputra Yudhishthira." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be170d0b73145a55ee5ea147> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9929]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I am a lord of the rakshasas and I am Dashagriva’s82 equal in strength." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be183cf8c436ffe1868b2e99> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[832]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that he75 was angrily descending with foot soldiers and horses, King Yudhishthira countered him with sharp arrows, like a crazy elephant checked with a goad." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be249b9abf39b01790ba85a6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5245]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having thus spoken to Keshava and voiced his intentions, he33 embraced Janardana and, having taken his leave, departed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be25b93adb8835190f81e913> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10940]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The circle of the sacrifice was resplendent, because it was surrounded by gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be3046778d3ce3b0f1e2f26a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[174]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having slain half the soldiers29 who remained after the slaughter by the great-souled Bhishma and Drona, Vaikartana Karna was killed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be39363c98c2a2f5cabadb95> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[419]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He joined his hands in salutation and told Shalya, who was like Rama45 and Bhishma in battle, ‘O one who is devoted to friends! The time has come for friendship." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be3b5ea056118963dbcf7a83> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3593]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At this, he453 ascended another chariot that had been duly prepared earlier, and stationing himself within Karna’s army, began to fight with the Pandus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be3f9f6d5db308f2e019d403> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1829]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Cream represents the essence of clarified butter." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be5f1ef90dfa684294183e22> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5880]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! On seeing that they were oppressed by Bhishma’s arrows, he298 desired Bhishma’s death and anxiously thought about the means." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be6a2010f571eb0d76be1b6b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5713]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘So as to hide her misconduct and frightened of her relatives, Kunti262 hurled the son, who bore all the auspicious marks, into the water." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be7cf7450ee30015eef35490> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13527]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I will blaze amidst the soldiers, like the rays of the sun, and use weapons created by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be84d78d6ff2dcea19ee11fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2737]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When the noise died down, Radheya, who was almost senseless with anger, gripped his lustrous arms212 and uttered these words, “I have witnessed many distortions in Vikarna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be99c0a63d43d542a3d566a1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1949]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘ “The best of men, Arjuna and Keshava, performed their religious ceremonies and worshipped Lord Bhava274 in accordance with the proper rites." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/be9eb1b1d94624d9c0ae5e14> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3479]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The mighty-armed one is radiant and is stationed like Mount Meru." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bea37555a9e5c490a57e1c33> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23269]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "1105 He first used these to worship the lord of the gods and then used the remnants to worship the grandfather." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/beb47f2e12a11a25d1436825> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10573]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This is the place of the grandfather185 and Brahma’s essence arises from there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/beb8d007ae0275273ecbe754> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4719]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Even the king of the gods is incapable of defeating you in a battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bebd22f8a4810f5c33085e61> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[264]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let a man recite this chant to the supreme of gods, after concentrating and purifying his mind." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bec08ecc66cb04dc58809691> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9155]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Rohini’s son15 glanced at Vasudeva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/beca2eac2e002f0f7ed1623d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2421]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Then the immensely energetic Vrishabhadhvaja284 smiled, and grasping Phalguna’s beautiful hands, said, “I have pardoned you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/becf87b4a35cb8dcb776e1fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[958]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lords of the earth then made Dasharha42 share in their riches." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bed0aaa0c8adb6b70e8ab70d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5125]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The brave one then confronted all of Duryodhana’s younger brothers— Duhshasana, Durvishaha, Duhsaha, Durmada, Jaya, Jayatsena, Vikarna, Chitrasena, Sudarshana, Charuchitra, Suvarmana, Dushkarna, Karna237 —and a large number of other maharathas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bedad23a35ee8fafa64529f7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5244]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On going to Venna292 and worshipping the ancestors and the gods, a man obtains a celestial chariot drawn by peacocks and swans." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bededd8d3ad18a1c6cac4a70> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24046]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the best among the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bee6fcce8c1af866990df77c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13428]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“But suddenly those from the world of the gods were seen to be worsted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bf01a707ed0656874f2bcb97> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10961]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kanchanavarma’s87 messenger went to Drupada." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bf14d91166749b934f2c9e62> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3390]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ 66 ‘Shakuntala said,104 “Having been thus addressed, Shakra105 commanded the wind, who was always mobile, to be present with Menaka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bf1e33e2acaefc69e8412697> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7819]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The illustrious Soma1062 comes after the rishis and the eternal gods after Soma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bf1f2eeda3052a1ccca1eefb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[147]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O Sanjaya! I had no hope of victory when I heard that thousands of snatakas40 and great Brahmanas who lived on alms followed Dharmaraja41 to the forest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bf38c8ab8cc547c628858a95> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3719]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "19 Dispel your sorrow and do not weep." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bf42843729e2ee3f390fc2c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21292, 21294]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O scorcher of enemies! Know that restraining the breath895 is the foremost and supreme aspect of yoga.
896 O son! O unblemished one! When the body is destroyed, one cheerfully abandons it and, in subtle form, uses the eight qualities of yoga897 to roam around in the worlds.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bf460ec2d9396f6b04097c13> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3366]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At that time, Sanjaya52 told him, “O lord of the earth! You have obtained the entire earth, with all its riches." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bf47f3644873c26b9280ddb0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1818]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because of the crimes of your deeds, the Kurus will be burnt up, like the one with the black form118 burns up dry wood." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bf54bb28e26b371c3462b759> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8127]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The servitude of the Shudras43 is the vajra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bf62121f9ba65bf294675579> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[411, 412]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Look at the gods and the asuras.
O king! The gods prosper after having slain their own relatives.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bf64a8a7a9c418455315ddd8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13705]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Duryodhana, Shakuni, the son of the suta5 and the extremely evil-minded Duhshasana only saw the honey." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bf83d856901ae29d54959aa7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2587]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With arrows piercing all his limbs, the son of Shakra’s son47 was seen to angrily roam around amidst the soldiers, like Yama with a noose in his hand." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bfa642f0ede77ed5abafc88c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9431]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His15 spirit is never dejected." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bfb074bbeb371219e6a8c1ba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 271 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18880]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In joy, you will be counted among the Siddhas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bfb9abe84a0c041d67aca122> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2658]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They357 were like the great Indra and Vishnu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bfd1e78c0840bca46315596b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4244]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bahuka recognized Indrasena186 and her brother." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bfd804a55f407629f55e6cfd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4918]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is no doubt that a twice-born who observes vows, takes up the sacred thread, fasts and follows rituals is a brahmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/bffed3c8d01444bc548294ae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7470, 7471]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O fortunate one! Let us go there quickly, before Suyodhana18 discovers us.
” The scorchers of enemies and tigers among men19 agreed, as did their mother, and left, with the rakshasi Hidimba following.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c003c0aaf59ce5167f04ccf2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23210]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The rites for gods and ancestors are based on his instructions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c00a7ae64d4b11c84da81d84> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4466]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Partha showered down arrows on the enemy, like Parjanya25 pouring down rain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c00b4f69bf029bf1b7136a2d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8127, 8130]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O supreme among men! Having spoken to the rishi, revered in the worlds, the one with dharma in his soul1088 worshipped him.
‘“‘All the sages surrounded that bull among men.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c0122ebef25a2496c6e815db> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[392]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The time for the sacrifice, in which priests rigid in their vows establish six fires2 to the chants of sama, is free and depends on kshatriya riches." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c0136a4fbefe2476cdf75247> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10771]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is my view that the proof for this lies in the words that emanated from the mouth of the grandfather, the great-souled god of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c013a95428a3dc9d77e6780e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[815]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The rishi became extremely learned in the Atharva Veda, the Vedas,68 and the application of kalpa69 and also obtained excellence in astronomy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c01de7a5e9aaa7cde7e63bda> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13646]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The beautiful Satyabhama, Krishna’s queen, circumambulated Krishna9 and ascended Shouri’s10 chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c020f68f7d80d67ca3ae17cf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1023]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "What you have asked me is a great mystery, even to the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c034221fab7dbd4715013e5f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15019]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Svayambhu197 has earlier laid down the course of time it must follow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c0380672b07eaed7d96e0bd5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6543]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among those of the Bharata lineage! The sage who was born from the fire334 gave knowledge of the great weapon agneya to Bharadvaja’s son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c044a2949e61be557f4f5ed7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4509]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among the gods! You should never disregard him as a mere man." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c0523b2e227a5c6729251765> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2997]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Kounteya! The mother gave her own charu to her daughter and ignorantly, consumed her467 charu herself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c05b9ddb8c3518a09b3917a4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7903]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ The descendant of Bhrigu13 agreed and gave those to him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c06b23705101d6558a1af289> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7668]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The ancestors, the rishis and the gods are pleased with him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c07b4ffd3bd7345d2ff4e782> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1068]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The illustrious Kumara from the Panchalas was protecting his93 wheels and countered the advancing Drona, like the shoreline against the lord of the rivers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c0877a7c0bb4a1e0f68542c4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19436]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The great sage691 was accomplished in yoga." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c08fd2963e2a6cbbf1777f45> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5525]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ This is what he121 told Krishna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c0a5c9fddd4c9a6001c647b5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 285 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19788, 19789]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """How can those born from different wombs, those born from shudra wombs and those born from inferior wombs become sages?’ ‘“Parashara replied, ‘O king! Though these are not brahmanas by virtue of their inferior birth, these great-souled ones can resort to austerities and cleanse their souls.
O king! Here and there, the sages had sons.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c0b151daf620ff51546c4ad1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5404]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Today is the seventeenth day629 of this extremely terrible destruction of men, elephants and horses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c0cd35b2573b274e0329458b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14657, 14658]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """If a brahmana never eats until they156 have eaten, through that act of not eating, he conquers heaven.
If one survives on the leftovers after gods, ancestors, servants and guests have eaten, that is said to be like surviving on what is left at a sacrifice.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c0fa4b16754b5cd7916a2055> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9045, 9048]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He is successful in all his objectives and is served by the daughters of the gods.
If a man is forgiving for an entire year, if he only eats on every eighth day, if he is always devoted to the tasks of the gods and if he offers oblations into the fire, he obtains the supreme fruits of a poundarika sacrifice.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c10516bb33e64298d844ebbc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9350]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "18 Without him, Phalguna19 is not even worth a fourth of Radheya20 in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c10eb4fbffac6d5123a3931b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[434]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He then performed the funeral ceremonies over the bodies of the great Vasudeva125 and Rama126 and the chief among those of the Vrishni lineage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c129ec492f9027819028a35e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1352]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 1967(36): 33 shlokas Chapter 1968(37): 18 shlokas Chapter 1969(38): 23 shlokas Chapter 1970(39): 24 shlokas Chapter 1971(40): 21 shlokas Chapter 1972(41): 28 shlokas Chapter 1973(42): 17 shlokas Chapter 1974(43): 18 shlokas Chapter 1975(44): 52 shlokas Putra means son and darshana means sight." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c1484a0eb5533a7b31a0361c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11025, 11031]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Through the grace of the gods, all of this will happen.
O lord of the earth! Then worship the gods, as you please.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c155e529cf4cd1dad9d313c8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6291, 6292, 6293, 6294]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Ghee is always in my heart.
Ghee is always established in my navel.
Ghee is in all my limbs.
Ghee is established in my mind.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c1587ad331b870b6b69c6d3d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6747]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In ancient times, the gods performed austerities there and kings regard it as the most sacred of places." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c17bb1dba6d35c50ee52b3ef> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3736]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The intelligent Krishna267 said this, desiring the welfare of the Kurus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c1861281f29fb98bb9ef62b4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9304]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Indra among kings! Those five elements350 are satisfied." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c19b8edff5b2606c54d464af> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3185]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Having extended their arms to take these many oaths, all these tigers among men went to Dhritarashtra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c1a7d69f0507871f65c6840a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4909]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Her garments, as white as moonlight, were blown away by the wind and immediately the masses of gods lowered their faces." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c1aac4fdf4931c258aa40273> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5827]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Shakra said, ‘I have a doubt about the prosperity seen by those who reside in Goloka72 and it transcending that experienced by the residents of the world of heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c1bb3f689824c5904eaae974> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7169]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If a person eats179 with his head covered in cloth, if he eats facing a southern direction, or if he eats with his footwear on, all the resultant learning is obtained by the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c1bfb3f5c51beb92d92e8813> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12856]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! On seeing that mountain peak descend, Shatakratu236 splintered it with his vajra and it fell down on the ground." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c1e069134bc7e2d6cd473369> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1725]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowledge is shrouded in ignorance." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c1e6263ef8543ea00c2fdea0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19434]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because of the compassion in his soul, he became engaged in ensuring what was pleasant for the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c1ebb441f159cbdc7785c24f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11073]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When King Hemavarma96 has returned to Dasharna, I will become a maiden again and you will become a man." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c1f3b724c8af793db33fea21> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16114]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those who expound on them are superior, because they uphold all kinds of dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c20b72cd99c252ca5c2398c4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12011, 12013]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Remembering his earlier enmity, he256 had come to him on his own, promising to fight and kill Bhimasena in the battle.
Having seen that he258 had been killed by Bhimasena’s son, he thought that Bhimasena’s pledge259 had already been fulfilled.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c24c4f581da71bd867c69988> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16244]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Kill those evil-souled rakshasas, who have forms like yours." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c284fe73d9311015d40053c8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6863]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Why should he not rule the earth when he has Madri’s two sons worshipping him? When the great-souled lord of Panchala, the lords of Kekaya and Chedi538 and we, march into battle together against the enemies, Suyodhana will depart the world of the living." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c28c53c09eef291b536d22e3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4377]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! The illustrious destroyer of the lineage of the daityas was consecrated by the gods as the general of the celestials in that tirtha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c29ab09e9d8e21ca20a2c65d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7655, 7658]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """This is the lord’s1006 great rod of chastisement and everything is established on this rod of chastisement—in particular, the gods, the rishis, the great-souled ancestors, the yakshas, the rakshasas, the pishachas and the mortals.
You have said that everything that is seen in the worlds—gods, asuras and men, mobile and immobile objects—is touched by the rod of chastisement.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c2a1075e2d4aecba2f4879a5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4919]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Hearing Narada’s words, he225 honoured the bulls among the brahmanas and took their leave." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c2b902a7484382b64f1e0746> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14132]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Purity72 leads to the supreme paramatman, the god who is without decay and without change." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c2b945c05ed03970c9df15d7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4742]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When Drona’s son advanced before Phalguna in the encounter, Jaya556 used a kshurapra arrow to slice down the harnesses that yoked the horses to the chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c2bbcecba218854af5ef65f8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4470]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! On seeing that the immensely valorous and radiant Krishna and Dhananjaya were advancing, the immensely strong one535 made great efforts to kill Dhrishtadyumna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c2c968ba444fe80f34d3c016> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8859]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "No one is capable of vanquishing him in battle, not even the wielder of the vajra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c2d363b2eb660234797e1e4e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "What shall I say? Shall I state the sacred stories of the Puranas, the source of dharma and artha? Shall I speak of the history of kings among men and sages and great souls?’ The sages replied: ‘Tell us that ancient story that was told by the supreme sage Dvaipayana, that which was worshipped by the gods and the brahmarshis10 when they heard it—and that which is full of wonderful words and divisions and is the supreme of narratives, with subtle meanings and logic, adorned with the essence of the Vedas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c2d59d009f32ceae33ffacd7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[368]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Having spoken these words, Dharmaraja Yudhishthira stopped and the youngest Partha43 replied." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c2db38b37cdad557d1a5027c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24734]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is also known as Kala1281 and he was born out of my rage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c2f02c1fc8faedd8c796f8b9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7329]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On going there, she saw that the Pandavas and Pritha3 were asleep, while the invincible Bhimasena was awake." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c2f24ee36c5db121d95f90bc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2207]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Yudhishthira asked, “Other than the sons of King Dhritarashtra, who are the other rogues121 who are there to play? O Vidura! I am asking you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c2fbf5436e98f67853f249d4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2975]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those who were born in royal lineages in Bharata461 were again slain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c3000b4a8f2ac3b96343d784> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1625]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Krishna102 asked for the boon that the powerful one should always be his vehicle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c30ae5f9802b2620d7f426d9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22024, 22026]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Kshana, truti and nimesha989 are the body hair.
Shuklapaksha and krishnapaksha, equal in strength, are the eyes.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c31957c5fce519c02922aeb6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20845]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He843 realizes that just like himself, Prakriti is devoid of qualities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c32c4753dc818407240e7adc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 221 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13427]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Thus an extremely terrible and fearful battle raged between the gods and the danavas, creating muck out of flesh and blood." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c33bf6e8ec701db3d36b1b06> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5393]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ 98 ‘Bhishma said, “Jamadagni’s son Rama234 was angry when his father was killed and in his anger, the immensely illustrious one killed the king of the Haihayas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c3495b90c2c6381978b1d49b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3416, 3417]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O kings! The gods agreed to what he had said and returned to where they had come from.
Trita cheerfully returned to his own house.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c35ae78fa162f6239559b0f3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6008]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "For the sake of desire, anger or hatred, he should not abandon dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c3607eddbef19b64b4a9c0a0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2291]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He hurled the nail of a tortoise138 at Partha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c36114f682378057baba4d26> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2997]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O bull among the Bharata lineage! Today, I will free myself of the debt I owe to the illustrious kshatriyas16 —Bahlika, Drona, Bhishma, the great-souled Karna, the brave Jayadratha and Bhagadatta, Shalya, the king of Madra, Bhurishrava, my sons, Shakuni Soubala, my friends, well- wishers and kin." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c37928c1bca7c83071f57105> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 126 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8150]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O brahmana! Your words are the words of the Vedas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c391de6b1b8f6d08caec2779> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[68]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Maharatha Kripa and Bhoja12 succumbed to sleep." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c3936578c486621ce41099e9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17672]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Even if there is only one person in the world and he is without faith, the gods do not accept his oblations." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c39ba75152458bfd6073232e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8207]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! On seeing that Durmukha had been killed, Adhiratha’s son mounted his342 chariot and stationed there, was as radiant as the blazing sun." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c3b031e0b7c02580bbbdd3aa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[402]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Know that I have come here as a messenger instructed by Indra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c3b0fd27750beffaaa99848d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19082]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "King Vaishravana671 was also there, served by the guhyakas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c3b4bc4beb399833a4656771> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2067]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The ocean now brought it for him97 and Krishna anointed him with that." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c3f5c3bb27d03253ed45e909> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10086]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In a desolate forest, he confronted a catastrophe because he was seized by a rakshasa who intended to eat him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c42dd590e79555527e0a72d8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6139]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“While that terrible destruction of the best of brave ones was going on, Partha176 suddenly heard the sound of Panchajanya being blown." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c432ef3e73f7fb08f64aff4f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6762]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rama507 and Janardana got to know about his practice of severe austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c445dc1ac7d561e1c635088c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7955]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the subjects! There are many beautiful objects that are offered to the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c46f62c1e2bfb1b40b93b872> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11117]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Ghee is better than what is left of milk after churning." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c491b24e5a37185dc7976b1a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1044]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! Rathas and riders were oppressed by them and suddenly fell down on the ground, like trees broken by the wind." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c49469a0d48c2f48b0d4dac7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8603, 8605]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘“Then Vidura, devoted to the truth and knowledgeable about dharma, glanced towards his father’s74 face and spoke these words.
This lineage of the Kouravas was destroyed75 and you made it rise up again.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c49d60557113d2602b173a89> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4358]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In ancient times, all the gods and rishis assembled and worshipped the grandfather192 on Mount Gandhamadana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c4b8e774122c92f38e034827> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2075]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Vishvakarma294 constructed it for Indra’s sake." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c4ba8be76cc48caa48a11893> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9390, 9391]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The great-souled Bharata26 acquired the earth through his valour.
The slayer of Paka27 obtained lordship of the three worlds through his valour.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c4c14c2a07c4ebe8849cc083> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2554]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He2 saw there the immensely radiant and extremely blue flag known as Vaijayanta, as dark as a blue lotus3 and with a staff that was ornamented with gold." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c4c5a3ac90822e07ad877707> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4951]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As he advanced on foot, armoured and mailed, and with the club in his hand, the gods in the firmament uttered words of praise and honoured him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c4cacdf00e67cdc295db68c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2254]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having crossed the Himalayas and Gandhamadana and traversing unwearied over inaccessible terrain during night and day, Dhananjaya reached Indrakila256 and stopped there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c4f32be0e6d3af963dd63c3d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4955, 4956]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Through the power of his weapons, he has vanquished Bhoja Hardikya58 and you, who are an equal of the gods.
His arrows have killed Shrutayu, Sudakshina, King Shrutayudha, Shrutayu59 and Achyutayu.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c4f8299de2156a173f93df03> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21086, 21090]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """There are the unmanifest, Mahat, ego, earth, wind, space, water and light as the eight.
874 O Indra among kings! O one from Mithila! Those that originate in the five great elements875 are known as Vishesha and the senses of knowledge are known as Savishesha.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c50133de9976e2c18e32ef09> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13955]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is the eternal Purusha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c5016c3da6262b81c8fa9b3a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2176]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Delight all the citizens and rule the earth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c5042dfadc27bdc2f907b3b5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4825]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Arjuna! If I go there, these brave ones565 will say that I am frightened." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c50b755d2609be022632d14d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1142]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘ “When his brother was killed in the battle, Danda advanced, wishing to kill Indra’s younger brother178 and Dhananjaya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c51e4364c67437b8ee01b349> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3129]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He spoke to all the gods and uttered these words, ‘In the midst of all the gods, she has chosen a man as her husband." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c541c8cf61f248fe5c86ec21> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[573]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! In the dead of the night, when the midnight hour had passed, man-eating rakshasas, whose deeds are terrible, begin to roam around." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c551a13d0d27d5bd39e091b1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3922, 3924]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """To save the rakshasas, they said, “Food in which there are insects and worms, food that has been mixed with leftovers, food that is mixed with hair, food that is mixed with grain that has not been broken and food that has been touched by dogs—these will constitute the share of rakshasas.
Those who partake of such food will eat food that is meant for rakshasas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c552074a725f5f7c9e559451> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1868]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Misfortune characterizes the lazy man who sleeps." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c55cf0231a69d8d9c770894d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7040, 7042]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Man-eating rakshasas began to roar in terrible tones.
Dogs uttered many terrible howls.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c56792ee1f7f49dfa387358e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3315]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is only after offering water to the dead that those aryas40 will enter Gajasahrya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c567acb89161099460fcc583> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[195]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O Sanjaya! I had no hope of victory when I heard that the son of Drona76 killed the unborn in the womb of the daughter of Virata77 through a great weapon, and that the son of Drona was cursed jointly by Dvaipayana and Keshava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c567d177fb8f3509c9065dcd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1051]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You worshipped the lord of creatures94 and obtained sons through Rukmini—Charudeshna, Sucharu, Charuvesha, Yasodhara, Charushrava, Charuyasha, Pradyumna and Shambhu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c56c4f9e7e5568d0b49b400b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1562, 1563]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The gods thought of all the oblations as his share.
O lord! When Bhava67 was enraged, the entire universe was in disarray.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c572c8307c10a46241438711> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[512]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let all the gods hurl their weapons towards me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c5736a8f9d09dfb66813180f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 110 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9112]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He comprehends the form of the universe and gets to see the divine rishis known as the Bhurbhuvas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c59b6c6767ae01dd7ef421d4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7862]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O ruler of the earth! They gave offerings of gratitude to the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c5b1bed7d1d810b8f5adcad2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[761, 762]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Krishna29 sought refuge with the one who is all refuge and uttered these words.
‘“It has been said that when all the beings were first created, you were the only Prajapati.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c5bd1956eefa5b728ac24071> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2207, 2215]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Umbrellas were shredded and brought down.
‘Alas, father! Alas, son! Friend, where are you? Stay! Where are you going? Strike! Capture! Kill!’ These and other words mixed with the roars and sounds of laughter and many other kinds of noise were spoken and heard.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c5d3049761c6cf6dd5b00677> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1269]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Satyavati’s son14 himself acted as the brahman." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c5d9fa3ec3f72aef9b17c952> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5665]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord! I have witnessed all this earlier, in the era of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c5ddcbe5139358db339ee012> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5193]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There was a standard with the Indra among birds29 on it and the chariot uttered an excellent roar, thereby increasing Krishna’s glory." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c5e2cd741e71ff215413d7b7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18355]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’” ‘Y ‘Bhishma said, “He saw587 men stationed there, enveloped in desire, anger, greed, fear, intoxication, sleep, laziness and procrastination." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c5ee2bdf4700f189c4d2a3a7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25966]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He1398 described this sacred account to the great-souled Narada." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c5f51e183c3c9e2b7f502a65> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 66 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3058]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! As soon as he was born, he howled like a jackal." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c60eb6a5e697fc4fa78647e8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4064]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There were many others from the large numbers of gods that I have not named." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c61bec8a616cedcf6161d0e8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1492]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Whomever that tiger among men4 wishes to take, his intelligence goes as astray as that of the king of Chedi." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c6294f31fc99c31307c3dcad> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17602]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The mighty-armed one thought that this must have been the work of yakshas or rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c633800371fb7ee7674e61e0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[573]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bibhatsu28 has committed no crime, nor have Partha Vrikodara, Nakula and Sahadeva, and certainly not Yudhishthira." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c639c4394a295ea705731f11> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 194 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9379]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Even if we give him our entire kingdom, it is certain that he will not desert the sons of Kunti." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c63efaec385d3f443a8aeacd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[473]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The chastiser of Paka34 was astounded on learning that it looked upon happiness and unhappiness equally." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c6789d624d98d8141a555066> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9320]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He ordered that many ornaments be made for Droupadi and sent word to his son Duryodhana that Krishna6 should be brought in." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c67c423f50819ee92beccbe8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7853]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Gods, humans, gandharvas, ancestors, serpents, rakshasas and all mobile objects resort to waterbodies." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c688c9ba6589c2e964c83956> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3931]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He joined his hands in salutation, composed himself and asked, “What is dharma for all the varnas? What is it for each of the varnas separately? What are the views on the four ashramas and for rajadharma? Why does a kingdom prosper? Why does a king prosper? O bull among the Bharata lineage! Why do citizens and servants prosper? What kind of treasury, punishment, forts, aides, advisers, officiating priests, priests604 and preceptors should a king avoid? When there is a hardship, whom should a king trust? Whom should a king firmly protect himself against? O grandfather! Tell me this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c692853f4f418e41afaefd2b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3063]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Who will breach a dam10 that has been constructed? Who will rekindle a dying fire? O descendant of the Bharata lineage! The sons of Pritha are now established in peace." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c6af7ca6ed61feb0de723d88> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13564]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Eighty-eight thousand snataka householders5 were supported by Yudhishthira, with thirty servant girls for each." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c6ba43e47897674651f0aa2d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13727]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Who can withstand the energy of those three?”8 Having secretly heard these words of the king, Duryodhana and Soubala9 were disturbed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c6bc4a02e6340a0b1f18f03b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6039]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But except Agastya, who is capable of drying up the ocean?’” ‘Lomasha said, “On hearing Vishnu’s words about drying up the ocean, the gods took Parameshthi’s414 leave and went to Agastya’s hermitage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c6be6200443c7b3f618a0c50> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7970]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The great ascetic Upayaja instructed the king of men25 on the sacrificial rites that would produce a son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c6c1d392fb6edd6849e00a35> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10607]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is through austerities that the gods attained greatness." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c6cfc94dcd75aa35afcb375b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10461]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Nor could the gods save the forest with their strength or quench the fire, so they retreated." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c6dcb7faf5fc3597635af968> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1999, 2000]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Because, O Lord, even the gods and the demons do not know your manifestations.
371 O supreme being! O creator of beings! O lord of beings! O lord of the gods! O lord of the universe! You alone know your own self through your own self.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c6e0e92b11a85525024f4f86> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6566]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ 770(107) ‘“Suparna said, ‘In ancient times, Vivasvat performed a shrouta160 sacrifice here." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c6ffe9648f609974c6cd7f28> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11827]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Sparing those who should be spared, he slays the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c71723cb58155478aa627ae5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1452]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Vanga’s210 elephant was stationed in front of him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c71aabc089438ee981cdcc3b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10055]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! With Revati, the lord Haladhara1 was intoxicated and was followed by many gandharvas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c721c5274f50304217d7b01b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3157]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Following the king21 in the assembly of Kurus, he spoke these words and went out, “I will be the slayer of Duryodhana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c73df0401e6f40c8bf78605a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11594]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The rajarshi directed his son to the great-souled Utanka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c7564e472f04c3bbf076c470> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9353]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Or, one after another, we can seduce them with pretty women so that Krishna21 is disenchanted with Kunti’s sons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c775f6daa60820aa4d49114c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11745]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord! Chyavana has seized the earth and the Kapas1397 have taken over heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c77b973d21bde541ec96b528> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3620]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! The king of the gods glanced at her again." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c7ad8a7a54be46584ffd638a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8512, 8515]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O son! Your father was devoured by a rakshasa in the deep forest.
’ Having been thus addressed, the best of rishis112 was grief-stricken, because he always spoke the truth.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c7d24205e04ec1f43f0288ae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 23 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2196]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He single-handedly killed the soldiers of your son, like the wielder of the vajra against the daityas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c7e36162b83d90e11cb3d83c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[95]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "20 But Ajamidha21 challenged the son of the king of Gandhara, who was skilled in gambling with the dice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c7e613cdc0e54c477b1e853e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4705]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having approached the great river, the gods, the Vasus, bathed there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c7ebdb3c4755d8449a82036f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9399]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O lord! I then purified and prostrated myself before those best of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c7eedc8ba8485efbcbb3c099> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2536]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Seated there, with dharma in his soul, the king339 cheerfully touched the white flowers, the svastika signs, the unhusked grain, the ground, gold, silver and jewels." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c80a38115cb5f5dda44d7294> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9546]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O illustrious one! It is my view that without any more delay, you should issue instructions for the Pandavas to go there58 with their wife." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c82710237a3f2fd2ca57c484> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13740]" ;
