300): 17 shlokas Chapter 1629(301): 27 shlokas Chapter 1630(302): 18 shlokas Chapter 1631(303): 21 shlokas Chapter 1632(304): 27 shlokas Chapter 1633(305): 21 shlokas Chapter 1634(306): 108 shlokas Chapter 1635(307): 14 shlokas Chapter 1636(308): 191 shlokas Chapter 1637(309): 52 shlokas Chapter 1638(310): 29 shlokas Chapter 1639(311): 27 shlokas Chapter 1640(312): 46 shlokas Chapter 1641(313): 51 shlokas Chapter 1642(314): 49 shlokas Chapter 1643(315): 57 shlokas Chapter 1644(316): 59 shlokas Chapter 1645(317): 30 shlokas Chapter 1646(318): 63 shlokas Chapter 1647(319): 29 shlokas Chapter 1648(320): 41 shlokas Chapter 1649(321): 43 shlokas Chapter 1650(322): 52 shlokas Chapter 1651(323): 57 shlokas Chapter 1652(324): 39 shlokas Chapter 1653(325): 4 shlokas Chapter 1654(326): 124 shlokas Chapter 1655(327): 107 shlokas Chapter 1656(328): 53 shlokas Chapter 1657(329): 50 shlokas Chapter 1658(330):71 shlokas Chapter 1659(331): 52 shlokas Chapter 1660(332): 26 shlokas Chapter 1661(333): 25 shlokas Chapter 1662(334): 17 shlokas Chapter 1663(335): 89 shlokas Chapter 1664(336): 82 shlokas Chapter 1665(337): 69 shlokas Chapter 1666(338): 25 shlokas Chapter 1667(339): 21 shlokas Chapter 1668(340): 11 shlokas Chapter 1669(341): 9 shlokas Chapter 1670(342): 16 shlokas Chapter 1671(343): 11 shlokas Chapter 1672(344): 10 shlokas Chapter 1673(345): 13 shlokas Chapter 1674(346): 13 shlokas Chapter 1675(347): 16 shlokas Chapter 1676(348): 20 shlokas Chapter 1677(349): 16 shlokas Chapter 1678(350): 15 shlokas Chapter 1679(351): 6 shlokas Chapter 1680(352): 10 shlokas Chapter 1681(353): 9 shlokas Moksha means liberation, as opposed to the pursuit of dharma, artha and kama." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c82a62cab89b7dc315b9d87c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8202]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Yajnasena’s maharatha son420 bears an inauspicious mark on his standard." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c83be72bc7ee4a90f59d28ba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10294]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But after that, when the Dasharha warriors have cut down the warriors,31 the city of Nagapura32 will await your return." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c84992c82b95b1933d84a767> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 277 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19410]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The rishis, the gods and the asuras have gone from this world to other superior worlds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c85a50c5bfa062a4ede06692> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4337]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods were worshipped in all the temples." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c863823c9513005002280cb7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8869]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Then the mighty Vaikartana30 Karna rushed at Arjuna, eager to fight, like an elephant rushes at a rival over a female elephant." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c86bc30076d5ebda2d0f6c91> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2919, 2920]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Having instructed the gods, Shakra1 returned from Narayana’s abode.
One after another, for the destruction of the enemies of the gods and for the welfare of all the worlds, the dwellers of heaven took birth on earth.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c86d8ec6e9dce877b3063a6e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1649]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "90 O Sanjaya! Somadatta’s son91 is the most venerable among the Kurus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c873dabb62ceaec3970fe39e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1471, 1478]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Elsewhere,58 the gods are radiant because of their deeds.
The destroyer of Bala59 has a lot of energy and ceaselessly showers down, resounding in the sky and in heaven.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c879ec17d625758743530f20> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9279]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He did not even fear the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c88e58e2f71086b4a151deb9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3237]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having encountered Duhshasana’s son, Krishna’s son departed for Vaivasvata’s137 eternal abode." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c896f1456823c6b4d25d556c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2082]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Asses, camels, buffaloes, lions, tigers, small deer,108 kites, bears, wolves, vultures, monkeys, reptiles and many other kinds of flesh-eaters109 hungrily dashed towards Arjuna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c89ae73c745824a81ae44b61> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14193]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Gladden all your well-wishers and chastise the enemies." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8a1c2cb8c36f1fb468508bf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[900]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In this fashion, in that battle, the brahmana78 countered Dhrishtaketu and fought with him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8a4053b3cf19244b89e0544> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9691]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It was filled everywhere with asuras who were always happy, armed with weapons like spears, swords, clubs, bows and maces in their hands." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8a58aff27ee3a3347b07eb8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 94 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5158]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! The gods always revere him and so do the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8a651783e0b7b2263bc28a7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2495]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The one who is the essence of the three worlds released the arrow towards Tripura." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8a9169b74b776d43802cb14> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24691]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The oceans dried up and the Himalayas were shattered." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8aa33fc19fe3cf66b971b4e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3488]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O bull among men! Bhimasena then grasped a large and heavy club made out of steel125 and leapt down from his chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8aaee9d7716a90700f9d4ac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3046]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Abandoning the battle with Pandava Savyasachi, he73 rushed towards Panchala Drupada, surrounded by his soldiers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8ab8e23e678f0f7d194a579> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2823]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ The king agreed to these words of the lord of the gods and awoke from his sleep." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8bc3a05727f97e4dea9a68b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1681]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Maghavan215 showered gold on him for an entire year." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8df7debc110d4c859ef8ea3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11439]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They represent gods among the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8e1e2bc89fcc7fb95bfef14> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13474, 13476]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The gods were like straw to him.
O mighty-armed one! You have destroyed the thorn of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8e77604286ab1869b338021> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13562]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Pritha4 is the equal of the earth itself and I never complain about her." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8e84341ef065ca536dd9749> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[369]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Artisans manufactured golden vessels." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c8f251005d7eef4f9fe2a7f7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[468]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "How could he have been taken away by death? This is like the ocean drying up, Mount Meru moving, or the sun falling down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c92f701fa1380c5f690b47fc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13798]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Listen to the acts of adharma they34 have performed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c932e3e1c509cadc9fa0c830> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4126]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He possesses celestial weapons and he is capable of withstanding the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c93400d98e473ddc97adcdc4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9077]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You march in front of us, like the son of the fire6 leads the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c93fecb6189dbdaa6cb71f1c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[339]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "And that the yakshas, guhyakas, rakshasas, gandharvas, apsaras and Shiva166 are in that of the lord of riches." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c95785e9042153fef6d3cb30> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6585, 6586, 6589]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ Hearing this, Maghavan758 prostrated himself before the grandfather and said, ‘Let the entire universe not be destroyed because of Karna and Arjuna.
O self-creating one! You had earlier said that Vijaya and the other one759 are identical.
’ Brahma and Ishana760 spoke these words to the lord of the thirty gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c95d9a0c03c79c3b7b4f19f0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7868]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That best among Brahmanas then reassured us and smilingly comforted us." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c962e2f4f1a3b449335fb253> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 160 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10941, 10954, 10955]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘“I have heard that the rishis suffered something terrible there.
On witnessing the tumult and the being that had arisen, the grandfather told the maharshis, the gods and the gandharvas, ‘This valiant being is known as a sword and I have thought of it.
This is for the protection of the worlds and for slaying those who hate the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9635c5b8eebd4bd7eabc544> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13056]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The army of the gods was immensely radiant." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c96d107737f5d3cf9a5f6a73> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[699]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "85 O lord of the gods! You are our refuge." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c97c3b3fdf99d6f4fb6f971f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6546]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In earlier times, this was the first region to be covered by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9825ab7d6bef2f38cfd78f4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13346]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In accordance with what you have described, what were their ends? What was the conversation between them? What transpired and what did they do there?” ‘Bhishma replied, “He183 accepted the agreement and worshipped Dharma, Yama, Time, Death and Heaven, as they deserved to be honoured." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9a1b0bca54535fef03fb4e4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 32 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1339, 1340]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Those skilled in the knowledge of mantras offered libations, clarified butter and oblations at the sacrifice and gratified the gods and the maharshis.
Like the gods, the brahmanas were also gratified with gifts, food and great wealth.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9a5a575004c885cea47981e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3644]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods destroy his prosperity." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9b067baf68a9dcc644571c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5522]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In front of the Pandaveyas and the Kurus, Karna spoke harsh and cruel words to Krishna649 in the assembly hall." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9b53a6906f1c8a8a039d028> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10754]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! The illustrious chastiser of Paka80 no longer showers rain at the right time." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9b6d818dde171ce1d5d5f3f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4611]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But ready to give up their lives and seeking refuge with Bhimasena, they542 are driving it away." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9ba0b9444a44cff6322bc20> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2388]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "And the word “Sat” is also used for auspicious acts." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9cdd1c124259ea22200f060> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8780]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing the five Pandavas, like elephants in rut that had come to a lake full of lotuses, like a fire covered with ashes, the chief of the Yadus16 began to wonder." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9d75697d67b4903aa2e2ef8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11695]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In his form as the sun, he saved the gods and slew the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9e918ca354fdc3b35637eeb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[26]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O gods! Grant me peace." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9fa6652615415603000dba0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1734]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "192 He is Pradhana and Mahat." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/c9fcd915de00d5bde14c07e0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5956]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! They armoured themselves and formed a vyuha to counter the Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca04538e8a8db8a2212f14f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 7 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[660]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord! I have told you what the rishis said about the fruits of good and bad deeds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca21c9feeecbab3c1d3eb622> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[47, 48]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """After having caused a great slaughter of the enemy in the battle, Vrisha6 was brought down by Phalguna, while all the sons of Dhritarashtra looked on.
Sanjaya then went to the city of Nagasahvya7 and told Dhritarashtra everything that had transpired in Kurujangala.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca24831d2aff508ceb6208cd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22642]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The second wind is known as Avaha1047 and it blows with a loud roar." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca2534be2c1d656c16adedfb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1489]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! It is certain that Adhokshaja3 will take away Shishupala’s energy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca2b7e409eb7fd661d8ef952> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2597, 2599]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """With the approval of the sacrificial assistants, the lord offered a golden seat, as did Shakra6 to Brihaspati.
Then the king offered his grandfather Krishna9 water to wash his feet and mouth, oblations and a cow, as laid down in the rituals.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca2c4bcdec83f849412f9067> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8410]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rajarshi Kalmashapada Mitrasaha96 said, ‘O Brahmana! Stay here for a while." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca2ea78994b26f7f5197a6e4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5585]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Earlier, it58 had been burnt by the divine weapons of the maharathas, Drona and Karna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca3d2ef059def5d047ccda2b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6619]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Surrounded by your own soldiers, you will be able to vanquish the bull among the rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca51ccfcb4c836a3ad3fffae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1559]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The bulls among the Kurus40 have surrounded Drona from all sides." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca6187be1a8bc07939ef862a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4317]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With diverse weapons in their hands, the gods pursued them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca6a0c97cbe610cd214c2ae0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7376, 7377]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O descendant of the Bharata lineage! In this connection, an ancient history is recounted about a conversation between Vrishadarbhi205 and the saptarshis.
Kashyapa, Atri, Vasishtha, Bharadvaja, Goutama, Vishvamitra, Jamadagni and the virtuous Arundhati206 had a common female servant named Ganda.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca6aa63d6b66ec35f660542c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2014]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With my arrows and with my bow, I am capable of conquering all the worlds, with the gods, the asuras and humans." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca6eec90c88aefff66f5315b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13033]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There are regions for the gods with supreme souls." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ca886e00d296dce8e740f901> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6689]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The assembled gods in the sky were delighted and applauded by sounding their trumpets." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/caa58998a0900039ad6d8c31> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10278]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "23 They do not feel any jealousy towards the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/caa63609b56174b1f98ddba6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20858]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This845 is alone my friend and my emancipation is with it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/caa9a59ae46e344378083eb1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9437]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the lord of the gods! Those who satisfy you do not obtain sin, nor are they defeated in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cab6cbef571bde33a6d74a02> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2782]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "For the sake of a maiden, he216 quarrelled with Sudhanva, the son of Angirasa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cad1dde9cb7001af301e9c98> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7494]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Goutama said, ‘Unlike us, he is not clad in three pieces of kusha grass and one piece of ranku213 hide." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/caec0c75c49783c9695e1b2f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1009, 1010]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! Together with him, Savyasachi, the scorcher of enemies, vanquished the land of Shakala5 and King Prativindhya, the king of Shakala.
Shakala was one of the seven regions6 and there was a tumultuous battle between Arjuna and the armies of the kings of Shakala.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/caf50876546fda1bb784724b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7299]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, the gods and the ancestor suffered because the food wasn’t digested." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/caf91d67a6c11f1c83f7b8b9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6109]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is being devoured in the battle by the brave one,173 like the sun by Rahu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb07e3f8f8c841e55d63e049> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6099]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, there are also inferior men, who are like rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb0bd2935157ddf5044944b4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2938]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let these young boys, who do not know of Prativindhya’s239 intelligence, refer to him as the son of a slave when he arrives." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb0c5cd1535a09c0389b2ea9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4195]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are firm in your valour and are engaged in bringing pleasure to the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb14479010fa25d28eba284c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 101 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7979, 7984]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O lord! O king of the daityas! When a person gives beautiful objects to the gods, with an auspicious end in mind, they are pleased with him.
There are garlands that ensure welfare for the asuras and for the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb1a1c8384285d6030c1cbb9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11139]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "She429 was intelligent and full of humility." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb2708dc139491ef72760211> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[587]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The earth is the refuge and is desired by those who have the bodies of gods and men." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb2a1a6688fdc34ab58f03c9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7600]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The guardians of the world were on his arms283 and Agni was created from his mouth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb2ab2e48c168301c098596e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4818]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Subjugating them, the protector of the horse went to Surashtra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb2d9a97dfb56e609dc70add> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21341]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If it emerges through the knees, he obtains the immensely fortunate gods known as the Sadhyas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb2ddbec69274a63283414aa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9784, 9785]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Together with the other gods, the king of the gods repeatedly congratulated me and spoke these gentle words.
‘In battle, you have accomplished a deed that was impossible for the gods and the asuras.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb3b96511711789432357d75> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 192 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13302]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It has been determined that kings must protect their own dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb4312afda8b3c1e6c3ad0d6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 180 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10485]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O descendant of the Bharata lineage! I did not strike Jamadagni’s son any more." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb45074f54a5bfec9dd11dd0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25438]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ In the manvantara known as Svayambhuva, he1352 collated the Vedas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb88685dd9ace23abb50e934> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3090]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bhoja115 killed his horses and Goutama116 the charioteers who guarded his flanks." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cb95337192c140d3058740e3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20427]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Maitravaruni785 was seated." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cbaaf0ad9f2b64228ce7f26a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1946]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They attain sanctified heaven 345 and in heaven, enjoy the celestial objects enjoyed by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cbac90d559ea45fc7326e73a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 182 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12474, 12481, 12482]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """89 The sages are always in control of their souls, self- restrained and always engaged in the observance of austerities.
In this way, a brahmana can obtain bliss in the brahman.
Constant purity, devotion to good conduct and compassion towards all beings—these are the signs of a brahmana.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cbad2665027533d231f74fdc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5742]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He fed this to the brahmana and summoned him385 back." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cbb0b9cdc435d064d94a6bd5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13896]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that the sons of Dhritarashtra were fleeing from the field of battle, the brave Vaikartana33 was the only one who wasn’t reluctant to do battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cbb5e560f734a8b95ec59142> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3579]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The great-minded one was surrounded by five armies256 and wished to get at Drona." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cbbf6869a56f4b51343a6fc4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8938]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If a man eats only one meal a month during the month of Kartika,327 when he is reborn, he is brave, obtains great fame and has many wives." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cbd12250152114821dd06836> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7014]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is certain that anything that serves to hold up is dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cbdc6a419b471a3ed622eebb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6347]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The destroyer of Bala strikes with his weapons only after he127 has struck first." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cbde8d81a00d084624c2cd01> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2730]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This son of Pandu211 was addicted to vice and challenged by deceitful gamblers, staked Droupadi." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cbebc1769f4a703249123e4d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17298]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This is what the Creator ordained in ancient times, for the sake of ensuring accumulation in the worlds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc04348c261a1fe5f614c653> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11280]" ;
        mbh:sourceText ") Pushkaraksha;954 (513) Maha-mana;955 (514) Bhagavat;956 (515) Bhagaha;957 (516) Nandi;958 (517) Vanamali;959 (518) Halayudha;960 (519) Aditya; (520) Jyotiraditya;961 (521) Sahishnu;962 (522) Gati-sattama;963 (523) Sudhanva;964 (524) Khanda-parashu;965 (525) Daruna;966 (526) Dravina-prada;967 (527) Divah-sprik968 (528) Sarva-drik;969 (529) Vyasa; (." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc0897f4367ec059f6a41785> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9674]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘I seek refuge from whatever gods reside here." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc283c837973f0eb0340fe9a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19345]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’” ‘Bhishma said, “Tarkshya683 was knowledgable about all the sacred texts." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc29c84037fbb74103797789> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6973]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Puru and Yadu228 followed their sister to the hermitage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc333339ad8bf4dff0120063> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1240]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Had those tigers among men been alive, not even the wielder of the vajra120 himself would have been able to kill Shura’s son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc35871fa7a473dc2b3295a5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9940, 9942]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Sarasvati’s banks were covered with many plakshas,21 akshas,22 rohitakas,23 cane, snuhas,24 badaris,25 khadiras,26 shirishas,27 bilvas,28 ingudas,29 pilus,30 shamis31 and kariras.
It was the sacrificial ground of the gods themselves.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc3794a015e494a45e04293a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13337]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Airavata302 had two bells known as Vaijayanti." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc3fa0e341d17c94dfe6f409> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1869]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Thus addressed by Sanjaya, the king spoke again." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc500b241a2ab1df6de9981f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7053]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lord161 protected the gods and did what would bring Shankara pleasure." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc536f9bef6a6bda477b5e00> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9272]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In that chariot that was unmatched in its splendour, he then returned to the lord of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc712c505dc359c1683cc0c0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[80]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The messenger of the gods went on ahead and the king followed at the back." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc865b522b3a278d4a2b8d2c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6293]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Rathas, on your side and on theirs, killed masses of infantry and chariot- riders and many horses in that encounter." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc8b7ddd89f54a075d9e81cd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 164 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9389, 9390]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The sound of delightful and divine musical instruments was heard on all sides, together with chants in praise of Indra.
Masses of apsaras and gandharvas began to sing various songs in front of the god of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cc9472785399c81fc4507ef8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4753]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Section 87 will be concluded in Volume 10." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cca249bc430032399578e5e4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10242]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Through a long period of faith and certain and firm devotion, and through the grace of the god of the gods, fruits are swiftly obtained." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ccdef27a9dc8a9c03576472e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10334]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He worshipped all the gods and attired in armour, with guards for his fingers and wrists, and with a sword slung against his chest, ascended it, like a virtuous man on a vimana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ccec8f75e97f33be1cbce841> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4976]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "217 Whatever tirthas exist on earth and in the sky, female rivers, male rivers, lakes, all streams, wells, ponds and everything else that is sacred, there is no doubt that they are gathered every month at Samnihiti." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cced0e8a59d700c4b1932e65> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2723]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "64 ‘O son! It is through good fortune that you are alive amidst this destruction of the Kurus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ccefe3eede77819f96f17ad2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18900]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having presented themselves at that battle, the gods and the asuras roared and sounded musical instruments." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cd08f0c805c85749bbb4d1ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[531]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O foremost among the Bharata lineage! That army54 made a sound like that of the agitated ocean." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cd2d2bc24a2a4c5251648b8c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7058]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Together with your brothers, you must offer oblations to the ancestors and the gods there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cd49197290ab4462a1be180c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[211]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "So that he might surpass him, Harivahana14 summoned Brihaspati and, together with the other gods, spoke these words to him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cd5be57b4fc47299b18f1b88> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3018]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "1 O bull among the Bharata lineage! On arriving before Duryodhana and his advisers, the foremost of the Bharatas2 spoke these miserable words, “O maharathas! That old man has made us lose everything that we had obtained with great difficulty." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cd5d6be763d4394154dbe31d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3406]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Hair, bones and skulls will be scattered around, as if Prajapati25 left his work incomplete." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cd68aea4955cd5755c836aac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10424]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As long as Pandu’s son131 is alive, the Pandava army is incapable of being quickly defeated." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cd6bff72f4dbec48968fac61> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3805, 3806]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He did not possess the knowledge known as sanjivani139 that the valorous Kavya possessed.
Thus, the gods were immersed in supreme misery.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cd798559f458c4aad471f85c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3030]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I have come here as a messenger of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cd880637c5fd97532dc0a606> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5855]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But he675 seized it and hurled it back and it penetrated the great-souled Pandava’s left arm." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cd89d2eb2847024bc923f621> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[579]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "11 Six spokes12 and one axle bear the immortal nectar to which the gods of the universe are addicted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cd8d01ffcd1dd020fd238f5f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6326]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Had Krishna’s son194 been here, with the makara on his banner and with the bow in his hand, I would have handed you over to him and he would have protected you, like Arjuna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cdc5e41923b306660bac666c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13189]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At that, thousands of armies of the gods came to him from all the directions and said that he was their lord." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cdd7399b5d3592ca0d01b2b8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2806]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Among the rivers of earth, Ganga is like the lord of the gods1229 to men, the moon to the ancestors and the sun to the stellar bodies in the firmament." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cde21c5d805022c6161c8c8a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7437]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among men! There were many kings, hundreds and thousands, who had assembled on your side and that of the Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cde79188e3a5fec325dbe3b8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 45 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2214]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was born in Uttara’s womb when the Kuru lineage was almost destroyed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cded38e4871da7fb0ff2f55a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15390]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Kuru lineage! King Dasharatha looked at such a son, one who extended Kousalya’s67 joy, and was extremely delighted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce18ba1ec9c262f6676de685> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3875]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Abandon desire, anger, avarice and price and cast these off far away." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce1adb4053eb00cc57961985> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1677]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“O kings! This son of a lady of the Satvata lineage38 is a great enemy of the Satvata clan." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce322a48ac5bbb99a3424ac8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2261]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When he is enraged, no one can fight him single-handedly in battle, other than the god with the thousand eyes133 and Devaki’s son Krishna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce38017db5ce0134708289db> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4435]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He also got the riches of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce3e663dd9618799e1e45770> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[672]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Your dharma is that of a dasyu9 and is not deserving of an assembly hall." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce50384386739dab74bcf487> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[119]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Gada’s elder brother15 foresaw the destruction of all the kings, but Janardana thought that this would be supremely beneficial." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce53477820a62dd19bc117d2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15348]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There was this unmatched radiance that illuminated the three worlds and it was astride Vishnu’s vehicle, with both Suparna209 and the sun situated there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce5f80ddc86c32638c9ec9c4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8929, 8930, 8931, 8932]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """If a person is devoted to his father and eats only one meal during the month of Magha,318 he is reborn in a prosperous lineage and obtains greatness amidst his relatives.
If a person eats only one meal during the month of Bhagadaiva,319 he is loved by women and they are under his control.
If a person is controlled and eats only one meal during the month of Chaitra,320 he is reborn in a great family that has a wealth of gold, jewels and pearls.
If a person conquers his senses and eats only one meal during the month of Vaishakha,321 regardless of whether the person is a man or a woman, the person obtains superiority among all the relatives.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce625e4683bcfb28ecc8f5c2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2445]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” O great king! At that time, the women praised Krishna323 thus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce6fc502bdd90f46fb811ae9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2241]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘ “‘The gods and the asuras engaged with each other in a mighty battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce79e4561494a390a0d705d3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1842]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O venerable one! Angered, he quickly attacked all the Pandus, Parshata Dhrishtadyumna, Shikhandi, Droupadi’s sons, the large numbers of Panchalas, the Kekayas, the Somakas and the Panchalas16 and countered them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce7c7a4b3eb35dfca5a03351> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1241]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The angry king of the Trigartas10 spoke to the maharathas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ce9238ca4918e7f435266c86> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1887, 1890]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Though Kounteya36 loves dice, he has no knowledge.
”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Having been thus addressed by Shakuni, King Duryodhana then instantly addressed these words to Dhritarasthra, “O king! This one37 is skilled in dice.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ced75e5a87325a08845b1c2b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13307]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His108 grey hair hung down, up to his ears." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf0187cf09d19ad468a1e36c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8812]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He7 was learned, skilled, knowledgeable on everything concerning dharma and knew the past and the future." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf0b24498aa71a166aabfadd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6148, 6149, 6151]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Soma is obtained through sacrifices and sacrifices depend on cows.
When a means of subsistence was first arranged for subjects, the gods were delighted.
Thirsty, and seeking a means of subsistence, they approached the one who was like a father and a mother.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf1633d7e51454ecf03d79a8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7641]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! We have heard that with his terrible and great austerities, he caused great distress to the king of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf20b6352bd6cd0e38c75953> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7490]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The son of the suta274 is firm in his anger and so is your brother, Duhshasana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf263ee291de463307bf8ce0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6560]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Drona said, ‘Your preceptor219 has abandoned the battle and departed like a coward." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf3247673314d78618f1c0ce> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5068]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O best of the gods! O one who increases good deeds! Please bring them quickly." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf3513db3e3b0f99d2d107e5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12116]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“In ancient times, the valiant asuras had three cities in the firmament and these were made out of iron, silver and gold." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf3ac14907046d914d12fc87> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[826]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He56 was accomplished in jnana and vijnana and knew the past and the future in great detail." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf3fe760ab2e0246622b35f0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17235, 17236, 17239, 17240]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """When their lives are over, all gods among beings depart and return again.
486 O lion among kings! In that way, when their lives are over, all men go away, like the gods.
That is the reason the wind is special and is known as the god of the gods.
All the gods are characterized by traits of mortality.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf41cd65c0ff45c048e1fd13> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1362]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Desire is created in man." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf41e4f4cb1ed9e9c26fdcd6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2892]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I will be censured by the gods by speaking to you about those." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf51772818a29a5e1b2acf09> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6913]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Having been thus addressed by Madhusudana, the wielder of Gandiva, fierce in using the bow and arrow against enemies, asked, ‘Who is the serpent who is advancing against me of his own accord, as if into Garuda’s gaping mouth?’ Krishna replied, ‘In Khandava, you satisfied the blazing one794 with the bow in your hand." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cf968409dfbd3f8507b80a00> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2638]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "And the sons of Pritha20 lived there for many years." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cfbdf32daa5448f366790c50> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[612]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Pandava45 protects like all the large number of kings who have preceded him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cfd4e5e356e27db391353ec5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[406, 407]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! All the other gods are under his subjugation.
Hear the message of the king of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cfdc6ae0fe9eda480b918be1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[155]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Are the sons of good families chiefly loyal to you? In the field of battle, are they ever ready to give up their lives for you? In military affairs, is there a single one who is beyond control and causes harm to many because of selfish reasons? If a man performs an extraordinary act beyond what he is required to do, does he obtain greater honour, rations and wages? Do you reward, with wealth and honour, men who are learned, humble and skilled in any type of knowledge in accordance with their qualities? O bull among the Bharata lineage! Do you support the wives of men who have given up their lives for you and those who have otherwise come to grief for your sake? O Partha! Do you offer protection, like to a son, to an enemy who has been defeated in battle, or surrenders, having become fearful and weak? O lord of the earth! Are you impartial towards everyone on earth and can they fearlessly come to you, like a father or a mother? O bull among the Bharata lineage! When you get to know that an enemy is in distress, do you inspect the three parts of your force45 and swiftly advance on him, knowing that the rear of the army is the root of defeat? O great king! Do you pay wages to your soldiers in advance? O scorcher of enemies! Do you distribute riches from the enemy kingdom among the chiefs of your army, in accordance with what they deserve? O Partha! After having first controlled your own self and senses, do you seek to defeat enemies who are enslaved by their own passions and senses? Before marching against your enemies, do you first employ the four techniques of sama, dana, danda and bheda,46 in accordance with their qualities? O lord of the earth! Do you first strengthen your base before marching out? Do you attack to win and having won, do you protect? Does your army have four types of forces47 and is it divided into eight wings,48 well trained by superior officers and capable of defeating the enemy? O scorcher of enemies! O great king! When attacking the enemy in battle, surely you do not kill during seasons of sowing and harvesting." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cfed957aac70ed8dc8d842af> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6280]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Using large arrows, he706 severed Shikhandi’s bow and standard and then pierced Shikhandi with six fierce arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cfee4863ec10a28036808d5d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4371]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Choose the game of dice, or bend your bow in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cfeef951ed15b5e0ede719f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5961]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is artha in this world and eternal bliss in Brahma’s world." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/cffa3db9e532dc9c7254f136> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10804]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In the twinkling of an eye, he152 picked up another bow and pierced Pandava with sixty arrows and his charioteer with nine." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d0265e0cd5a8db2f0225f117> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25236]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Brahma had a third birth from his1322 great speech." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d0304c6c8f2b41c185308ed4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6022]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Jamadagni’s son80 then spoke these words in that assembly of the Kurus, “O king! Listen to the example that I am going to cite." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d03831c55bb8234e9c77df7e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5526]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O one with the beautiful hips! Bear a son who is equal in radiance to the king of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d03a388596edf5d19abbba2b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10255, 10256]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘They reached that beautiful pleasure ground, dotted with many trees and adorned with many tall houses, like Purandara’s8 abode.
Flavoured and expensive food and drinks were spread out and many perfumed garlands were adorned for Varshneya9 and Partha.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d0577b332c3d71cfb53f5cca> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12075, 12078]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """What else should one say about them? However, there are those who speak agreeably towards gods and guests.
49 Those who do not find reasons in dharma are like shrivelled grain among grains, termites50 among birds and the worst among men.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d0586fc8b626eff041060883> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1984]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The seven great sages, 361 the four who came before them 362 and the Manus 363 owe their origin to me and were created from my resolution." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d059402382210fab9036d779> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4020]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I used them to bring down all the enemies of the gods in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d06fd24e16d6de73594808dc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6455]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But the lord of Gandhara731 severed his head, while he was still roaring." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d07d78d2da229bd6193ed8f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[802]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Depending on his valour, your son embarked on that game of dice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d09c2670a15b5858d71b8393> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19476]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Earlier, the bull among the thirty gods had closed all the other outlets." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d0a96f42ce5dd1a898d80f7f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4575]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! He who goes to Agastya’s38 lake and engages himself in worshipping the ancestors and the gods, residing there for three nights, obtains the merits of an agnishtoma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d0b3b9daba7217521bbf9195> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3328]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Predatory animals are screaming, together with vultures, jackals and crows, in the temples of the gods, in sanctuaries and from the tops of walls and houses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d0b4d1cca6e18e016bfd223f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2972]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Hearing the words of Narada, the slayer of Bala and Vritra81 asked, ‘The righteous lords of the earth give up their lives in fighting." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d0b7cd2eaa7ef44a38a2078d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4480, 4482, 4483]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """That was the abode of the god of the gods.
The thirty gods have paid me homage.
I have rivalled the gods in power and glory.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d0b887abb8053e33cf85efa5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[623, 625]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """I will make large offerings of blood to Baka.
I will obtain supreme peace by removing this thorn of the rakshasas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d0cfe1be2933007bd09baf78> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7408]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In this battle, the gods, the asuras, men, gandharvas, serpents and rakshasas will angrily kill one another." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d1032aaa72c600e3e581e248> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2149]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having spent the night in this way, the brahmana arose in the morning." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d105184247249e476ef04521> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 40 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2832]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Even one single angry brahmana destroys a kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d11f7bdb00f5ac5935fbbba7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13713]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That became the fire of destruction for the Kurus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d1267387af3898397d70f825> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2060, 2061]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Chekitana92 gave the quiver, the king of Kashi the bow and Shalya the sword with a golden hilt and with straps inlaid with gold.
Dhoumya and the immensely ascetic Vyasa performed the anointing, after having placed Narada and the sages Devala–Asita93 at the forefront.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d12bde1ff9374416f8c01513> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11633, 11636]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O god! O lord! O supreme among the best of the gods! But there is one thing that we wish you to do.
O god! O supreme among gods! Know that this is the boon that we ask for.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d12d67266956a1dcd6d2b574> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[646]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Armour and headdresses were scattered around." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d135effb99429ff9dac6a952> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3587]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Duhshasana saw that he452 was without a chariot and devoid of weapons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d14a6a09a9ca9a1cad3e717b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9991, 9996]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’”’ Chapter 1804(123) ‘Bhishma said, “Thus addressed, the illustrious one377 replied to Maitreya.
The gods have shown you their favours.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d15315829e397cba81d22a89> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12414]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Krishna! On learning that Pandava, the one with the white horses, had left in search of weapons, the great archer20 had come to me in Kamyaka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d15903bd8bbfafb99725c28e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6712]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! In that battle, he spoke these words to Vasudeva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d164fac57ed0c59f3d640c53> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1500]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You have once again injured our minds by specially recounting this one’s deeds, such as the killing of Putana6 and so on." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d184c4b7c3edce32f202bdfc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3196]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With all the Yadavas, he set out when the conjunction of nakshatras known as Maitra37 occurred." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d194c0f0b7a4aff115dd4763> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1331]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The two of you are like gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d1980e1256780a05a7fb291a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2663]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Why did those tigers among men, despite being innocent and capable of wreaking vengeance on their enemies, suffer the oppressions of those evil ones quietly? O supreme among Brahmanas! Why did Vrikodara, who in his mighty arms had the strength of 10,00030 elephants, keep his anger under control, despite being oppressed? Why did not the pure Krishna Droupadi, oppressed by the evil sons of Dhritarashtra, burn them with her angry eyes, capable though she was of doing it? Why did those tigers among men, the two sons31 of Pritha and the two sons of Madri,32 though oppressed by the evil ones, follow Yudhishthira, addicted to the evil vice of gambling? Why did Yudhishthira, the best among righteous men and the son of Dharma himself, suffer extreme misfortune, though he knew the path of virtuous conduct? Why did Pandu’s son Dhananjaya, with Krishna as his charioteer, and capable of dispatching many warriors to the land of the dead with his arrows, suffer so much oppression? O blessed with the power of austerities! Tell me everything that those great warriors did in every situation." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d19ecc296d1aa2e6f64c44a6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16350, 16351, 16352]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘O one for whom truth is valour! You have removed the misery of the gods, the gandharvas, the yakshas, men, asuras and serpents.
Therefore, all the worlds, with the gods, the asuras, the gandharvas, the yakshas, the rakshasas and the serpents will speak of your deeds as long as the earth exists.
’ Speaking these words to Rama, supreme among all wielders of weapons, he147 took his leave and having honoured him, departed in the chariot that was as resplendent as the sun.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d19ed73a2555d00eeaffaf08> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1263]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Umbrellas are scattered around and so are fans and whisks." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d1a2f039e1b0bd5aa85946ba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8585, 8586]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! O Kouravya! O unblemished one! After having established the one without decay69 on the kingdom, he left for the forest with his wife.
Vidura, tiger among men, humbly accepted a position that was inferior to him70 and served him, like one fanning him with a whisk.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d1ba25fe91b6023524b6b416> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13366]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On the right was his radiant staff, accompanied by Shri, with Bhrigu, Angiras314 and the gods worshipping it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d1babed616a9b5a12dc069a5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6766]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But, strong in spirit, and in accordance with the prescriptions of dharma, he508 went and offered homage to Rama, Janardana, Krishna’s son Samba, Shini’s grandson509 and all the other Vrishnis." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d1c7f75748a894c8d192868c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3602]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Why are you dancing around in this way? O supreme among sages! What is the reason for your delight? Tell me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d1df530f1d89b05b0ea302aa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22200]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Driven by this resolution, he prayed to the lord of ‘B the gods, one whom those with unclean souls find difficult to obtain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d1f6149fe2a6c0e875b1bbe6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 19 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1345]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He looked like the full moon, in conjunction with Krittika." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d200d890e8fc2d999c94168f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7566]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘One day, when the bulls of the Bharata lineage had gone out begging, Bhimasena was at home with Pritha1 for company." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d2049601afa3e2b32762ee2a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4898]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having performed one’s ablutions there, one should worship the ancestors and the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d217bd3431ad8a3e18818d25> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[83]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Kouravya13 saw that Dharma’s son followed the extremely intelligent king and also followed him, but his heart was not in it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d2261bf2cd842b5f029ac17c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16465]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Act in a way so that we are not condemned by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d2390e2c7c27c9a2427c4a74> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8407]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Thereafter, the wise king was possessed and tormented by the rakshasa within him and found it difficult to save himself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d257e367bdf6868583aa0cbe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1773]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He struck Durmukha in the midst of his eyebrows with an iron arrow and his73 face looked as beautiful as a lotus with a stalk." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d26e0477c8cb93584093aca9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1080, 1081]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """They were astride elephants that looked like the elephant of the king of the gods.
They were angry and insolent, as insolent as the enemies of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d275f076a43696525838fba8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O illustrious one! When the supreme among archers was killed, what did Kouravya2 do? O supreme among brahmanas! Tell me all this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d2781092f13c611d277e4cd9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5039]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Desiring to do what was agreeable to Partha, Kunti herself honoured the queens350 and they made themselves comfortable on extremely expensive beds and seats." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d28cc83bcab636c9ced0d654> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3327]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With the fire god at the forefront, the gods reside in the eastern direction." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d297d642240dcbd83666afa0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[649]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When he was numbed by the force of the rock, the rakshasa rushed at him, like Svarbhanu14 dashing at the sun and dispersing the rays with his arms." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d2a39df85e93394e9b8e1016> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6330]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On beholding it advance, the angry rakshasas grasped weapons in their hands." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d2a469d02c9917949315fb11> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8504]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In the encounter, the king of Chedi433 struck Pourava, bull among men, on the shoulder joint with the sharp tip of his giant sword." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d2dcffdff8c484332ca27b2b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2977]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Sthanu12 had eleven great sons through the powers of his mind—Mrigavyadha, Sarva, the famous Nirriti, Aja, Ekapada, Pinaki the destroyer of enemies, Dahana, Ishvara, the greatly radiant Kapali, Sthanu and the great lord Bhaga." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d30e6fa1329c664b166182c2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23066]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the gods also looked towards him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3152acd701f0929d3232875> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8387]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! On seeing that thirty-one of your maharatha sons had been killed, Duryodhana remembered the words of Kshatta,364 which had been spoken at the time of the gambling match to your evil-minded son, when Karna had spoken harsh words to Krishna365 in the assembly hall." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d32e55bef792cc4b18aff0f4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5417]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "For your sake, I will take on the gods, the daityas and all the worlds, not to speak of the enemies here." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d330ab7a9847c2470f0f44c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15109]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Headless torsos and torso- less heads were strewn all over the entire earth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3451f138c241d8a0d59c74c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8836]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The drums of the gods were sounded with a great roar." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d34c5d71df9e120c904ee78f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17473]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Karna replied, “I wish to kill only one enemy37 in a great battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d36690dc5aad91d8ff36997a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4688, 4689]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """37 But quickly and forcefully, Bhoja38 struck him with ten arrows that were tufted with the feathers of herons.
O king! Arjuna pierced him with sharp arrows and confounded Satvata39 by striking him again with three arrows.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d36c4f57d6a8cd5385c3d7e8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6299]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O mighty-armed one! Having said this, he444 went to the Himalayas, surrounded by his terrible attendants, who held diverse upraised weapons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3725806539f1c9355fd593e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22788, 22800]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Abandon adharma and violence.
Everything results from the atoms1064 of Mahat.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3797598a3df016fbecf0b8d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5035]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The queen Chitrangada and Kouravaya’s daughter349 met Pritha and Krishna with humility." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d37d4104b6db0a97ea097318> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8948]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He obtains greatness in Brahma’s world for a full one thousand years." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3801215de1d4e621a9365c3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1987]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "After presenting a receptacle that was like iron58 and swords with handles of ivory, Bhagadatta of Pragjyotisha left." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d383eee2ccf67f3ddeacf2bc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5504]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those who were not virtuous fled, like atheists turning away from the Vedas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3862a2fb625a60ff908728b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16535, 16536]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The fourth stage391 is generally referred to as the dharma of the Upanishads.
This follows after garhasthya and vanaprastha.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d38c1738e586aedcb14bfe41> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2049]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The immensely radiant one satisfied the gods and the ancestors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d38f0f07cb76624766aa3434> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1652]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Blazing in gold, it fell down in front of Yuyutsu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3924b72fb24bdc28681b3a3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7924]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It was as swift as thought and the wind and quickly reached Drona." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3934645620da58ae85211f5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5789]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that they were advancing against Dhananjaya, foremost among the wielders of weapons, with Shikhandi at the forefront, they291 advanced to protect Arjuna’s chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3946da826dccd6ae9123cb8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9661]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "365 Blazing in their prosperity, they remained in Brahma’s world." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d39fe77c0896c7a815d71c18> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[868]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, Shrutakarma, the great archer, angrily used his arrows to drive away those soldiers, like the wrathful lord of the dead147 at the time of the destruction of all beings." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3bdfce8ffdd65c8db86723f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[260]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The descendant of the Kuru lineage saw Nakula and Sahadeva in the region of the Ashvins, blazing in their own energy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3c05fb2fdfda4bc2cbbb525> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3144]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage and O ruler of men! The brave and lotus-eyed Ashvatthama, of great valour, tormentor of enemies and fearful to enemy armies, was born from three parts of Mahadeva that merged into one—yama,65 kama66 and krodha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3f8531f94d3f614b0ab6b1b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6657]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "226 O Sanjaya! When that bull among the Pandavas227 swiftly entered and penetrated my ocean of soldiers on a single chariot and Yuyudhana followed him, I do not see any remnant being left." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d3ff9c019ee0ca9f85f6853e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24105]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among gods! Depending on the acts undertaken and conduct followed by creatures, determine their spans of life." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d40721134567ee59df7bf7a2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15562]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then, glancing towards Rama, he dragged him89 towards his mouth, and afflicted with despair, he90 told Rama, ‘Look at my state." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d40fecf524e42cbbafc7f946> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 189 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9207]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Having heard this, the wielder of the vajra once again spoke to the greatest of the gods,43 ‘With my semen, I will create a man who can accomplish this task." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d41df6794c340ad33c8fa49e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1940]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When you rule it, you shine like the lord of the gods in heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d42258191808dd2ae53a0253> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25683]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O guest! You possess the strength of intelligence and know the truth about the purport of dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d426dea8aa97e3bcc9aac4d8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14040]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that the mace had been cut into many pieces by the arrows of the nimble one, he57 made himself invisible and began to fight with Pandava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d42c5be6fe9b28718fafa8fa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16232]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was surrounded by terrible rakshasas, with many weapons in their hands." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d42cf828c29096c0bafc7159> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3341]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But with his soldiers, how did he encounter him112 in battle?” ‘Sanjaya replied, “O Indra among kings! Thus instructed by your son, the immensely strong one was protected by a large army and advanced towards Bhima’s chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d4676afc37f168290bc328a2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11552]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Ghatotkacha shattered into tiny fragments his216 chariot, his charioteer and all the fierce weapons, capable of destroying life, that were hurled at him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d474b77830a9369e79f3955b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8193]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Dharmaraja1099 looked towards that bull among men and bowed down before him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d487b85eee9a5a2e5ddeee25> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15506]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "230 The bull among the gods arrived there, on a chariot that was yoked to tawny horses and was immediately honoured by all the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d491f9e996cc41735517adde> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 188 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11166]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! Rahu will envelope the sun at the wrong time." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d4a77c5d020b5d80776234df> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4230]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With the gods as their aides, they cannot be repulsed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d4a86bf6f99a99209c3e4b1a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[834, 841]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ ‘“The priest asked, ‘Whenever sacred oblations are being offered, the rites of dharma performed and chants of peace recited, why do you glance towards me and laugh? Since you laugh at me, my mind is ashamed.
’ ‘“The king replied, ‘O brahmana! If you ask me in this way, I must certainly tell you the truth, even though this is not something that you should hear.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d4beccf0fef31a37eb4660cb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5281, 5282]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Under Ardra, if a man fasts and gives krisara37mixed with oil, then he is freed from all difficulties, including those that are as razor-sharp as the edges of mountains.
O beautiful one! Under Punarvasu, if one gives sweet cakes and food, one is reborn in a family that has a lot of food and one is also famous and handsome.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d4d4b7cc9f38086ad60cfd20> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19453]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lord of the gods therefore bent the bow with his hand." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d4dd61d5e564afb098ed28d3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10481, 10482]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """In this world, Mahendra Prajapati46 occupies the foremost place.
’ Atri then replied to Goutama, ‘He47 is as much of a sustainer as Prajapati Indra.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d4dfd3b62b1ab2e99759b0e5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10075, 10076, 10077, 10079]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """On hearing, the mighty-armed Pandava9 agreed.
’ 212 Vaishampayana said, ‘O Janamejaya! Dhananjaya10 learnt that the lady had gone to Raivataka.
Having learnt of the sanction11 and after obtaining Vasudeva’s permission, the bull of the Bharata lineage discussed and got Krishna’s sanction about the course of action.
It was yoked with Sainya and Sugriva12 and decorated with nets of small bells.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d4e3ada2b89f8a8cc2cec169> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2493]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In the battle, having been struck by Bhima with arrows washed in oil, he47 angrily covered Sahadeva with a shower of arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d530aeee5cffee69d6619d6d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8881]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They are slicing through my body, like the month of Magha distresses cattle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d54030b44ebb059be5a56585> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3511]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“Once, Brihaspati and Ushanas51 presented themselves before Brahma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d54d7ff5a914c009f3193abf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7579]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Like Surabhi4 dashes at her tethered calf, Kunti hurried towards the inner quarters of the great-souled Brahmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d5714890f3bedbd4071d77b8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[719]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "100 Shrutakarma101 picked up a club and attacked him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d5b39fb6f4d78ada79726c69> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12279]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If the Vedas, direct perception1438 and conduct are the three yardsticks, they are seen to be different." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d5ca38d5e38cc1afdf42f3bb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[729]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ 677(14) ‘Shalya said, “On seeing that the goddess90 was endowed with youth and beauty, thus did Upashruti appear before the beautiful and virtuous one." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d5d416ce3a641d53901796c2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1273]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The wielder of the Sharnga31 bow was like Vasava on that chariot, with the two Ashvins on either side." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d5e6b6ed692800e4446d65c6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[896]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O invincible one! Even if I had not been invited to the gambling match by the Kouravas, by Ambika’s son51 and by King Duryodhana, I would have gone and prevented the gambling by pointing out the many evils that result." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d5e7afe5cf26d37208c916b3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2844]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Indra among kings! In that battle, Shrutakarma51 attacked the valiant maharatha, Sudakshina from Kamboja." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d5f36ed17719e0d32ebd38ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20655]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son! Skin, flesh, fat, bile, marrow and sinews—these belong to the senses and you have spoken to me about them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d60509f659be520bb9f7e51e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13733]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "26 Having struck your grandfather27 in the battle, you thought that you were acting in accordance with dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d606509e309c28cc17c44b24> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10692]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is the being whom even the gods do not know." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d62e9d2592046bc01199a397> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12504]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "91 When Rahu devours the moon, the moonlight is no longer radiant." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d634aa7f077e3a1841ec8ced> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7322]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The worst among men laughed at Krishna819 when she had been won in the gambling match." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d64805faf5e55f6127fd2233> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7777]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Once, it was the month of Jyeshtha234 and the sun was in the middle of the sky." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d64bda9c5aa3a7d20b521e59> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2020]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "380 I am Meru." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d64fc5bbc3f4323a5c901a3a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[50]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The army of the Kurus looked like the firmament, devoid of stars, or the sky without any air, or the earth with crops destroyed, or words without refinement, or the ancient army of the asuras after Bali had been brought down, or a beautiful woman6 who is a widow, or a descending river whose waters have dried, or a cow hemmed in by wolves in the forest when the leader of the herd has been killed, or a large mountainous cavern rendered impotent because the lion has been killed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d66d1ddca9fcd61ae310f641> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2273]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods do not protect with a staff, like herdsmen looking after animals." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d67388179c4618e451cb4147> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7211]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! In that great battle, Drona clashed against Partha and it was like Budha and Shukra376 meeting each other in the firmament." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d67f0b881ed65597914a81d7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[547, 548]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """More important is the slightest bit of fear in the world of the gods.
38 Deeds and human enterprise follow destiny.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d686baa9455c6e5fbbf43251> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1499]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This tiger among men has been worshipped by the gods and the demons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d68dd8031f9632792658d3ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11618]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "We have heard that the gods were dislodged from their prosperity and began to wander around on earth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d6b006f7042827b60cbfa7b8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10234]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "2 That bull among Bharatas3 served dharma, artha and kama equally, looking upon the three as relatives, like one’s own self." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d6c7de173b30fa89b863eaf2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11715]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O unblemished one! Restraining the senses and controlling the mind, it must be very difficult to continuously think of husbands as gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d6d0ba9adc8e586ded130ff6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6970]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ 781(118) ‘Narada said, “The king227 wished to hold a svayamvara for her." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d6d328243e16baff6294703d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17062]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "470 Beings are always attached to those qualities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d6df4bc45c0f684d354cb7fe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9326]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” O ruler of the people! Then Duryodhana and Radha’s son7 came to Dhritarashtra and told him, “We cannot speak in Vidura’s presence." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d6ec9a1a2bdde9bc8bf7d01d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4445]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 376(79) Janamejaya said, ‘O illustrious one! When my great-grandfather Partha left Kamyaka forest, what did the Pandavas200 do without Savyasachi? It seems to me that the great archer, the vanquisher of enemy armies, was their refuge, like Vishnu is that of the Adityas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d6f71527bc0190f6956d3066> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11828]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "While the rakshasa looked on, they were shattered and their limbs were mangled." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d704dbc678b999da55c354b6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1516]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Hearing this, Shakra82 spoke to the guardians of the amrita, “An immensely valorous and strong bird has decided to take the soma away." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d709fcdaacd8734e7be6d496> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7519]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowing that the prescribed time of her stay with them was over, Hidimba made another agreement with them25 and went where she wanted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d70caaa75652f2e6c3cc89fe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7907]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, the descendant of the Pandu lineage smiled and quickly severed the string of his304 bow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d712c2cad4f788b20546ef8f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4544]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His322 divine standard was decorated with gold and looked like a golden palm tree." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d7135224f3b6aeeb64c72c48> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1585, 1587]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘When the darkness had disappeared, the gods attacked the bird.
Attacked by the army of the gods, the immensely valorous king of the birds, the destroyer of enemies, rose into the sky, above the heads of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d7174c4e2d68a283a740325f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4690]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "103 O Indra among kings! There the gods, the rishis, the siddhas and the charanas,104 with Brahma at the forefront, go on the fourteenth day of shuklapaksha105 in the month of Chaitra and worship Janardana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d74f7612ffa9c250142dd9db> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24393]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When Rudra consecrated himself and advanced for the destruction of Tripura, Ushanas1234 uprooted a strand from his matted hair and hurled it down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d75843330ebf1198f760b808> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4308, 4309]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """If he gives them large quantities of riches, he is established in the ashrama of vanaprastha.
O descendant of the Bharata lineage! If he does not cause injury to any being and practises non-violence, he is established in a state that has all the stages.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d765beb09a96d8a7d45f8868> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3809]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Drive." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d771df2357ff07c9dfb37569> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11251, 11252]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """) Prajapati;608 (181) Amrityu;609 (183) Sarvadrikimsaha;610 (184) Samdhata;611 (185) Samdhimat;612 (186) Asthira;613 (.
) Aja;614 (187) Durmarshana;615 (188) Shasta;616 (189) Vishrutatman;617 (190) Surariha;618 (191) Gururgurutama;619 (192) Dhama;620 (.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d78e9008801a09acdb0ef5bb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14145]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "81 Drona’s son saw the extender of the Kuru lineage82 stationed in front of him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d79365724f6d7e7e7f969a81> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 82 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5923]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O descendant of the Bharata lineage! When the sun assumed a reddish tinge, King Duryodhana spoke to all those who were on your side." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d7a3f5f9b88a1055ae27ffc2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11143]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Shudras107 will quarrel with brahmanas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d7aa243587980642e60bd1f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7411]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Pandu’s elder brother! The Pandavas surrounded Bhishma in that battle, with their chariots, elephants and horses, so that Madhava387 might be rescued." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d7b04cedbe4525fa372a3c09> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5399]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There are sacred tirthas, holy to separate gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d7b3262f47a073d2b7efcdb4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7546]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I will bring down the aged and invincible grandfather of the Kurus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d7c1252bcbf85cb4b9837869> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6750]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! The lord of the earth saw the holy sites of the Vasus, the masses of Maruts, the two Ashvins, Vaivasvata,499 the Adityas, the lord of riches,500 Indra, Vishnu, the lord Savita,501 Bhaga,502 the moon, Divakara,503 the lord of the waters,504 the masses of Sadhyas, Dhata,505 the ancestors, the great-souled Rudra with his masses of ganas, Sarasvati, the masses of Siddhas, Pushan506 and all the other immortals." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d7c8986a4c725bbb2da1fdf3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1597]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among men! Rathas were seen to fall down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d7f57be097e295be4a84d0db> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[955]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On finding her, the best of the sages was driven by compassion and adopted her." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d7f62b1274f68c92fad45640> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9937]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Favour all beings through your own conduct." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d7fba2329b0a19dce47f200f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3504]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With ten sharp and swift arrows, Panchala’s immensely strong heir126 killed the horses of Drona’s son, which were renowned in the world." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d803a8ddab00e1cd065606e0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16362, 16363, 16364]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """150 Together with them, and with Soumitri, Rama followed the same road151 towards his city.
Having reached Ayodhya, the lord of the kingdom sent Hanuman as a messenger to Bharata and he152 observed the signs and told him153 all the pleasant news.
When Vayu’s son had returned, he154 went again to Nandigrama.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d80510eab4416d5c0e3d2a26> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4605]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If I act the way I have never done before, what righteousness will come of that?” ‘Pratardana174 said, “O one with beauty that leads to envy! My name is Pratardana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d81b098f7dda7c854fec626d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23489, 23491]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Because of our boon, that god1126 will be pleased with you and will convey you to Brahma’s world.
The gods and the rishis, rich in austerities, returned to their own abodes.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d82fa9c95e9ffe4332b1ffc1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10618]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I touched my mother’s feet and those of Arshtishena52 and ascended my chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d84f2ab67969fc47c6bf02ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[597, 604]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Maharathas surrounded elephants and the best of chariots.
Horses adorned with whisks were routed and drank up the earth61 and were like swans on the slopes of the Himalayas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d86fb1e5107eec87ce637f29> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2520]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Those associated with jatakarma1191 must be performed for all the three varnas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d87546bbf8c8438aa3726a9d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14046]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Dhananjaya used the weapon known as shabdabheda58 and restrained his disappearance into many different forms." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d8a7e8495b2c89f63fd4a5e8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9828, 9829]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """She was extremely happy with the five valourous ones as her husbands, like Sarasvati54 with her elephants,55 and they were also delighted with her.
Since the great-souled Pandavas abided by dharma, all the Kurus56 increased in prosperity, were bereft of sin and were happy.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d8b4082ba64a5818478412a0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13378]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Having said this, he again imparted consciousness189 and without any anxiety, the brahmana entered into his190 mouth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d8b510060a1f895a0a2dd102> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1215]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having circled again, that bull among men defeated the clans known as Utsavasamketa who dwelt in the forests of Pushkara, the immensely powerful Gramaneyas who lived on the banks of the Sindhu,76 the clans of shudras and abhiras77 who lived along the Sarasvati,78 all those who live on fish and all those who live in the mountains, the land of the five rivers, the western Paryatas, the northern Jyotika, the city named Vrindataka and Dvarapala." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d8c4edeb9dfceaae62cda08b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23715]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lord of gods and the lord of sacrifices held these in his hands and was cheerful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d8c9cca9f40f2ed9dca671b6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19676, 19677]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """With the combined energy of the gods, with a single arrow, he brought down the three cities from the sky onto the ground.
728 Their lord was terrible and fearsome in valour, frightful to the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d8d169cfac19fccbb763bb73> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5520, 5523]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The one who follows dharma52 was unskilled and Soubala was knowledgeable about the heart of dice.
The wicked Jayadratha afflicted Krishna53 in the forest, in Trinabindu’s hermitage, when they54 had gone out on a hunt.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d8ec40178e2cd782ee3820ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9391]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Masses of Maruts172 arrived in celestial vehicles, together with Mahendra’s followers and those who live in his abode." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d8ee48e704f66d5cbe9376c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9916]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“On seeing that his immensely strong son had been killed by Ashvatthama, he79 approached Drona’s son, whose armlets seemed to be blazing with anger." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d90b48c4499e570e805108a3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4179]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The evil-souled one130 does not understand this, because he depends on Drona and Bhishma and listens to Karna’s bragging." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d90d815ada5605a28485800c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1642, 1646]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """In this world, people who desire success in their action, worship gods.
186 Actions do not touch me, nor do I desire the fruits of action.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d90e5ed31ae8f5e216dd1b68> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16728]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Earth, water, fire, wind and space are the great elements in beings and are like the waves of the ocean." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d92c705488e7a44f8281965e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4295]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Sanjaya! I cannot detect any reason as to why this should be the case." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d92cff3311e4c7b788c56cff> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17299]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O beautiful one! All the gods will speak about me in jest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d9332be4bd4c5e35561712db> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13741]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In that battle, it was through his favours that those bulls among men performed superhuman deeds, difficult for the gods and the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d97a81f291d264ae26fd4017> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18307]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If the gods are pleased with me, I desire that favours should be shown to him, so that he can obtain happiness." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d97bbe60080c30399c0d3eef> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9587]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This greatest of cities was as resplendent as Bhogavati13 of the nagas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d97bda67e5d869a503ca64f6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[110]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He then quickly went to Rama11 on Mount Mahendra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d993cbafd62783501ab3ed82> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8426]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Being possessed by the rakshasa, the king soon lost all his senses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d99850c3689d56b1fc105046> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5045]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In that way, the king351 humbly presented himself before Krishna, the wielder of the chakra and the gada, like Pradyumna presenting himself before Govinda." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d99de5ba48d511ad7d4c816e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 145 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7565]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O best of the Bharata lineage! O king! Those great-souled ones lived there like that and a great deal of time passed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d9a6e0af6b33c519e4e250c8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2140, 2143]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The asuras were elder brothers and the gods were younger.
At that time, the gods killed the daityas and obtained possession of heaven.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d9a7b44fccf0898e0f792c7a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[537]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He came with a large number of gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d9bd2d90398a46760fd07d8c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13858]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! It so happened that on the same day, Dharma’s son, Yudhishthira, performed the sadyaska sacrifice31 undertaken by rajarshis." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d9c9de82284311ecd6db0759> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[331]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! You must always protect yourself and your food21 using men who are born in noble lineages and have good conduct." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d9d2f38197368291aba61f28> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 329 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24409]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As a priest of the gods, he outwardly gives them their shares and only gives us a share privately." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d9dd31ce42ac41c98ca7981a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6875]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The foremost among the Yadus returned to their own houses and the king542 went on to the tirthas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d9df4c6c44868828e3230c8f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9043]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘When he1 left, all the bulls among the Kurus2 sent the priest on ahead of them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d9e05a4ec85b5394f972d3fc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2126]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O bull among men! This265 is an instrument of time." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d9f842434578873edcb5eeaf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[701]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was entreated by the illustrious Vishtarashrava himself, Krishna Dvaipayana, the lord Devasthana, Narada, Bhima, King Nakula, Krishna,47 Sahadeva, the intelligent Vijaya48 and many other tigers among men and brahmanas who were learned about the sacred texts." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/d9fef0c1ddc2d1c182781de4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1732]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Thus does the powerful snake Ananta111 always live under the ground, holding up the earth on Lord Brahma’s command." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da03dd8adc9ed8d6e9cc8b1a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[691]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All his limbs were covered with blood and he was like Death, created by Destiny." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da0de7612f24f22fa59677ee> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[596]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Dvapara comes after that and pushya follows thereafter." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da0f0c7fb2cf5940d9a335ad> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5103]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Sanjaya! Such a preparation236 on earth has never been seen before, by men, or by the immensely fortunate and ancient rishis." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da2187040e69d8354ab4aa54> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1925, 1926, 1927]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """) Vara;1022 (803) Characharatma;1023 (804) Sukshmatma;1024 (805) Suvrisha;1025 (806) Go-vrisheshvara;1026 (807) Sadhyarshi- vasuradityavivasvansavita-mrida;1027 (808) Vyasa-sarvasya-samkshepa- vistara;1028 (809) Paryaya;1029 (810) Naya;1030 (811) Ritu;1031 (812) Samvatsara;1032 (813)Masa;1033 (814)Paksha;1034 (815)Samkhya- samapana;1035 (816) Kala; (817) Kashtha; (818) Lava; (819) Matra;1036 (820) Muhurta; (821) Aha;1037 (822) Kshapa;1038 (823) Kshana; (824) Vishvakshetra;1039 (825) Praja-bija;1040 (826) Lingamadya;1041 (.
) Anindita;1042 (827) Sadas;1043 (.
) Vyakta;1044 (.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da383991b657324ef7f24e25> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6042]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’” ‘Rama81 said, “The king gathered a large army with six divisions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da3b9650ff56c5010b420154> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7277]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! The gate to Manasa582 is evident here." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da455166d30a1849f8593f0b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8243]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is like Upendra424 and is dark." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da4c0e7b8581150fbc825aac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12087]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On hearing these in a battle, even the hearts of the gods are shattered." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da6257464a28889a913abe30> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6160]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The immensely fortunate grandfather of all the worlds told them, ‘O thirty gods! With all the worlds, go back to where you came from." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da628dfeb064a7c677f2d5c0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10499]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Maya was Namuchi’s52 brother." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da6adb0e4ee9b9817279c566> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13030]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If the protectors are killed, Panchala78 will kill him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da71fefea08e40b25dd8f67c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4072, 4073]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Having been severely pierced, maharatha Kripa, supreme among brahmanas, deprived Parshata496 of his horses, charioteer and chariot.
With his horses slain, the maharatha497 descended from his chariot and grasping a sword and a shield, quickly advanced against the brahmana.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da77f1f3c617913c8a94856f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9505]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I know how to prepare the great battle formations of gods, gandharvas and humans." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da7aad6d629e900271f6e372> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3154]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the earth! The powerful and great archer, Bharadvaja’s son,87 followed him, with the Kuntalas, Dasharnas, Magadhas, Vidarbhas, Mekalas, Karnas88 and Pravaranas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da81ce5b1e5325eb576044f3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6272, 6273]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """“Slice.
Pierce.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da850f2baf0ccd4810a14a28> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8708, 8709]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """One must also wear a different garment when worshipping the gods.
Otherwise, the gods are dishonoured.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/da8ee876c12bce3fbcdb6807> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[568]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He summoned the large numbers of gods with mantras that were pronounced extremely well and offered oblations into the fire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dac37690bf0825bcc6290ed5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3083, 3085]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘I have heard from the elders about the marks of the gods.
’ Having decided this and having reflected on this in many ways, she resolved that the time had come to seek refuge with the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/daf350136f192f942b5db02e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2790]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They2 saw the Kourava maharathas there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/db100a4d98a45855745daeba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3130]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Gada’s elder brother then left the city of Nagapura216 on a divine chariot, with four tawny horses yoked to it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/db253f098d6c3dbe3c697aa1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1608]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In battle, I will terrify Duryodhana, Shantanu’s son,30 Vaikartana Karna, Kripa, Drona and his son31 and all the other great archers who have assembled, like the wielder of the vajra against the danavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/db32bd6939482f0782e22e30> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6287]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The rakshasa made it fall down on the ground." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/db431c863bc40e84366ed61c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6114]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king properly upheld the dharma that the god of the gods92 had instructed Mandhata about." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/db48452f238e40cb8d5b3dd6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4236, 4238]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """They presented themselves before the great-souled and illustrious Kartikeya.
Instructed by the gods, those brave ones became the companions of Skanda.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/db51ef428aff591802758814> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10246]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O mighty-armed one! Kill Bhishma, like Purandara23 slew Vritra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/db909704f704df3337a7844f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17683]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Slander is like the conduct of those without virtue." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/db9147d625fc46a58bb014ae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11862, 11864]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """All the asuras were defeated by him.
1402 He exists in gods, men and the ancestors.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/db922de6d207f9ed622ccb15> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8575]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The application of cosmetics, dressing the hair, applying of collyrium, brushing the teeth and worshipping the gods must be done in the forenoon." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dba077ea1c7a626f46d58de8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8831]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "One should also bathe before worshipping the gods and saluting the preceptor." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dbacfcf0040aa9133a913e2e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12689]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "201 This terrible and cruel one is established in all beings by the name of Svaha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dbb28c4ecb985b1835fdd479> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1203]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "72 The conqueror of enemies and one with dharma in his heart73 used conciliation and knowing this to be determined by destiny, the intelligent lord74 happily accepted the suzerainty and sent many kinds of riches—firstly sandalwood and aloe, and then divine ornaments, expensive garments and priceless jewels." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dbb5a6af781db3af9eef7988> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5385, 5386]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O undecaying one! The great-souled gods performed their sacrifice.
At the right time, the bulls among gods completed the sacrifice.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dbb86e3728c7adbe016de1d3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "16_Mausala" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[419]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Partha, supreme among men, instated Hardikya’s son48 V there and left the remaining wives of the king of Bhoja there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dbc3ac7b70290828414a0b4a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9746]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Once they confronted a hated man like you, a great destruction has arrived before the Kurus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dbc4ab3976cea279fb57a670> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 5 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[153]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Do you use groups of three spies, who do not know one another, to find out about the eighteen ministers on the other side and the fifteen on your own territory?43 O destroyer of enemies! Unknown to them, do you always keep watch over your adversaries, with care and on guard? ‘“Is your priest humble, born of a good lineage, famous, untouched by jealousy and do you pay him homage? Is he in charge of the sacrificial fires and is he intelligent and upright, knowledgeable in the rituals? Does he always know the time when sacrifices and offerings must be rendered? Is the appointed astrologer skilled in the knowledge of rituals and in treating all the omens and destinies? Have you appointed superior servants in superior positions and medium ones in medium positions? Have you employed inferior servants in inferior positions? For the best tasks, have you appointed the best advisers, those who are without deceit and pure, up to their fathers and grandfathers? O bull among the Bharata lineage! Surely your subjects are not oppressed by harsh punishments when the ministers govern your kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dbd22ea8fe53aa04507cbcf3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10156]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On hearing that Madhava had come, King Yudhishthira sent the twins12 to receive Krishna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dbe211c28e60a6477ff135a7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4312]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of men! Resolution, Victory, dharma, Success, Prosperity, Fortitude and Learning159 advanced ahead of Mahasena’s terrible army, who were armed with spears, clubs, maces, bludgeons, iron arrows, javelins and spikes in their hands." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dbe4e70398b3eb711f591938> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17092]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O immensely radiant one! With your beautiful earrings, you will be as resplendent as the azure moon in the sky, in the midst of the two Vishakhas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dbeb7e3b6e6e9d7d4c415705> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4336, 4339]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Some enemies of the gods were killed by the flags.
There were many such who hated the gods, powerful assassins.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dbfada4f325bb2c506743eb9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4723]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That supreme of sages will hurl it into the ocean, in the form of the subterranean fire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dc0ab0972834e2f09391e7ac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9575]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” They9 worshipped the feet of Dhritarashtra, Bhishma and others who deserved it, and asking about the welfare of everyone in the city, entered the place earmarked for them at Dhritarashtra’s command." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dc4394e1b4d1f93e36fc7ae0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7045]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Deceit should be used against those who are deceitful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dc4851d129c36bb426b6f429> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[958]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Krishna! He was Krishna’s67 son and was infinitely energetic." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dc532fab4e076c72a406bf6b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[486]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O bull among the Bharata lineage! When King Jarasandha heard about their deaths in the water, he left Shurasena32 and returned to his own city." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dc5796a62992d7bb9c71204c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2794]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king of Madra sliced the revered one’s40 bow into two." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dc8bb5b7a893480b317d3f7b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10267]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Pandava! When the assembled inhabitants of Kurujangala20 saw Krishna afraid and outraged in the assembly hall, an act that was contrary to dharma and good conduct, who but you could have endured it? There is no doubt that you will soon protect your subjects again and be restored to all the prosperity that you desire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dcb1d2881a731592f8505d9a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[376]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They will then be devoted to you and will not waver, like the great mountain, Meru." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dcb86baf8bed775fc89aaea8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1274]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Having been punished, he176 went to his brother, Shankha, and said in great distress, ‘I have been punished for my stupid intelligence." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dcbe2d253a5e50e4234a4954> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1634]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Pandava Gudakesha206 addressed Hrishikesha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dccb3b23505217205d8f917b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7857, 7858]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘After killing him,24 Bhima returned to the Brahmana’s house and described in detail to the king25 all that had happened.
The next morning, the inhabitants of the town came out and saw the rakshasa lying dead on the ground, his body wet with blood, horrible and spread out, as huge as the peak of a mountain.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dcd3bd0bceb3c517107dfc7c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[885]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having been unable to persuade Pritha to return, the Pandavas circumambulated the king73 and withdrew." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dcda473ed2d5ac1288cead41> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5076]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Arjuna! Because of its austerities, that animal had been granted a boon by the self-creating one598 that it would be able to kill all beings, but would be blind." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dcf059205ff5e351b9af9a60> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7315]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Brahma-rakshasas198 are then unable to cause any harm at a funeral ceremony." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd02b3f81ebe2e9380b8fbc1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1525, 1528]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """On knowing that the immortals had not thought of a share for him at the sacrifice, Krittivasa60 quickly determined to obtain a share and created a bow.
Kapardi62 constructed a bow for the sake of a sacrifice that was a sacrifice for the worlds.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd13de166f72a754d7979911> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3560, 3561]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He ignores those brave sons of the gods, the destroyers of enemies.
60 What extremely difficult task has he61 accomplished in the past that can rival any one deed accomplished by any one of the Pandavas earlier? In Virata’s city, he saw his own beloved brother killed through Dhananjaya’s valour.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd1e64308e7bf03a80797482> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3448]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Piercing with lances and striking with razors, he killed six thousand in Nirmochana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd1ef577800f5c4328bcbce8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5129]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O lord of men! The visitor of tirthas should then go to Rajagriha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd2283877c21175bc4d47de2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1348]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He23 was surrounded by many brave kings from the mountainous regions, adorned with diverse weapons, and was like Shakra, surrounded by masses of gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd434649e6b80d68c02b1c3b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1838]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Why do you not examine and determine the exact reasons why your eldest son is so miserable with a grief that can only result from an enemy?” Dhritarashtra asked, “O Duryodhana! O son! What is the reason for your great grief? O son25 of the Kuru lineage! If it is something that I can hear, please tell me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd5455434113f3e8ade1301d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22003]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "988 Desire, anger, death and the five senses are the water in the river that flows from birth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd556179c49245c39cba38c2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6005]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The thirty gods were extremely distressed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd5d0e520306759ef671fdc6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23430]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He honoured the gods and completed the sacrifice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd61d9ae4201ba5ca4f3d6d9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14741]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The lord of the three worlds161 worshipped the Indra among the daityas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd716164f5c198a804d08fe1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5284]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Krishna! You can never take the kingdom back from Babhru758 and Ugrasena, especially because that will lead to conflict within the clan." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd726140410ac410befe8382> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7780]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The god with the thousand eyes became the lord of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd7a4c52f132a3320ccc392c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 138 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10692, 10697, 10698, 10702]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The army of the sons of Pandu was illuminated with others who were in the midst and held flaming torches in their hands.
O king! As that radiance spread up towards the sky, the masses of gods, the gandharvas, the yakshas, the asuras and large numbers of siddhas were awakened and assembled, with all the apsaras.
The place was full of gods, gandharvas, yakshas, leaders among the asuras, masses of apsaras and brave warriors who had been killed and had ascended to heaven.
Those large armies of chariots, horses and elephants were arrayed in battle formation and were as resplendent as the gods and the asuras, arranged in vyuhas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd7ff197c0f5d5ebda3f019e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[278]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ 235(10) ‘Narada said, “O king! Vaishravana’s125 radiant and white sabha is one hundred yojanas long and seventy yojanas wide." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd825ff67be7eb8e2885f604> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3704]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son! King Koushika performed a great sacrifice91 and obtained the immensely ascetic Vishvamitra as his son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd8a1a2a491369e874304146> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1417]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Do not deviate from the path that leads you to the road followed by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd95f133e6c48ee1bc09b9e2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1033]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In ancient times, Tandi82 was born from Brahma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dd9a7710b4feb8be0d6595f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3724, 3725]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O son! You should not sorrow about him266 or any of the other Kurus.
They have earned and gone to the indestructible worlds of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ddad97faef7c317722431a00> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10541]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O mighty-armed one! I unleashed an arrow that could not be countered and all those arrows, Rama’s and mine, remained in the air47 and swiftly covered the sky in every direction." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ddd5fa2259f38d5236dae045> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8765]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In all kinds of purification, the brahma tirtha must be touched first." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ddea0771d297ac6040fd18e3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2443]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On earth, in heaven and even among the gods, there doesn’t exist anything that is free from these three qualities generated from nature." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ddf673f315efb66e85e64473> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6161]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O friend of the lord of the gods! By obtaining this, the gods obtained their divinity." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ddf7f785638399647032f5bd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10627]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If the eldest one does not know, what can the younger ones do?” ‘Drona said, “The one with the golden seed67 is swiftly advancing towards our abode in flames." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/de0f1ed3a66893f9da0bffdd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10334]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As they desired, they could all soar up to the sky to meet with the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/de19663aed52379a3ebd0384> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8141]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Vaikartana Vrisha333 wished to kill Bhimasena." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/de19dc60d448cd9ed769ed46> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3292]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the gods! Because of his decay, all the subjects have been overcome by decay." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/de24bc9f782f2544b0f4130d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 349 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25881, 25884, 25889]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O brahmana rishi! I am that serpent and you have now met me.
O brahmana! That is the reason I have myself come here to meet you.
’ ‘“The brahmana replied, ‘O immensely fortunate one! I have come here with a desire to meet you.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/de41cdfcadeb1ef98dd85c5d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1578]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those intelligent ones know the seven subtle forms,178 the six of your attributes179 and the main ‘K techniques of yoga and penetrate into you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/de5345fafc3b028936c0e457> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[58]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Vaishampayana said, ‘O great king! When Karna was slain, with a distressed mind, Gavalgana’s son11 set out in the night for Nagapura,12 on horses that were as fleet as the wind." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/de66c9a4bb475e08ba4ac42d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[565]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods themselves offered the food and oblations." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/de7689e5f41189af5dd34655> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2212]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "140 O Janamejaya! Govinda141 loved your father." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/de9e744e23fc39e08df40d00> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1955]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O king! Pandava showered down arrows on the assembled army, and like Suparna92 swooping down, approached Pragjyotisha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/deadafc87b72ad9fae196a69> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1829]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 696(33): 104 shlokas Chapter 697(34): 83 shlokas Chapter 698(35): 67 shlokas Chapter 699(36): 72 shlokas Chapter 700(37): 60 shlokas Chapter 701(38): 44 shlokas Chapter 702(39): 70 shlokas Chapter 703(40): 30 shlokas Chapter 704(41): 11 shlokas Prajagara means sleeplessness, lying awake at night." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dec830ded4ff9678f926e180> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11840, 11841]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The gandharvas, the apsaras and hundreds of gods always worship him.
The rakshasas bear him.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/decd9c9d56b139910195443a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1093]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then that valorous one, bull among men, defeated the Gandakis and the Videhas27 and after some time, went on to Dasharna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dee326cdb626fdc059d5c4e1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6892, 6893]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """It could not be destroyed by Hara, the lord of the waters or the protector of riches,790 and by the pinaka, pasha or vajra791 and the best of arrows.
The supreme gods were incapable of withstanding it.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/defe8c009c22a195c6a7bcde> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20321, 20338]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Injury represents the swift and strong current.
Vedanta is an island one advances towards and all creatures can use it as pots778 for support.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df10a25270fb7c66d691f725> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3207]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Dogs, jackals, crows, wild crows, birds,132 wolves, hyenas, ravens, others who feed on blood, masses of rakshasas and large numbers of pishachas133 were extremely delighted in that terrible field of battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df164cd470f648fad827de74> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11820]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He238 was himself struck with the sharp arrows released by Karna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df27cb120e41cf0bbb49dd6d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[443]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "49 That god surpasses all the gods in austerities and in valour." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df34e87a5f6ff8866cdc5f69> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10811]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In that battle, in an instant, the foremost of brave rathas among the Vrishni lineage153 made Yudhishthira devoid of his horses, charioteer and chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df36f5fd34a955d5b8324824> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11098, 11099]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Savitri is Brahma’s virtuous wife, Shachi is Koushika’s421 virtuous wife, Dhumorni is the wife of Martanda’s son,422 Riddhi is Vaishravana’s423 wife, Gouri is Varuna’s wife, Suvarchala is Surya’s wife, Rohini is the virtuous wife of the moon, Svaha is the wife of Vibhavasu424 and Aditi is the wife of Kashyapa.
All of them regard their husbands as gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df37776ecf4370660ebc23ed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8112]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In that way, the great-souled one became the king of the gods by giving lamps and all the other required objects, observing all the rites for rendering offerings and performing all the other separate tasks that are meant for auspicious days." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df46df9f55f57fd7b670599f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21745]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "952 Deceit leads to destruction." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df4f32c0f8da42d794a51a12> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2411]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Your son44 was on the back of a horse and attacked Sahadeva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df631dc00b71114c0c07f2b4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[928]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Cold is checked through heat and heat is checked through cold." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df702c3ecd918ff98665be2e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8280]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Why give her somewhere else?’ Thereupon, Tapana64 himself gave the unblemished and perfect Tapati to the great- souled Vashishtha, for Samvarana’s sake." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df7283fb8ca6e5844ee65a58> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5951]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I will worship the ancestors and the gods with food found in the forest, water and words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df7507a3fc04d89011a99db5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2655]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Though he has been born as a kshatriya, this one is not a mere mortal." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df80bd8c3a1b7ed7a5fd54d9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2673]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On witnessing his valour as he burnt down the soldiers, all the warriors sought peace, while Dhritarashtra’s son175 looked on." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df89059ee0d86ed4e2d4a946> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18487, 18488]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Certainty is used to conquer doubt.
Loquaciousness is conquered through silence and fear through valour.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/df97d8381c6826d4bc08de7e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1311, 1312, 1314]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """They were constructed out of many metals and looked like the peaks of the Himalayas.
‘After resting there for some time, those lords saw Dharmaraja Yudhishthira, surrounded by many sadasyas23 and donating innumerable gifts.
’ 257(32) Vaishampayana said, ‘Having shown homage to his grandfather25 and preceptor26 and having welcomed them, Yudhishthira spoke these words to Bhishma, Drona, Kripa, Drona’s son27 and Vivimshati.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dfa674a7160375112260c5b8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2238]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "129 O king! The king inhaled the fragrances of the heads130 of the descendants131 of the Kuru lineage and of the four Pandavas,132 led by Bhimasena." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dfb5b25ddcacec3e0eeb42d1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 204 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14049]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "56 The earth, the sky, heaven, beings, the rishis, the gods, the asuras and nothing else existed, with the exception of the soul." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dfba052276c26f52e3f4b13f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4765]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They were the equals of the gods themselves." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dfce998e56bc7f32ccb83125> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 89 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5749]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O descendant of the Bharata lineage! The wealthy are referred to as a great limb of the kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dfcf202fc0c66b726ec03c2a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9160]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ The gods said, ‘Since the mortals have become immortals, there is no difference any more." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/dfcf7b194d69433f4970be72> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4087, 4088]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """You are dharma.
You are Prajapati.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e00bf2c6f5c30ff46c19fcb8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9260]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods and the siddhas, with the grandfather11 at the forefront, know about the infinite prowess of those two." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e027cb1dad431f79826e7c02> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11947]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, the rakshasa roared and destroyed it with his own terrible club." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e02d62713be63cd7f919293d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13980]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Having heard these words of Ajatashatru,50 Dhananjaya agreed to his senior’s51 words about freeing the Kouravas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e03553b0d57f006b9ec7f90f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5768]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His mother Kousalya275 embraced that bull among men, unequalled in his energy, the way Poulomi embraces Jayanta." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e03725c31a167fe496830471> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6550]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With Bharadvaja’s son339 at the forefront, all of them wished to kill Bhimasena." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e0378e6720dd469a6a99b0fe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9188]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Brahma’s sacrificial site133 is there and Prajapati,134 the soul of all beings and the creator of everything that is mobile and immobile, resides there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e046f7c4743380655da19eae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2637]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘The mighty-armed Dhananjaya advanced to conquer his enemies, but the one who was terrible in his deeds172 countered this fearful advance." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e04e38b3ae2e3624c4def58a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9803]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O king! Your sons62 advanced towards Bhima’s chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e050c1ef24e8b59e753615ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18926]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“The illustrious son of Angiras657 and the other supreme rishis witnessed Vritra’s valour and went to Maheshvara." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e0550d33cabaa5cd7f393b39> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5063]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If a person is tranquil in his soul and gives away land, the ancestors in the world of the ancestors and the gods in the world of the gods are satisfied." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e058185fcf25cd3a76d0c2f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9182, 9184]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """This is sacred Samyamana, extraordinary to behold.
O king! The learned ones call this king of the mountains Asta.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e064fa89c8c5213d7c1d34cb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1705]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On witnessing Goutama’s form advancing towards Dhrishtadyumna’s chariot, all the beings were terrified and thought that he243 was confronting destruction." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e0751a1d4b5363dabe09b6c9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 141 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9673]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Joining his hands in salutation, he spoke these words to the tree." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e08d1307fd12a8b51081705d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5799]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "What is given in this world sustains gods and the large number of ancestors and also men, serpents, rakshasas, birds and animals." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e08d74f6df794752c5f4be4d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24715]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He cheerfully met Rudra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e09859601f061081286f77e4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4744]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "We have heard that he instated the Pourava182 as the emperor of all the Kshatriyas, like the tusk183 of the entire expansive earth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e0a9ba668e46458122edc4cc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[605]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘O king of the gods! Conquer your anger." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e0af8c636a3cbe498dde189f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19667]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because of this, insolence was generated among subjects and this destroyed dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e0ceee64adcfcbde1a8debe6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4282]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At that time, a forest dweller who survived on roots and fruits arrived before Nahusha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e0de22208762dd9c54104c22> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17702]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "512 Therefore, one should follow the instructions and know the subtle nature of dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e0e2c14749b04294ab48289c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1398]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This grief is exploiting my senses and I don’t see what will remedy that, even if I win lordship over the gods, or this earth, without any enemies and prosperous." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e0eab355a2d5e5b0b4e6508c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1275]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Given specific instructions, artisans built large shelters that were filled with jewels and were like the mansions of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e0f784977efd4fc3a10b9021> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2476]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! If food has been tasted by an unworthy person1183 or by someone who is armed and if food has been tasted by an evil-souled person—the learned say that the rakshasas obtain a share in it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e0ff017fa823a67ff505cc72> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9787]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! He struck Vishoka57 with three arrows and his standard with one." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e10d8a164e7261ad923b0fe0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1242, 1243]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Ajatashatru4 is humble and follows his brothers.
Why should Partha5 not follow a conduct that ensures the welfare of those obedient and great-souled ones? That is the reason they have been waiting for this time to arrive.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e11dd50a1a8170ce80b7f260> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15854]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As a consequence of this, my wings were burnt, but not those of Jatayu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e12efd3ddd27ad5c73da1a28> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7354]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O fearful one! There is no rakshasa who can withstand my valour." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e13a7bdbf118608e8b3042dc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5431]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is the beautiful grove of the gods there, adorned with ascetics." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e13a8087b5f614166cb5a49a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7662]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the masses of gods! Favour me with boons so that I become superior to others." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e14a7b30c31df9615e2d4285> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3762]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With great power, he worshipped the ancestors and the gods, who were always present." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e14d2c4d13e2a9ec45da369e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1627]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 631(35) Vaishampayana said, ‘O king! On seeing his friend, the large-eyed princess, he35 smiled and asked her why she had come." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e14db5fc25f8a877f985a83f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18799, 18816, 18820]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The gods then decided that the ends of creatures were determined by their colour and that their colour was determined by time.
A creature may roam around in the world of the gods.
O brave one among the asuras! I will now tell you about how a creature in the world of the living can obtain success, if it so desires.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e14e647c821ee9f69c8e4d72> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24076]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If these are properly used on earth, the gods will be pleased." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e153dc80edc812c8af85330e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6240, 6246, 6255, 6257]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Ghee is offered as an oblation into the fire.
These are surabhis and the descendants of Surabhi.
Our dung will always be used for purifying gods and humans.
O one who grants honours!102 Among all the mobile and immobile objects that are given, those who gift us will go to Goloka.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e1636832076edd3109e59fb2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4028]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Wrestlers, actors, fighters, narrators, soukhashayikas289 and large numbers of bards and minstrels praised Janardana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e16c7796e792f7bcd8669cf6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1362, 1363, 1364]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """2 The lord Narayana, slayer of enemies of the wise ones3 and destroyer of cities of the enemies, had himself been born as a kshatriya to keep his pledge.
In ancient times, the creator of beings had himself commanded the gods, “You will regain your own worlds after you have killed one another.
” Having thus instructed all the gods, Shambhu4 Narayana, the illustrious lord of the universe, was himself born in Yadu’s dynasty.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e177ea93774a842825c74f7f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6319]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In a single lineage, there are many thousand, million and crore of nagas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e179fe8fb6c4a3fbf19f7a69> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6705]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O one who travels at great speed! Refrain, because I cannot bear your speed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e17e9177c40fb86b9c1d09e7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8837]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All of them were full of every kind of fruit and were radiant with every kind of flower—mangoes, blossoming hog-plums,10 coconuts, tindukas,11 ajatakas,12 jiras,13 pomegranates, citrus trees,14 jackfruit, breadfruit,15 plantains,16 dates, tamarinds,17 paravatas,18 kshoudras,19 beautiful nipas,20 bilvas,21 wood-apples,22 roseapples,23 kashmaris,24 badaris, figs,25 udumbaras,26 fig trees,27 holy fig trees,28 kshirinas,29 marking-nuts,30 myrobalans,31 haritakas,32 bibhitakas,33 ingudas,34 karaviras,35 tindukas36 with a lot of fruit and many other trees that were on the slopes of Gandhamadana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e181e0df5aa0651a6deedcd7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9244]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O destroyer of enemy heroes! He possesses the blazing weapon that was given to him by Vasava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e1a9a1153cd461bf0176cbe7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9615]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On a single chariot, he is capable of slaying even the army of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e1abfd594487574ba289bb86> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[383]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! The powerful Drona travelled through that army of the Pandvas like a circle of fire38 and it was wonderful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e1ce3608ba74449dae84f113> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11008]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! That rakshasa was as beautiful as an unbroken mass of collyrium." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e1d4365f6337aaf5256c02d9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1907]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Having heard this, the intelligent Vidura knew that the door to kali40 was nigh." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e1e00d850fa165cfeee7b752> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8291]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 1457(129): 14 shlokas Chapter 1458(130): 21 shlokas Chapter 1459(131): 18 shlokas Chapter 1460(132): 15 shlokas Chapter 1461(133): 26 shlokas Chapter 1462(134): 10 shlokas Chapter 1463(135): 23 shlokas Chapter 1464(136): 211 shlokas Chapter 1465(137): 109 shlokas Chapter 1466(138): 70 shlokas Chapter 1467(139): 94 shlokas Chapter 1468(140): 37 shlokas Chapter 1469(141): 27 shlokas Chapter 1470(142): 44 shlokas Chapter 1471(143): 10 shlokas Chapter 1472(144): 12 shlokas Chapter 1473(145): 18 shlokas Chapter 1474(146): 18 shlokas Chapter 1475(147): 22 shlokas Chapter 1476(148): 35 shlokas Chapter 1477(149): 117 shlokas Chapter 1478(150): 36 shlokas Chapter 1479(151): 34 shlokas Chapter 1480(152): 32 shlokas Chapter 1481(153): 14 shlokas Chapter 1482(154): 38 shlokas Chapter 1483(155): 13 shlokas Chapter 1484(156): 26 shlokas Chapter 1485(157): 18 shlokas Chapter 1486(158): 13 shlokas Chapter 1487(159): 72 shlokas Chapter 1488(160): 87 shlokas Chapter 1489(161): 48 shlokas Chapter 1490(162): 49 shlokas Chapter 1491(163): 23 shlokas Chapter 1492(164): 26 shlokas Chapter 1493(165): 31 shlokas Chapter 1494(166): 25 shlokas Chapter 1495(167): 24 shlokas Apad means a misfortune or a calamity." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e1f1920e37729f06dae7054d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12651]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Drona, with Duryodhana at the forefront, advanced against the Vatsas47 and the Panchalas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e20b4ac4ca84b68be429542b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[569]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Kouravya! O lord! There are aryas and mlecchas110 and men from mixed lineage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e20d465a3246e0f8599c9330> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24274]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The water is known as Nara1220 and Nara obtained birth from the waters." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e210f5f80e621e3b199c067e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6468]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! O king! Having adopted the form of one of the saptarshis, he went to Koushika’s146 hermitage, as if he was hungry and wished to satisfy his hunger." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2128851f0251ee49cc907af> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3826]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Pundarikaksha25 spoke these words to his sister." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2160b431613f34735f2dddf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7138]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The man and the rakshasa, foremost among rathas, swiftly confronted each other in battle on their respective chariots, like a god and a danava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e219fe5bd306773d03fc344b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7700]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is spoken of in eight names—Ishvara, Purusha, Prana, Sattva,1036 Vitta,1037 Prajapati, Bhutatma1038 and Jiva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e21afdad5ed21608fa1bdc07> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3734]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is said that Manu131 had ten mighty sons who were devoted to the pursuit of the Kshatriya dharma— Vena, Dhrishnu, Narishyanta, Nabhaga, Ikshvaku, Karusha, Saryati, Ila as the eighth and Prishadhra as the ninth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e235a9f8d6a291b01b1a3fbe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 42 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2546]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 340(43): 38 shlokas Chapter 341(44): 32 shlokas Chapter 342(45): 38 shlokas Chapter 343(46): 41 shlokas Chapter 344(47): 12 shlokas Chapter 345(48): 41 shlokas Chapter 346(49): 43 shlokas Chapter 347(50): 31 shlokas Chapter 348(51): 29 shlokas Chapter 349(52): 24 shlokas Chapter 350(53): 21 shlokas Chapter 351(54): 38 shlokas Chapter 352(55): 13 shlokas Chapter 353(56): 18 shlokas Chapter 354(57): 23 shlokas Chapter 355(58): 34 shlokas Chapter 356(59): 25 shlokas Chapter 357(60): 38 shlokas Chapter 358(61): 125 shlokas Chapter 359(62): 43 shlokas Chapter 360(63): 24 shlokas Chapter 361(64): 19 shlokas Chapter 362(65): 37 shlokas Chapter 363(66): 26 shlokas Chapter 364(67): 22 shlokas Chapter 365(68): 24 shlokas Chapter 366(69): 34 shlokas Chapter 367(70): 39 shlokas Chapter 368(71): 34 shlokas Chapter 369(72): 30 shlokas Chapter 370(73): 28 shlokas Chapter 371(74): 24 shlokas Chapter 372(75): 27 shlokas Chapter 373(76): 19 shlokas Chapter 374(77): 29 shlokas Chapter 375(78): 23 shlokas Chapter 376(79): 29 shlokas Indraloka means Indra’s world and abhigamana means to go or visit." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2376f1c4d4359d193095a36> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1782]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As the warrior Satvata74 advanced against Drona, the brothers Kshemadhurti and Brihanta countered him and wounded him with their sharp arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e246ff37b5f80cd201e36565> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[937]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In her season, Krishna118 was in a single garment and was brought into the assembly hall, while the sons of Pandu looked on." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e24963e82cc2e42188fc3455> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1898]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All of them sorrowed over the aged king who had lost his sons and had now been burnt down and about the ascetic Gandhari." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e24fc47be6d035a589c8be27> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12849]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Grasping the maiden by the hand, Vasava234 told him, ‘Why are you acting towards this maiden like someone who is not an arya? Know me to be the wielder of the vajra and refrain from causing her any violence." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e251fdaeb95376af83433c51> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1128]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son!134 O Keshava! In those ancient times, Vishnu’s terrible chakra and Akhandala’s135 vajra were shattered on the evil one’s body." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2643bfa5c12ca9c51cd6fd9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18689]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In those ancient times, Vritra lost his riches and Ushanas622 spoke to him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e26fa6b481ed3c317b9f2aa6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8293]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Chapter 1457(129) ‘Yudhishthira said, “O descendant of the Bharata lineage! He1 may be weak." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2789fcf7eec37db67b125cf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4795]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bathing there and worshipping the ancestors and the gods, and staying there for only a single night, one obtains the fruits of agnishtoma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e27d981736d564f730d1b0d8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11844]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Even if Mithila35 is set ablaze, nothing that belongs to me will be consumed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e27eb4502be72662e23d0737> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[911]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! In the battle, the valiant Bhurishrava enveloped Yajnasena’s maharatha son81 with a shower of arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2800f74029908d866e34a75> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The great sages, performers of difficult austerities, were present at the twelve-year sacrifice of Kulapati3 Shounaka and were comfortably seated in Naimisharanya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2837f637babd1c002f33078> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9735]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The worship of the gods was stopped." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2842de574f6333cb7492614> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7911]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Separate oblations are recommended for the Prajapatis." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e28b5fb6fd4dc6f7b021759c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[610, 612]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O lord of the gods! Be pacified.
O fortunate one! You are the king of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e28df28fe45dce0d042c1fac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 81 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4794]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "One brahmana fed there is equal to one crore brahmanas being fed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2c02440be5b556e8cbfd88e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9728]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having been born as different kinds of species, they are cooked in the hell known as Kumbhipaka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2d0444487756dd7fa73ca4e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25856]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This is the sin that the powerful Dashagriva1387 fell prey to." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2d1361d73438332fcfde754> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10978]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Having learnt about their resolution, the lord of men89 again sent his kshatta90 to Parshata with the words, ‘Be steady." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2db5c131bb3261cc97fccfa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6773]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Desire a little." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2dc4a67e16dd73a5f50c568> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7096]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Indra among kings! On that night, the great-souled maharshi, who was Bhrigu’s son, performed a sacrifice so that Soudyumni554 might obtain a son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2ec08c7b7fbde463f49a15e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4786, 4791]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """She fasted and worshipped and satisfied the ancestors and the gods.
In that deserted forest, she was devoted to worshipping the ancestors and the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2f0895877a44ccd824aec0e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[640]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king will leave for the forest on the day of the full moon in the month of Kartika." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2f8dbbc831e9a11ce5b002f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5360]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 381(84) Vaishampayana said, ‘Having ascertained the thoughts of his brothers and those of the wise Narada, King Yudhishthira then spoke to Dhoumya, who was like the grandfather325 himself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e2fee10d39a2cf47d8135816> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2178]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods themselves are always desirous of seeing this form." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e30de695de81bf0b709b2c0d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11905]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because of the adharma practised by kings, subjects always endure hardships." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e31b025e9a2eb3304608ace3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 203 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9773]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The other gods faced the north, while all the rishis faced various directions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e3203a81e8f1f37d590946ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2556]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing those two great-souled and brave ones, like two leaders of herds engaged in combat, all the Kurus were astounded." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e323cb2ca4f53b3e5850b3f3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7081, 7083]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O bull among men! He is engaged in ensuring Jishnu’s958 welfare.
He is Vaikuntha959 Purushottama.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e3250f4c59fd979b06a611e0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8928, 8929]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Shura’s descendant was the immensely illustrious Shouri407 Vasudeva, foremost among men.
Shura was a supreme archer and was equal to Kartavirya408 in battle.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e3354b10937020364a9da207> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[854]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having recovered his senses, maharatha Chitrasena severed his145 bow with a broad-headed arrow and pierced him with seven arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e33e75c5a1c755df3da96651> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16335]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the equal of the gods and the immortals and you have performed a great deed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e340b69d231bd9e5125e227a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3027]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘While this was being described, Pandava19 remained concealed in his disguise." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e346f3995d3c6a1a1d2558b2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1420]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of Chedi, Bhishma knows Krishna’s true nature and you yourself do not know it as well as the Kouravya10 does." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e3855977ddeb74bc76080374> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15958]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ On hearing Rama’s words, Varuna’s abode122 was extremely aggrieved and stood there, hands joined in salutation." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e38ee85cd60cfa1b156febb2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6678]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because of the curse imposed by the goddess, the gods no longer had offspring." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e39eb4a6adf87adb1063522d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2212]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘Yudhishthira said, “It seems that some of the most feared rogues122 have assembled there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e3b760b91324bdae997e847d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1701]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! It was like the army of the daityas being crushed by the king of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e3c7bc3aaba883653361ad91> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8784]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Biting their lower lips in anger, those other warriors, the sons and grandsons of kings, had set their eyes, hearts and natures on Krishna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e3d7b189802e6e246f4fd111> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8324]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That is the reason I have restrained you from travelling along this road, frequented by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e3f4b0e01e27ad299937a8f0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 109 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6675, 6676]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Which one do you wish to go to? O foremost among brahmanas! O brahmana! I am ready to show you all the directions and the entire earth.
O brahmana! Climb up on me.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e422211d8be4569b7534caf4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6872]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O king! Having thus spoken, the lord of men then addressed Karna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e42359a354ad49b7d4fb1839> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2151]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Progressively, Mahat is thought of in these different words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e426bf5d83b7f56cdc170842> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15800]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "From one yuga to another, dharma266 is created in that fashion." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e42c67e3922f7ba35538ecba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1997, 2004]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """There were large and colourful garments pleasant to the touch, from Bahlika66 and China.
Shakas, Tukharas, Kankas, Romashas70 and men with horns brought as tribute one hundred million71 horses that could travel great and long distances.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e450bf1e55d244bab0392948> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8128]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The rakshasas started to obstruct his sacrificial rites." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e4592c4eaf0e02914ee5dca2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14987]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ ‘“Shri replied, ‘This is one quarter of me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e45d341ffad4e2ace9a45522> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6114]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Drona’s son then afflicted those unvanquished and supreme men691 with supreme arrows and pierced them from a close distance." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e45d35b61b450ed29a5a5a63> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5333]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All these superhuman arrangements were made worthy of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e45e86e2a636f7d401f2b28a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[162, 166]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The bodies of the gods dazzled.
The river Vaitarani, the thorny shalmali trees, the iron pots and the terrible mountains also vanished.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e46d42455c9d409ff8742b21> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4189]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those two brave ones were resplendent in the battle, equals of the sons of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e476575a966133a89c5a9119> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6868]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Madhava! O foremost among the Shinis!540 When this foremost of men541 knows that the time has come to display valour, then you and Keshava will vanquish Suyodhana in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e4802ee615ed488336d3d047> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8211]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If the king who has dharma in his soul and is rigid in his vows10 knows that I am Kunti’s first son, he will not accept the kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e487105d6a5e6a976195aff2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6767, 6768]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """When the two constellations of Proshthapada198 are in the ascendance, Shukra grants men the riches that they have earned.
Those riches are guarded by Aja Ekapada,199 Ahi Budhnya200 and the lord of riches.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e49f73bf241897c04c2cb7c0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15012]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, when the midday sun shines and does not set, there will again be a battle between the gods and the asuras and I will defeat you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e4ad8a9e0280d1619670f739> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3439]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Amidst the creepers there, the gods and the ancestors find delight." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e4b444a1fa65fe1576a24d94> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9368]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In your very sight, I will kill Vrishasena22 in this battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e4b619f7502596f6024123c3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13245]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They and their gods are different from you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e4c13263bca5d6270145abf0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 89 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6478]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O best of the Bharata lineage! There was the sound of weapons and the roar of men." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e4c5e2150630e7eaab358722> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9972]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Austerities, learning and birth—these are the three ways of becoming a brahmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e4cdd232d5ff5acb125f8a58> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20450]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The immensely energetic one creates consciousness793 and Prajapati is created from that consciousness." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e4cf0844459ce6e2849253e8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2433]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "And he26 spoke these words to Abhimanyu, the slayer of enemy heroes." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e4d218112723be9db4083908> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[875]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It80 was famous as the vajra and possessing eight sides, it was embellished with diamonds, gems and jewels." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e4db579b13aad5d8c12f953d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2466]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘O charioteer! Who is Drona? Who are these assembled kshatriyas? Even if Shakra on Airavata32 advances in the forefront of the battle, with the masses of immortals, I will engage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e4f6ffa60e14defecdeb9a98> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5033, 5034]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O lord of men! On performing ablutions in that tirtha of the nagas, a man obtains the fruits of one thousand tawny cows.
Then one should go to Lalitika, Shantanu’s supreme tirtha.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e506d56647aa13cbcc8de25c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5086]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 743(80) Vaishampayana said, ‘On hearing the king’s words, which were in conformity with dharma and artha and ensured welfare, Krishna22 was afflicted with grief." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5104e6e6cde43ec35f6675c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8492]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In great joy, all the people came out to welcome the great-souled and sinless one,108 like gods welcome their chief." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e51c400f44605263c7c071d9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2117]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord of the gods! O refuge of the universe! Have mercy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5279e5d996efa075455650b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3259]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Just as all the gods listen to the words of the king of the gods, the wielder of the vajra, in that way, all the Pandavas6 and Srinjayas listened to the capable words spoken by Kiriti." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e52e69861daf784c03e29b6d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7423]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“O beautiful one, equal to the offspring of the gods! Who are you? Where have you come from? What business has brought you here? Are you the goddess of this forest or are you an apsara? Tell me everything and also tell me why you are standing here." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e53beadd305a721c3f5b5167> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5978]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! It was called Shringataka303 and it was destructive of the vyuhas of enemies." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e540537d5f8c13751c5e08db> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[342]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Virata gave his daughter Uttara to Kiriti92 for Abhimanyu, the son of Subhadra and the slayer of enemies." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5421eb37c3759741cb17258> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9708, 9709]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """I will use my weapons to destroy those who hate the thirty gods.
There are no evil haters of the gods who do not deserve to be slain by me.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5432a7da4fd8d5ec73914d7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5409]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Heaven is obtained through lawful conduct, austerities and donations." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e551b82454eb887d26dfa829> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4985]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Conquer heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e55895ea248b107f60596533> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22983]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Using this, the gods abandoned the mortal world and went to heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e558e1fc6be25287a7708673> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 43 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3029]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He who has not deviated from the truth should be known as a brahmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e567b11bbef7479e98f61ee7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4473]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Vasava’s son205 obtained hundreds of excellent gandharva horses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e56c65ff61e0f73df7a94aaf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 34 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1877]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ ‘“The brahmana said, ‘Knowledge of the brahman is the lower arani and the preceptor is the upper arani." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e56f5f373ae0d2a03d66941a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3683]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The strong and powerful Balabhadra86 went there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e577507eeb5b6c06b12da1ec> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1343]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the best of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e57ed55027288388b4975583> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2373]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Show your favours to the gods and grant this to the residents of heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e59a9d7e5e09ba9922c6d707> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4005]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They are like the gods of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5a34bd383ff5b8d2679e432> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8903]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "King Yudhishthira ensured that strings of bows, bows, armour, weapons, honey, clarified butter, mountainous heaps of resin16 and sand, plenty of water and fodder, chaff and charcoal were made available to every camp." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5a9c2d27c5a76538a35ede4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3058, 3059]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """His wife was Nirriti and so rakshasas48 are known as nairritas.
She also had three other terrible sons, always engaged in evil deeds—Bhaya,49 Mahabhaya50 and Mrityu,51 the destroyers of beings.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5ae89dd2876da215321ee70> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8925, 8926]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """At the time of parvasandhi, Vaishravana Naravahana93 can be seen there in his prosperity, surrounded by apsaras.
All the beings then see the lord of the rakshasas seated on the peak of the mountain, as resplendent as the rising sun.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5af35362733eb380ccf24f8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20779]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "835 O Indra among kings! That is the reason the best among ascetics say that it836 is the presider." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5b8badfc92041a73690066a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8385]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having heard Bhimasena’s roar, Partha363 attacked Drona, supreme among the wielders of weapons, from every direction." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5d3ea5ad11f9a258a5dc6ec> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 14 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[621]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "34 For these blind and aged ones, why could you not have saved a single one? O son! Had you left one, I would not have felt this sorrow at your having slain our sons, as long as you acted in accordance with dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5d4af7d7cc5718201e86d74> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1100, 1102, 1104]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """” O foremost among those who have knowledge of the brahman! In times gone by, the snakes were cursed by their mother4 that they would be destroyed in Janamejaya’s sacrifice by the one whose charioteer was the wind.
‘Accepting her in accordance with the prescribed rites, he7 had from her a great-souled son named Astika, great-souled and an ascetic and learned in the Vedas and the Vedangas.
Then, after a long time, we have heard that a ruler of men8 from the Pandava lineage conducted a great sacrifice known as the snake-sacrifice.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5dd2db731b13bba1c9a5fa1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25898]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’”’ Chapter 1678(350) ‘“T he brahmana said, ‘Vivasvat’s1391 chariot has a single wheel and in due course, you firmly draw it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5e0113727b25f78b7d3e875> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1102]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” The riders shouted, “Yoke the mounts." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e5ecb4684ad7f95ef4ec27e6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8153]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O illustrious one! Tell me, if it is not a secret, is there anyone more emaciated than you? O brahmana! In this world, is there anything that is more difficult to get?”1094 Krishatanu1095 replied, “It is rarer to find a petitioner who is satisfied with what he has got." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e602045b1d5340365c8b0056> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23829]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Narada! Look at Dhruva1175 and the best of the stellar bodies in the firmament and also at the oceans full of water, the lakes and the rivers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e60f18c0bb310801c79bf0b2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10361]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "As Khandava blazed, thousands of beings leapt in the ten25 directions, uttering frightened yells." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e617069b5de497e8bfe556c7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17783, 17784, 17785]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Because she nurtures his limbs, she is known as Amba.
Because she gives birth to a brave one, she is known as Virasu.
Because she nurtures the child, she is known as Sushru.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e61a4aa99a7cae44ccf27894> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4898]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He224 asked the devarshi about what had happened to the Kurus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e61bd2e3309e8274afaf41c9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 1 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[251]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He who makes a Brahmana listen to one verse of a shloka at a funeral ceremony, his offerings of food and drink to his ancestors become inexhaustible." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e62cdf79b9bb7f71dae68cf5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4968]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O evil-minded one! On the seventh day after you were born, an invisible voice spoke to Pritha588 from the sky." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e62ffc88578cff995e945f5e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8309]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘The gandharva said, “Desire and anger, which even the gods find difficult to conquer, were overcome through his71 austerities and washed his feet." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e6344849ee4530dc129597ec> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2963]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Thus I have narrated to you, as I heard it in the ancient tales, the origins of the dynasties of the gods and the powerful and strong demons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e63e7ec9d2b325b208ec49a7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3003, 3004, 3007]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He is like the one with the vajra in his hand16 and ascended my chariot.
He has won back the cattle and he has vanquished the Kurus.
He released arrows and repulsed Sharadvat’s son,17 Drona, Drona’s valorous son, the son of the suta18 and Bhishma.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e640470953dc542e80094ed0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2562]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Krishna182 has not yet become a slave." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e6411235dda06c9b87da2ae1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14773]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“Is she an apsara, a daughter of the gods, or an illusion created by the gods?” Thinking this, all of them joined their hands in salutation and gazed at the unblemished one." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e64b30574cfcd57f3894a6df> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4696]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "(28) Without any pride, he must worship the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e6a1b055e492263ce4f11896> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17102]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The blazing god, the granter of boons, spoke to Shiva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e6a8ec2869ce258700b6ec85> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2308]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Infantry was seen to be engaged with infantry." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e6c60bac7b9e213d56619f51> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 19 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1788]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It was as if a giant mountain peak had been shattered by the vajra, unleashed by the lord of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e6d24ac6fa5f8b22f2ea5254> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17726]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The dharma of the three24 always leads to fruits." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e6e420b703161e56d3f9036e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[770]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Thus addressed by the king of the gods, his lotus-eyed wife told him that it would be this way." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e6e8ee00465e9a58fbfdf724> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15632]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was full of jealousy and suspected that her mind was attracted towards Sugriva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e70b01b4526ca018f09d0a2b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9045]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Having heard from the priest the words of Dharmaraja, he3 kept ready a large collection of things like fruits, sanctified garlands, shields, armour, seats, cattle, ropes, and other objects used in agriculture, to determine the nature of the Kurus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e742500a9596b11642a7a890> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[812]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O best of warriors! O Pandava! On seeing Sahadeva engaged with cows, covering himself with calf skins at night, how can I bear to live? ‘“He24 always possessed the three qualities of beauty, weaponry and intelligence." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e75abf0f57a33912a2e8c45d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19145]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O supreme among gods! There is this man who has been born from your sweat." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e76a2563c89c493c421c2531> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1906, 1907]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """) Vardhana;861 (655) Vriddha;862 (656) Maha-vriddha;863 (657) Ganadhipa;864 (.
) Nitya;865 (658) Atmasahaya;866 (659) Devasura-pati;867 (660) Pari;868 (661) Yukta;869 (662) Yukta-bahu;870 (663) Dvivida;871 (664) Suparvana;872 (665) Ashada;873 (666) Sushada;874 (.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e7717041b3a5e167f6b8b52b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[776]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Alone on a single chariot, he defeated gods, men and serpents." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e78751ac784deef8d093daa4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7433]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Look at the man and the rakshasa, both with great strength and valour, grasping each other with great force and fighting and roaring." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e78e069a2e1d32aef8b1251e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12126]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He yoked all the gods to his supreme chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e79d0303b6df239914a9f7ce> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[505]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Birth, death, old age, disease and pain are without any substance and transient." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e7a658e5db6968b29adbbcc7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[308]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O lord of men! Then the illustrious and valorous Surya143 took me to Brahma’s unblemished sabha, one that knows no fatigue." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e7e8d7a56391846adfb9f618> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10187]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Truthfulness, self-control, austerities, non-violence and constant benevolence are the means whereby men attain salvation, not through birth or lineage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e7f7ac8713a7fe2f2f49015e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1850]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I do not yet know the words that brave one among the Kurus2 has addressed towards me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e808e4538f04c7f31e9791a8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[944]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing Saindhava, Krishna’s son85 let go of Pourava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e815d9d5dd0765400889070a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8843]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having appointed a general under Krishna’s instructions, when the rest of the night has passed, we will march out to the field of battle, anointing our weapons with fragrances12 and performing auspicious ceremonies." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e8328e7c18e11d2713bdb3dc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[328]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then follows the pilgrimages of the great-souled Pandavas, the slaying of Jatasura, Bhimasena’s journey to Gandhamadana at Droupadi’s request, where he transgressed a lotus pond in search of a mandara flower82 and had a great fight with the rakshasas and yakshas led by Manimana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e833e2e115b43caece16b9cb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[177]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O Sanjaya! I had no hope of victory when I heard that Yuyudhana60 of the Vrishni race threw Drona’s army into disorder with the strength of his unassailable elephant and returned to where Krishna and Partha61 were." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e84dace7a21fbc67941163de> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3108, 3118, 3122, 3136]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He is the one whom the gods worship.
It is because of him that the two gods are in the firmament.
Both these gods carry earth and heaven.
There is a terrible river with twelve flows protected by the gods and one drinks from it.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e84e27a89310f5ec13b819be> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8008]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The unhappiness from the loss of the kingdom, the defeat at the game of dice and the banishment of my sons was nothing compared to the unhappiness when that large, dark and weeping lady was brought to the assembly hall and made to listen to harsh words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e85e352f841df986d9d5a5cd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5164, 5169]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """You605 have never done anything like this.
He is immensely strong and like Vaishravana607 and Yama.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e86598e40ac5f3cb478b53fc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4538]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "178 He is Purushottama because he fills up179 and destroys again." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e8bd835a200dd3bce02cdc49> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5709]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was born with natural armour, blessed with good fortune and handsome like a son of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e8bdf9dc2f85a5411e3c32c4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7014]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He released a broad-headed arrow that was like the vajra or thunder and sliced off the head of his243 charioteer." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e8c7a8c67f262de93c4dccd3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7376]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He265 was like Mount Mainaka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e8d920989027b26eb750644a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9241]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Krishna Parshati53 was preordained to be the wife of five and remain unblemished." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e8e05ad567f2e0285858da56> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 81 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4758]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Composed, the brahmachari should then go to Kapila tirtha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e8f143ccc0c3da30c1a519a9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15168]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But Phalguna restrained the angry Bhimasena, saying, “O Kourava! For Duhshala’s sake, remember what the king40 has said." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e8f41071f3a6255163a16570> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15299]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In the same way, the great grandfather addressed Kumbhakarna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e8f6935ad21d26051a6a5c62> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19057]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Partha! Khurvundas668 were born from Vritra’s blood." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e9050b12b00458ce9d192343> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10854]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Vows imposed on men who violate other men’s wives must also be imposed on them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e909038f4471368dc327415d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1685, 1687, 1690]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """I have heard from aryas188 that a king protects dharma and dharma in turn protects him.
O tiger among men! Like a man is followed by his own shadow, you have always steadily followed dharma.
O Partha! You have always served the gods, the ancestors and the brahmanas through svahas,189 svadhas190 and other forms of worship.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e90a3a40ec4079396ef976ac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7279, 7284]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """With the one with a bird on his banner815 with him, he showered torrents of arrows on the Kurus.
Panchajanya and Devadatta816 roared.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e90eec34be43256b0cacca5b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15416, 15424]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """As is appropriate, they worshipped the ancestors, the gods and guests.
O lord! Truthfulness, generosity, austerities, purity, compassion, gentle speech and lack of injury towards friends—they possessed all these.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e911f352467ae8c8aeba7fd6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3943]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! With one angry, severe and swift blow, I will dispatch Bhima to Vaivasvata’s104 domain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e92c2be7883578f98b472045> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11041]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His169 bow was severed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e92c8bf2c8047ff6702653fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[76, 77]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Let the messenger try to persuade them that half of the kingdom should be returned to Yudhishthira.
”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘O king! On hearing Janardana’s sweet and calm words, full of dharma and artha, his elder brother13 strongly welcomed and applauded those words and spoke these words of his own.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e92cfc6b5a05e960e467ef3c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5672]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Prosperity went to the gods and ill fortune went to the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e930c7ab454cb5e3cb822735> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9118, 9119]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Instructed by Krishna, the one with infinite energy, those greatest among men20 also sat down on expensive seats.
O lord of the people! After some time, in sweet words, Parshata21 asked the great-souled one about Droupadi.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e933aa06c4f49c473f628a38> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2851]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The descendant of the Kuru lineage6 spoke these words to Vasudeva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e953223c7e2830500fabe3b9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23344, 23346]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Shedding tears of rage, he told Uparichara, ‘I have placed a share1121 in front.
The other gods are seen to have appeared in person and have accepted the shares offered to them.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e9549ffa353e46761d0dde8e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17688]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ‘The yaksha asked, “Which is the single sacrificial chant? What is the sacrificial formula? What do sacrifices need? And what can sacrifices not transgress?” ‘Yudhishthira replied, “The breath of life21 is the single sacrificial chant." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e957e9740c35f913145422a2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15618]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But Tara93 restrained him and said, ‘From the manner in which the mighty monkey Sugriva is roaring, I think that he has obtained a protector." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e967ea1aca1e3fe4f370e0f8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2986]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The word Mrityu has two syllables." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e96f2d32cd5e6062fb325212> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4997]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "How have you withdrawn as a result of your fear of Karna? O evil-souled one! Had you given the bow to Keshava and become his charioteer in the battle, then Keshava would have slain the fierce Karna, like the lord of the Maruts593 bringing down Vritra with his vajra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e96f357fc533ad42075928f9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2068, 2072]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """She said, “O son! Through Koushika’s1149 favours, you have been adorned with knowledge of the Vedas.
I controlled my atman and devoted myself to Mahadeva.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e975939c9c4e2649c9920135> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3443]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Madhava63 bathed there and donated riches to the brahmanas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e98410b36fd571d460871378> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1367, 1368]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """When they were seated, the immensely intelligent king who was the extender of the Kuru lineage2 also sat down, surrounded by the sons of Pandu.
Gandhari, Kunti, Droupadi, Satvati3 and the other women also seated themselves.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e99c7d0a4cc9c22a8c24e5d5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7118, 7119, 7120]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘In the month of Magha,169 during uttarayana, on the thirteenth day, a person who has been born in our lineage must give us payasam mixed with ghee.
When the nakshatra Magha is in the ascendant, he must observe the vows and offer us petals of the kanchana flower, with goat meat.
When the nakshatra Hasta is in the ascendant,170 he must offer this in accordance with the rites, using whisks made from the leaves of the Indian laburnum tree.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e99d5e0ca04c4b78bd3cff27> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11180]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With her husband, she satisfies gods, guests and servants." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e9a0589586c5ae66a0a77f38> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10502]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With three sharp arrows, Drona’s son killed three other maharathas, while Drupada’s son133 and Phalguna looked on." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e9b66e9161aa3ecc873827ae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4705]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "114 Bathing there and worshipping Hari, the lord of the three worlds, one obtains a horse sacrifice115 and attains Vishnu’s world." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e9b7b791063b64bb47aaed33> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2069]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I gave my word to Dhritarashtra’s son91 earlier and I will repay that debt today." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e9ba440b4ed3f423684a07bc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5140]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is also rajarshi257 Janaka’s well, worshipped by the thirty gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e9c0cf44c1f3093207fb8ae5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6467]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The third son of the king of Kuninda struck your son732 between the breasts with excellent arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e9db709759859533619ca54b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4182, 4183]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O tiger among kings! In that sacrifice, King Mandhata placed the two feet of the great- souled Parameshthi647 Vishnu on his own head.
Vishnu adoped the form of Vasava and showed himself and surrounded by kings, he648 worshipped that lord.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/e9ea5e2e337a72aafe1eddce> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4256, 4257]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The gods always ignore sentiments that have nothing to do with divine affairs.
Their divinity would be called into question if the gods were seen to be motivated by love, hatred and avarice.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ea3128b7a3d3c4f607ae4c4a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5238]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But Dhritarashtra’s son doesn’t know about the right code of conduct." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ea3a9c392116618cd46c3f04> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "17_Mahaprasthanika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[49]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All of Parikshit’s mothers8 surrounded him and began to instruct him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ea457ea28cc9af1c39da2596> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8304, 8305]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The sharp and extremely radiant planet Shanaishchara32 is oppressing the nakshatra Prajapatya,33 implying greater suffering for all beings.
O Madhusudana! Angaraka34 is retrograde in Jyeshtha and is aspiring for Anuradha, as if seeking its friendship.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ea5fa75873da7bd197e7cc56> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4791, 4793]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O lord of the earth! The river renowned as Apaga158 is only a krosha159 to the east of Manusha.
A man offering a meal of grain160 to the gods and the ancestors there attains all the great fruits of dharma.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eaa62e07710c9222e7a97eb7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[362]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The supremely wise Vasudeva dispelled there95 Partha’s96 lassitude born out of delusion, by invoking the teachings of salvation." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eab040c632ade5b00d09c972> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 78 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6267, 6268, 6269, 6270]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """If a person covers a well-behaved and milk-yielding white cow with a piece of cloth and gives it away, with her calf, he obtains greatness in Indra’s world.
If a person covers a well-behaved and milk-yielding black cow with a piece of cloth and gives it away, with her calf, he obtains greatness in Agni’s world.
If a person covers a well-behaved and milk-yielding smoky-complexioned cow with a piece of cloth and gives it away, with her calf, he obtains greatness in Yama’s world.
If a person covers a cow that has the complexion of foam on water with a piece of cloth and gives it away, with her calf and a brass vessel for milking, he obtains Varuna’s world.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eab27664cc2cbfc5f9ebc4d8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13676]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "How is it that the truthful Ajatashatru, pure and devoted to the conduct of aryas, must now sleep on the ground? He earlier used to sleep on beds covered with soft ranku4 skin." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eab9e5d4f22039657f26b1da> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5592]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Could those have brought them happiness? I am tormented because Krishna54 was molested in the assembly hall by Dhritarashtra’s son, in the midst of the Kurus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eac8a6c8cdf0a56fed254902> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4285]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I rejected the gods and chose you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eaebd26e304dc2891324f16b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13403]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "From that great and terrible shower of weapons, the entire army of the gods was scattered in an instant and was seen to waver." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eaffb48dacb6ef6015043080> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5853]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Abandon excessive pride, insolence and anger." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eb0e1f70dfe8e0fbc1d87f36> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 193 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9341]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Or let artful and skilled men create dissension among the sons of Pritha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eb11731b5c9b86ab27ad0fba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1034]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ 315(18) ‘Vasudeva said, “O bull among the Bharata lineage! After having uttered these words to the Yadavas, Rukmini’s son88 ascended his golden chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eb166ff8578f3185f4eb9779> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9745]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ 203 ‘Narada said, “On witnessing this great destruction, all the devarshis, the siddhas27 and the supreme rishis were extremely distressed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eb45cc953a180303ea7cc63d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4996]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "221 Brahma, the gods, the sages and the ascetics are there and the siddhas, the charanas, the gandharvas, the kinnaras222 and the great nagas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eb4c42c752f370f5d600c206> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 114 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8910]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They defeated all the other Kurus and showered him with arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eb50b25acc365d4bc840bcf8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9031]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In that battle, Kiriti, invincible in battle, struck them and severed them416 into two, three and eight fragments." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eb5bd5821ab09c535f90f3db> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[241]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I have been engaged by the king of the gods and have given him an undertaking." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eb5ffb08790497f44b9fce6c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6369]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is recommended that the soldiers should march in the months of Chaitra and Margashirsha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eb669bd14c56ba97cf7d003f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7676, 7677]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """When they are satisfied through pure worship, the gods give men constant svaha, constant svadha,294 long lives, riches and sons.
Ancestors and gods always desire generosity, learning, sacrifices and the protection of the subjects in their sons.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eb9a8df658684a1936b2a1eb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10897]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Having thus spoken, Mahadeva Kapardi Vrishadhvaja76 disappeared, while all the brahmanas looked on." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eb9bb259a5197b25ad970c86> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[700]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Thus addressed, he told the queen, “Madam! Be reassured." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ebc2ec9ecc184cdb68330a19> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[624, 627]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """74 O great king! Know that the gods decided to base themselves on action.
Know that those who censure the Vedas75 have been dislodged and are extreme non- believers.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ebd72c1f74920cbb484a720a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2716]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I shall give you a great and excellent flying chariot,40 made of crystal and possessed by the gods alone, that is capable of carrying you through the sky." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ebd8d37e63480406457876b2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7823]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Kounteya! There are innumerable yakshas, rakshasas and kinnaras, serpents, divine birds653 and gandharvas, in the direction of Kubera’s abode." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ebda0530e45795bc5afb1922> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5716]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let those gods bless me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ebdad31979c98df28045442d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10366]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In the original subtle body created by the gods, man accumulates a great store of good and evil deeds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ebdbbb119ba12edc07b4381c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2973]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Sairandhri11 attended to him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ebdf7b36022a13d94e39bdc1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[890]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” The gods acted in accordance with these words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ebe425832525c6fc408e86c8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1946]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Vasusena271 was oppressed because of the arrows of the bull among the Shinis, and the atirathas and well-wishers on your side quickly advanced towards that bull among rathas,272 together with their elephants, chariots, horses and foot soldiers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec26d0d987cc07086fdd1170> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9901, 9904]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O great king! The lord of the rakshasas35 is the son of Bhimasena and Hidimba.
There are brave rakshasas and advisers who follow his instructions.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec2aac28fb27cb6570857b36> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3399]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That vyuha was as resplendent as one of the gods or the asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec2d14c6fb4495c0cb6a30b2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6318]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Chapter 1428(100) ‘Bhishma said, “In this connection, an ancient history is recounted about when Pratardana879 and the king of Mithila fought a battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec2ec8dfd86a9d8cdd0e0f6e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9075]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He is on a celestial vehicle that has the radiance of the twelve Adityas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec31127d178f12761788454b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10276]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing the mighty-armed Karna, in that great battle, they123 let out a roar." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec39f2b43ce808ed7a8b51a4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[498]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At that, the illustrious chastiser of Paka suddenly let loose a great shower of rain there and caused an obstruction to the act of ploughing." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec66ac5d7ae952aed727913e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8173]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let the Pandavas proclaim Vasushena’s8 triumph." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec6dc828f074695ccfc87cb6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4038]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He knows about the battle formations used by men, gods, gandharvas and asuras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec76061a902478b0058c86de> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2988, 2989]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """On witnessing his dexterity, even the gods were satisfied.
On seeing the success with which Krishna’s son64 hit the targets, all the charioteers, with Bhishma at the forefront, thought that he possessed the spirit of Dhananjaya himself.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec8799143d9510d5ec9eb56e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9963]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I vanquished all those kings, like the king of the gods against the danavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec89dc64be8ccdfb2efc5519> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1440]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Absolute ruin soon comes to those who are separated." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec8aacf3510980f90b52644c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1130]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "39 He vanquished Samudrasena and King Chandrasena, the king of Tamralipta40 and Kacha, the ruler of Vanga." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec8d0998a9757069d29bf838> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5658]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "However, the rakshasa sliced them down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ec9d0baaf602d585397f0580> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9395]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! That bull among the gods then spoke to me in comforting words." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ecbfabc8b5fa6130e7398752> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 26 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1525]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With unparalleled strength, energy and radiance, capable of razing the cities of the asuras and displaying themselves in forms as radiant as the blazing fire, the gods stood there, their minds set upon protecting the amrita." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ecdaf8a4864357f10fc934ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2871]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A shudra who shows homage in due order to brahmana, kshatriya and vaishya classes93 and satisfies them—enjoys happiness in heaven after he has given up his body, because his sins are burnt up." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ecdc55d330184d68e7f69ffc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2423, 2425]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Itihasa337 and the Yajur Veda protected the rear.
O Indra among kings! Vashatkara338 was the goad there.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ece4a11679eea70f46dd1a24> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7723]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The rakshasa then rushed at him, with an upraised spear." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ed00d21cb0af1589d966951b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6750]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When Phalguna352 succeeded in this task, Drona embraced him and deduced that Drupada and his relatives had already been vanquished in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ed0c222c055009fe9b3da1a5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19741]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Discontent leads to misery." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ed29b7c02887621484594a18> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1611]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowledge is covered by this desire that is insatiable like the fire." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ed2c47e766d232a3ef5679b6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10129]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Slaughtered by Drona, the Panchalas fled, while Bhimasena and the great-souled Partha111 were looking." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ed38d73f4cad147ff4cde485> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6507]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’215 Having been thus addressed, he216 replied, ‘O Satyaki! Go and accomplish your objective." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ed40bbc0dae9bbc1999e7994> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7028]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His body was incapable of being measured by the gods or the demons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ed58f90964d74e1f804f0b1e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3842]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Humble servants produced sacrifices27 offered every night to Tryambaka." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ed65400e4a41b5782beb058d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5654]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He797 must check the sales, purchases, expenses, shops and routes of traders, impose taxes and act so that their yoga and kshema are ensured." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ed7eae8295e2575a0625cf66> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5112]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O best of the gods! Among the brave ones who are killed in battle and among the ones who give to those who solicit gifts, there is no one who is superior to the one who gives away land." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ed8f528551b246cd4a0c290c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1505, 1506, 1508]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Even the God of the gods rained showers of blood.
Garlands on the necks of the gods faded and the sky’s energy withered.
The swirling dust darkened the splendour of crowns worn by the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ed9854d1d1e3bd2ef04b26b9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[869]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Heaven and the world of men are established on the rod." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/edaa2a5b802e41c3c9dcb181> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[877, 878]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """You ensured the greatness of the gods.
Save the world of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/edaf06afb375fd5ae3d6bf94> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6257]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The slayer of enemies countered the rakshasa who was seeking his death." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/edff2b1524a08b49ef7ddb20> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[154]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "24 Engagement and withdrawal are seen to be the result of this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ee00237ebf5c378a109c1e03> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6309]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Droupadi’s son rescued their maternal uncles710 with well-prepared chariots, like providing boats on an ocean." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ee08eba061faa10c4ab453c8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6316]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those rathas713 armoured themselves well and again attacked, desiring to protect the foremost one from the Shini lineage." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ee11cbb56fc9faf213f4d9c2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15694]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "238 One year239 is again one day and one night for the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ee1d16b7301837d80f16116c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 36 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2387, 2388]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """By destroying what is due to the gods, by stealing the property of brahmanas and by causing offence to brahmanas, lineages degenerate.
O descendant of the Bharata lineage! By oppressing brahmanas and speaking ill of them and by stealing what has been entrusted to them, lineages degenerate.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ee1e0d1a095cc0aa7937e3aa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[749]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Like Death created by Destiny, he severed the feet of some and the thighs of others." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ee46c995caf8d095e8a128a6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17095]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O unblemished one! You will be able to repulse the desire of the king of the gods for the earrings with many kinds of words and by citing reasons again and again." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ee6455f0d6435242216bbcad> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10628, 10629]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Listen to the tasks that must be observed by those who are in vanaprastha.
They must perform ablutions thrice a day and must perform the rites for worshipping the ancestors and the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ee6908a158b64ca492bf1792> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6229]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Slain, they fell down with a great noise." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ee84489cca4f81d8e9e25876> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10203]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He worships his seniors and the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ee8bafa9905d741f48e7dee0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8403]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having been cursed by Shakti, that best of kings95 sought Shakti’s mercy and worshipped him, so as to pacify him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eea625e562f0c515cfb0d4ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15731]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "249 Mana is far-reaching and flows in many different ways." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eeb8eeaa28c8f9b7aa2589ad> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3566, 3568]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """” When the great-souled Bharadvaja64 heard Bhishma’s words, he showed his respects to Dhritarashtra in the midst of those kings and said, “O king! O best of the Bharata lineage! Act in accordance with what Bhishma has said.
Before embarking on a battle, I think that we should negotiate with the Pandavas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eee3a3eca1a86428f087f4fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3213]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The great archer Drona was engaged in ensuring Gangeya’s102 welfare." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eef43932d9c7e01ea251e2ad> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1206]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In Vasudeva’s presence, while he110 was fighting with another one in the battle and was distracted, he was brought down." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/eef94b663050f5a881432654> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 19 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1134]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "“How is the food, eaten every once in a while, digested in the stomach? How does it become juices? How is blood generated from that? How does this sustain flesh, marrow, sinews and bones? How do all the limbs of embodied creatures grow? As one keeps growing, how does the strength increase? How is waste that is without substance separately excreted? How does one inhale and exhale? Which part of the body is inhabited by the atman? How does the jivatman exert itself and move the body around? What is the complexion of the mind and where does it dwell?” O Madhava! I was asked this by that brahmana." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ef001ab79ec5938d7e9e0844> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3611, 3614]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O wielder of the trident! You are the refuge of the universe, the gods and the asuras.
Even the gods are incapable of comprehending you.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ef066c48b881f7a47394e081> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1394]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "How does he deserve to be honoured foremost among all these kings? O bull among the Bharata lineage! You cannot consider Krishna to be the eldest when the aged Vasudeva7 is here? How can the son he shown homage first? Or you may consider Vasudeva to be one who always does that which ensures your welfare." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ef312e115a7b0f648e0a7c11> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7582]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O one who has been born from the fire! Because of the lump that stands out on my cheek, know me to Ganda." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ef3928850359eaac4456cbcb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1709]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His severe form is seen to be like that of the Destroyer." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ef4362fd9fb0c48732ff9eef> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1503]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On a single chariot, he defeated gods, men and serpents." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ef48463f183e4ce5752a1627> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10347]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "These men were overcome by greed and delusion and the gods abandoned them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ef583faacd06edac27190fd2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19647]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Sages who are truthful in speech say that gifts given indifferently and disrespectfully are the worst." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ef6ee20bf8c5a35cbfa378ca> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 27 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1129]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O great king! He then attacked the king of Vanga." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ef711292c12a34c10ad372cc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1613]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "52 He was the equal of Partha in battle53 and was on supreme horses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ef742014021bf28a37938661> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3201]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bring the fire from Dvaraka39 and the priests." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ef7457721b8537f4c0b3b6ab> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2848]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Let us kill the sons of Dhritarashtra before the twelve64 years have passed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ef82d4109897ce0009a56bcf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 32 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1981]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because, in every way, I am the original cause of the gods and the great sages." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/efb22401d880a67ceec009aa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1345]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He slaughtered the soldiers, like Death, the Destroyer." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/efb901a266c03f4fc10d070c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2557]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Surrounded by his brothers, he9 penetrated the enemy army, full of arrows and lances, and swiftly advanced towards Bhishma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/efccaf6439938cbb89137a03> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7130]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘After Vidura, Bhishma and the citizens had returned, Kunti went to Ajatashatru55 and said, “What did kshatta56 tell you among so many people? He spoke as if he said nothing and you replied similarly." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/efcd3c56ce393ed0a022daa0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2880]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Axles of chariots clashed against axles of chariots." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/efcfb1d7a51f3f91e7193338> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5056]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Austerities, sacrifices, learning, good conduct, lack of greed, devotion to the truth and worship of seniors and the gods—all these are vested in a person who gives away land." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/efe0567b0d2ab832d409ca98> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9427]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It was divine, magical and sacred and was driven by Matali." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/efff4936eee61757630ad640> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6658]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Through his austerities, he brought the gods under his control." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f0010eec3dc2da60ffb39f76> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3354]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Janardana! I know the dharma for countries, clans516 and families." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f0131fe3b1ee439aebe5e6f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1847]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the acts that I start are for the gods, the ancestors, the elements and the guests." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f03764aa94622f76911f8409> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 260 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17976]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The one who is in vanaprastha goes there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f03ebbfa90acad00701bdb67> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5549]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord! These have been held to constitute eyes for the gods and the ancestors." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f04b5798ff8f639e33be2fd9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1720]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The sages who know the truth visualize this in a different way and alter their course, like the wind in the sky." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f0560f27c28b95f5fd81c09c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4826]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "216 Tuskers shatterd large numbers of chariots." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f05aeedc7dccb32cc109d8c4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[76]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "17 In a form that was as radiant as that of the gods, he obtained divine weapons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f05e01850e0b821c09b60e7b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1904]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "65 That is the reason I am famous among gods and men as Jishnu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f0795b3e0922a011631d3ad7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9700]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It has been said that slaughtered animals are oblations offered to the ancestors and the gods in sacrifices." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f0960aeb0275392a31963161> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 166 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11442]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“If someone kills a brahmana, if someone is a drunkard, if someone is a thief, if someone has broken his vows—there are indicated means of atonement." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f0a1b2dc3af18c1d50156b26> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[994]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But the army avoided cremation grounds, temples of the gods, anthills and chaityas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f0a582d4c43ad9f3f72a2c67> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1499]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Ominous and fearful portents appeared before the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f0c60f769dc6b69f31637c09> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1973]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that the elephant was descending, like angry Death, Janardana quickly wheeled the chariot, so that it93 remained on the left." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f0da4be7b6d97f4d2c22705b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4662]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Umbrellas and bows were pierced." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f0e10d519a15aecb85a21052> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8344]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "11 Slander must never be spoken, nor heard." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f0ed02739425aa04d105987a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7671]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son! On this, an account recited by the gods is cited." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f10b9047380a2468c4eab3e9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[708, 710]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """“I have been comforted by the aged ones who are bulls among sages.
I have also obtained a great deal of riches, with which, I can sacrifice to the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f11502ad6b0bd146b51aee6f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[36]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "After resting for a while, Vishvakarma2 reflected and began to build an assembly hall for the great-souled Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f11747b71a43eb1f2ef70627> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1436]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Prana and apana are the offerings of clarified butter and the fire is between them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f11844c3fd4569d445e2d108> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9895]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Arjuna said, “O fortunate one! I have been commanded by Dharmaraja72 to observe brahmacharya for twelve years and do not have control over myself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f129e5e3f05b5f1982744a16> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9616, 9617]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """There was a terrible and great battle for the slaying of Shambara194 and I was the charioteer of the king of the gods then too.
Like that, I drove the steeds at the killing of Vritra.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f133c734fb9fc616145b4e5b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9345, 9365]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Jupiter80 moved in a retrograde direction.
No resolutions were made to the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f150373014bc5761dd027a28> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8020, 8022, 8024]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Dakshinayana is mixed with a period of intense darkness.
247 Light moves upwards and it is an antidote to darkness.
It is because of light that the gods are energetic, powerful and radiant.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f154454b7e79b217315d15d4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3821]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘O king! Having been thus sent by the gods, he soon arrived at the capital of the king of the demons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f1570efad3bab2441089fe69> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10139]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But since he158 always followed dharma, the very next day, he could again bring the dead back to life." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f15d171411f6724c7fc82a99> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 152 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8589]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the rakshasas tried to restrain him, asking him to desist." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f15dab909dbaef32d14ea0be> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[556]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With the Shakas and the Yavanas, Goutama56 was on the right flank." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f15ff89b835bcbe8c96d2bdc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8024]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "321 He made Karna322 ascend his chariot and left with Satyaki." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f1653b8f7ab854925042057e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3384, 3385]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Why should someone like me not be afraid? O lord of the gods! Nevertheless, commanded by you, I must go to that sage.
O king of the gods! Find a means so that I can accomplish your wishes under your protection.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f1717bb8e12de05c45d24b65> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5997]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O tiger among men! Through your acts, accomplish what the gods have destined for you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f1793bb6da0f34073d895682> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[20222]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The Suparnas768 and the Maruts are associated with objects." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f19b39c3c8b7b3aafd8bfd5f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6349]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Brahma saw that cows were engaged in praya106 near him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f1a5f0d4d2dabe31cedfa16c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8075]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The Himalayas, giant among mountains, the ocean, the great store of water are regarded as vast and so is the space between heaven and earth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f1bd9134b0914533ad0a8f32> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[787]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "After the citizens had returned, the king63 sought Dhritarashtra’s permission to return, with the women from the inner quarters of the palace." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f1bf4b73f0c592d979907a98> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3193]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Vidura said, “Arya Pritha27 is a princess." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f1cc5196c7ac754c58c3744e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6195]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Indra among kings! O great king! Even if Keshava, Rama,182 Aniruddha,183 maharatha Pradyumna, Gada,184 Samba185 and all the Vrishnis armour themselves for our sake and seek to help us in the forefront of the battle, I will appoint Shini’s descendant, that tiger among men, for whom truth is his valour, as our aide." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f1f1bf91e361961203a0c0e3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13131]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When he is satisfied, the lord of the gods grants everyone their shares." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f1f657f8d2671eee16b6ea50> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[18700]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Creatures are born as inferior species, men and gods and go to hell." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f20c70566abbfe883f6b0662> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7288]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Monsoon arrived and a great flood submerged the world." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f2277c86a796cca8da65d9d8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8862]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ 181 Vaishampayana said, ‘Those bulls among the Brahmanas shook their deerskins and water pots29 and said, “Do not be frightened." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f23e043994634b9e152fba66> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10284]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He finds great satisfaction in the valour of your sons and of Abhimanyu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f241ca7f09555aac491551fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[659]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O best among the gods! What is good for her will also be good for me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f26be8cf99070fa4ea73ee84> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6370]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The extremely powerful and great-souled one danced, like the one with one thousand eyes721 after Vritra’s death." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f26d929a353102ad7a86ff79> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8605]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O unblemished one! In this way, your vow will remain true and the worlds, with their gods, will not be destroyed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f273e6bcaac53ade2106b41f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6439]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having obtained me, Indra, Vivasvat, Soma, Vishnu, the water113 and Agni have obtained prosperity and so have the rishis and the other gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f2781d46db34089247165aa6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2799]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Knowing that dharma loses one leg at the end of every yuga58 and that human life expectancy on earth and strength follow the pattern of the yugas, and moved by his desire to please Brahma and the Brahmanas, the learned one divided the Vedas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f2875b4de146069f45267f31> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4939]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At this, Goutama’s son226 took Lakshmana up on his own chariot and carried him away on the chariot, while all the soldiers looked on." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f29876fd7d8e32020d59050b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4215]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In ancient times, Vishnu used the dharma of kshatriyas to crush the enemy650 and protect all the gods and the infinitely energetic rishis." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f29b5da901b1232b7871e7f0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9809]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They were like the lord of the waters63 and Mitra attacking Taraka, supreme among daityas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f2c53ff62164741031073dd5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[504]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O god! That is the reason you have been established as a lord of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f2ca815e77803efbd5ac82da> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11245]" ;
        mbh:sourceText ") Vishva-yoni;562 (143) Punarvasu;563 (144) Upendra;564 (145) Vamana;565 (146) Pramshu;566 (." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f2d74a957f53ffc384bc5d59> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8292]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! For those twelve years, the one with a thousand eyes67 did not pour any rain in the king’s city and kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f2f2f044994a4a87db4e07d2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1311]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It arose into the sky in the form of Sudarshana127 and descended, like a second sun when the destruction of an era is near." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3064b7caa1e6d0de4b2108f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3800]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods killed all the demons who had assembled for battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3079bdc9f9fcfd684d56683> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4701]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Hardikya41 became angry at seeing that the one on white horses was thus penetrating." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f313591be4c4512777eeef55> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[587]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They were the equals of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3189c8da05d4e5c08b2051f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6712]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This has not been accomplished by the destroyer of Bala,772 Yama, the illustrious Prachetas773 and the king of the yakshas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3296d4733203ea6914414bf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2398]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Then Mahadeva grasped his277 body firmly and attacked him with energy and force, so that he was deluded of his senses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f34312cf96374dc2f2e4d4bd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2061]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He134 is slowly killing the misguided Jaratkaru, engaged in austerities, who is greedy for austerities, but has lost his mind and senses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3480543cfeeece05e21d2c1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2155]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bhurishrava, Shalya, the valorous Jarasandha, Bhishma, Drona, Karna, Drona’s valorous son240 and Dhritarashtra’s invincible sons with Duryodhana at the forefront—all of them have their weapons ready and are prepared to murder." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f350d3b51038d7d44325dc84> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11041]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O destroyer of enemies! Prithu created the first bow and with this, Vena’s son242 protected the world earlier." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3514f2529b7d61d02c6b36b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11581]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“The rakshasa grasped the head by the hair, with the blood dripping from it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f35f66f7143f3bf28790b3ac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11263]" ;
        mbh:sourceText ") Karta;788 (356) Vikarta;789 (357) Gahana;790 (358) Guha;791 (359) Vyavasaya;792 (360) Vyavasthana;793 (361) Samsthana;794 (362) Sthanada;795 (." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f367ff367450d05ef58549ac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[878]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 616(20) ‘Bhimasena said, “Shame on the strength of my arms and on Phalguna’s28 Gandiva! Your hands used to be red earlier, but are now covered in callouses." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f371fae1d55e54c4e9340c10> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3576]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He prided himself in battle and was protected by Kripa, Vrisha255 and the others." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f38191a0b2d2eaba7ce119f9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11414, 11435]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """They are ahead of ancestors, gods and guests.
They can turn those who aren’t divinities into gods and turn gods into those who aren’t divinities.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f388a5803c5a62e5c804751f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[109, 116]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He was skilled in samkhya yoga12 and he spoke to the king, “There are a thousand reasons for grief and a hundred reasons for fear that delude people every day.
I will recount to you the shlokas that the great- souled Janaka16 chanted in earlier times, for imparting stability to one’s soul.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f38fd60b71152e7063ad2e59> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2001]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "219 But the gods conquered them through deceit." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f39d160b504065802162d8c7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11488]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘O god! All beings, with the gods, the asuras and men, and all mobile and immobile objects, have been created by you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3b9545a47e9bdf0020fd0ed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6198]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Through the valour of his arms, Havyavahana303 will be supremely satisfied with the fat of all beings in Khandava." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3bfa3a7222eb5b12aeb42b9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24502]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing that Indrani1241 had returned, Nahusha told her that the time period was over." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3c347c58cccac2491fe24d5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[628]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Who restrained his advance against Drona? Ushinara’s maharatha son54 covered the entire earth with the pole of his chariot, as if girding it with the hide of a calf." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3c988893998d903ef1a8605> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 69 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3681]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”125 Having heard these words of those who dwell in the sky, the king of the Puru lineage was delighted." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3cdd7d916ae8ee66c3c5476> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2590]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Having been thus addressed, he352 agreed and ascended the chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3d256bd8bfef0e677162328> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3984]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He was the one who was worshipped by gods, danavas, yakshas and humans." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f3d6e6734eb8fb9a4a92eb17> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1289]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing him, all the beings43 sought the refuge of Vibhavasu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f401682e75120cefb215da58> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3983]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Or is it that she has thought of a great means for my sake? Why has the ascetic daughter of Vidarbha decided to perform this cruel act? I am mean and deceitful and my intelligence has been deluded by sin." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4106c99c6bd1afebc421bf0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[386]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "His shoulders, eyes, gait and voice was like that of Sthanu’s36 bull." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f411e193289fd0cc0f3554bc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6019]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O god! O lord of the gods! It is for this reason and for the welfare of the world that we are bringing this to your notice." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f41a1f702f9cec0022f913d6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[273]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On the instructions of Vichitravirya’s son25 and on Govinda’s words, he will allow you to retain the kingdom." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f42a5a9883de1fdda1f31fdc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10783, 10784, 10786]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """It penetrates the earth and goes all the way to the nether regions, generating great terror among the gods, the danavas and the yakshas.
It burns down the world of the nagas and whatever can be found on earth.
Twenty yojanas at a time, that fire of destruction, helped by the inauspicious wind, consumes everything in hundreds and thousands, with all the gods, asuras, gandharvas, yakshas, serpents and rakshasas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f42d4a24ef46043a0f03620d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9764, 9766, 9767, 9785]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O Yudhishthira! The question that you have asked me is an extremely appropriate one.
O Yudhishthira! This is a conversation between Dvaipayana and a worm.
In ancient times the brahmana Krishna Dvaipayana, the essence of the brahman, was roaming around.
’” ‘Bhishma continued, “Thus addressed, he369 replied, ‘O worm! What will bring you happiness? Since you have been born as inferior species, I think that death should bring you happiness.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f450b3b51a3b253fd687bb82> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1578]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All of them were cheerful in their minds, like immortals in the world of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f457f53ffc340e1126fa7ed8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[85]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Narada recited it to the gods, Asita-Devala25 to the ancestors and Shuka to the gandharvas,26 yakshas and rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f45a8e96c0adee98f97026a0> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 118 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9815, 9817]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """But I worshipped my aged mother and on one occasion, I worshipped a brahmana, when he came to my house.
Since I worshipped that brahmana as a guest, I have not lost my memory.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f483a5d8800f7adf4087975d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3858, 3861]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Slain, he fell down on the ground.
Agitating your soldiers in the battle, the immensely strong Bhimasena conveyed Nanda and Upananda472 to Yama’s abode.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f48d1ecd986ae37ed5f76415> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22785]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "1062 Cast aside truth and falsehood." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f48e32be38c7ae9585f4ccf7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[693]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Subala’s daughter46 was knowledgeable about dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4a9fbfffcee73ad02ea242e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9598]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Know that predatory beasts and rakshasas are devoted to deceit and falsehood." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4bd1904103f0cb8957a39b3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 205 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12491, 12497, 12501, 12504, 12507]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O brahmana! Because of my association with him, I also became supreme in wielding the bow.
The brahmana fell down on the ground and shouted, “I am innocent.
I then told the extremely ascetic brahmana, who was dying on the ground.
O brahmana! I should be forgiven.
“O cruel one! O brahmana! You will be born as a hunter and will be born from a shudra womb.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4be8b9401055047ef21ad8e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13100]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You will be successful in passing through all the hells that are inhabited by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4c4240e200a670acf4f541e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7361]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On seeing this malformed one descend,4 Hidimba5 was frightened and told Bhimsena, “The evil- minded maneater is coming and he is angry." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4cc7e1f5c0a5b16a1d476ba> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22482, 22484]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘Is there anyone superior to me? Is there anyone who loves brahmanas more? Is there a second valiant Brahmanya1032 in the three worlds? If there is any such person, let him raise this spear, or make it tremble.
The large number of gods were frightened that he wished to become Indra.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4d47ccd996dad73704d5680> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4237]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The kings know him to be one who can vanquish the gods in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4d95bc45807547ceec2ebfc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7639]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let him never worship the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4df81d273d0ce7a8647b640> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1311]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He38 is wise among the Kurus and wishes for the welfare of the Kurus." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4e66a62308454bb4532428a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3171]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king of Kashi, Shaibya, maharatha Shikhandi, Dhrishtadyumna, Virata, maharatha Satyaki, the great archer from Panchala91 and Droupadi’s five sons—all of them blew on giant conch shells and roared like lions." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4f8aa1be752de9ed2e2b92b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24615]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The quality of Vaikuntha1259 is in me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4fa9137bf102d7972af2c80> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16539]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O son! There were large numbers of Yayavara393 rishis, fierce in their austerities and accomplished and far-sighted about dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4faba5b8a342ea34c1ee850> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8082]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In ancient times, this agneya missile was given by Brihaspati, Shatakratu’s38 preceptor, to Bharadvaja." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4fd1ba82e5e373c86e7eca4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 134 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7173]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let us live here in a way that neither Purochana nor the inhabitants of the city know what we are doing." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f4fe83daa2371dada7f56d70> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11974]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Once, Pradyumna1412 was enraged by some brahmanas and asked, ‘O Madhusudana! What are the fruits associated with worshipping brahmanas? In this world and in the world hereafter, how do they get that sovereignty? O one who deserves honours! What are the fruits from constantly worshipping brahmanas? O father! Tell me everything about this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f50eae725d9a10c5dc8029a3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[420]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Vaishravana73 sports there with the guhyakas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f5411b440f850ea81d8a6911> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23168]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The energy of their austerities was such that even the gods were unable to look at them." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f542e4a734e6c00fb7acef11> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8285]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Thus Samvarana obtained his wife through austerities and worship of the Lord Gopati65 and Vashishtha’s energy." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f545c7998f611ea9ac90d88d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1827]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ When he heard this, the virtuous Shounaka smiled and told Ugrashrava117 that the names were appropriate." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f54bd4f8a160f0e3899ef8f5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11565, 11566]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O king! He will destroy the thirty gods and the world.
He cannot be killed by the gods, the daityas, the rakshasas, the nagas, the yakshas or any of the gandharvas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f550fd46b4d0379338a627ec> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[707]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O bull among the Bharata lineage! On seeing the great archer, Karna, stationed at the front of the vyuha, no one128 thought of Drona’s loss." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f55ec6cab20e6c05604d825f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25431]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I will slay the insolent enemies of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f563b756ef2dae12160d00be> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10471]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They deserve the worship of all the gods, asuras, yakshas, rakshas, gandharvas, humans, kinnaras50 and serpents." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f56b80eeb98f5f7edc1c27da> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6524]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He pervades all the gods and the asuras and all the comforts are established in him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f595ecbf7fd33b5aaaa94bb6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[19019]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ ‘“Brahma said, ‘If there is a man who is confounded by tamas and indulges in cutting down and chopping on auspicious days, then it664 shall penetrate him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f59920771c70dbadf82b6196> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21433]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "918 In that way, Ashva and the negation of Ashva are said to be the couple." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f5b3a2815741fa0296964eed> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2057]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ 639(43) ‘Karna said, “I see that all you honourable ones88 are frightened and terrified." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f5b54647fb7254b397d140dd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2168]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "32 Clubs and maces were the paths and chariots and elephants were the large trees." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f5cc2540b133b6740fe8804c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3232]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At that, great lamentations were heard from the inner quarters of the Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f5f03ec0b3c55b36c6285c0c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2688]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "34 The learned man who recites it to Brahmanas during sacred parvas35 is cleansed of his sins and becoming victorious over heaven36 attains union with the eternal brahman." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f5f2f5f8d1050a1b64929d8c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 301 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21198]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Spirit, joy, prosperity, contentment, radiance, happiness, purity, lack of disease, satisfaction, devotion, generosity, lack of hatred, forgiveness, fortitude, lack of injury, equanimity, truthfulness, repayment of debts, mildness, humility, lack of fickleness, cleanliness, uprightness, observance of conduct, lack of passion, lack of fear in the heart, indifference at separation from good and bad things, lack of boasting about acts performed, receiving when given, lack of desire for riches, the welfare of others and compassion towards all beings—these are said to be the qualities of sattva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f602bb0d926541d5ea778ffc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[830]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those are the principles laid down by the gods and a learned person is not confused by this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f61090ff6bfd6655a9db0a18> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5991]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "158 All the beings were astounded and delighted at the battle between the man and the rakshasa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f631ec215f9c9d5133fc5219> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4913]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Shakra’s son! Has Karna been killed by you today? In the assembly hall, in the midst of the brave Kurus, the evil-minded Karna spoke to Krishna579 and said, “O Krishna! Why don’t you abandon the Pandavas? They have fallen and are extremely feeble." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f63a5c279713b626e8cc9fd1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2286, 2287]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Atiratha135 Vikarna, foremost among the Kurus, fiercely attacked Partha, Bhima’s junior, from a chariot and showered down arrows on him.
He136 drew the firmly stringed bow that was embellished with the best of gold and routed Vikarna.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f64027a73ffd87279d228dc5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5941]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’” ‘Bhishma continued, “O bull among the Bharata lineage! This is what the grandfather79 told Indra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f64d163f0ddbe5702f80616e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6965]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” At the time of the origin of the worlds, this is what happened at the sacrifice of the great-souled one, the best of the gods who assumed the dazzling form of varuni." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f6535f4d8a5837533cbc03af> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3792]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He defeated all the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f6612d9765c4c8bea6010145> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22567]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘Go wherever you wish, to earth, or to the world of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f66b2f9cfb71eef4bee754bb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[87]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Yudhishthira is a great tree created out of righteousness, Arjuna is its trunk, Bhima is its branches, the two sons of Madri27 are its plentiful fruit and flowers, and Krishna, Brahma and the Brahmanas are the root." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f67e4796b660c01cfb46dea5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25027]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "With the desire to create the universe, he assumed the form of Purusha." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f683ffa1dcc26de759b31cfb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24353]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the one who is engaged in the welfare of gods, men and the worlds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f69a544e5a69e1cac2330243> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[251]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Chapter 1994(4) aishampayana said, ‘King Yudhishthira was praised by the gods, the rishis and the Maruts and went to where the bulls among the Kurus were." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f69b3a2c153ed3016f27a8cb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 38 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2665, 2668, 2669]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O descendant of the Bharata lineage! It is my view that the learned ones are those who can grasp the general principles, rather than the specific details.
‘“Having abandoned those supreme archers, the infinitely energetic Pandavas, you have entrusted the great prosperity of the Bharatas to Duryodhana.
You will soon see him dislodged from that, just as the foolish Bali, intoxicated with his riches, was dislodged from the three worlds.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f69bc018140e5a260a090c2a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 25 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1401]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He also saw many emancipated rishis." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f69d9cfcc5d9d122cc64cee6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3187]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "75 She charmed the minds of five men who were like Indras." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f6aceb37bcaffa2f7a8216df> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[543]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On hearing that Vaikartana has been killed in a duel with Savyasachi and on witnessing the victory of the Pandavas, what did Duryodhana say? He heard that Durmarshana and Vrishasena107 had been killed in the battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f6b9d199141a3777c0a21d10> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8603]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Bhishma did not strike him in battle, though he436 did not understand the reason." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f6c5bf2d6b24422ef8866505> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6927]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If Phalguni is unwilling to fight with someone who is not a king, I install him23 as king in the land of Anga." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f6e62f54ae875d3e619ac727> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5037]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "70 In ancient times, at the time of battle, Hiranyagarbha71 himself fastened it on Vishnu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f6e72a9c583c2af4dffe61c7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17839]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Is he taking a long time530 because of repentance? Has he been delayed because he has slept for a long time? Perhaps Chirakarika is not showing himself because of the great torment it will cause to both of us." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f6e76e0bfc73111c5ef41519> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7934]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Was his409 chariot shattered? Did his bow break into fragments?” ‘Sanjaya said, “O bull among the Bharata lineage! When he fought in that battle, Bhishma’s bow was not shattered." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f6ea1f57bf9f6fadf257c63d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4551]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O lord! Adityas,25 Vasus,26 Rudras,27 the Sadhyas,28 with the Maruts29 and gandharvas and apsaras30 are always present there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f6f7eae584b470f4d4daa9eb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22655, 22656]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """In the sky, it bears the celestial vehicles of the gods.
This fourth wind is named Samvaha1050 and it shatters mountains.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f70123d7dbd560aa4fa200eb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[713]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "She was like a creeper embracing a large and flowering sala tree11 on the banks of the Gomati, like the wife of the king of animals12 waking up a sleeping lion in the deserted forest." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f702889d3542ee62f8885224> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9850]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They are as extensive as the ocean and are like the masses of gods in battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f7054db208a917a37b799eb5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3513]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At this, Lakshmana used shafted arrows to slice down his128 bow at the handle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f710a5cec69ceb1379baf8cf> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4783]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Heaven is obtained through austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f71b54807f3c149f405c03cd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4372]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O Arjuna! Is Gandiva not in your hand? Or are you not stationed on your chariot? Are your arms well? Is your valour still there?’ Having been thus addressed by Krishna, he524 was enraged." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f728051dcf46b4739dec078c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6702, 6704]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """To kill the one who hates the gods, he will have a son who will surpass all the gods, danavas, rakshasas, men, gandharvas, serpents and birds.
He will destroy the one who has led to your fear and all the other enemies of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f72dcfaa5992177e3c639467> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2186, 2187]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O Pandava! For the sake of weapons, he must go to the great Indra, Rudra, Varuna, the lord of riches245 and Dharmaraja.
246 Because of his austerities and valour, he has the power to see the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f73a1044498c389f9249bde6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17005]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Section Forty-Three Kundala-aharana Parva This parva has 294 shlokas and eleven chapters." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f746d0f1ba51a560da18ede7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25955]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods are not superior to you in any way." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f7584cbb096cc864399f6076> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[289]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! This subsequent craving36 only leads to sorrow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f7599150b1b12f0793b4ae00> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2583]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In a delighted frame of mind, the intelligent descendant of the Kuru lineage7 ascended upwards." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f75eacb0c2cdc2584909dc8d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2925]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "2 Following him, the gods also go into a decline." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f7644b32f66b7f7d65a90252> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[375]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He went to the door of the sabha and deluded by his memories of Vidura, fell down unconscious in the presence of the lords of the earth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f7702e6aabc3cbcca2acef33> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7207]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘ “His806 mind was overcome with great grief." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f77e7a3dd47f627818d78af5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7800]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having revived all of them, the gods returned to heaven." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f7843c133250e4ce83673a28> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4063]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In that battle, the sons of Madri, the delight of their mother, enveloped their maternal uncle168 with a wonderful torrent of arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f787f0097203d2eb4ac6dc7d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2683]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If one resides in Kanyahrada, one goes to the world of the gods and never goes to Vaivasvata’s1221 abode." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f793e1d0f5f00041f96cc32c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1216]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Dvaipayana said, “O Yudhishthira! Bibhatsu’s173 words are completely true." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f793e98e00f862580cbd49cd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3530]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He who degrades his own self and represents falsely cannot find refuge with the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f79ae2fe47b529d61ce1071e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7066]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On witnessing this valour, which warriors will run away? O mighty-armed one! Who are the ones whom King Vaivasvata247 has remembered today?’ ‘“Satyaki said, ‘Like Vasava against the danavas, I will slay the ones with the shaved heads and fulfil my vow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f7b533caa9b01df25e92124e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12835]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In ancient times, the gods and the asuras were always engaged in destroying each other." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f7b8685d4c777ceab80ae91a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9122]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The kings who honoured the grandfather were as brilliant as the gods worshipping the grandfather,467 the lord of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f7b884980526b51b38581be2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6917]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Having heard this and much else spoken by Galava, King Ushinara216 gave him this reply, ‘O Galava! I have heard the words that you have spoken." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f7bc444a5b1cbc3c90dd0c5a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2338, 2340]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ 48 Shounaka said, ‘At the snake-sacrifice of the wise king Janamejaya of the Pandava lineage, who were the supreme rishis who acted as sacrificial priests? Who were the sadasyas148 at that terrible snake-sacrifice that brought great fear and misery to the snakes? O son! You should describe this in detail.
’ Souti said, ‘I shall certainly tell you the names of those wise ones who became ritvijas149 and sadasyas for the king.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f7c6b79cfe7c5a367b44564f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6971]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ They again told her, ‘We are the physicians of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f7f7406498803d66f776530c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7347]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! In that battle, Drona was enveloped by Panchala’s261 arrows and on seeing this, great sounds of lamentation suddenly arose." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8100eb3032bc3fff70932c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2620]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“Fire arose from water." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f81423c43d219785607415bb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5795]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Your soldiers were terrified by the standard of the wielder of Gandiva." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f818c3a75670e387bf935c37> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9826]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Because of their deeds, gods also have to come down to earth, or are born as inferior species." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8382ca616b7a5840fc1217c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2834]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O descendant of the Bharata lineage! Manu85 has said that for the sake of good fortune, a goat, an ox, sandalwood, a veena, a mirror, honey, butter, iron, copper,86 a conch shell, gold, the nave of a wheel and yellow pigment for honouring gods, brahmanas and guests must be kept in a household." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f84d70d9b3fc4698930f0ed7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1885]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "At that time, the powerful Sahadeva bore the brave and unvanquished king19 away from the field of battle on his chariot." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f85382ac3296736e58479480> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4390]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "How was the lord of the waters consecrated by the gods and the asuras? O immensely wise one! O supreme one! You are skilled in narrating." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8541576df589ef3e42649b1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5556]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That terrible weapon arose with the ambrosia359 and Savyasachi has now obtained it, together with the mantras for withdrawing, repulsing and releasing it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f85585680d5bec923373fdac> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[24317]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Light, earth and wind vanish." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f85e0ec896094e003a9ca33a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8107]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Even in the forest, together with Droupadi, Partha Pandava331 enjoys a kingdom,332 surrounded by his brothers, who wield weapons." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f863d257eef71a84f56b5225> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 71 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3361, 3362]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Go back to the Pandavas.
If they do not return, offer respect to the Pandavas.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f865946b03b6cf06fb8ce881> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17649]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods, the gandharvas, the asuras and the rakshasas are incapable of withstanding them in a great battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8671f13e13ad3e1b618ecbe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2828]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "How is it that the chaste wife of the Pandus, the sister of Parshata’s son221 and a friend to Vasudeva, has been brought into this assembly of kings? O Kouravas! I am Dharmaraja’s wife and I was born in the same varna as he." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f883d151e677a90bc787828b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15335]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ At this, all the gods, the gandharvas and serpents happily descended on earth, with respective parts from their own bodies." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8aeaf58cab1b6220d2b507f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[325]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I have myself heard what the gods wanted done." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8b2504836f669dd3517eadc> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9774]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "But while she was thus circumabulating the gods, only Indra and the illustrious god Sthanu45 managed to maintain their composure." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8b5c3029395dde499e46c17> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10906]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "77 He said, ‘O illustrious one! I wish to have a son to exact vengeance on Bhishma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8bb9b9e06081b44b60e6a51> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5496]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "A javelin was obtained50 for the destruction of Pandu’s son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8c4852f52536da1617212b9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2151, 2153]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He is equal to the king of the gods112 in archery.
Who will not show homage to Partha? He will fight and destroy divine114 with divine, human with human, weapons with other weapons.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8c702e4180f3547f122ed63> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12141]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ O king! He saw that the army was being destroyed by the rakshasa in the night." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8d51e009cc37b73e545dffd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14244, 14245]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Gods, asuras, giant serpents, pishachas, gandharvas, men, rakshasas, birds, snakes and other beings born in this universe will not be able to withstand you.
The gods will not be able to defeat you in a battle.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8e3aa78d97bf835c9a2c7cd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2024]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Armour was smeared with blood." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8f8808410e08b6fe7b2034a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2621]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "That evil son of Dhritarashtra gave poison to Bhima with his food, but the warrior Vrikodara14 digested it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f8fc053a1253809ac27e30eb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3749]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Those great archers will station themselves on the ancient path followed by Indra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f909bbc70edff0eda47dec9b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4629]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "195 The intelligent one saw him in the worlds meant for those who sacrifice with animals and roaming around in the unblemished worlds revered by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f9110c18ef5dbc44016221f2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1128, 1134]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """’ Chapter 1294(11) Vaishampayana said, ‘O Janamejaya! On seeing that his sons, brothers and friends had been slain in the encounter, his8 soul was immersed in great grief.
‘At that time, when it was morning, Nakula brought Krishna9 there, on a chariot that was as radiant as the sun.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f92ace3c75ece81dc8640b7f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11569]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He1391 invited Utathya and gave away the illustrious one as a wife and he received her in the proper way, with a lot of dakshina." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f9360848b16e141dff13c907> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3580]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! Bhimasena’s son131 was there, together with the maharatha Kekayas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f9493308fb740fca353e6261> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3784]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Yet again, extremely angry, Bhishma used straight-tufted arrows to cover the two Krishnas141 on every side." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f94fb1f21c923cee48e85295> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4717]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ’ ‘S Chapter 1195(45) anjaya said, “O king! Surrounded by a large array of chariots, Drona’s son swiftly descended on the spot where the king553 was." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f953b716a1c2ffa796c746be> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8319]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Peacocks, pushpashakunas,37 swans, cranes, chatakas and masses of jivamjivakas38 follow the Pandavas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f95a35e342f24f49b792ebf3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6282]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "323 The rakshasa was enveloped by many kinds of nagas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f971fb3950cc67df169a52d7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1261]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O immensely fortunate one! However, in prana’s absence, you rushed towards Prajapati and asked the illustrious one to rescue you." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f972206472f4a518b1535589> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16012]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If you do not release her, with my sharp arrows, I will rid the world of all rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f97a7d5355a24adb9cdd560d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12837, 12838]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """On witnessing that his armies had been destroyed by them several times, Purandara232 was greatly anxious about finding a general for his army.
He thought, ‘I must find an extremely powerful person who, on seeing the army of the gods destroyed, will have the valour to protect it.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f97fb5b954789895e6a92955> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5164]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Repeatedly resorting to the koushika26 technique of jumping up and circling, he27 discerned when Bhimasena would strike down with the club and deceived him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f980f06540b74886bec6a33d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "18_Svargarohana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3, 6, 7, 9]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """It is the last Parva of the Mahabharata.
Yudhishthira is shown hell and then goes to heaven.
In the numbering of the chapters in Svargarohana Parva, the first number is a consecutive one, starting with the beginning of the Mahabharata.
J Chapter 1991(1) anamejaya said, ‘My great grandfathers obtained heaven, the abode of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f986e5e4616dd1e3a59b9f24> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2500]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "333 They were pure and by censuring the wicked rakshasa, killed him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f99e5033d5c1d7ffe9c7ff42> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9113]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The daughters of the god of the gods offer him pleasure there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f9a8cc37367cea82c5f11cae> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9718]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Snakes, animals, pishachas and rakshasas do not strike him." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f9c33b228bbbbe8730166140> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[13641, 13643]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Keshava instructs them, with Bhanu7 and the others.
With Rama8 and the others, all the Andhakas and Vrishnis are devoted towards them.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f9d5ef3862e981b8675e125f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23472]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods anxiously reflected on the king’s good deeds." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f9da70ad5bf018060cb0a09a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3972]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O Yudhishthira! Then Damayanti summoned that brahmana173 again." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/f9e028a1069b8bd0ca95c5f1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3412]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let Droupadi’s sons441 and Shikhandi advance against the remaining sons of Dhritarashtra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fa29d0a220d283d56caebb93> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4906]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "194 This has been sung by Sanatkumara195 and the great-souled Vyasa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fa2f8df0da47cf61e082fa19> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7605]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The conch shell, the chakra, the club, the spear, the Sharnga,285 the plough and Nandaka286 could be seen." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fa3d5565090c3524877ce898> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[850]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The king of Abhisara143 struck Shrutakarma with nine straight-tufted arrows and pierced his charioteer with five." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fa65751e833d34381536807b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1259]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” Having thus obtained Krishna’s permission, Pandava8 and his brothers began to prepare the means for the rajasuya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fa708abecaccf37ecf64bf2c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[355]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "63 He was foremost among the gods and was a great ascetic." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fa76545ddfcaae74a3220fa5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2112]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "So as to please you, Nakula, Sahadeva and the aged mother236 who has given birth to warriors are seated, benumbed and dumb." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fa8de398c0dd4dfc833210e6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4590]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having offered oblations to the ancestors and the gods, one obtains the fruits of agnishtoma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fa929d973262a9845dda9cff> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[91]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In accordance with what is laid down in law, their two mothers29 conceived sons from Dharma, Vayu, Shakra30 and the two gods, the Ashvins." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fab6c25b32fd933af81b7c60> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4819]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“O unblemished one! But it pleases me, and is also worthy of you, that you should bow in obeisance and show your respects to your father10 and Bhishma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fab9ab7a5e15af515578d087> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4458]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O best of the Bharata lineage! The maharatha534 tried his best." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fabd8622474d2f0e54d7add6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14342, 14345, 14366]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """He is the lord of the gods.
He is Sharva.
He is the one who bears oblations to the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fac86c30c6439787d0033df7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6822]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Let Dhartarashtra524 go to the eternal world of Yama." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fae3e2b944b43088f0455622> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[14886]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Like a man who has kicked it, you wish to counter the angry and terrible Jishnu." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/faec923a83484c37dc6446c5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[249]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Vishvakarma built it after spending a long time in austerities." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/faeeab0ac7aac97b167c391f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[21390]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Not understanding what the great-souled Bhaskara907 intended, I became angry." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb036d84b4ea8f14b898e4e7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2170]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In ancient times, this is what the grandfather and the gods told me." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb03fbf1d8ffbb89c6005863> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7259]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Brihaspati afflicted Rohini812 and assumed the complexion of the moon and the sun." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb05f2b8f92df07ad8411470> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "10_Souptika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1191]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The preceptor gave it16 to his beloved Dhananjaya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb1029da31f2ca9e764e7209> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 23 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2458, 2465, 2467]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """There are bulls among brahmanas who have studied the four Vedas and the six Vedangas and have withdrawn from action.
Even one brahmana who is excellent is capable of saving an entire lineage.
If one hears that a brahmana who possesses the qualities and is revered by the virtuous lives some distance away, even then, one must honour him and worship him in every possible way.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb23074df5745b73bad4db81> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6448, 6451]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """They728 had been prepared well, were crazy and were from the Himalaya regions.
Using ten arrows that were completely made out of iron, the son of Kuninda729 severely struck Kripa and his charioteer.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb244bf30da2c62b7a947fa8> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[496]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "We repaired its fortifications so that it became impregnable even to the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb38848460d9e2901392c9e9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[967]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Heaven is superior to these." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb50a27a882a266a30fff99c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3072, 3073]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """In a horse sacrifice, he then gave it479 to Kashyapa as dakshina.
O king! Wishing to save the remaining kshatriyas, Kashyapa held the sacrificial ladle480 in his hand and spoke these beneficial words.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb5777b72823b2cb51f1e69a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9788]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "‘“One day, they went to sport in a rocky plain on the Vindhya Mountains that was dense with shala50 trees crested with blossoming flowers." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb5dc409a7891421e2e577d9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16259]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods roared like lions in heaven and sounded drums." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb60d5ba41479ae3c5d9b97b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8022]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The mighty-armed Bhimasena wished to kill Saindhava and he covered him319 with arrows." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb6f363d5ab4e91bd07eb5fe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[16153]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He332 has been spoken about in the words of the Vedas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fb8d728de3a1fac4894d9b8b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1953]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘The brave and strong one75 took the bracelets off from his arms." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fba0ad9969a9182de0656c80> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8531]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "373 All the Kurus and the charanas applauded this attempt of snatching Karna from his chariot, like Tarkshya374 grabbing a serpent." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fbad8f9b88a433a9492f2b9b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3244]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’41 Janamejaya asked, ‘Why was the illustrious Soma afflicted by tuberculosis? How did Chandra42 bathe in that supreme of tirthas? Having bathed there, how did Shashi regain his energy? O great sage! Tell me everything about this in detail." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fbb4c8cb1350cca1168ba793> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3004]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "26 Aha was Rata’s son and the fire27 was Shandilya’s son." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fbfa5a59ae38ae019efe78fd> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[23422]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You will then become aides in performing a task for the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fc00fd0d0dc60cb40d359c2a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 42 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3920]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” On hearing these words, the sages praised the great river." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fc0ca8cd3626e04f1a1907ca> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17179]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The god of the gods, the lord of the lords,481 was himself silent." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fc0e830f275115344941c9fb> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8880, 8881]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O supreme among Brahmanas! Are you Rama,33 the personification of the knowledge of weapons?34 Or are you Harihaya35 himself? Or are you Achyuta Vishnu himself? Have you assumed the form of a Brahmana to disguise yourself and are now fighting strongly with me for self-preservation, mustering the strength of your arms? When I am angry in the field of battle, no one except Shachi’s husband36 and Pandava Kiriti37 can withstand me.
” Hearing these words, Phalguni38 replied, “O Karna! I am not the science of weapons personified.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fc15c38541d82e4c32c6496f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1831, 1832]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """In the duel, the brave one was deprived of his chariot by Satyaki.
At this, all the soldiers15 were overcome by great fear and your sons were miserable, because Kritavarma had been deprived of his chariot and his horses and charioteer had been slain.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fc2797516fe911761d6141ca> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1478]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It was like the greatly energetic Puruhuta1 speaking to Brihaspati." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fc5f55fcfc0af5f58d410514> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5751]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The intelligent person808 must protect the wise, the brave, the rich, the powerful, those who follow dharma, the ascetics and the truthful." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fc6d84673862fabb5f808584> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[12119]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "All the assembled gods spoke to the great-souled one." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fc735b5ccb73b20a030e48d3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9063]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "You are the equal of Ushanas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fc9709f5e6a3b15cec88a6c1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1954]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "348 Those who worship the gods attain the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fcba15e700e03c1537c12106> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9667]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Rathas fought against rathas and caused fierce flowing of blood." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fcc6713089d8927b2ae46200> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3650]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "We witnessed the valour displayed by Hidimba’s son137 and it was extraordinary." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fcd02d2b1cb8030368ae9a3d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[17085]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Desiring peace, he roamed around on earth472 and saw Narada." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fcd99708557c4bfa170939e1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8741]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "9 When they were about to engage in that terrible battle with arms, Madri’s two sons10 were also extremely angered and rushed forward." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fcf4bad98def8958b4ed2649> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6366]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Why did the chastiser of Paka454 not rain down in his territory? O lord! O exalted one! Tell me all this exactly, and in detail." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fcf7e05811deddd9d660c746> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 203 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9748]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There they saw the grandfather seated with the gods, surrounded by siddhas and brahmarshis." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fcfc743317a586b50de4a62c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2960, 2962]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Lakshmana95 was extremely energetic and used his arrows and weapons to attack Arjuna’s son.
Other maharathas also returned and followed Duryodhana.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fcff381eb916c17055bdc95e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3362]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Just as a snake is swallowed up by a hole in the ground, a king who is unwilling to fight and a brahmana who does not dwell far away1267 are both swallowed." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd0b47562e3a5b1906d72c4e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6063]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods told him everything." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd1b87ef9384f5fe5cdd4f89> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11967]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In the night, there was an extremely tumultuous battle between the rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd1f71ed16eb1cd85f5e7e9c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4721, 4723]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Suhotra was a king who ruled over his subjects in accordance with dharma.
People and crops were plentiful and the earth was adorned with the presence of the gods.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd3646c735c299f345453f33> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8716]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He saw the stupid rakshasa, who had lost his path, his intelligence having been robbed by time." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd3b4788cf259cccffd8e7ea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6203]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having been struck by the shower of weapons released by the yavanas698 on elephants, Phalguna smiled and severed those with his sharp broad-headed arrows and arrows in the form of a half-moon." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd4bebd36496847b5b37e51f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[939]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The gods rejoiced in heaven, as did the many living beings on earth." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd5ac8a1502d2c9632a4cc68> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10925]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I am present in the sacrifices of the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd61002b05ea4e139746dab3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2448, 2452, 2458]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The great Vishnu, immersed in the brahman, is the origin of the world and the universe.
Day ends when the sun sets.
Association ends in disassociation.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd67b8a4afcc1bb44db524a2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4957]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’” ’ ‘S Chapter 1198(48) anjaya said, “On hearing that the immensely valorous Karna was still alive, the infinitely energetic Partha586 became angry with Phalguna." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd7122e894192496a2db5d02> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[385]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The illustrious Pashupati65 himself, the creator of beings, sports there, surrounded by divine beings and accompanied by Uma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd8d12c3df2cb3a97442adc3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6556, 6557, 6558]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘The great-souled son336 of Jamadagni was a conqueror of enemies.
O king! He337 heard that he was giving away all his wealth to Brahmanas.
Bharadvaja’s son spoke to him when Rama338 was already leaving for the forest.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd8d529a09e9e61c0a30b1ea> a mbh:Passage ;
