        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1887, 1888, 1889]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """) Bhuta-bhavana;689 (484) Sarathi;690 (485) Bhasma-shayi;691 (486) Bhasmagopta;692 (487) Bhasmabhuta;693 (488) Taru- gana;694 (489) Agana;695 (490) Lopa;696 (.
) Mahatma;697 (491) Sarva- pujita;698 (492) Shanku;699 (493) Trishanku; (494) Sampanna;700 (495) Shuchi;701 (496) Bhuta-nishevita;702 (497) Ashramastha;703 (498) Kapotastha;704 (499) Vishvakarma;705 (500) Patirvara;706 (501) Shakha;707 (.
) Vishakha;708 (502) Tamroshtha;709 (503) Ambujala;710 (504) Sunishchaya;711 (505) Kapila;712 (506) Akapila;713 (507) Shura;714 (508) Ayu;715 (.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fd8f4ca33bcbd139e1a5358d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[22583]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It is like the moon, when it is invaded by Upaplava1042 and enveloped in dust and darkness." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fda8b52571b6cc506d0c6f19> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1892]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "He262 picked up another bow and pierced Pandava back." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fdad8a10cef9ffbc14bdb56e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8933, 8934, 8935, 8936]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """If a person eats only one meal a day during the month of Jyeshthamula,322 that person obtains the greatest and supreme prosperity, regardless of whether the birth is as a man or as a woman.
Without any distraction, if a person eats only one meal during the month of Ashadha,323 he is reborn with a lot of grain, a lot of riches and a lot of sons.
If a person is controlled and eats only one meal during the month of Shravana,324 he enhances his relatives and is consecrated by them as superior.
If a man eats only one meal during the month of Proshthapada,325 he swells with wealth and his prosperity remains stable.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fdb08c3375cbe327a3604cea> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4449]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Without the one whose deeds are undecaying, the forest became like Chaitraratha201 when Kubera is not there." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fdbdebf49f06fc1a87dc2a6a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6826]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Partha526 is my brother." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fdc516561d36ee16348337b5> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1166]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "” ’ ‘S Chapter 1164(14) anjaya said, “Jishnu again returned, like the planet Angaraka181 in its forward and retrograde motions, to kill large numbers of samshaptakas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fde17e2fe6e7c46277861b24> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[135]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There is an extremely terrible comet and it is based in Pushya and is oppressing it." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fdec8dd4b1835894b0ddef41> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7169]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Deceiving this evil one64 and that evil one, Suyodhana, let us live here for some time, hiding where we go." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe071bab19d9d9643d7086b2> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "14_Ashvamedhika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2946]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Depending on their qualities, many different kinds of beings have originated from the five elements—gods, men, gandharvas, pishachas, asuras and rakshasas." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe11652c266e715fca285b3f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9391]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "If a person eats without having completed the rites of oblation for the gods and the ancestors, he is born as a crow." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe23807701d12abfaca7ea66> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1793, 1794]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Through the favours of the god,197 in ancient times, the great-souled lord of the gods198 uttered those names.
’”’ Chapter 1698(17) asudeva said, “O father!199 O Yudhishthira! The brahmana rishi200 controlled himself.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe24b8a1a3dbb919c79954fa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9169]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "On the instructions of the lord of riches, the dead bodies of the rakshasas were removed from the summit of the mountain." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe2eb0c918594e648760875c> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1154]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Surrounded by them, the king’s86 eyes were filled with tears of joy and he thought himself to be back in his house in the city of Gajasahvya." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe352fcf7edd0a136003fdbe> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2594]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "There he saw King Janamejaya seated, surrounded by his many sacrificial assistants,4 like Purandara5 surrounded by the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe3ca49a170b5c12b8109e4a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[5697]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "In her father’s258 house, she was appointed to honour the gods and guests." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe4bf5fd0d21629307a80b02> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2015]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "While that was going on, I was given the task of reciting Sama hymns and he1138 told me, ‘O foremost among brahmanas! The rathantara is not being chanted properly." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe5122415a100331b42e3091> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2830]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Miserliness destroys fame." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe6131bec6140c04fe94ab08> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3988, 3990]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """”’ CHAPTER 917(57) ‘Sanjaya said, “O venerable one! Drona’s son, Bhurishrava, Shalya, Chitrasena158 and Samyamani’s son159 fought with Subhadra’s son.
No one was equal to Krishna’s son160 in sureness of aim, courage, valour, knowledge of weapons and dexterity.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe6a62f2dd9027d5767b642a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 148 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7754]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Today, I will go to that rakshasa with my entire family, so that the evil one can eat all of us together." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe7ec3211bf07b6f98e94dde> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "09_Shalya" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4736, 4738]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """Prajapati’s son was Bhrigu, the creator of worlds, and that supreme rishi had obtained him211 through his fierce austerities.
The lord212 was famous and was as tall as the Himalayas, the greatest of mountains.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe8f602487c3239b640954ff> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[25512]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "1358 The lion among rishis1359 thought about this." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fe9834e54096814b9c63129f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[10065]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 474(177) Vaishampayana said, ‘On seeing his beloved brother encircled in the coils of the snake, the wise Yudhishthira approached and told the brave one, “O one whose mother is Kunti! How has this misfortune befallen you? Who is this supreme of serpents, with a body that is equal to a mountain?” On seeing his elder brother Dharmaraja, he47 told his brother everything that had happened and how he had come to be grasped." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fea292b5a2c5a03a5d481700> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "08_Karna" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7300]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "The infinitely energetic one818 used the vajra to slay Vritra in a battle." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/feb407bfb99b0ea39882702a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7223]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This is the region where King Nahusha568 performed an extremely holy sacrifice and gave away ten padmas to the assisting priests." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fed1181cb58fd2dc83d5bf2e> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[11262]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They advanced over the plain ground to the western120 side of Kurukshetra." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fee749471d915664881905a9> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[534]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O king! All of them have been dislodged from the world of the gods and are without sin." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/feea9e4a91ad950c71c14525> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9073, 9074, 9075]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """You are like Suparna2 to the birds.
You are like Kumara3 to the demons.
4 You are like the bearer of oblations5 to the Vasus.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fef8fd28a8a97f92f14f5f5d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4410]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having entered, the lord of the Nishadhas comforted the citizens." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fefb9156e83cc9a6cd059950> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1424]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "When there is a calamity, depending on one’s livelihood, dharma and adharma should be followed accordingly." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/fefc547694439c65fe64e4da> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8382]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Through all his radiant energy, he became a Brahmana and Kushika’s son89 eventually drank the soma90 juice with Indra himself." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ff008c8b0d1764c2a34fbf2a> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8332, 8335]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """O Arjuna! She yielded products of villages and forests, herbs, milk, juices with six different flavours73 that tasted like ambrosia itself, and different types of food that could be chewed, drunk, eaten, licked and sucked, all tasting like ambrosia.
With great surprise, he74 saw Vashishtha’s beautiful and unblemished cow, named Nandini75—six measures long, three measures wide and five measures around, with beautiful flanks and thighs, with eyes prominent like those of frogs, with a beautiful carriage, large udders, beautiful tail, uplifted and straight ears, handsome horns and a well-developed head and neck.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ff0d07e25070d8d9bc81145b> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[3093]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "93 She then saw all the gods, without sweat and with fixed glances." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ff2bd3342b9052b24763eeff> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "04_Virata" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2361]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Crowded with gods, yakshas, gandharvas and giant serpents, the cloudless sky was dazzling, as if with the planets." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ff48d9ae15af12c2ec69c651> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:chapterOrdinal 80 ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel true ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4548, 4550]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """It is famous in the three worlds and is known by the name of Pushkara.
O lord of the earth! At the time of the three sandhyas,24 ten thousand crores of tirthas can be found in Pushkara.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ff6eb063141097f4a46f9fd3> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "01_Adi" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7352]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "I will save all of you from the desire of that man-eating rakshasa." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ff7fc52b7ca046182d8ff9aa> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "13_Anushasana" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[6989]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "It has been said that it154 is like Agni and its donation brings happiness." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ff862c019b6fa65c819ec9c7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "07_Drona" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[9573]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Krishna35 was born in a noble lineage and in her conduct, followed all forms of dharma." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ff890f06a4a8b0d2db496be1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "15_Ashramavasika" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[1489, 1490]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """The gods possess the power to enter human bodies.
Since they are gods, they can have offspring through resolution, words, sight, touch and intercourse.""" .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ff917d558b0bf9734dd24c4f> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[7009]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "They are the physicians of the gods and their acts make them unworthy of worship." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ffb27d99f0f52959c42092a4> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "05_Udyoga" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[4292]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ 724(61) Vaishampayana said, ‘Disregarding Vichitravirya’s son,141 who kept reflecting on the Parthas, Karna addressed Dhritarashtra’s son142 in the assembly of Kouravas, so as to cheer him up." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ffb54dbe872590110721c6b7> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "11_Stri" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[356]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "This is the entire truth and eternal mystery about the gods." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ffb9f4b95940026674a3d375> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15753]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "O beautiful one! Whatever the thirty gods have, I possess that." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ffc97ef8c9f14683ad827081> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "03_Aranyaka" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[15775]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "’ Thus addressing the one with the unblemished limbs, the lord of masses of rakshasas instantly disappeared and went in whatever direction he desired." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ffcb37545ef2789bf54085a6> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "12_Shanti" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[2589]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "Having taken the king’s349 permission, follow dharma and perform all those tasks." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ffd345c850729c5f5274ce5d> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "02_Sabha" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[717]" ;
        mbh:sourceText "”’ Vaishampayana said, ‘Having been thus addressed by that illustrious one and on seeing Bhima and Partha2 standing there with smiles on their faces, Yudhishthira replied, “O Achyuta! O Achyuta! Do not speak to me in that fashion." .

    <http://example.org/mbh/semantic/passage/ffe987146ef5018467e22bd1> a mbh:Passage ;
        mbh:citedAtChapterLevel false ;
        mbh:parvan "06_Bhishma" ;
        mbh:sourceSentenceIds "[8827, 8828]" ;
        mbh:sourceText """‘I am capable of slaying all the Pandavas with a single bow, had the immensely strong Vishvaksena447 not been their protector now.
There are two reasons for me not to fight with the Pandavas—the Pandus cannot be killed448 and Shikhandi’s feminity.""" .

